protege:defaultLanguage a owl:AnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000111 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "editor preferred term"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "The value of this annotation property provides the preferred term that an editor has chosen, from among all the alternative terms available, to represent a given class or property in a human readable form."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000112 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "example of usage"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "The value of this annotation property shows the correct usage of the class or property to which it is attached, in the form of a natural-language sentence or a subject-predicate-object statement.",
        "A phrase describing how a term should be used and/or a citation to a work which uses it. May also include other kinds of examples that facilitate immediate understanding, such as widely know prototypes or instances of a class, or cases where a relation is said to hold."@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "GROUP:OBI:<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi>"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:iao.owl ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000114 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has curation status"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000115 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "definition",
        "definition"@en ;
    IAO:0000111 "definition"@en ;
    IAO:0000114 IAO:0000122 ;
    IAO:0000115 "The official definition, explaining the meaning of a class or property. Shall be Aristotelian, formalized and normalized. Can be augmented with colloquial definitions."@en ;
    IAO:0000116 """2012-04-05: 
Barry Smith

The official OBI definition, explaining the meaning of a class or property: 'Shall be Aristotelian, formalized and normalized. Can be augmented with colloquial definitions'  is terrible.

Can you fix to something like:

A statement of necessary and sufficient conditions explaining the meaning of an expression referring to a class or property.

Alan Ruttenberg

Your proposed definition is a reasonable candidate, except that it is very common that necessary and sufficient conditions are not given. Mostly they are necessary, occasionally they are necessary and sufficient or just sufficient. Often they use terms that are not themselves defined and so they effectively can't be evaluated by those criteria. 

On the specifics of the proposed definition:

We don't have definitions of 'meaning' or 'expression' or 'property'. For 'reference' in the intended sense I think we use the term 'denotation'. For 'expression', I think we you mean symbol, or identifier. For 'meaning' it differs for class and property. For class we want documentation that let's the intended reader determine whether an entity is instance of the class, or not. For property we want documentation that let's the intended reader determine, given a pair of potential relata, whether the assertion that the relation holds is true. The 'intended reader' part suggests that we also specify who, we expect, would be able to understand the definition, and also generalizes over human and computer reader to include textual and logical definition. 

Personally, I am more comfortable weakening definition to documentation, with instructions as to what is desirable. 

We also have the outstanding issue of how to aim different definitions to different audiences. A clinical audience reading chebi wants a different sort of definition documentation/definition from a chemistry trained audience, and similarly there is a need for a definition that is adequate for an ontologist to work with."""@en,
        """2012-04-05: 
Barry Smith

The official OBI definition, explaining the meaning of a class or property: 'Shall be Aristotelian, formalized and normalized. Can be augmented with colloquial definitions'  is terrible.

Can you fix to something like:

A statement of necessary and sufficient conditions explaining the meaning of an expression referring to a class or property.

Alan Ruttenberg

Your proposed definition is a reasonable candidate, except that it is very common that necessary and sufficient conditions are not given. Mostly they are necessary, occasionally they are necessary and sufficient or just sufficient. Often they use terms that are not themselves defined and so they effectively can't be evaluated by those criteria. 

On the specifics of the proposed definition:

We don't have definitions of 'meaning' or 'expression' or 'property'. For 'reference' in the intended sense I think we use the term 'denotation'. For 'expression', I think we you mean symbol, or identifier. For 'meaning' it differs for class and property. For class we want documentation that let's the intended reader determine whether an entity is instance of the class, or not. For property we want documentation that let's the intended reader determine, given a pair of potential relata, whether the assertion that the relation holds is true. The 'intended reader' part suggests that we also specify who, we expect, would be able to understand the definition, and also generalizes over human and computer reader to include textual and logical definition. 

Personally, I am more comfortable weakening definition to documentation, with instructions as to what is desirable. 

We also have the outstanding issue of how to aim different definitions to different audiences. A clinical audience reading chebi wants a different sort of definition documentation/definition from a chemistry trained audience, and similarly there is a need for a definition that is adequate for an ontologist to work with.  """@en ;
    IAO:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "GROUP:OBI:<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi>"@en ;
    dcterms:description "The official definition, explaining the meaning of a class or property, shall be a genus-differentia definition wherever the term admits one; for primitive terms that cannot be defined non-circularly, an elucidation is supplied instead." ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:iao.owl ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000116 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "editor note",
        "editor note"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "An administrative note intended for its editor. It might record a rationale for a design decision, flag whether a definition/example is a verbatim quotation from the source ontology versus a paraphrase/reconstruction, or explain how a term connects to a domain ontology (here, TARA) that depends on it.",
        "An administrative note intended for its editor. It may not be included in the publication version of the ontology, so it should contain nothing necessary for end users to understand the ontology."@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "GROUP:OBI:<http://purl.obofoundry.org/obo/obi>"@en ;
    OboInOwl:hasDbXref "IAO:0000116" ;
    OboInOwl:is_metadata_tag true ;
    OboInOwl:shorthand "editor_note" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:iao.owl ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000117 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "term editor",
        "term editor"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000119 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "definition source"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "Formal citation -- e.g. the identifier of a document, an ISO/IEC standard, a book, a personal communication, or a URI -- for the source of a term's definition.",
        "Formal citation, e.g. identifier in external database to indicate / attribute source(s) for the definition. Free text indicate / attribute source(s) for the definition. EXAMPLE: Author Name, URI, MeSH Term C04, PUBMED ID, Wiki uri on 31.01.2007"@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "GROUP:OBI:<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi>"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:iao.owl ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000232 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "curator note",
        "curator notes",
        "curator note"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "An administrative note of use for a curator but of no use for a user"@en ;
    OboInOwl:hasDbXref "IAO:0000232" ;
    OboInOwl:is_metadata_tag true ;
    OboInOwl:shorthand "curator_notes" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:iao.owl ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000234 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ontology term requester"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000412 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "imported from"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "Annotation property connecting a term to the ontology document, denoted by an IRI, from which it is imported."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0000589 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "OBO foundry unique label"@en ;
    IAO:0000111 "OBO foundry unique label"@en ;
    IAO:0000114 IAO:0000125 ;
    IAO:0000115 "An alternative name for a class or property which is unique across the OBO Foundry."@en ;
    IAO:0000116 "The intended usage of that property is as follow: OBO foundry unique labels are automatically generated based on regular expressions provided by each ontology, so that SO could specify unique label = 'sequence ' + [label], etc. , MA could specify 'mouse + [label]' etc. Upon importing terms, ontology developers can choose to use the 'OBO foundry unique label' for an imported term or not. The same applies to tools ."@en ;
    IAO:0000117 "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
        "PERSON:Bjoern Peters"@en,
        "PERSON:Chris Mungall"@en,
        "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en ;
    IAO:0000119 "GROUP:OBO Foundry <http://obofoundry.org/>"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

IAO:0006012 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "scheduled for obsoletion on or after",
        "scheduled for obsoletion on or after"@en ;
    IAO:0000111 "scheduled for obsoletion on or after"@en ;
    IAO:0000115 "Used when the class or object is scheduled for obsoletion/deprecation on or after a particular date."@en ;
    IAO:0000117 "Chris Mungall, Jie Zheng"@en ;
    IAO:0000234 "GO ontology"@en ;
    OboInOwl:hasDbXref "IAO:0006012" ;
    OboInOwl:is_metadata_tag true ;
    OboInOwl:shorthand "scheduled_for_obsoletion_on_or_after" ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:iaoAnnotationProperty .

RO:0002475 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has no connections with" ;
    IAO:0000112 "'pectoral appendage skeleton' has no connections with 'pelvic appendage skeleton'" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A is has_no_connections_with B if there are no parts of A or B that have a connection with the other." ;
    OboInOwl:hasDbXref "RO:0002475" ;
    OboInOwl:is_class_level true ;
    OboInOwl:is_metadata_tag true ;
    OboInOwl:shorthand "has_no_connections_with" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:oboInOwlAnnotationProperty .

mondons:curated_content_resource a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "curated content resource" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A curated content resource is a web-resource that contains curated content about the ontology term." ;
    OboInOwl:is_class_level true ;
    OboInOwl:is_metadata_tag true ;
    rdfs:comment "This property is likely to change the ID. Please do not use in production systems." ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:mondoAnnotationProperty .

mondons:excluded_from_qc_check a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:mondoAnnotationProperty .

mondons:excluded_subClassOf a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "excluded subClassOf" ;
    OboInOwl:is_metadata_tag true ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:mondoAnnotationProperty .

mondons:should_conform_to a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "should_conform_to" ;
    OboInOwl:is_metadata_tag true ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:mondoAnnotationProperty .

dc:language a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Language" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:dctermsMetadata .

dc:member a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Member" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:dctermsMetadata .

dcterms:URI a rdfs:Datatype ;
    rdfs:label "URI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3986.txt> ;
    skos:definition "The set of identifiers constructed according to the generic syntax for Uniform Resource Identifiers as specified by the Internet Engineering Task Force."@en .

dcterms:W3CDTF a rdfs:Datatype ;
    rdfs:label "W3C-DTF"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-datetime> ;
    skos:definition "The set of dates and times constructed according to the W3C Date and Time Formats Specification."@en .

dcterms:abstract a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "abstract" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy dcterms: ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ;
    skos:definition "A summary of the resource."@en .

dcterms:accessRights a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Access Rights"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Access Rights may include information regarding access or restrictions based on privacy, security, or other policies."@en ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:RightsStatement ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:rights ;
    skos:definition "Information about who can access the resource or an indication of its security status."@en .

dcterms:alternative a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Alternative Title"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The distinction between titles and alternative titles is application-specific."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:title ;
    skos:definition "An alternative name for the resource."@en ;
    skos:note "In current practice, this term is used primarily with literal values; however, there are important uses with non-literal values as well. As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is leaving this range unspecified pending an investigation of options."@en .

dcterms:available a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Date Available"@en ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:date ;
    skos:definition "Date (often a range) that the resource became or will become available."@en .

dcterms:bibliographicCitation a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic Citation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Recommended practice is to include sufficient bibliographic detail to identify the resource as unambiguously as possible." ;
    rdfs:domain dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:identifier ;
    skos:definition "A bibliographic reference for the resource."@en .

dcterms:conformsTo a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Conforms To"@en ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:Standard ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "An established standard to which the described resource conforms."@en .

dcterms:created a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Date Created"@en ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:date ;
    skos:definition "Date of creation of the resource."@en .

dcterms:dateAccepted a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Date Accepted"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Examples of resources to which a Date Accepted may be relevant are a thesis (accepted by a university department) or an article (accepted by a journal)."@en ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:date ;
    skos:definition "Date of acceptance of the resource."@en .

dcterms:dateCopyrighted a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Date Copyrighted"@en ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:date ;
    skos:definition "Date of copyright."@en .

dcterms:dateSubmitted a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Date Submitted"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Examples of resources to which a Date Submitted may be relevant are a thesis (submitted to a university department) or an article (submitted to a journal)."@en ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:date ;
    skos:definition "Date of submission of the resource."@en .

dcterms:extent a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Extent"@en ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:SizeOrDuration ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:format ;
    skos:definition "The size or duration of the resource."@en .

dcterms:hasFormat a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Has Format"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "A related resource that is substantially the same as the pre-existing described resource, but in another format."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:hasVersion a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Has Version"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "A related resource that is a version, edition, or adaptation of the described resource."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:instructionalMethod a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Instructional Method"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Instructional Method will typically include ways of presenting instructional materials or conducting instructional activities, patterns of learner-to-learner and learner-to-instructor interactions, and mechanisms by which group and individual levels of learning are measured. Instructional methods include all aspects of the instruction and learning processes from planning and implementation through evaluation and feedback."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:dctermsMetadata ;
    skos:definition "A process, used to engender knowledge, attitudes and skills, that the described resource is designed to support."@en .

dcterms:isReferencedBy a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Is Referenced By"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "A related resource that references, cites, or otherwise points to the described resource."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:isReplacedBy a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Is Replaced By"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "A related resource that supplants, displaces, or supersedes the described resource."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:isRequiredBy a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Is Required By"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "A related resource that requires the described resource to support its function, delivery, or coherence."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:isVersionOf a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Is Version Of"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Changes in version imply substantive changes in content rather than differences in format."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "A related resource of which the described resource is a version, edition, or adaptation."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:issued a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Date Issued"@en ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:date ;
    skos:definition "Date of formal issuance (e.g., publication) of the resource."@en .

dcterms:license a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "License"@en ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:LicenseDocument ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:rights ;
    skos:definition "A legal document giving official permission to do something with the resource."@en .

dcterms:medium a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Medium"@en ;
    rdfs:domain dcterms:PhysicalResource ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:PhysicalMedium ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:format ;
    skos:definition "The material or physical carrier of the resource."@en .

dcterms:modified a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Date Modified"@en ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:date ;
    skos:definition "Date on which the resource was changed."@en .

dcterms:provenance a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Provenance"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The statement may include a description of any changes successive custodians made to the resource."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:dctermsMetadata ;
    skos:definition "A statement of any changes in ownership and custody of the resource since its creation that are significant for its authenticity, integrity, and interpretation."@en .

dcterms:publisher a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Publisher"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Examples of a Publisher include a person, an organization, or a service. Typically, the name of a Publisher should be used to indicate the entity."@en ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:Agent ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dc:publisher ;
    skos:definition "An entity responsible for making the resource available."@en .

dcterms:references a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "References"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "A related resource that is referenced, cited, or otherwise pointed to by the described resource."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:replaces a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Replaces"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "A related resource that is supplanted, displaced, or superseded by the described resource."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:requires a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Requires"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
    skos:definition "A related resource that is required by the described resource to support its function, delivery, or coherence."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:rightsHolder a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Rights Holder"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:dctermsMetadata ;
    skos:definition "A person or organization owning or managing rights over the resource."@en .

dcterms:spatial a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Spatial Coverage"@en ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:Location ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:coverage ;
    skos:definition "Spatial characteristics of the resource."@en .

dcterms:subject a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Subject"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Typically, the subject will be represented using keywords, key phrases, or classification codes. Recommended best practice is to use a controlled vocabulary. To describe the spatial or temporal topic of the resource, use the Coverage element."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dc:subject ;
    skos:definition "The topic of the resource."@en ;
    skos:note "This term is intended to be used with non-literal values as defined in the DCMI Abstract Model (http://dublincore.org/documents/abstract-model/). As of December 2007, the DCMI Usage Board is seeking a way to express this intention with a formal range declaration."@en .

dcterms:tableOfContents a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "table of contents" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ;
    skos:definition "A list of subunits of the resource." .

dcterms:temporal a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Temporal Coverage"@en ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:PeriodOfTime ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:coverage ;
    skos:definition "Temporal characteristics of the resource."@en .

dcterms:valid a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Date Valid"@en ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:date ;
    skos:definition "Date (often a range) of validity of a resource."@en .

