    IAO:0000115 "A bone that is shaped as a broad flat plate and composed of two thin layers of compact tissue enclosing between them a variable quantity of cancellous tissue, which is the location of red bone marrow." ;
    OboInOwl:hasDbXref "FMA:7476",
        "NCIT:C32616",
        "SCTID:332907008",
        "UMLS:C0222649",
        "Wikipedia:Flat_bone",
        "galen:FlatBone" ;
    OboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "os planum" ;
    rdfs:comment "Examples: cranium, the ilium, sternum, rib cage, the sacrum and the scapula; the occipital, parietal, frontal, nasal, lacrimal, vomer, scapula, os coxC&, sternum, and ribs" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001474 .

