TARA:3448356 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Disease or Condition" ;
    dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
    dcterms:description "A broad ontology class representing any pathological process, abnormal state, or disruption of normal bodily structure or function manifested by a specific set of symptoms or signs. Within this ontology, it serves as the top-level concept for health impairments, encompassing both holistic pattern-based syndromic classifications and localized, etiology-driven physiological disorders without bias toward a specific medical paradigm."@en ;
    skos:altLabel "Disease_Or_Condition" .

TARA:3566953 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Back-Shu Point of the Heart" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 6, An Introduction to Acupunture Points, Sec. III, Specific Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    dcterms:description "The Back-Shu Point of the Heart meridian. Back-Shu points are specific points on the back where the qi of the respective zang-fu organs is infused. Situated close to their respectively related zang-fu organs, the Back-Shu points present abnormal reactions to the dysfunction of their corresponding zang-fu organs. They are often used for disorders of the internal organs." ;
