    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation ILX:0794954 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The dorsal branch of the ulnar nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "headache, redness of the eye, sudden deafness, sore throat, malaria, pain in the arm." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the dorsum of the hand, in the depression superior to the web margin between the ring and little fingers, at the border between the red and white flesh." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture obliquely 0.3-0.5 inch towards the interspace of the metacarpal bones. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Yemen" ;
