    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1" ;
    dc:title "Intraoperative Acupuncture for Posttonsillectomy Pain: A Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """LI4 (hegu), ST36 (zusanli), P6 (neiguan), SJ5 (waiguan), KI6 (zhaohai)
HT7 (shenmen) at the wrist crease
Auricular points: HT7, master cerebral, cingulate gyrus, tonsil""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received sham acupuncture using Streitberger needles, which are blunt control needles that do not penetrate the skin. This was used as a placebo control to compare with the actual acupuncture treatment. The study was double-blinded, with surgeons, staff, and parents unaware of the treatment allocation." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
