Penetration: Non-penetrating
Other details: Used specially designed needle holders for blinding; control stickers without tacks for ear points""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electroacupuncture at alternating frequencies of 4 and 100 Hertz using a Pantheon stimulator. Some needles were placed without stimulation. The stimulation aimed to optimize the release of endogenous endorphins, enkephalins, and dynorphins." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly translate the conditions into Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Postoperative pain following tonsillectomy" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the control/sham group in improving pain control and oral intake postoperatively, with statistical significance reported for these outcomes." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Time spent in the postanesthesia care unit, amount of opioids administered in the perioperative period, pain measures, presence of nausea/vomiting from postoperative home surveys.
Secondary outcomes: Oral intake.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper only describes a single administration of acupuncture during surgery without mentioning frequency or duration of treatments)" .

