tara-kb:S-112625-101 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-101" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for acute non-specific low back pain: a randomised, controlled, double-blind, placebo trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Basic point: D Temporal region, 4 cm from the helix, in front of the ear and 1 cm above the zygomatic arch
Basic points: D1‚ÄìD6 Another 6 points (D1‚ÄìD6), like beads forming a vertical line about 2 cm in length, behind the D point, in front of the ear, above the temporomandibular joint
Basic point: H 2 cm to the side of the midline and 0.5 cm above the hairline
Basic point: I 5 cm to the side of the midline and 4 cm above the hairline, at a 45¬∞ angle
Y point: Bladder Below the zygomatic arch
Y point: Kidney 1 cm above the Y point: bladder
Y point: Liver 1 cm above the top of the helix
Diagnostic points of cervical region: Kidney Posterior border of the sternocleidomastoid muscle or between the strands of the muscle in the insertion above the bladder point
Diagnostic points of cervical region: Bladder Posterior border of the sternocleidomastoid muscle, behind the clavicle
Diagnostic points of cervical region: Liver Middle third of the sternocleidomastoid muscle""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "control group: sham group (SG) received five non-penetrating acupuncture sessions where only the handle came into contact with the skin at the same points as the intervention group." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Brazil" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "0.3-0.5 cm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-101 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-101 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total sample size: 80; Intervention group (IG): 40; Sham group (SG): 40" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Type: Non-penetrating sham acupuncture
Needle type: Only the handle came into contact with the skin
Quantity and size: Not specified
Location: Same points as the intervention group
Penetration: Non-penetrating
Other details: Manual palpation was performed similarly for both groups""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The needles were stimulated manually and retained for 20 minutes. The patient's facial expression during palpation was used to indicate the location of needling." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Acute non-specific low back pain (ANLBP)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the control/sham group in several areas, although the primary outcome of pain did not reach clinical significance." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Decrease of at least 2 cm in VAS1 (visual analogue scale for cumulative pain)
Secondary outcome measures:
Roland-Morris Disability Questionnaire (RM) for functional capacity
Short Form 36 Health Survey (SF-36) for quality of life
Improvement rating
Number of anti-inflammatory tablets taken""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Five acupuncture sessions, each lasting 30 minutes, administered approximately every 3 to 7 days over a period of 28 days." .

