tara-kb:S-112625-1011 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1011" ;
    dc:title "An Evaluation of Electroacupuncture at the Weizhong Acupoint (BL-40) as a Means of Relieving Pain Induced by Extracorporeal Shock Wave Lithotripsy" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Weizhong acupoint (BL-40): Located behind knee joints, passes through the midpoint of popliteal striated muscle, and resides in between the biceps femoris tendon and semitendinosus muscle tendon.
Nonacupoint location: 3 cm away from the Weizhong acupoint on the leg of the affected side of urolithiasis.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control Group: No action was taken before operation.
Sham-EA Group: Same procedures as 100 Hz EA group but no electric current was applied.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Taiwan" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "BL 40" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:5290080 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:5290080\": \"BL 40\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0024647 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1011 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1011 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 74
Control group: 25
Sham-EA group: 24
100 Hz EA group: 25""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real acupuncture needles (30 gauge stainless steel)
Quantity: Two needles
Size: 30 gauge
Location: Weizhong acupoint and a non-meridian, non-acupoint location 3 cm away from the Weizhong site
Penetrating: Yes, needles were inserted into the skin
Other details: No electric current was applied; procedure was performed for 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """For the 100 Hz EA group: Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) at the Weizhong acupoint using a 100 Hz frequency, with the aim of inducing the sensation of "de-qi."
For the sham-EA group: No electrical stimulation was applied.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Urolithiasis (kidney stones)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcomes. The 100 Hz EA and sham-EA groups showed significant improvements in pain relief, reduced analgesic dosage, and shorter recovery times compared to the control group." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Numbers and dosage of analgesic requirements
Pain score (VAS values)
Time to first request for analgesia
Number of requests for analgesia
Dosage of opium derivative analgesic given
Secondary outcome measures:
Vital signs (blood pressure, heart rate, arterial oxygen partial pressure)
Satisfaction of procedure
Recovery time after anesthesia
Side effects induced by sedatives and opium derivative analgesic""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "20 minutes" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper only mentions a single application of EA for 20 minutes before ESWL, with no information on repeated treatments or frequency)" .

