tara-kb:S-112625-1013 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1013" ;
    dc:title "A therapeutic trial of acupuncture in neurogenic bladder of spinal cord injured patients - a preliminary report" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Chung Chi (Conception Vessel CV3): upper one-third from CV4 to symphysis pubis at midline
Kuan Yuan (CV4): midpoint from umbilicus to symphysis pubis at midline
Bilateral Tzu Liao (Urinary Bladder UB32): located at the sacral foramen S2""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group underwent a conventional bladder training program with intermittent catheterization, tapping the suprapubic area, and trigger point stimulation. Medications like Diazepam or Phenoxybenzamine were used for relaxation of the urethral sphincter in cases of non-relaxing sphincter or detrusor-sphincter dyssynergia." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Taiwan" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "CV 3, CV 4, UB 32" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0022762,
        TARA:6742407,
        TARA:9921528 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0022762\": \"CV 3\", \"TARA:9921528\": \"CV 4\", \"TARA:6742407\": \"BL 32\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0001445 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1013 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1013 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 80
Control group: 28
Acupuncture group: 32""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) using the Pulsator 3000 apparatus with a frequency of 20 ¬± 30 Hz, pulse duration of 200 usec, and intensity of 30 ¬± 50 mAmps. Needles were also manually manipulated to achieve a sensation of \"De Qi,\" characterized by muscle contraction, soreness, heaviness, or numbness." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for neurogenic bladder)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Neurogenic bladder in spinal cord injured patients" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcome of achieving balanced voiding, with statistical significance indicated by p-values (P<0.005 and P<0.01)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Time to achieve balanced voiding
Secondary outcome measures: Criteria for balanced voiding: easy passage of urine at low pressure, residual urine of approximately 100 ml or less, and no urinary tract infection
Number of days to reach self-voiding
Timing of acupuncture initiation affecting total days to achieve balanced bladder""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 15 minutes
How long the needles were left in place during a session: Not specified beyond the session duration""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "4 ¬± 5 sessions per week, each lasting 15 minutes, until bladder balance was achieved" .

