tara-kb:S-112625-1015 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1015" ;
    dc:title "Electroacupuncture on PC6 Prevents Opioid-Induced Nausea and Vomiting after Laparoscopic Surgery" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Neiguan (PC6): Located on the pericardium meridian, used for mind-relaxing, calming, and digestive effects. Depth of needle insertion: 1 cm with Deqi.
Gongsun (SP4): Mentioned as a point used in combination with PC6 in clinical conditions for nausea and vomiting symptoms.
Zusanli (ST36): Mentioned as a point used in combination with PC6 in clinical conditions for nausea and vomiting symptoms.""" ;
