tara-kb:S-112625-1021 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1021" ;
    dc:title "Stimulation of the wrist acupuncture point P6 for preventing postoperative nausea and vomiting" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "P6 acupoint: between the tendons of palmaris longus and flexor carpii radialis muscles, four centimeters proximal to the wrist crease; Shenmen (H7); Shang Wen (CV13); dummy point on lateral elbow crease; sham points on both arms. No specific criteria for choosing points based on TCM diagnosis or tender points mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review of Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham treatment: A device applied in a non-P6 location or an attempt to imitate P6 acupoint stimulation.
Antiemetic drugs: Various types of antiemetic drugs were used as control groups in some trials.""" ;
