    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 3347
Participants for nausea prevention: 1826
Participants for vomiting prevention: 2187
Specific sample sizes within groups: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham treatment was defined as either a device applied in a non-P6 location or an attempt to imitate P6 acupoint stimulation.
Sham procedures included using acupressure wristbands without studs at the P6 acupoint or at non-P6 locations.
Sham treatments involved applying elastic bandages or wristbands to non-acupoint locations or using devices without studs.
The sham procedures were designed to mimic the real treatment without actually stimulating the P6 acupoint.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Acupuncture: manual rotation of needles
Electro-acupuncture: electrical stimulation of needles
Transcutaneous nerve stimulation: applied 30-45 min before induction and continued for 6 hours postoperatively
Laser stimulation: performed over 30 seconds, 15 minutes before induction and 15 minutes after arriving in the recovery room
Acustimulation device: used as specified in individual studies
Acupressure: applied before surgery and left on for 24 hours""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Postoperative nausea and vomiting (PONV)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Incidences of nausea and vomiting
Secondary outcomes: Need for rescue antiemetic therapy, adverse effects""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Acupressure: Applied before surgery and left on for 24 hours; Applied before induction and worn until discharge or for a specified number of hours.
Acupuncture: 5 minutes of manual stimulation; Needles left in place until the next day in some cases.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide a specific frequency or duration for acupuncture treatments)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-1022 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1022" ;
    dc:title "Getting the Grip on Nonspecific Treatment Effects: Emesis in Patients Randomized to Acupuncture or Sham Compared to Patients Receiving Standard Care" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Verum acupuncture: PC6 (pericardium six), located between the tendons of palmaris longus and flexor carpii radialis, two body inches proximal to the wrist crease.
Sham acupuncture: A sham point located two body inches proximal to PC6, outside traditional acupuncture points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "standard care cohort: a reference cohort of patients receiving standard care without acupuncture therapy." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Sweden" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "PC 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:4311153 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0002013 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "0.75 cm (estimated from \"a half bodyinch\" with one body-inch being approximately 1.5 cm)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1022 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1022 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 262
Verum acupuncture group: 109 (99 provided data)
Sham acupuncture group: 106 (101 provided data)
Standard care group: 62 (62 provided data)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture was performed at a sham point located two body-inches proximal to PC6, outside traditional acupuncture points.
"Park's sham devise" was used, which is a blunt telescopic needle that does not penetrate the skin.
The sham needles were held in place by double-sticky marking tubes.
The procedure was non-penetrating, with the needles manipulated to touch the skin but not achieve "deqi."
The duration of needle pressure to the skin was approximately ten seconds per session.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Verum acupuncture: Manual manipulation by twirling and lifting until "deqi" occurred.
Sham acupuncture: No actual stimulation; blunt telescopic needles manipulated to give the illusion of penetration.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the disease/condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Radiotherapy-induced emesis (nausea and vomiting)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group in reducing nausea and vomiting, but the effectiveness was attributed to nonspecific factors rather than the specific characteristics of verum acupuncture." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Occurrence of emesis (nausea and vomiting)
Secondary outcome measures: Intensity of nausea, expectations of treatment effects, relationship between expectations and occurrence of nausea""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration of needle retention: Not specified for verum acupuncture; approximately ten seconds for sham acupuncture""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Three times a week for the first two weeks, then twice a week until the end of radiotherapy; each session lasted 30 minutes." .

