Verum acupuncture group: 109
Sham acupuncture group: 106""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Non-penetrating sham needles
Quantity: 106 patients received sham acupuncture
Size: 0.30 mm diameter, 40 mm length
Location: Non-acupuncture point, two cun proximal to PC6
Penetration: Non-penetrating
Other details: Sham needles were blunted and gave an illusion of penetration; manipulated similarly to real needles but without creating 'deqi'""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation by twirling and lifting until 'deqi' occurred for verum acupuncture; sham acupuncture involved brief manipulation without 'deqi'." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper focuses on radiotherapy-induced nausea, which is not explicitly identified as a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Radiotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting (emesis)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Number of patients with at least one episode of nausea.
Secondary outcome measures: Number of days with nausea, intensity of nausea (category-scale and VAS), proportion of patients vomiting.
Subgroup analysis: For patients receiving chemotherapy, focusing on at least one episode of nausea.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Frequency of sessions: Three times a week for the first two weeks, then twice a week for the rest of the radiotherapy period
Duration needles were left in place during a session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The acupuncture treatments were administered two to three times per week. For the first two weeks, treatments were given three times per week, and then reduced to twice per week for the remaining radiotherapy period. Each treatment session lasted 30 minutes and was conducted over a median of 12 days." .

tara-kb:S-112625-1024 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1024" ;
    dc:title "The Effectiveness of Acupuncture in Prevention and Treatment of Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting -A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """PC6: Located along the Pericardium Meridian of Hand-Jueyin, effective in preventing nausea and vomiting by avoiding adverse qi flow.
Korean hand points: K-K9, K-D2
Bladder points: BL10, BL11, BL18-26
Spleen points: SP4, SP6
Stomach points: ST34, ST36, ST44
GB34: Used in combination with BL10 and BL11 for reducing vomiting in children.
LI4: Located along the Large Intestine Meridian of Hand-Yangming, used in combination with PC6 and ST36.
ST36: Located along the Stomach Meridian of Foot-Yangming, functions in adjusting qi and blood, food transport, and gastrointestinal activity.
LI10: Located along the Large Intestine Meridian of Hand-Yangming, effective in PONV prevention and treatment in abdominal surgery.
Auricular acupoints: Effective in reducing pain, nausea, and vomiting.
CV12: Used as a supplementary acupoint in combination with PC6 and other points.
LV3, SP6, SP9, ST40: Used as supplementary acupoints in combination with PC6 and other points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control groups consisted of standard care, sham, medication, or counseling. Sham controls were specifically used for comparisons with PC6 acupressure and PC6 electro-acupoint stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China, Germany, UK, Ireland, USA" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper does not provide a link to a dataset or mention its availability)" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0002017 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """PC6 acupuncture: 5mm, 1cm
PC6 combined with other acupoint(s): 0.8-1 inch (approximately 2-2.5 cm)
Other acupoint(s): 1.0-1.5cm (for catgut embedment)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1024 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1024 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: Intervention 1276, Control 1258
Specific subgroups:
PC6 acupuncture: Nausea (0-6h) 200 participants, Nausea (0-24h) 231 participants, Vomiting (0-6h) 200 participants, Vomiting (0-24h) 276 participants
PC6 acupressure: Nausea (0-24h) 580 participants, Vomiting (0-24h) 582 participants
PC6 electro-acupoint stimulation: Nausea (0-24h) 426 participants, Vomiting (0-24h) 426 participants
Other interventions: Nausea and vomiting (0-24h) 527 participants, Nausea (0-24h) 234 participants, Vomiting (0-24h) 337 participants, Nausea and vomiting (0-24h) 396 participants""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not mentioned (the paper does not provide specific details on the sham procedure)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual acupuncture: rotating, reinforcing-reducing
Acupressure: using devices like "SeaBand" and "Vital-Band"
Electroacupoint stimulation: using devices like "ReliefBand" and electrodes with frequencies of 4Hz to 2-100Hz
Sensation sought: "deqi\"""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper describes the TCM principles related to PONV but does not specify a traditional TCM disease or condition name)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Postoperative nausea and vomiting (PONV)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Efficacy of different types of acupuncture and acupoint selection in prevention and treatment of PONV, divided by type of acupuncture (manual acupuncture, acupressure, electroacupoint stimulation) and acupoint (PC6, PC6 combined with other acupoint(s), other acupoint(s)).
Secondary outcomes: Optimal timing, technique of intervention, side effects, and use of rescue therapy.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """PC6 acupuncture: 5 minutes, 30 minutes, or whole duration of surgery
PC6 acupressure: At least 24 hours
Electroacupoint stimulation: 20 minutes, 30 minutes, or 60 minutes before induction until 6 hours or 24 hours postoperatively
PC6 combined with other acupoints: Every 7-8 minutes until end of surgery, or 30 minutes and 5-10 minutes in TEAS
Other acupoints: Various durations (e.g., 10 minutes for cupping, 25 minutes for electro-acupuncture, 1-3 minutes for auricular acupressure, 10-15 minutes for acupoint massage, every 30 minutes for auricular acupuncture)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper provides details on the duration of treatments but does not specify a standard frequency of treatment)" .

