tara-kb:S-112625-1026 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1026" ;
    dc:title "Does Auricular Acupuncture Reduce Postoperative Vomiting After Cholecystectomy?" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Sympathetic Point: Located in the terminal of the inferior antihelix crus as it meets the head.
Stomach Point: Located around the area where the helix root terminates.
Shen Men: Located at the bifurcating point between superior and inferior antihelix crus and the lateral third of the triangular fossa.
Occiput: Located at the posterior superior corner of the lateral aspect of the antitragus.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group used in this study was a sham control group. In this group, a piece of adhesive tape was applied to the same ear points as in the treatment group, but without needle insertion. This was done to mimic the appearance of receiving acupuncture without actually administering it. The study was single-blinded, meaning that the patients, anesthesiologist, and nursing staff were unaware of the group assignments." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Sympathetic Point, Stomach Point, Shen Men, Occiput" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:2442762 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:2442762\": \"HT 7\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Occiput",
        "Stomach Point",
        "Sympathetic Point" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0002017 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide a specific measurement or descriptive term for the depth of needle insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1026 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1026 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 100
Participants in auricular acupuncture group: 50
Participants in sham control group: 50""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Adhesive tape was placed on the same 4 ear points as the treatment group.
Needle type: No needles were used; plain adhesive tape was applied.
Quantity: Same 4 ear points as the treatment group.
Location: Same points as the treatment group.
Penetration: Non-penetrating.
Other details: No special sham needles were used; plain adhesive tape was applied to mimic treatment.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Needles were inserted perpendicularly and left in place until the final assessment period. No additional stimulation techniques were mentioned. Not specified if any type of sensation was sought. Needles were not stimulated further after insertion." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Postoperative nausea and vomiting (PONV)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"There was a significant difference between the control and auricular acupuncture treatment groups in the incidence of vomiting 24 hours after surgery (66% and 0%, respectively, p œΩ 0.01)."
"The incidence of nausea in the first 24 hours after open cholecystectomy in the sham control group was 74%. The auricular acupuncture group exhibited a significant decrease in the incidence of postoperative nausea during the same period (6%) (Table 2)."
"The incidence of vomiting in the first 24 hours postoperatively was 0% for the auricular acupuncture group and 66% for the sham control group, which was statistically significant by chi-square test (p œΩ 0.01)."
"Our results, which demonstrated an incidence of 6% for nausea and 0% for vomiting in patients receiving auricular acupuncture, strongly supports the role of acupuncture in treatment of PONV."
"We conclude that auricular acupuncture can reduce nausea and vomiting and may thus be a treatment of benefit to patients with PONV following open abdominal cholecystectomy."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome measures: Incidence of postoperative nausea and vomiting (PONV) after cholecystectomy. Secondary outcome measures: Grading of nausea on a visual analogue scale (VAS), classification of vomiting severity based on the number of episodes." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Duration of each acupuncture session: 2 minutes; Duration needles were left in place: Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency or duration of acupuncture treatments beyond the 2-minute administration for nausea)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-1027 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1027" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture against chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting in pediatric oncology Interim results of a multicenter crossover study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Pericardium 6 (Pc 6 or Neiguan): located 2 cun, twice the width of an individual's thumb, proximal to the distal wrist crease, between the tendons of the M. palmaris longus and M. flexor carpi radialis
Stomach 36 (ST 36 or Zusanli): located 3 cun below the inferior border of the patella, one finger breadth lateral to the anterior crest of the tibia
Conception Vessel 12 (CV 12 or Zhongwan): located on the midline, 4 cun superior to the umbilicus
Large Intestines 4 (LI 4 or Hegu): located on the dorsum of the hand, approximately at the midpoint of the second metacarpal bone, in the belly of the first interosseus dorsalis muscle
Points were chosen based on individual needs and TCM diagnosis""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT) with a crossover design" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of patients receiving antiemetic medication alone, as this was the standard treatment against which the efficacy of adding acupuncture was compared." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "PC 6, ST 36, CV 12, LI 4" ;
