    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1030" ;
    dc:title "Monitoring of Neuromuscular Blockade at the P6 Acupuncture Point Reduces the Incidence of Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """P6 or Neiguan acupuncture point: Located 2 Chinese inches proximal to the distal skin crease of the wrist, in the anterior ante brachial region on the ulnar side of the tendon of the flexor carpi radialis.
Electrode placement: One electrode between the tendons of the palmaris longus and flexor carpi radialis muscles, 1 cm proximal to the P6 point; the second electrode 2 cm distal to the P6 point.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study is the \"ulnaris group,\" where electrodes were placed over the ulnar nerve to monitor neuromuscular blockade during anesthesia." ;
