tara-kb:S-112625-1038 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1038" ;
    dc:title "Semi Permanent Acupuncture Needles in the Prevention of Post Operative Nausea and Vomiting" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Study group: PC.6 point on both wrists
Control group: Sham point midway between the ulnar styloid and the medial humeral condyle on each arm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT), Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group had SPANS inserted into sham points on their forearms, specifically midway between the ulnar styloid and the medial humeral condyle, which is not on any recognized traditional acupuncture meridian." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "PC 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:4311153 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0002017 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1038 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1038 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total participants: 36; Participants within groups: Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real SPANS
Quantity: Not specified
Size: Not specified
Location: Sham points midway between the ulnar styloid and the medial humeral condyle on each arm, not on any recognized traditional acupuncture meridian
Penetrating: Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Postoperative nausea and vomiting (PONV)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The use of SPANS does not reduce the overall incidence of PONV but reduces the severity of nausea in the second 24 hours.
There was a statistically significant difference (p < 0.05) in the severity of nausea between the study and control groups during the second 24 hours.
SPANS may be of value as an adjunct to conventional antiemetic therapy in some patients, particularly those with previous PONV or motion sickness.
The intervention was not effective compared to the control/sham group for the primary outcome of reducing overall PONV incidence.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Effectiveness ofSPANS inPreventingPostoperative nausea and vomiting (PONV)
Secondary outcome measures: Nausea, vomiting,Pain, and headache assessed at 8, 24, and 48 hoursPostoperatively""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of Treatment: 48 hours
Duration Retained: 48 hours
Duration of each acupuncture session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was a one time application of semi permanent acupuncture needles (SPANS) inserted before surgery and left in place for 48 hours." .

