    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group used in the study was a sham APA group. This group involved applying acupressure to points on the ear that are not typically used for treating pain, specifically the Stomach, Mouth, Duodenum, and Kidney acupoints. The sham group consisted of 9 participants and was used as a comparison to the true APA group to assess the effectiveness of APA in reducing pain and altering cytokine levels." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not applicable (the study uses non invasive acupressure with seeds or pellets, not needles)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-105 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-105 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total: 19; True APA group: 10; Sham APA group: 9" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "The sham acupoints selected were located away from the areas of the ear that would be used as true acupoints for where the participant was experiencing pain, including the Stomach, Mouth, Duodenum, and Kidney acupoints." ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation in APA involves manual pressure on seeds or pellets placed on the ear, with participants pressing them at least 3 times a day for 3 minutes. No needles are used. Not specified if any specific sensation was sought. Not applicable for needle stimulation methods." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic low back pain (CLBP)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Changes inSerumProand anti inflammatory cytokines
Secondary outcome measure: Reduction inPain intensity""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupressure session: 3 minutes
Duration seeds were left in place: 5 days""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency of initial treatment application: Weekly for 4 weeks
