tara-kb:S-112625-1058 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1058" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture Intervention in Ischemic Stroke: A Randomized Controlled Prospective Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Main acupoints: Neiguan (PC 6), Shuigou (DU 26), Sanyinjiao (SP 6), Jiquan (HT 1), Weizhong (BL 40), Chize (LU 5)
Auxiliary acupoints:
For dysphagia: Fengchi (GB 20), Yifeng (TE 17), Wangu (GB 12)
For tightened finger grasping: Hegu (LI 4)
For slurred speech: Lianquan (CV 23), blood-letting therapy on Jinjin (EX-HN 12) and Yuye (EX-HN 13)
For cross-foot: Qiuxu (GB40) toward Zhaohai (KI 6)
Manipulation details:
Neiguan (PC 6): 0.5-1 cun perpendicularly with reducing manipulation
Shuigou (GV 26): 0.3-0.5 cun obliquely toward the nasal septum with heavy sparrow-pecking
Sanyinjiao (SP 6): 1-1.5 cun along the medical aspect of the tibia with reducing manipulation
Jiquan (HT 1): 1-1.5 cun perpendicularly with reducing manipulation
Chize (LU 5): 1 cun perpendicularly with reducing manipulation
Weizhong (BL 40): 0.5-1 cun perpendicularly with reducing manipulation
Fengchi (GB 20), Wangu (GB 12), Yifeng (TE 17): 2-2.5 cun toward the Adam's apple with reinforcing manipulation
Hegu (LI 4): 1-1.5 cun toward Sanjian (LI 3) with reducing manipulation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was treated using sham-acupoints, receiving the same standard medical treatment as the intervention group but with a placebo form of acupuncture. The manipulation technique for the sham acupuncture was the same as for the resuscitating acupuncture group." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "PC 6, DU 26, SP 6, HT 1, BL 40, LU 5, GB 20, TE 17, GB 12, LI 4, CV 23, EX-HN 12, EX-HN 13, GB 40, KI 6" ;
