Duration: 10 weeks in some studies, 4 to 6 weeks in others, and 2 weeks in a few studies""" .

tara-kb:S-112625-1062 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1062" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture Efficacy on Ischemic Stroke Recovery Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial in China" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Main acupoints: Renzhong-DU26, Neiguan-PC6 (both sides), Sanyinjiao-SP6 (paretic side)
Auxiliary acupoints: Baihui-DU20, Zusanli-ST36, Fenglong-ST40, Taichong-LK3, Chize-LL5, Fengchi-GB20, Qihai-RN6
Needling methods:
Neiguan: perpendicular insertion (1.5-1.4cm depth), 'lifting, thrusting and rotating' (180 degrees, 50-60 circles per minute)
Renzhong: oblique insertion (0.5-1.0cm depth), 'sparrow-pecking'
Sanyinjiao: insertion (1.5-3cm depth), 'gentle lifting and heavy thrusting'
Auxiliary acupoints: 'lifting and thrusting' (40-60 times per minute) for limb acupoints, 'rotating' (180 degrees, 40-60 circles per minute) for trunk and scalp acupoints""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received standard care alone, which included routine ischemic stroke treatment such as antithrombotic medications and prevention of complications. No sham acupuncture was used." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "DU 26, PC 6, SP 6, DU 20, ST 36, ST 40, LR 3, LL 5, GB 20, RN 6" ;
