tara-kb:S-112625-1071 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1071" ;
    dc:title "Rehabilitation of Stroke Patients Using Yamamoto New Scalp Acupuncture: A Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Basic points: Scalp acupuncture points for pain and dysfunction related to specific body parts.
Ypsilon points: Related to the 12 acupuncture meridians (LU, LI, KI, BL, HT, SI, LR, GB, PC, TB, SP, and ST).
Locomotor system: Situated on either side of the boundary between forehead and hair.
Internal organs: Represented by Y points on both sides of the temple region.
Neck diagnostics: Start with palpation of the two kidney points to determine treatment area.
Specific YNSA points: Cerebrum, Cerebellum, Basal Ganglia, Liver on the skull.
Combination of Cranial Nerve points and Y points based on patient sensitivity.""" ;
