tara-kb:S-112625-1077 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1077" ;
    dc:title "Selection of acupoints for managing upper-extremity spasticity in chronic stroke patients" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Neiguan (PC6): On the palmar side of the forearm, 2 cun above the transverse crease of the wrist, between the tendons of the palmaris longus muscle and flexor carpi radialis muscle. Depth: Perpendicular insertion 0.5‚Äì0.8 cun.
Shaohai (HT3): With the elbow flexed, at a midpoint of the line connecting the medial end of cubital crease and the medial epicondyle of the humerus. Depth: Perpendicular insertion 0.5‚Äì0.8 cun.
Shounizhu (Ex-UE): Locate at the flexion side of the forearm, 6 cun above the transverse crease of the wrist, between the tendons of palmaris longus and flexor carpi radialis muscle. Depth: Perpendicular insertion 0.5‚Äì1.0 cun.
Zeqian (Ex-UE, A32): 1 cun below Chize (LU5), which is at radial edge of biceps tendon in elbow crease. Depth: Perpendicular insertion 0.5‚Äì1 cun.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 6 patients who received minimal acupuncture (MA) as a sham control, in addition to standard rehabilitation (SR). Minimal acupuncture involved limited needle insertion depth (0.05-0.2 cun) with no manipulation and no eliciting of \"de-chi.\"" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Taiwan" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Neiguan, Shaohai, Zeqian, EX UE A 32, Shounizhu" ;
