tara-kb:S-112625-1078 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1078" ;
    dc:title "Sensory stimulation promotes normalization of postural control after stroke" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """1. Two hand widths below patella and 4 cm lateral to the tibia
2. One hand width below patella and 4 cm lateral to the tibia
3. At the anterior lowermost corner of the head of the fibula
4. On the middle of the belly of the musculus adductor pollicis longus when it is contracted
5. Lateral on the volar side of the elbow
6. On the dorsal side of the arm between the ulna and the radius about 5 cm proximal to the wrist
7. On the vertex of the head, at the crossing of a line drawn between each external auditory canal and the midline
8. One hand width above the patella and in the midline of the thigh
9. Dorsal aspect of the hand into one of the interossal muscles
10. On the dorsal aspect of the foot, in the skin between the first and second toe""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received daily physiotherapy and occupational therapy without any additional sensory stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005098 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1078 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1078 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 48 survivors (22 treatment group, 26 control group) + 23 age-matched healthy subjects
Participants within groups: Treatment group = 22, Control group = 26, Healthy subjects = 23""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved acupuncture with 10 needles placed according to traditional Chinese acupuncture points. The needles were manually stimulated and kept in place for 30 minutes. Additionally, electric stimulation (electroacupuncture) was applied to four needles on the paretic side at 2 to 5 Hz to induce muscle contraction." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not use Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Hemiparetic stroke" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Assessment of postural control, specifically the ability to maintain stance during perturbations and the dynamics of postural control.
Secondary outcome measures: Swiftness and stiffness values to evaluate the dynamics of postural control.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Length of treatment period: Twice weekly for 10 weeks""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was administered twice weekly for 10 weeks, with each session lasting 30 minutes." .

