tara-kb:S-112625-1080 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1080" ;
    dc:title "Can electroacupuncture or transcutaneous nerve stimulation influence cognitive and emotional outcome after stroke?" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Non-paretic side: LI4 (thenar muscle), ST36 (tibialis anterior)
Vertex of the head: GV20
Hemiparetic side: LI11, LI4, EX28:2 (upper limb); ST36, ST40, EX36:1 (lower limb)
Second mode: Non-paretic side LI11 (elbow region), GB34 (tibialis posterior); Hemiparetic side LI11, LI4 (upper limb); GB34, ST40 (lower limb)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received low-intensity high-frequency subliminal TENS, which was designed to be below the perception threshold. This group served as a comparison to evaluate the effects of the other interventions." ;
