tara-kb:S-112625-1085 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1085" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for Upper-Extremity Rehabilitation in Chronic Stroke: A Randomized Sham-Controlled Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Active acupuncture intervention based on TCM-style acupuncture.
Combination of traditional acupuncture points on the body surface and scalp acupuncture.
Scalp acupuncture directed at sensory and motor components of the affected limb.
Needling performed on the side opposite the affected limb.
Points chosen from pools A, B, and C (10 to 15 from A, 3 to 5 from B, 1 to 2 from C).
Specific body acupuncture points listed in appendix 1 (not included in provided text).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture using a sham acupuncture needle that retracts without penetrating the skin, sham electroacupuncture with severed wires, and sham scalp acupuncture with needles placed away from active lines." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0001269 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1085 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1085 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 33
Active acupuncture group: 16
Sham acupuncture group: 17""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Sham acupuncture needle developed by Streitberger and Kleinhenz, which retracts upon application to the skin.
Quantity: 4 to 6 sham needles per body treatment visit.
Size: Not specified.
Location: At least 1cm away from any acupuncture point.
Penetration: Non-penetrating.
Other details: Sham electroacupuncture used with severed wires; sham scalp acupuncture with needles 2cm from active scalp lines.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual stimulation to achieve "de qi" (a sensation of heaviness or ache)
Electrostimulation (electroacupuncture) applied to points on the affected limbs""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the TCM terminology for the condition being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic hemiparesis from stroke" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No (based on ITT analysis), Maybe/Inconclusive (based on per-protocol analysis)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcomes:
UE motor function
Spasticity
Grip strength
Range of motion (ROM)
Activities of daily living
Quality of life (QOL)
Mood
Secondary Outcomes:
Modified Ashworth Scale for spasticity
Jamar dynamometer for grip strength
Barthel Index for ADLs
CES-D scale for mood
Nottingham Health Profile for QOL""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: approximately 60 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 20 to 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for 10 weeks; up to 20 treatment sessions (mean, 16.9) over a mean of 10.5 weeks." .

