    dc:title "Cupping for stroke rehabilitation: A systematic review" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details on needle locations or related acupoints used in the studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review (includes 3 RCTs and 2 UOSs)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Yuan (2008): Acupuncture plus exercise therapy
Zhang (2002): Acupuncture and warm needling
Ni and Shen (2004): Acupuncture""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Supplementary data associated with this article can be found, in the online version, at doi:10.1016/j.jns.2010.03.033." ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005098 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not applicable (cupping does not involve needle insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1089 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1089 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 292
Yuan (2008): 58 (30 in wet cupping group, 28 in acupuncture group)
Zhang (2002): 150 (34 in wet cupping group, 36 in acupuncture group, 80 in warm needling group)
Ni (2004): 62 (31 in wet cupping group, 31 in acupuncture group)
Liu (2000): 16
Huang (2009): 6""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham procedure was used in the studies reviewed)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not applicable (cupping does not involve needle stimulation)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper focuses on stroke rehabilitation and its symptoms rather than specific TCM conditions)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Stroke" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Maybe/Inconclusive (the effectiveness of cupping compared to acupuncture is mixed, with some studies showing superiority and others not)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Responder's rate, Pain intensity (VAS), Pain frequency, Range of motion, Reduction of myodynamia
Secondary outcomes: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Yuan (2008): Wet cupping for 10 minutes, once every 2 days, total 10 times.
Zhang (2002): Wet cupping for 10 minutes, once daily, for 5 days.
Ni and Shen (2004): Wet cupping for 10 minutes, 2 times per week, for 1 month.
Liu (2000): Wet cupping for 5 sessions.
Huang (2009): Dry cupping for 10-30 minutes, 5-10 times.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Yuan (2008): Wet cupping, once every 2 days, total 10 times
Zhang (2002): Wet cupping, once daily, for 5 days, total 6 sessions
Ni and Shen (2004): Wet cupping, 2 times per week, for 1 month
Liu (2000): Wet cupping, once daily, 5 sessions
Huang (2009): Dry cupping, 10‚Äì30 min, 5‚Äì10 times""" .

