tara-kb:S-112625-1091 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1091" ;
    dc:title "Additional therapeutic effects of electroacupuncture in conjunction with conventional rehabilitation for patients with first-ever ischaemic stroke" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Pai Hui (GV 20), Bilateral Feng Chih (GB 20), Chien Yu (LI 15), Chu Chin (LI 11), Ho Ku (LI 4)
Feng Shih (GB 31), Yang Ling Chuan (GB 34), Tsusan Li (St 36)
Selected based on traditional Chinese medicine principles
Needles: stainless steel, 0.25 mm in diameter, 50 mm long
Electrical stimulation: up to 10 mA, alternating pulses of 3 and 15 Hz
Treatment duration: 20 minutes
Acupoints located near muscles with high neurovascular density to stimulate muscle strength and motor control""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received conventional rehabilitation (physical and occupational therapy, with speech therapy if indicated) without any additional electroacupuncture during the study period. Electroacupuncture was offered to them 6 months after the stroke, outside the study's evaluation period." ;
