Recovery
Blood gases
Rapid return of consciousness
Absence of hypercapnia
Smaller decrease in pH
Secondary Outcomes:
Restoration of urinary and bowel functions
Convalescence in terms of self-reliance
Postoperative course in respect of fatigue and morbidity
Peri-operative blood loss
Postoperative convalescence and morbidity
Time to removal of bladder catheter
Return of colonic motility
First passage of flatus
Time to first oral intake
Daily activities and fatigue levels
Incidence of complications
Length of hospitalization""" ;
