tara-kb:S-112625-111 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-111" ;
    dc:title "A Randomized Trial Comparing Acupuncture, Simulated Acupuncture, and Usual Care for Chronic Low Back Pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Individualized acupuncture: 74 distinct points, half on the "Bladder meridian" (back and legs)
Standardized acupuncture: Du 3, Bladder 23 (bilateral), low back ashi point, Bladder 40 (bilateral), Kidney 3 (bilateral) on the low back and lower leg
Simulated acupuncture: Same eight acupoints as standardized acupuncture""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Usual care: Participants received no study-related care but instead followed the care they and their physicians chose, which typically included medications, primary care, and physical therapy visits.
Simulated acupuncture: A non-insertive method of stimulating acupuncture points was used to assess the need for needle insertion to achieve therapeutic benefits.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Du 3, Bladder 23, low back ashi point, Bladder 40, Kidney 3" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0992296,
        TARA:4362146,
        TARA:5290080,
        TARA:8807122 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:8807122\": \"GV 3\", \"TARA:0992296\": \"BL 23\", \"TARA:5290080\": \"BL 40\", \"TARA:4362146\": \"KI 3\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "low back ashi point" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "1 to 3 cm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-111 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-111 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 638
Individualized acupuncture: 157
Standardized acupuncture: 158
Simulated acupuncture: 162
Usual care: 161""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Simulated acupuncture using a toothpick in a needle guidetube.
Needle type: Toothpick (non-penetrating).
Quantity: Simulated at eight acupoints.
Location: Same acupoints as standardized treatment.
Penetration: Non-penetrating.
Other details: Skin held taut, toothpick tapped and twisted to simulate needle insertion, and quick withdrawal to simulate removal.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation (twirling of needles at 10 minutes and before removal) to elicit \"de qi\" sensation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic low back pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes:
Back-related dysfunction (Roland Disability score, range: 0 to 23)
Symptom bothersomeness (0 to 10 scale)
Secondary outcomes:
26-and 52-week outcomes for the primary outcome measures
Proportion of participants with clinically meaningful improvements in dysfunction and back pain
Self-reported medication use for back pain in the prior week
Physical and Mental Health Component Summary Scores of the SF-36
Number of days spent in bed, lost from work or school, or cutting down on usual activities due to back problems during past month
Participants' use of health services for back pain during the year following randomization""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Individualized Acupuncture: Needles retained for 18 minutes (range 15 to 20 minutes)
Standardized Acupuncture: Needles retained for 20 minutes
Simulated Acupuncture: Not specified
Usual Care: Not applicable""" ;
