    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Shoulder Periarthritis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Results: "Of the 210 cases in the treatment group, 158 cases were cured, 40 cases improved, and 12 cases failed. Of the 62 cases in the control group, 26 cases were cured, 21 cases improved and 15 cases failed. There was a significant difference in therapeutic effects between the two groups (P<0.01)."
Conclusion: The acupuncture intervention using Lingxia and Sanjian (LI 3) was effective compared to the control group.
Effectiveness: Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Cured: Complete restoration of the functions ofShoulder joints,Such as lifting, adduction, and backward extension.
Improved: The motion ofShoulder joints obviously increased 'in lifting, abduction and backward extension.
Failed: No obvious improvement.
Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes (needles retained for 30 minutes, manipulated every 10 minutes)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was given once daily, with 10 sessions constituting one therapeutic course and a 2 day interval between courses. Therapeutic effects were evaluated after 2 courses of treatment." .

