tara-kb:S-112625-1133 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1133" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture Treatment of Acute Lumbar Sprain:A Controlled Study in 238 Patients" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Paravertebral lumbar acupoints (commonly at L)
Supplementary Ashi acupoints (local tender points)
Yanglao (SI 6) point: located by pressing the left thumb on the patient's healthy hand and tibial tuberosity; Jiaji (EX B 2), Yaotong (EX UE 7), Ashi points
Acupoints chosen based on location of diseased tissues and principle of treating opposite sides for pain relief.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 126 patients who received acupuncture using the Yanglao and Ashi acupoints. The response rate after three treatments was 94.4%. The Yanglao point was used for its enhancing effects on lumbar muscles and Qi flow." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "SI 6, EX B 2, EX UE 7, Ashi" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:3734471,
        TARA:4125415,
        TARA:7584875 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4125415\": \"SI 6\", \"TARA:3734471\": \"Huatuojiaji\", \"TARA:7584875\": \"Yaotongxue\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Ashi" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Yanglao point: 0.5 1.0 cun
Ashi point: 1.5 2.5 cun""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1133 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1133 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 238
Control group: 126
Treatment group: 112""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual manipulation: Pushing and withdrawal
Twisting for 30 60 seconds to obtain a response
Thermal stimulation: Moxibustion applied after acupuncture""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly translate \"acute lumbar sprain\" into TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Acute lumbar sprain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "The response rate of three treatments in this group was 94.4%. For the treatment group, Jiaji (EX B 2), Yaotong (EX UE 7) and Ashi were used. The response rate of three treatments in the treatment group was 69.7% (P < 0.01). The difference therein is statistically significant."
Effectiveness compared to control/sham: No""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Complete disappearance of lumbarPain
Relief of tenderness by > 80%
Improvement in lumbar flexion and extension
Secondary outcome measures:
Relationship between number of treatments andSeverity of clinical manifestations
Response rate over different numbers of treatments
Timing of treatment as a factor influencing outcomes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of needle retention: 15 20 minutes (general treatment), 10 20 minutes (Yanglao point)
Duration of moxibustion: 10 15 minutes
Total length of each acupuncture session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of treatment in terms of how often acupuncture was administered)" .

