tara-kb:S-112625-1135 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1135" ;
    dc:title "Comparative Study on Acupuncture Needling Methods for Sciatica: Routine Needling vs. Point-to-Point Penetration and Deep Puncture" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """For pain along the Gallbladder channel: Long needles measuring 5 6 inches in length were inserted perpendicularly to a depth of 4 5 cun.
For trunk sciatica: "Jumbar 3needle" point combination involving Huatuo Jiaji points at L3, L4, and L5; needles inserted perpendicularly to a depth of 3 4 cun.
Acupoint selection based on clinical manifestations.
Main points for radicular sciatica: "buttock 3 needle" and "lumbar 3 needle" points.
Main points for trunk sciatica: "buttock 3 needle" points.
Supplemental acupoints incorporated as indicated.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group used filiform type acupuncture needles, which are shorter and thinner compared to the long needles used in the study group." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not mention the country or countries where the study was conducted)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0024333 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """For pain along the Gallbladder channel: 4 5 cun
For trunk sciatica: 3 4 cun""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1135 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1135 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 198
Study group: 108
Control group: 90""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation: Lifting and thrusting (ti cha) to induce needling sensation (deqi)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Bi syndromes (painful obstruction)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Sciatica" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group, as indicated by the highly significant difference in effectiveness (P<0.01) and higher effective rate in the study group compared to the control group." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcome Measure: Effectiveness ofPoint toPointPenetration and deepPuncture versus routine needling in treatingSciatica.
Secondary Outcome Measures: Cured, marked improvement, improved, no effect.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes (duration of each session), 30 minutes (duration needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on how often acupuncture treatments were administered)" .

