tara-kb:S-112625-1140 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1140" ;
    dc:title "Dry Needling of Muscle Motor Points for Chronic Low-Back Pain A Randomized Clinical Trial With Long-Term Follow-Up" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Muscle motor points or motor bands belonging to the affected myotome were chosen for treatment.
Specific muscles mentioned include:
Anterior tibial (innervated by L4 and L5 roots through deep peroneal nerve)
Tensor fascia lata (innervated by L4 and L5 roots through superior gluteal nerve)
Quadriceps femoris (innervated by L2, L3, and L4 roots through femoral nerve)
Emphasis on muscles showing myalgic hyperalgesia or tenderness to digital pressure.
No specific traditional acupuncture points or acupoints mentioned.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 27 patients who received the Clinic's standard therapy regimen, which included physiotherapy, remedial exercises, and occupational therapy, without dry needling at muscle motor points." ;
