        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1150" ;
    dc:title "Effect of Electroacupuncture on the Third Lumbar Transverse Process Syndrome: A Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """EA Group: Ah Shi point near L3 transverse process; second point 2cm vertically below Ah Shi; third point 2cm horizontally away from Ah Shi toward center/spine; fourth point 2cm horizontally away from second point toward center/spine.
Control Group: shenshu (BL 23), qihaishu (BL 24), dachangshu (BL 25), shangliao (BL 31), yanglingquan (GB 34), Ah Shi point near L3 transverse process.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study received classical manual acupuncture. The selection of acupoints for this group included shenshu (BL 23), qihaishu (BL 24), dachangshu (BL 25), shangliao (BL 31), yanglingquan (GB 34), and Ah Shi point located near the L3 trans process." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Australia" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "BL 23, BL 24, BL 25, BL 31, GB 34, Ah Shi point" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0906448,
        TARA:0992296,
        TARA:2465151,
        TARA:7357260,
        TARA:8758950 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0992296\": \"BL 23\", \"TARA:7357260\": \"BL 24\", \"TARA:0906448\": \"BL 25\", \"TARA:2465151\": \"BL 31\", \"TARA:8758950\": \"GB 34\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Ah Shi point" ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1150 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1150 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 80
Electroacupuncture group: 40
Classical acupuncture group: 40""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electroacupuncture (EA) group: Electrical stimulation using G6805S | EA stimulator with a square pulse wave at 50Hz and continuous waves. First intensity setting used. De Qi not required.
Control group: Manual manipulation with standard entwisting maneuver every 5 6 minutes. No electrical stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Third Lumbar Transverse Process Syndrome (TLTP syndrome)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"A Ridit analysis was used for this study, At the P< 0.001 level, an overall improvement occurred in 81% of people in the EA group vs an overall improvement in 42% of the control (classical acupuncture) group."
"The new EA method described in this study is more appropriate relative to other methods as a form of effective treatment for TLTP syndrome."
"The results showed that there was statistically and clinically significant differences between the group that received EA and the group that received classical acupuncture (the control group)."
"From this randomized clinical study, there was a statistical and clinical difference between EA treatment and classical acupuncture treatment after the completion of a 12 session treatment course."
"Thus, the new method described herein is more appropriate than classical methods as a form of effective treatment for TLTP syndrome."
The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group: Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome measure:PressurePointPain intensity test;Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified" .

