    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Renying (ST 9): vertically inserted 1 2 cun deep with pecking method
Jiquan (HT 1): obliquely inserted 0.5 1 cun with lifting thrusting reducing manipulation
Taiyuan (LU 9): vertically inserted 0.3 cun with twirling reinforcing manipulation
Xinshu (BL 15), Feishu (BL 13), Geshu (BL 17): obliquely inserted 1 1.5 cun with twirling reinforcing manipulation
Fengchi (GB 20), Wangu (GB 12), Tianzhu (BL 10): inserted 1 cun with twirling reinforcing manipulation
Jingming (BL 1), Zanzhu (BL 2), Qiuhou (EX HN 7): for hypopsia
Quchi (LI 11), Waiguan (TE 5), Hegu (LI 4): for numb upper limbs
Moxibustion at Taiyuan (LU 9) and Back Shu points""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control Group: Treated with Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) and Western drugs.
Specific Interventions:
Intravenous drip: 0.9% normal saline (250ml) with compound Danshen Injection (40ml) once a day.
Oral administration: Pletaal (50mg) twice a day for 4 weeks.""" ;
