tara-kb:S-112625-1197 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1197" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for hot flashes: a randomized, sham-controlled clinical study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """SP 4: In the depression distal to and below the base of the first metatarsal bone, on the medial side of the foot.
SP 6: 3 cun above the medial malleolus, dorsal to the posterior border of the tibia.
He 7: On the transverse crease of the wrist, radial to the tendon of medial flexor carpi ulnaris.
LI 11: With elbow flexed at 90 degrees, the point is on the anterolateral elbow joint in the midpoint between the radial side of the skin crease of the elbow and lateral epicondyle humerus.
Liv 2: Dorsum of foot in the fossa between the first and the second proximal phalanges and proximal to the margin of the toe web.
Ki 6: 1 cun directly below the tip of the medial malleolus.
LU 7: On the radial side of the forearm on the border of the radius, 1.5 cun proximal to the transverse crease of the wrist.
PC 6: Between the tendons of the tendons of palmaris longus and flexor carpi radialis 2 cun proximal to the transverse crease of the wrist.
GB 34: At the point of intersection of lines from anterior and inferior borders and head of fibula.
Liv 3: Between the first and second metatarsal bones, 2 cun proximal to the margin of the web.
Ren 4: On the midline 3 cun below the umbilicus.
GB 20: Between the origins of the medial border of sternocleidomastoid and the trapezius.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture: needling administered in nonacupuncture, nonnmeridian areas, whenever possible 5 cm or more away from the actual acupuncture point." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "SP 4, SP 6, He 7, LI 11, Liv 2, Ki 6, LU 7, PC 6, GB 34, Liv 3, Ren 4, GB 20" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:2108622,
