tara-kb:S-112625-1198 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1198" ;
    dc:title "Clinical Observati on Acupuncture for Treatment of Climacteric SyndromeA Report of 35 Cases" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Main points: Fengfu (GV 16), Baihui (GV 20), Qihai (CV 6), Shenshu (BL 23)
Adjunct points: Pishu (BL 20), Ganshu (BL 18), Taixi (KI 3), Sanyinjiao (SP 6), Zusanli (ST 36), Neiguan (PC 6), Taichong (LR 3), Sishencong (EX HN1)
Needling details:
Fengfu (GV 16): Slowly punctured toward the mandible for 1 cun
Baihui (GV 20): Needled posteriorly and horizontally for 0.5 cun
Qihai (CV 6): Perpendicularly punctured for 1.5 cun
Shenshu (BL 23): Needled by twirling obliquely toward the spine for 1.5 cun
Adjunct points: Punctured with the routine reinforcing reducing method""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 30 participants who were treated with oral administration of oryzanol 0.01 0.02g, vitamin B 0.01 0.02g, and vitamin E 0.5 1g, three times a day for four weeks." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the country where the study was conducted)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Fengfu GV 16, Baihui GV 20, Qihai CV 6, Shenshu BL 23, Pishu BL 20, Ganshu BL 18, Taixi KI 3, Sanyinjiao SP 6, Zusanli ST 36, Neiguan PC 6, Taichong LR 3, Sishencong EX HN1" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Baihui GV 20",
        "Fengfu GV 16",
        "Ganshu BL 18",
        "Neiguan PC 6",
        "Pishu BL 20",
        "Qihai CV 6",
        "Sanyinjiao SP 6",
        "Shenshu BL 23",
        "Sishencong EX HN1",
        "Taichong LR 3",
        "Taixi KI 3",
        "Zusanli ST 36" ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Fengfu (GV 16): 1 cun (approximately 3.33 cm)
Baihui (GV 20): 0.5 cun (approximately 1.67 cm)
Qihai (CV 6): 1.5 cun (approximately 5 cm)
Shenshu (BL 23): 1.5 cun (approximately 5 cm)
Adjunct points: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1198 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1198 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 65
Acupuncture group: 35
Control group: 30""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation (needles were manipulated twice during retention to intensify stimulation) with specific techniques such as slow puncture and twirling; no other types of stimulation mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Climacteric syndrome (implied as related to kidney and mental activity regulation in TCM)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Climacteric syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Results: "In the acupuncture group, 12 cases were cured, 16 cases markedly effective, and 6 cases improved, the total effective rate being as high as 97.14%."
Conclusion: "Acupuncture for regulating the mental activities and reinforcing the kidney is an effective therapy for climacteric syndrome."
Effectiveness compared to control: Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Clinical outcome
Improvement inSymptomScores (using a modified KuppermanScoringSystem)
Results of radioimmunoassays (serum E2, FSH, LH levels)
Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of needle retention: 15 20 minutes
Frequency of sessions: Once a day for 4 weeks with a one day interval in each week""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was given once a day for 4 weeks as one therapeutic course, with a one day interval in each week." .

