tara-kb:S-112625-120 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-120" ;
    dc:title "German Acupuncture Trials (GERAC) for Chronic Low Back Pain Randomized, Multicenter, Blinded, Parallel-Group Trial With 3 Groups" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific acupoints or their locations)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham acupuncture: superficial needling at non-acupuncture points
Conventional therapy: a combination of drugs, physical therapy, and exercise""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Verum Acupuncture: 5 to 40 mm
Sham Acupuncture: 1-3 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-120 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-120 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 1162
Verum acupuncture group: 387
Sham acupuncture group: 387
Conventional therapy group: 388""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles (sterile, disposable) identical to those used in verum acupuncture
Quantity: 14 to 20 needles
Size: 0.25œ´40 mm or 0.35œ´50 mm
Location: Non-acupuncture points on the lateral part of the back and lower limbs
Penetration: Superficial (1-3 mm)
Stimulation: No stimulation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Verum acupuncture: Needles were stimulated manually to elicit the sensation of de Qi.
Sham acupuncture: Needles were not stimulated.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic low back pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Results: At 6 months, response rate was 47.6% in the verum acupuncture group, 44.2% in the sham acupuncture group, and 27.4% in the conventional therapy group. Differences among groups were as follows: verum vs sham, 3.4% (95% confidence interval, -3.7% to 10.3%; P=.39); verum vs conventional therapy, 20.2% (95% confidence interval, 13.4% to 26.7%; P œΩ .001); and sham vs conventional therapy, 16.8% (95% confidence interval, 10.1% to 23.4%; P œΩ.001).
Conclusion: Low back pain improved after acupuncture treatment for at least 6 months. Effectiveness of acupuncture, either verum or sham, was almost twice that of conventional therapy.
Effectiveness compared to control/sham: Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Response after 6 months, defined as 33% improvement or better on 3 pain-related items on the Von Korff Chronic Pain Grade Scale questionnaire or 12% improvement or better on the back-specific Hanover Functional Ability Questionnaire.
Secondary outcome measures: Responder rate at 1 1/2 and 3 months after randomization, scores on the 12-item Short Form Health Survey, and patient global assessment of therapy effectiveness on a scale of 1 (very good) to 6 (fail).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Depth of needle insertion for verum acupuncture: 5 to 40 mm
Depth of needle insertion for sham acupuncture: 1-3 mm
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: Generally 2 sessions per week
Duration: 30 minutes per session
Number of sessions: Ten sessions, with an option for five additional sessions for partial responders""" .

