tara-kb:S-112625-1216 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1216" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for Bell's Palsy: A Systematic Review and Meta-analysis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Tong (2010): Ipsilateral affected side SI18, ST2, ST4, ST6, GB14, LI4, TE17, ExHN7
Liu (1996): Ipsilateral BL14, ST2, BL1, TE17, ExHN5, BL2, GB1, SI18, ST4, LI20, GB20, LI4
Yang (2006): Ipsilateral affected side BL2-BL1, GB14-ExHN41, TE23-ExHN46, LI20-ST2, ST4-ST6, SI18, ST7, TE17, GB20, contra-lateral LI4
Zhu (2006): GB14, TE23, ST2, ST4, LI20, SI18, ST6, GB20, contra-lateral LI4
Wang (2007): Acute stage: Both GB20, LI4, LR3; Restoring stage: Ipsilateral affected side ExHN1-Nasal root, ST2, ST4-ST6, ST7, TE17, LI4 (bilateral), LR3 (bilateral); Incomplete eye close: GB14-ExHN41, BL2, BL62, KI6; Asymmetry mouth: GV26; Asymmetry nasal groove: LI20, LI19
Xuan (2007): GV11; Ipsilateral LI4, ST4, ST7, ST6, GB14, LI20, BL2
Dai (2009): Ipsilateral affected side BL2-ExHN41, LI20-ST2, ST4-ST6, ExHN46-ST7, GB20, LI4, LR3, TE17 (bilateral)
Shao (1999): 4‚Äì5 points among ipsilateral affected side ExHN5, ST7, ST6, ST4, SI18, TE17, LI20; Plus 1‚Äì2 points among LI4, ST40, ST36, LR3""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Drug therapy alone: Patients received medications such as prednisone, vitamin B, and mecobalamin.
Drug therapy combined with acupuncture: Patients received both acupuncture and drug therapy.
Specific medications used in control groups: dexamethasone, vitamin B, acyclovir.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005665 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1216 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1216 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: Not specified
Sample size for acupuncture vs. drug therapy: n=463
Sample size for acupuncture plus drug therapy vs. drug therapy alone: n=512""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not mention the use of a sham acupuncture group in the studies reviewed)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electroacupuncture (electrical stimulation) was used in studies by Wang and Dai.
Manual stimulation with de-qi was used in studies by Wang, Xuan, and Shao.
A "wild needling technique" was used by Xuan.
De-qi sensation was sought in manual acupuncture studies.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Bell's palsy" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, but with limitations due to low trial quality and number. The meta-analysis showed significant improvements in disease response rates for acupuncture groups compared to control groups, but the evidence is considered limited." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Disease response rate
Secondary outcome measures: House-Brackmann facial nerve grading system scores at various time points (e.g., 4 weeks, 2 weeks, 2 months)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place during a session)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Tong (2010): Acupuncture treatment was administered for 20 minutes, three times weekly for a maximum of three months.
Liu (1996): Acupuncture treatment was administered daily for a total of 10 times.
Yang (2006): Acupuncture treatment was administered daily for 10 days, with a rest period of two days, and then repeated for a total of two sessions.
Zhu (2006): Acupuncture treatment was administered daily for 10 times, with a rest period of two or three days, and then repeated for a total of two sessions.
Wang (2007): Acupuncture treatment was administered daily for six days, with a rest period of one day, and then repeated for a total of two sessions.
Xuan (2007): Acupuncture treatment was administered once daily for 10 times.
Dai (2009): Electroacupuncture treatment was administered once every other day for a total of 10 times.
Shao (1999): Acupuncture treatment was administered daily for 15 times, with a rest period of four days, and then repeated for a total of three sessions.""" .

