    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation (even method) with needles retained for 30 minutes and manipulated at every 5 minute interval; thermal stimulation (moxibustion) for cases with weakness of the spleen and stomach; sensation of \"qi\" sought." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Diabetic Gastroparesis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "The results turned out to be that the total effective rate in the treatment group reached 94.2%, that in the control group 1, 72%, and in the control group 2, 40%, the treatment group showing a better therapeutic effect than the other two control groups (P<0.05, P<0.01)."
Conclusion: Acupuncture was effective compared to the control groups.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Total effective rate
Secondary outcome measures: Cured, Markedly effective, Effective, Ineffective""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The acupuncture treatment was given once daily, with each course consisting of 10 treatments. Patients underwent two courses with a 5 day interval in between." .

