    dc:title "Observation of the Therapeutic Effect of Acupuncture on 58 Cases of Functional Dyspepsia" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Zusanli (ST 36): Lower He sea point of the Stomach Meridian of Foot yangming; regulates the spleen and stomach.
Zhongwan (RN 12): Front Mu point of the stomach; regulates the middle jiao, stomach, and spleen.
Neiguan (PC 6): One of the eight confluent points; regulates the spleen and stomach.
Tianshu (ST 25): Front Mu point of the Large Intestine Meridian of Hand yangming; promotes qi and relieves dyspepsia.
Liangqiu (ST 34): Xi Cleft point of the Stomach Meridian of Foot yangming.
Shangjuxu (ST 37): Lower He sea point of the Large Intestine Meridian of Hand yangming.
Xiajuxu (ST 39): Lower He sea point of the Small Intestine Meridian of Hand taiyang.
Selection based on differentiation of symptoms and signs for syndrome classification.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was administered 10 mg Cisapride three times a day for one consecutive month." ;
