    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Sham acupuncture was performed at BL-60 (urinary vesicle meridian) using a needle, with the procedure being similar to true acupuncture but at a non-therapeutic point. The sham procedure involved actual needle penetration. The significance of the choice of points was not explained to the patients, and the physician administering the treatment was blinded to the type of treatment." ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Needles were inserted manually; no further stimulation (e.g., manual manipulation, electrical stimulation) was mentioned." ;
