tara-kb:S-112625-1278 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1278" ;
    dc:title "Treatment of 60 Migraine Sufferers with Penetration Needling of Points and Point Selection Based on Following the Corresponding Meridians" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Sizhukong (SJ 23): Needled transversely to Shuaigu (GB 8) on the scalp.
Shuaigu (GB 8): Used in combination with Sizhukong (SJ 23) on the scalp.
Taiyang (Extra 1): Selected as a local point on the scalp.
Jiaosun (SJ 20): Selected as a local point on the scalp.
Waiguan (SJ 5): Needled perpendicularly on the extremities.
Zulingi (GB 41): Needled perpendicularly on the extremities.
Points were selected based on TCM principles, specifically the six channel syndrome differentiation, and involved both local and distal points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was prescribed 0.5 mg ergotamine and 50 mg caffeine to be taken orally. This group served as a comparison to the acupuncture group." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
