    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcome Measures:
Cured: Disappearance of headache and its accompaniedSymptoms, no recurrence happened within one year.
Effective: Headache was relieved by above 70% and after disappearance of headache there was no recurrence within half a year.
Improved: Headache wasSomewhat relieved or the attacking interval wasProlonged and the duration of headacheShortened.
Failed: TheSymptomsShowed no improvement.
Secondary Outcome Measures:
Relapse rates after one year
Therapeutic course effectiveness
Age related therapeutic effects
Differentiation type related therapeutic effects
Disease duration related outcomes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 1 to 3 minutes (manipulation time)
Duration of needle retention: 30 minutes (standard), up to 24 hours (for stubborn cases)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment is given once daily, with one therapeutic course consisting of 10 treatments. Needle retention and manipulation are part of the protocol, with some points retained for 30 minutes and manipulated every 10 minutes. For stubborn cases, the needle may be retained in the Ashi point for about 24 hours." .

