    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 72
Deep insertion group: 28
Normal insertion group: 24
Control group: 20""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation was used for stimulation, with a strong sensation sought in the Taiyang (EX HN5) area." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "upward intrusion of liver and gallbladder wind fire" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Migraine" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Result: "Deep insertion at Fengchi (GB 20) can shorten the duration of the headache remarkably and prolong the time between recurrences."
Conclusion: "Migraine patients treated by deep needling Fengchi (GB 20) had better results."
Statistical Significance: "There were remarkable differences among the three groups (P< 0.05)."
Effectiveness Compared to Control: Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Time necessary to relieve the headache completely
Secondary outcome measures:
Curative effectStandard of migraines (full recovery, effective, invalidation)
Follow upPeriod (one year or until headache recurred)
Effectiveness rates (asShown in the table)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 30 minutes
Frequency of sessions: Once daily for 14 days""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Needling was done once daily for 14 days." .

