tara-kb:S-112625-1284 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1284" ;
    dc:title "Efficacy of acupuncture for the prophylaxis of migraine: a multicentre randomised controlled clinical trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details about the needle locations or related acupoints used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture group using Streitberger placebo needles at the same acupoints as the verum group." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005277 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1284 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1284 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 50
Verum acupuncture group: 25
Sham acupuncture group: 25""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Streitberger placebo needles
Quantity: 25 subjects in the sham group
Size: Not specified
Location: Same acupoints as the verum group
Penetration: Non-penetrating
Other details: Fitted with a blunt tip, simulated penetration by shortening inside the handle, held in place by a plastic ring and plaster""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation for verum group; simulated penetration with pricking sensation for sham group." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Migraine" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The study found a statistically significant reduction in pain intensity for capsaicin-induced pain in the verum group compared to the sham group (P = 0.009).
However, this effect was described as "clinically questionable" and occurred mainly in a rating range that is not relevant to clinical pain.
The study concludes that acupuncture has a minor effect on experimental pain in healthy subjects, but this effect is not clinically significant.
The answer to whether acupuncture was effective compared to the control/sham group is "No" because the effect was not clinically significant and did not differ significantly in secondary endpoints.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcome Measures:
Difference in migraine days between 4 weeks before randomization and weeks 23 26 after randomization
Effectiveness quantified using a gradingScale (1=very good to 6=fail)
Secondary Outcome Measures:
Improvements inSecondary outcomes
No differences inSF 12SummaryScales
BetterPatient global assessmentScores for acupuncture groups
BetterScores for verum acupuncture inPain related impairment and intensity according to von Korff""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 1 hour and 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 1 hour and 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of treatment beyond a single session per participant)" .

