tara-kb:S-112625-129 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-129" ;
    dc:title "The effectiveness of acupuncture in treating chronic non-specific low back pain: a systematic review of the literature" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit details on specific acupuncture points or areas used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Minimal (sham) acupuncture
Conventional treatment
Placebo TENS
No treatment at all
Delayed acupuncture
Waiting list
Usual care
Physiotherapy alone""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the country where the study was conducted, but references to UK data and guidelines suggest a possible connection to the UK)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Haake et al.: Acupuncture 5-40 mm, Sham 1-3 mm
Brinkhaus et al.: Sham 20-40 mm
Leibing et al.: Acupuncture 10-30 mm, Sham 10-20 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-129 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-129 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 13,874
Witt et al.: 11,630
Haake et al.: 1,162
Brinkhaus et al.: 298
Thomas et al.: 241
Cherkin et al.: 638
Kerr et al.: 60
Leibing et al.: 131""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Haake et al.: Sham acupuncture with needle insertion of 1 to 3 mm.
Brinkhaus et al.: Minimal acupuncture (sham) with needles inserted 20 to 40 mm into non-acupuncture points, not stimulated.
Leibing et al.: Sham acupuncture with needles inserted to a depth of 10-20 mm, not stimulated.
Cherkin et al.: Simulated acupuncture using a toothpick and guide tube (non-penetrating).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual stimulation to achieve De Qi, a feeling of warmth and heaviness." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic non-specific low back pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes (acupuncture is more effective than no treatment), No (no significant difference between acupuncture and sham/minimal acupuncture), Maybe/Inconclusive (conflicting evidence regarding effectiveness over other treatment modalities)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Bodily pain dimension of the SF-36 at one year
Secondary outcome measures: Roland Morris Disability Questionnaire (RMDQ), 'Bothersome' Score, SF-36, Visual Analogue scale (VAS), Pain Disability Index, Von Korff chronic pain scale, HFAQ, Low back pain rating scale, EuroQol, Oswestry Disability Index, McGill Pain Index, Analgesics, Days spent in bed/ loss of work days, Lumber flexion ROM""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each session: 30 minutes
Number of sessions: Varied (e.g., 10 sessions, up to 12 or 15 sessions)
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Haake et al.: Ten, thirty minute sessions usually twice a week and an extra 5 sessions if they showed a 10-50% reduction in pain.
Brinkhaus et al.: Twelve, thirty minute sessions over eight weeks.
Thomas et al.: Ten individualized sessions over 3 months.
Leibing et al.: Twenty sessions of traditional standardized acupuncture over 12 weeks.
Kerr et al.: Standardized using set points and 11 needles only for a duration of 30 minutes, 10 sessions.""" .

