tara-kb:S-112625-1294 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1294" ;
    dc:title "The effect of acupuncture and moxibustion on physical performance by sedentary subjects submitted to ergospirometric test on the treadmill" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """K3 (Taixi): Located on the mid point of a horizontal line between the most salient part of the medial malleolus and the calcaneal (Achilles) tendon.
VC4 (Guanyuan): Located on the abdomen, on the anterior median line, 5 cm below the umbilical scar.
B123 (Shenshu): Located in the lumbar region at the level of the second vertebra (L2).
B147 (Zhishi): Located in the lumbar region at the level of the second vertebra (L2).
VG4 (Mingmen): Located in the lumbar region at the level of the second vertebra (L2), not bilateral.
B113 (Feishu): Located on the interscapular region along a vertical line, relating to the spinous processes of the 3rd thoracic vertebra (T3).
B114 (Jueyinshu): Located on the interscapular region along a vertical line, relating to the spinous processes of the 4th thoracic vertebra (T4).
B115 (Xinshu): Located on the interscapular region along a vertical line, relating to the spinous processes of the 5th thoracic vertebra (T5).
B137 (Pohu): Located at the same level as B113, B114, B115, with 7 8 cm lateral to the same spinous processes.
B138 (Gaohuangshu): Located at the same level as B113, B114, B115, with 7 8 cm lateral to the same spinous processes.
BI39 (Shentang): Located at the same level as B113, B114, B115, with 7 8 cm lateral to the same spinous processes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Group III (Control) consisted of 9 subjects, instructed to return after 45 days for an ergospirometric re evaluation, without receiving any intervention during this period." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "K 3, VC 4, B 123, B 147, VG 4, B 113, B 114, B 115, B 137, B 138, BI 39" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:4362146,
        TARA:8557069,
        TARA:9921528 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4362146\": \"KI 3\", \"TARA:9921528\": \"CV 4\", \"TARA:8557069\": \"GV 4\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "B 113",
        "B 114",
        "B 115",
        "B 123",
        "B 137",
        "B 138",
        "B 147",
        "BI 39" ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1294 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1294 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 31
Group I (Acupuncture): 11
Group II (Acupuncture Sham): 11
Group III (Control): 9""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham group: Group II (Acupuncture Sham)
Procedure: Acupuncture and moxibustion sessions on non acupoint locations
Location: 8 cm above and laterally to actual acupoints
Frequency and duration: 10 sessions over 5 weeks, twice a week
Needle type: Real needles (implied)
Penetration: Penetrating""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation: Thermal (moxibustion)
Needles: Not specified if manually manipulated or otherwise stimulated
Sensation: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the paper focuses on sedentary habits and fatigue, but does not specify a primary medical condition or disease)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The acupuncture and moxibustion sessions did not increase maximum oxygen uptake (VO,max) significantly."
"Other variables presented a significant increasing: oxygen uptake in anaerobic threshold (VOLa); velocity in anaerobic threshold (Vel LA); caloric consumption (Gast Cal)."
"The heart rate decreased when compared to velocity pre and post treatment."
"The results show peripheral, afferent stimulation (acupuncture and moxibustion) could alter the functions of structures or internal organs."
"The decrease in heart rate and the significant improvement in oxygen uptake in anaerobic threshold are similar to adaptations to physical training."
"Although there was a trend to the increase of the averages both in Group | (Acupuncture) and Group U (AcupunctureSham), (Table 1 ), we found no significant difference in maximum oxygen consumption (VO,max)."
"Oxygen consumption at the anaerobic threshold was significantly larger, both for Group I (Acupuncture) and Group II (AcupunctureSham) (Table I )."
"A significant increase in the relation to caloric consumption was observed (Table I )."
"Conclusions 1) With Acupuncture and moxibustion sessions, in post treatment, there was a significant decrease in heart rate in relation to velocity during the ergospirometric test on the treadmill."
"2) Following the acupuncture and moxibustion sessions, there was a significant improvement in the following variables: oxygen consumption at the anaerobic threshold, velocity of the anaerobic threshold, caloric consumption and percentage benefit."
"3) The decrease in the heart rate is a characteristic that simulates sports training."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Maximum oxygen uptake (VO,max)
Secondary outcome measures: Oxygen uptake at the anaerobic threshold (VOLa), velocity at the anaerobic threshold (Vel LA), caloric consumption (Gast Cal), decrease in heart rate""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment: 10 sessions, twice a week, for 5 weeks
Duration of each session: Not specified
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice a week for 5 weeks, with a total of 10 sessions." .

