tara-kb:S-112625-13 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-13" ;
    dc:title "Auricular acupuncture reduces intraoperative fentanyl requirement during hip arthroplasty--a randomized double-blinded study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Specific acupuncture points: MA-AH4 (hip), MA-TFl (shenmen), N4A-IC1 (lung), MA-AT4 (forehead)
Location: Ipsilateral to the surgery site
Criteria for selection: Frequently found patterns of lower skin resistance in patients during orthopedic surgery and previous clinical reports
Non-acupuncture points for sham procedure: Located on the helix of the ear""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received a sham procedure involving the insertion of needles at non-acupuncture points on the helix. This was used as a comparison to the auricular acupuncture group to assess the effectiveness of auricular acupuncture in reducing intraoperative fentanyl requirement." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "MA-AH 4, MA-TFl, N4A-IC 1, MA-AT 4" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "MA-AH 4",
        "MA-AT 4",
        "MA-TFl",
        "N4A-IC 1" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005178 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "1.5 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-13 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-13 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 57
Participants in AA group: 30
Participants in control group: 27""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure involved inserting needles at 4 non-acupuncture points on the helix.
Same type of needles used for both acupuncture and sham procedures: indwelling fixed "Carbo" AA needles.
Needle size: diameter of 0.22 mm and length of 1.5 mm.
Sham procedure was penetrating.
Needles were fixed with skin-colored adhesive tape.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual stimulation by massage of the AA needles for 5 minutes at specific times during surgery, totaling 15 minutes. No other type of stimulation was mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Degenerative osteoarthritis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, auricular acupuncture was effective in reducing intraoperative fentanyl requirement compared to the sham group, with a statistically significant difference (P=0.005)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Amount of fentanyl given during general anesthesia.
Secondary outcome measures: Duration of anesthesia; heart rate and blood pressure; body temperature; frequency of vasoactive agents and atropine administration; success of patients' blinding.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Not specified
Duration needles were left in place: 24 hours""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Once, with needles retained for 24 hours and manual stimulation during surgery" .

