    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The study found no significant difference in RMDQ scores between verum acupuncture and sham groups over time.
Verum acupuncture showed a statistically significant analgesic effect for worst pain at the 3-month follow-up (p = 0.034).
Verum acupuncture resulted in significantly fewer doses of analgesic medication compared to the sham group.
The acupuncture intervention was effective for worst pain but not for function.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Roland and Morris Disability Questionnaire (RMDQ), Visual Analogue Scale (VAS)
Secondary outcome measures: Multidimensional patient-centred questionnaire (work absenteeism, analgesic medication consumption, additional healthcare)""" ;
