    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0011918 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1319 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1319 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 240
Sample size per group: 80 (AO), 80 (DO), 80 (CAD)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Anxiety neuroses" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The cure rates in the AO, DO, and CAD groups were 20.0%, 26.3% and 52.5%, respectively. The difference in effectiveness of CAD was statistically significant (P<0.01)."
"The cure rates in the acupuncture only, behavioral desensitization only, and the combined acupuncture and desensitization groups were 20.0%, 26.3% and 52.5%, respectively (see Table 1 ). The results in the American Journal of Acupuncture, Vol. 26, No. 2/3, 1998 CAD group were significantly higher (P<0.01) than the other two groups."
"Our results showed that the synergism of acupuncture with behavioral desensitization therapy can be a successful alternative to the use of either therapy alone; the combined therapy also has the advantage of being free of the side effects encountered in conventional anti anxiolytic drug therapy."
The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham groups based on the primary outcome: Yes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Cure rate (clinicalSymptoms disappeared completely andSAS decreased to within normal range: <45)
Secondary outcome measures: Effective (symptoms improved markedly andSAS decreasedSignificantly), Improved (someSymptoms alleviated andSAS decreased, but notSignificantly), Ineffective (symptoms andSAS remained unchanged)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Each subject received 1 4 courses of treatment with an interval of 3 7 days between courses." .

