    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1324 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 60
Acupuncture group: 30
Control group: 30""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation (even reinforcing and reducing maneuver)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Melancholia (depression categorized as emotional strain induced disorder of qi functions and mental run away)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Depression" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The cured plus markedly effective rate in the acupuncture group was 73%.
Significant differences in plasma cortisol and ACTH levels were found before and after treatment in both groups (P<0.05).
No significant difference was found between the two groups in these biomarkers (P>0.05).
The therapeutic effect of acupuncture is parallel to the function of the hypothalamus pituitary adrenal axis.
The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group: Yes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: CuredPlus markedly effective rate
Secondary outcome measures: Changes inPlasma cortisol and ACTH levels, HAMDScores""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each session: 30 minutes
Duration retained: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The acupuncture treatments were administered once daily for 4 weeks, with 30 treatments constituting a therapeutic course." .

