    dc:title "Electro-Acupuncture of Paravertebral Points in Treating Cervical Spondylosis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Treatment Group (T): Paravertebral acupoints chosen based on site of lesion and neuro anatomic distribution. Points set one vertebral body proximal and distal to the site of the lesion if conforming relation exists; otherwise, chosen based on neuro anatomic localization.
Control Group (C): Ashi, Jianjing (GB 21), Tianzong (SI 11), Jianliao (SJ 14), Quchi (LI 11), Waiguan (SJ 5), Hegu (i 4).
Additional points: Shenshu (BL 23), Ganshu (BL 18).
Technique: Needles introduced perpendicularly to the vertebral lemina.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control group (C group): Conventional acupuncture at specific acupoints (Ashi, Jianjing (GB 21), Tianzong (SI 11), Jianliao (SJ 14), Quchi (LI 11), Waiguan (SJ 5), and Hegu (i 4)).
Techniques: Enhancing and reducing manipulation for 1 minute by withdrawal pushing and twisting.
Use of G 6805 Electric Acupuncture Unit with the same current as the treatment group.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Ashi, GB 21, SI 11, SJ 14, LI 11, SJ 5, LI 4, BL 23, BL 18" ;
