    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0008480 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Jiaji (EX B2): 1 Cun deep
Baihui (GV 20): 1.2 Cun towards Houding (GV 19) along subcutaneous tissue
Fengchi (GB 20): 1 1.5 Cun towards the inner canthus of the opposite side""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1337 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1337 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 96
Treatment group: 50
Control group: 46""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation (twirling the needle) for 30 seconds, retained for 30 minutes with manipulations every 10 minutes." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cervical spondylosis of the vertebral artery type" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The cured rate and the total effective rate were 42.0% and 98.0% in the treatment group, and 28.3% and 67.4% in the control group, respectively, with significant differences between the two groups in the cured rate and the total effective rate(P<0.01, P<0.05)."
"Acupuncture combined with massage has a definite therapeutic effect on cervical spondylosis of the vertebral artery type."
"It can be seen from Table 1 that there is a very significant difference between the two groups in the cured rate(P<0.01), and a significant difference in the total effective rate(P<0.05), the treatment group being better than the control group."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Cured rate, Total effective rate
Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes (duration of each session), 30 minutes (needles retained)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was administered once daily for 14 consecutive days." .

