    dc:title "Acupuncture Treatment for 15 Cases of Post traumatic Coma" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not mention specific needle locations or related acupoints)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received basic neural medical treatment in the rehabilitation ward. This is equivalent to usual care or standard treatment without any additional interventions like acupuncture or point injection therapy." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the country where the study was conducted)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0009764 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on needle insertion depth)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1369 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1369 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total sample size: 30; Group distribution: Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide details on how the acupuncture needles were stimulated)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Post traumatic Coma" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "The results showed that the GCS value in the treatment group was higher than that of the control group, but with no statistical significance (P>0.05). However, the main symptoms of the patients in treatment group, such as aphasia, hemiplegia, and injuries of cranial nerves (including injuries of the facial, oculomotor and abducent nerves) were obviously improved, showing significant differences as compared with the control group (P<0.05). Conclusion can be made that acupuncture combined with point injection has the consciousness inducing effect for post traumatic coma, and shows good effects for the cranial nerve injuries and aphasia."
Effectiveness: Maybe/Inconclusive (GCS scores not statistically significant, but significant improvements in other symptoms)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: GCS evaluations
Secondary outcome measures: Changes in mainSymptoms (aphasia, hemiplegia, injuries of cranial nerves)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of acupuncture treatments)" .

