tara-kb:S-112625-1376 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1376" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for fibromyalgia-a systematic review of randomized clinical trials" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Points chosen according to traditional Chinese medicine principles.
EA group: Two peripheral points and up to six near painful sites.
Control group: Sham treatment 20mm from actual points.
Some studies standardized points; others used individualized points.
Specific points not detailed in text; table likely provides more information.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control groups in the studies included sham acupuncture (e.g., placebo needle that did not penetrate the skin, acupuncture at non-suited points, non-penetrating simulated acupuncture), nonacupuncture treatments, and no treatment. Specific interventions included sham needling, sham laser acupuncture, and medical treatments like Oryzanol, Vitamin B, and Amitriptyline." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005546 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1376 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1376 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Assefi et al.: 100 participants
Delzue et al.: 70 participants (EA: 36, Sham EA: 34)
Guo and Jia: 60 participants (EA: 22)
Sprott: 30 participants
Total sample size: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure involved using a placebo needle that did not penetrate the skin.
Sham treatments included acupuncture at points not suited for fibromyalgia, needle insertion at non-acupuncture points, or non-penetrating simulated acupuncture.
Control group received just perceptible EA treatment 20mm from points that would have been used.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) was used in several trials, with some trials using it exclusively and others combining it with manual stimulation. The intensity was high enough to cause muscle contractions in some cases. Sham stimulation was used in control groups, with placebo needles and no electrical current." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide the disease or condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Fibromyalgia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes:
Subjective pain (VAS) [Assefi et al.]
Pain threshold [Delzue et al.]
Secondary outcomes:
Intensity of fatigue (VAS) [Assefi et al.]
Sleep quality (VAS) [Assefi et al.]
Overall well-being (VAS) [Assefi et al.]
Physical and mental functioning (SF-36) [Assefi et al.]
Number of analgesics used [Delzue et al.]
Regional pain score [Delzue et al.]
Morning stiffness [Delzue et al.]
Patient and physician-rated improvements [Delzue et al.]""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Twice weekly for 12 weeks
Six treatments over a 3-week period
At least once a week
Treatment length varied between 6 and 40 sessions""" .

