    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Jiaji points from C1 C4 (bilateral); Taiyang (EX HN5); Touwei (ST 8); Sizhukong (TE 23); Shuaigu (GB 8); Fengchi (GB 20) on the affected side; Taichong (LR 3) for hyperactivity of the liver yang; Taixi (KI 3) for kidney deficiency; Sanyinjiao (SP 6) for blood deficiency; Geshu (BL 17) for blood stasis.
Penetrating needling from Taiyang (EX HN5) to Shuaigu (GB 8), from Sizhukong (TE 23) to Shuaigu (GB 8), and from Touwei (ST 8) to Shuaigu (GB 8)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 29 cases and received only drug treatment, which included intravenous drip with 250ml of 5% glucose, 20m of salvia injection, and 10mg of 654 2 at the acute stage; and oral administration of sibelium, 10mg once daily at the remission stage. The drug treatment lasted 30 days." ;
