tara-kb:S-112625-1378 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1378" ;
    dc:title "Treatment of 68 Newborns with Brachial Plexus Paralysis with Shallow Puncture and Multiple Points" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "\"Jianyu (LI 15); Quchi (LI 11); Shousanli (LI 10); Waiguan (TW 5); Yangchi (TW 4); Hegu (LI 4); Neiguan (PC 6); Binao (LI 14); Jiquan (HT 1); Taijian (1.5 cun directly below the anterior acromion); Ashi points; Adjunct points:; Hongzhong (2.5 cun below Tianquan (PC 2)); Bizhong (the mid spot of the connecting line of the carpal cross striation and the cubital cross striation and between the two bones); Waiguan (TW 5) for weakness in flexion and extension; Tianzong (SI 11) for difficulty in raising the arm; Jubi (3.5 cun below the acromion) for difficulty in raising the arm; Zhitan (the intraclavicular fossa) for difficulty in raising the arm; Shaohai (HT 3) for outward rotation of the hand; Houxi (SI 3) for outward rotation of the hand; Neiguan (PC 6) for outward rotation of the hand; Yangchi (TW 4) for adduction of the hand; Yangxi (LI 5) for adduction of the hand; Lieque (LU 7) for adduction of the hand; Waiguan (TW 5) for wrist drop; Ashi point for wrist drop." ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was treated with medication consisting of 10 mg of Vit B1, 10 mg of Vit B6, and 150 to 250 pg of Cobamamide taken orally, tid. for one month, along with local massage performed once daily for 10 sessions per therapeutic course." ;
