tara-kb:S-112625-1379 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1379" ;
    dc:title "Improvement in Fibromyalgia Symptoms With Acupuncture: Results of a Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Bilateral points at large intestine 4, stomach 36, liver 2, spleen 6, pericardium 6, and heart 7.
Axial paramedian points along the bladder meridian at the cervical spine (first 3 sessions) and at the lumbar spine (last 3 sessions).
Total of 18 needles for the first 3 sessions and 20 needles for the final 3 sessions.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received simulated acupuncture, where patients were positioned identically to those receiving true acupuncture, but instead of inserting needles, the skin was indented with a dull surgical instrument, and a bandage was applied with a modified needle that did not pierce the skin. Electrical stimulation was applied in the same manner as for the acupuncture group, but without actual current flow due to skin resistance." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States (specifically in Minnesota)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4, ST 36, LR 2, SP 6, P 6, HT 7" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:2442762,
        TARA:4311153,
        TARA:4385250,
        TARA:6463344,
        TARA:6862058 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:6862058\": \"LR 2\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\", \"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\", \"TARA:2442762\": \"HT 7\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005546 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1379 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1379 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 50
Acupuncture group: 25
Control group: 25""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Sham needles were used, which were bent to form a tripod and did not pierce the skin.
Quantity and size: Not specified.
Location: Identical points as the acupuncture group.
Penetrating or non-penetrating: Non-penetrating.
Other details: Electrical stimulation was applied but did not result in perceptible current flow due to skin resistance.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) was used at 2 Hz between large intestine 4 and stomach 36, and at 10 Hz over axial circuits. The sensation of de Qi or \"needle grab\" was not specifically elicited." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Fibromyalgia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"Total fibromyalgia symptoms, as measured by the FIQ, were significantly Improved in the acupuncture group compared with the control group during the study period (P=.01)."
"The largest difference in mean FIQ total scores was observed at 1 month (42.2 vs 34.8 In the control and acupuncture groups, respectively; P=.007)."
"Fatigue and anxiety were the most significantly improved symptoms during the followup period."
"This study paradigm allows for controlled and blinded clinical trials of acupuncture. We found that acupuncture significantly improved symptoms of fibromyalgia."
"We found that acupuncture improved symptoms of fibromyalgia significantly more than placebo."
"Specific symptoms that showed the most significant improvements included fatigue and anxiety."
"The improvement was both clinically and statistically significant."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: FIQ total score
Secondary outcome measures: Individual subscales of the FIQ and MPI""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "20 minutes per session; needles left in place for 20 minutes during each session" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Patients received treatments every 2 to 4 days during 2 to 3 weeks for a total of 6 sessions." .

