    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s). The study found significantly higher elevations of pain threshold under stimulation of classical acupuncture loci compared to needling of points outside the 'meridians' (P< 0.01)." ;
