        TARA:5290080 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0992296\": \"BL 23\", \"TARA:0906448\": \"BL 25\", \"TARA:5290080\": \"BL 40\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific depth measurements for needle insertion in either PRF or electro-acupuncture therapy)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-139 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-139 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 100
Participants within groups: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """PRF therapy: Pulse train with a period of 0.5 sec, duty cycle of 5%, modulated by a 500 KHz sine wave, applied to the dorsal root ganglion.
EA therapy: Single pulse with a 1/15 second duration, low pulse frequency of 15 Hz for 30 minutes, aiming for sensations of fullness, numbness, tingling, and heat.
Control group: No stimulation by PRF or EA.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM diagnosis or terminology for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic Low Back Pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The study found that PRF therapy is significantly more effective than EA therapy after one month, with a 35% improvement in pain relief compared to 16% for EA.
EA therapy showed functional improvement in the lumbar spine, but the improvement in motion recovery was not significantly different from PRF.
Both PRF and EA therapies are related to electricity effects, but PRF has better electrical penetration due to its higher frequency pulse.
Yes, the acupuncture intervention (EA) was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcome of functional improvement in the lumbar spine.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Visual Analog Score (VAS) for pain relief, Oswestry Disability Index (ODI) for functional disability, Short Form 36 (SF-36) for health assessment.
Secondary outcomes: Not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place during a session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Three times a week for four weeks, with each session lasting 30 minutes." .

