tara-kb:S-112625-1400 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1400" ;
    dc:title "Induction of Cervical Dilatation in Preparation for First Trimester Abortion and Its Influence on HCG" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """LI4 (ho ku): Located on the middle radial aspect of the second metacarpal bone, at the highest spot of the first musculi interossei dorsalis when the thumb and index finger are brought together.
SP6 (san yin chiao): Located a four finger breadth above the tip of the medial malleolus, just posterior to the tibial border.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control groups consisted of patients who did not receive any preparation for cervical dilatation (no acupuncture) and were used for comparison in both cervical dilatation and HCG evaluation. There were two control groups: one for general cervical dilatation and another specifically for HCG evaluation, restricted to patients at or below 10 weeks' gestation." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4, SP 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:4385250 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "approximately 2 1 inch" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1400 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1400 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 20 (intervention group) + 20 (control group for cervical dilatation) + 20 (control group for HCG evaluation) = 60
Participants within groups:
Intervention group: 20
Control group for cervical dilatation: 20
Control group for HCG evaluation: 20""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Needles were stimulated using electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture).
The stimulation involved strong electrical stimulation for SP6 and weak stimulation for LI4.
The frequency used was 250 cycles/sec, and the intensity was adjusted until the patient felt the current without pain.
Specific sensations were sought during the stimulation, such as radiations to the fingers and toes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not mention a disease or condition in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cervical dilatation for first trimester abortion" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group in increasing cervical dilatation, with a statistically significant p value of <0.001. The method was also found to be safe with no systemic side effects and no detrimental effect on pregnancy as indicated by HCG levels." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Increase in cervical dilatation as assessed by Hegar dilators.
Secondary outcome measure: Effect of acupuncture onSerum human chorionic gonadotropin (HCG) levels.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of treatment beyond a single session)" .

