    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0031169 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "The needle depth varied depending on the point being stimulated; Seirin 1-2 inch needles were used with a 32 gauge (0.25 mm) diameter and inserted using a guide tube." ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1403 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1403 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 364
Treatment group: 181
Control group: 183""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture points were not traditional acupuncture points and were inserted away from classical acupuncture points and meridians.
Points were located on the sacral area, hand, foot, a point below the knee, and lower leg.
Specific locations included the foot anterior to the junction of the third and fourth metatarsals, 4 cun below and two fingerbreadths lateral to the knee, 2 cun above Kidney 3, 2 cun above the wrist crease, and 1 cun lateral away from sacral points Shangliao UB31 and Ciliao UB32.
The procedure involved minimal insertion and stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation was used to stimulate the needles, with the aim of eliciting a de qi sensation characterized by soreness, numbness, or heaviness." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Deficiency of Blood or Qi or stagnation of Qi and Blood" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Postterm pregnancy and labor induction" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcomes:
Need for induction methods
Time from intervention to delivery
Change in Bishop score
Length of active labor
Secondary Outcomes:
Methods of pain relief
Mode of birth
Apgar scores less than 7 at 5 minutes
Admission of the mother and neonate from the labor room to postnatal ward together
Subsidiary Endpoints:
Meconium-stained amniotic fluid
Incidence of nonreassuring fetal heart rate tracing
Neonatal jaundice requiring phototherapy
Neonatal seizures
Acceptability of treatment""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 45 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 30-40 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Two 45-minute sessions over a 2-day period, with needle stimulation lasting up to 30-40 minutes per session." .

