    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, acupuncture was found to be effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcomes. The results show significant improvement in symptoms and pain reduction in the acupuncture group compared to the pseudo acupuncture group, with statistical significance (p < 0.001 and p < 0.005)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Reduction inPain as assessed by a horizontalPainScale
Self reported improvement inSymptoms
Secondary outcome measure:
Reduction in analgesic intake""" ;
