tara-kb:S-112625-1414 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1414" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture and Chronic Pain Management" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """LI.4 (Hegu acupoint), ST.36 (Zusanli acupoint).
Acupoints specific for the treatment of eye disorders (not specified)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Not applicable (the paper is a review of existing studies, not a primary trial)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham acupuncture: Needling at incorrect, theoretically irrelevant sites.
Minimal acupuncture: Acupuncture away from usual locations, very shallow needling, and very slight stimulation.
Placebo acupuncture needle: Specially designed needle with a blunt tip, not fixed inside the handle.
Mock TENS (placebo controls): Transcutaneous nerve stimulation with surface electrodes, but no current passing.
Alternative treatment (standard care comparisons): Comparison with standard treatment (e.g., physiotherapy, medication).
Adjunctive care comparisons: Assessing the efficacy of acupuncture plus standard care relative to standard care alone.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state where the study was conducted, but mentions funding and research initiatives in the US and UK)" ;
