tara-kb:S-112625-1415 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1415" ;
    dc:title "Clinical Research on Improving VAS Value of Patients with Thalamic Pain with Mind-Regulating and Pain-Relieving Acupuncture" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Treatment Group: Renzhong (DU26), Neiguan (bilateral, PC6), Yongquan (bilateral, K11), Laogong (bilateral, PC8); Adjunct acupoints: Jianyu (LI15), Jianliao (SJ14), Quchi (LI11), Tianjing (SJ10), Waiguan (SJ5), Yangchi (SJ4), Huantiao (GB30), Biguan (ST31), Chengfu (BL36), Fengshi (GB31), Dubi (ST35), Heding (EX), Qiuxu (GB40), Shenmai (BL62)
Control Group: Jianyu (L115), Jianliao (SJ14), Quchi (L111), Tianjing (SJ10), Waiguan (SJ5), Yangchi (SJ4), Huantiao (GB30), Biguan (ST31), Chengfu (BL36), Fengshi (GB31), Dubi (ST35), Heding (EX), Qiuxu (GB40), Shenmai (BL62)
Selection based on TCM diagnosis: dredging the meridians and choosing points both along the meridians and locally""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control group: Body acupuncture treatment group
Number of participants: 31
Acupuncture points: Jianyu (L115), Jianliao (SJ14) in the shoulder, Quchi (L111) and Tianjing (SJ10) in the elbow; Waiguan (SJ5) and Yangchi (SJ4) in the wrist, Huantiao (GB30) and Biguan (ST31) in the hip, Chengfu (BL36) and Fengshi (GB31) in the thigh, Dubi (ST35) and Heding (EX) in the knee, Qiuxu (GB40) and Shenmai (BL62) in the ankle.
Method: Filiform needles (0.35 x 50 mm) used for acupuncture.
Double blind method used.
Stopped taking analgesics or sedatives 2 weeks before the study.
Efficacy assessed by decrease in visual analogue scale (VAS).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "DU 26, PC 6, K 11, PC 8, LI 15, SJ 14, LI 11, SJ 10, SJ 5, SJ 4, GB 30, ST 31, BL 36, GB 31, ST 35, EX, GB 40, BL 62" ;
