Treatment group: 34
Control group: 31""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation: Needles were inserted, twirled, and rotated for 2 minutes at a speed of 200 r/min. A needling sensation was sought. No electrical, thermal, or laser stimulation was mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly use TCM terminology to describe the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Thalamic pain caused by cerebrovascular diseases (infarction or hemorrhage)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"Efficacy in the treatment group was significantly better than the control group (P< 0.05), VAS score of the treatment group was significantly lower than the control group (P < 0.01)."
"mind regulating and pain relieving acupuncture can ease central nervous system pain, and relieve symptoms of thalamic cerebrovascular pain."
"Mind regulating and pain relieving acupuncture was more effective in treating thalamic pain than body acupuncture treatment."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Decrease in visual analogueScale (VAS)Scores before and after treatment.
Secondary outcome measure: Total effective rate, including clinical cure (disappearance ofPain and no recurrence).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Needles were manipulated for 2 minutes.
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified.
Overall treatment duration: 4 weeks.""" ;
