tara-kb:S-112625-1416 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1416" ;
    dc:title "A Comparative Study of the Pain Alleviating Effect of Vibratory Stimulation, Transcutaneous Electrical Nerve Stimulation, Electroacupuncture and Placebo" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific acupuncture points or areas, nor does it detail the criteria for point selection)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Group P: Placebo acupuncture therapy was performed at precisely located regions with no actual stimulation. The needles were inserted to a depth of 1 3 mm, and no sensations were perceived by the patients. Group P received placebo electroacupuncture, where the needles were connected to a constant current source but no impulses were given." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003326 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1416 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1416 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 17
Group A (correct acupuncture): 8
Group P (placebo acupuncture): 9""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles used for sham procedure
Quantity: Not specified
Size: Not specified
Location: Non acupuncture points (precisely located regions with no differences in skin resistance)
Penetration: Penetrating (needles inserted to a depth of 1 3 mm)
Other details: No sensations typically associated with real acupuncture were elicited; sham electroacupuncture involved no impulses""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used was electroacupuncture with chain frequencies of 4 Hz and 100 Hz at an intensity just below the pain threshold. The needles were stimulated for 20 minutes during each session. Sensations of heaviness or parasthesia were sought to ensure correct stimulation and location." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM diagnosis or terminology for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Myalgia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, but with limitations. Acupuncture showed a modest effect compared to the placebo group, with significant improvements in some parameters 2 weeks after starting therapy. However, these effects were not substantial and did not persist beyond the initial period." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Reduction inPain intensity as assessed byPatients using a visual analogueScale before and after eachStimulationSession.
Secondary outcome measures: Duration ofPain relief,Percentage ofPatients experiencingPain relief exceeding 50%, magnitude of thePlacebo effect.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment period: 5 weeks
Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was approximately twice a week, with each session lasting 20 minutes, over a 5 week period." .

tara-kb:S-112625-1417 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1417" ;
    dc:title "The Efficacy of Dry Needling and Procaine in the Treatment of Myofascial Pain in the Jaw Muscles" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """The locations of trigger points in the jaw muscles are correlated with known acupuncture points in the jaws.
Specific locations for sites M1, M2, M3, T1, T2, and T3 are provided:
M1: 10 mm posterior to the anterior border of the masseter muscle and 10 mm superior to the inferior border of the mandible.
M2: 10 mm posterior to the masseter muscle's anterior border and 10 mm inferior to the lowest point on the zygomatic buttress.
M3: 10 mm anterior to the masseter muscle's posterior border, equidistant from M1 and M2.
T1: 10 mm posterior to the anterior temporalis muscle's anterior border and 10 mm above the highest point on the zygomatic buttress.
T2: 20 mm above the central point of T1.
T3: 20 mm posterior to the central point of T1.
Specific acupuncture points are not mentioned by name or number.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control group C: Simulated local anesthetic + simulated dry needling (double placebo)
No treatment control group was not used due to ethical considerations""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0040264 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific information on the depth of needle insertion for the dry needling treatment)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1417 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1417 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 30
Participants within groups: 10 per group (Group A: Procaine + simulated dry needling, Group B: dry needling + simulated local anesthetic, Group C: simulated local anesthetic + simulated dry needling)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Simulated dry needling and local anesthetic injections.
Location: Non painful sites in the face.
Needle type: Not specified.
Quantity and size: Not specified.
Penetration: Likely non penetrating or minimal to avoid stimulating trigger points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention any type of stimulation beyond the insertion of the needle itself)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not mention the condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Myofascial pain in the jaw muscles" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No (the acupuncture intervention was not found to be effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcomes)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:Patients'Pain reports (pain intensity and unpleasantnessScores using VAS),PainPressure threshold (PPT)
Secondary outcome measures: Reduction in muscle tenderness""" ;
