    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-142" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture Treatment of Chronic Back Pain A Double-Blind Placebo-Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """For localized low back pain: points 23, 25, 36, and 40 on the urinary bladder meridian
For sciatica: points 30, 34, 39, and 60 on the gallbladder meridian
Average of eight needles used per session""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study was a placebo group. The placebo treatment consisted of an intradermal injection of 2 percent lidocaine at non-acupuncture, non-tender sites in the lumbar area, followed by superficial insertion of acupuncture needles without stimulation." ;
