Participants within groups: Group I = 36, Group II = 41""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Intradermal injection of 2 percent lidocaine at non-acupuncture, non-tender sites in the lumbar area.
Needle type: Real acupuncture needles used superficially.
Quantity: Similar number of needles as in real acupuncture sessions.
Location: Non-acupuncture, non-tender sites in the lumbar area.
Penetration: Superficial insertion without deep penetration.
Stimulation: No stimulation during the sham procedure.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual stimulation until the sensation of \"teh 'chi\" (heaviness and numbness) was elicited, then left in situ for 30 minutes without further stimulation." ;
