tara-kb:S-112625-1428 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1428" ;
    dc:title "Observation on therapeutic effect of acupuncture on hyperemesis gravidarum" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Main acupoints: Dazhu (BL 11), Shangjuxu (ST 37), Neiguan (PC 6), Gongsun (SP 4), Zhongwan (RN12), Zusanli (ST36)
Additional acupoints based on TCM diagnosis:
Weakness of the spleen and stomach: Pishu (BL20), Weishu (BL21)
Incoordination between the liver and stomach: Ganshu (BL18), Weishu (BL21), Taichong (LR3)
Stagnation and phlegm damp: Fenglong (ST40), Yinlingquan (SP9)
Deficiency of both vital energy (Qi) and yin: Zhaohai (KI6)
Insertion depths and techniques:
Dazhu (BL 11): 1.5 cm, perpendicular twisting reducing method, no retention
Other back points: 1.5 cm, twisting manipulation, no retention
Shangjuxu (ST 37): 3.0 cm, perpendicular twisting reducing method, no retention
Neiguan (PC 6), Gongsun (SP 4), Taichong (LR3), Zhaohai (KI6): shallow insertion, no retention
Zusanli (ST36), Fenglong (ST40), Yinlingquan (SP9), Zhongwan (RN 12): 3.0 cm, perpendicular twisting method, retained for 25 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Western Medicine Group: Received oral administration of Luminal for sedation and antiemetic effects.
Chinese Medicine Group: Received traditional Chinese herbal decoctions based on syndrome differentiation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
