tara-kb:S-112625-1429 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1429" ;
    dc:title "Success of Acupuncture and Acupressure of the Pc 6 Acupoint in the Treatment of Hyperemesis Gravidarum" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Pc 6 (Neiguan) acupoint: Used for both acupuncture and acupressure to reduce emesis.
St 36 (Zusanli) acupoint: Calms the ascending qi of the stomach.
Ren 13 (Shangwan) acupoint: Treats fullness in the epigastric region.
DuMai 20 (Baihui) acupoint: Has anxiolytic and sedation effects.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Group 3: Superficial intracutaneous placebo AP (n = 8)
Group 4: Placebo APr (n = 7)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Pc 6, St 36, Ren 13, DuMai 20" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:4311153,
        TARA:4525270,
        TARA:6463344 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:4525270\": \"CV 13\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "DuMai 20" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0006791 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper describes the insertion as \"superficial intracutaneous\" but does not provide a specific depth measurement)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1429 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1429 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 36
Group 1 (Acupuncture Pc 6 acupoint): 10
Group 2 (Acupressure Pc 6): 11
Group 3 (Placebo acupuncture): 8
Group 4 (Placebo acupressure): 7""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture group: Superficial intracutaneous insertion of the same type of needles at points without de-qi effect.
Sham acupressure group: Not explicitly detailed in terms of technique, but implied to be a non-stimulating version of acupressure.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation was used for stimulation in the acupuncture group. The placebo group involved superficial insertion without stimulation. A sensation (de-qi effect) was sought in the active treatment groups." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Vomiting in early pregnancy due to general weakness of the stomach qi ('vital energy') and reaction to the development of the fetus." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Hyperemesis gravidarum (HG)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s). The success rate for AP was 90%, and for APr was 63.6%, with statistical significance indicated by p-values (p < 0.0001 for AP and p < 0.1 for APr)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Disappearance of nausea symptoms and vomiting, no need for medicamentous therapy.
Secondary outcome measures: Success rates (e.g., 90% for AP, 63.6% for APr), patient reports, independent gynecologist evaluations, number of cases, age, weight, anxiety and depression symptoms, gestational age, intravenous infusion, parenteral antiemetics.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency or duration of acupuncture treatments)" .

