tara-kb:S-112625-1445 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1445" ;
    dc:title "A Randomized Pilot Study of Acupuncture as an Adjunct Therapy in Adult Asthmatic Patients" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Active Acupuncture Points:
CV22: Inserted perpendicularly for about 0.5 mm, then changed direction by approximately 40 degrees downward, inserted about 30 mm in depth, parallel to the posterior surface of the sternum.
Bilateral LUS: Inserted perpendicularly by the inducer for about 10 mm.
ST40: Inserted slightly directed into the medial side about 30 mm in depth.
BL13: Inserted approximately 30 degrees oblique to the vertebrae.
EXB1: Inserted perpendicularly by the inducer for about 20 mm.
Dingchuan: Mentioned but no specific details provided.
Sham Acupuncture Points: Nine non acupoints corresponding to each active acupoint, with minimal skin penetration (about 0.5 mm in depth) without manipulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT), Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Verum acupuncture group: Received actual acupuncture treatment based on traditional Chinese medicine principles.
Sham acupuncture group: Received a part standardized sham acupuncture procedure.
Standard therapy group: Received standard migraine prophylaxis with beta blockers, calcium channel blockers, or antiepileptic drugs.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Korea" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "CV 22, LU 5, ST 40, BL 13, EXB 1, Dingchuan" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:1357729,
        TARA:6050541,
        TARA:6472655,
        TARA:8009041,
        TARA:9531666 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:6472655\": \"CV 22\", \"TARA:1357729\": \"LU 5\", \"TARA:9531666\": \"ST 40\", \"TARA:6050541\": \"BL 13\", \"TARA:8009041\": \"Dingchuan\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0004979 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """CV22: 30 mm
LUS: 10 mm
EXB1: 20 mm
LI4: 30 mm
ST40: 30 mm
BL13: Not specified (only angle mentioned)
Sham acupuncture: 0.5 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1445 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1445 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 794 (intention to treat), 443 (per protocol)
Participants within groups:
Verum acupuncture: 313
Sham acupuncture: 339
Standard therapy: 308""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Needling at non acupuncture points
Quantity: Mean of 13.8 needles per session
Location: Non acupuncture points
Penetration: Penetrating""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the stimulation method used in the acupuncture treatment)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the disease or condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Asthma" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The primary outcome showed significant improvements compared to baseline for all groups (p<0 0001), but not significant differences between the groups (p=0 09).
The proportion of responders was not significantly different between groups (p=0 133).
Treatment outcomes did not differ significantly between verum acupuncture, sham acupuncture, and standard therapy.
Exploratory analyses suggested verum acupuncture was more effective than sham acupuncture (p=0 017).
The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s): Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome: daily morningPeak expiratory flow (PEF)
Secondary outcomes: forced expiratory volume oneSecond (FEV), quality of life questionnaire for adult Korean asthmatics (QLQAKA), transition dyspnea index (TDI),Serum eosinophil count, totalSerum immunoglobulin E (IgE)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment: 6 weeks with 10 sessions (up to 15 sessions for some patients)
Duration of each session: Approximately 32.5 minutes (verum group), not specified for sham group
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Ten sessions over 6 weeks, with the possibility of up to 15 sessions if treatment was deemed only partly successful. Duration of sessions was approximately 32.5 minutes." .

