    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 1787
Participants within groups: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Hsu 2009 and Su 2009: Sham techniques involved plain adhesive tapes or heat pad therapy on the same stimulation points.
Tsay 2003a and Tsay 2004a: Sham acupressure used non-acupoints 1 cm away from the meridian, following the same treatment protocol as manual acupressure.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electrostimulation using a penetrating needle or nonpenetrating pad
Manual acupressure with finger pressure (force of 3 to 4 kg)
Moxibustion (heating the herb mugwort)
Other types of heat stimulation on acupuncture points
Needle stimulation: reduction technique, manipulated every 10 minutes
Response sought: de-qi response (soreness, numbness, heaviness, distension, warmth)""" ;
