tara-kb:S-112625-1478 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1478" ;
    dc:title "Clinical Observation on the Treatment of Chloasma by Chinese Herbs Combined with Acupuncture" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Primary acupoints: bilateral Zusanli (ST36), Sanyinjiao (SP6), right side Fenglong (ST40), Chize (LUS), left side Ligou (Liv5), and Yinlingquan (SP9)
Depth of needling: 0.5-1.0 cun
Dorsal points needled first without retention, others retained for 40 minutes
Shallow needling around skin lesions: 0.2-0.5 cun
Additional points based on syndrome differentiation:
Anxiety and irritability: Bilateral Taichong (Liv3) and Hegu (LI4)
Chest stuffiness and palpitation: Bilateral Quze (PC3) and Jiaji of T4-5 (EX)
Constipation: Bilateral Tianshu (ST25) and Xiajuxu (ST39)
Menstrual disorder: Jituxia of T1, 3, 5, 7, 9 (EX), Geshu (BL17), and Shenshu (BL23)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 30 patients who received conventional treatment with oral intake of vitamin C and E, and external application of Quban Powder (#4 #7)." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "ST 36, SP 6, ST 40, LUS, Liv 5, SP 9, Liv 3, LI 4, PC 3, EX, ST 25, ST 39, BL 17, BL 23" ;
