Other points were needled and retained for 40 minutes, suggesting manual stimulation.
Shallow needling around lesions with needle tip directed towards the lesion, indicating manual stimulation.
No other forms of stimulation (electrical, thermal, laser) were mentioned.
No specific sensation was sought during stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Chloasma, related to gloomy moods, insufficiency of essence and blood, qi-blood disharmony, and Shen or Pi deficiency causing Gan stagnancy." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chloasma" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes. The total effective rate and cure-effective rate were significantly higher in the treated group (P<0.01), and there was a more significant decrease in lesion size and color, as well as symptoms (P<0.05 or P<0.01)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Total effective rate, cure-effective rate, size and color of skin lesions
Secondary outcome measures: Scores for symptoms (irregular menstruation, menalgia, insomnia, chest stuffiness, palpitation, constipation)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 40 minutes
Frequency of sessions: Once a day in the first week, twice a week from the second week onwards
Overall duration of treatment: 3 months""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """First week: Once a day
After first week: Twice a week
Duration: 3 months""" .

