Treatment group: 35
Control group: 35""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Baihui (DU20): Twisted with reinforcing method at small amplitude and high frequency.
Sishencong (EX HN1): Inserted until soreness and distending sensation were felt.
Neiguan (PC6) and Shenmen (HT7): Punctured until numbness and distending sensations were felt; no further manipulation.
Needles retained for 30 minutes with one manipulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper describes symptoms and criteria for TCM diagnosis but does not explicitly state a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Insomnia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "Results: according to the symptom scores, the total effective rate was 97.14 and 94.28% in the treatment and control groups, respectively; according to the Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index (PSQI) deduction rate, the total effective rate of the treatment group and the control group was 94.28 and 91.42%, respectively; in comparison, the treatment group was more effective in improving sleep quality than the control group (P< 0.05)."
Conclusion: Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Total effective rate based onSymptomScores
PittsburghSleep Quality Index (PSQI) deduction rate
Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles retained in place: 30 minutes
Frequency: Once a day, 6 times a week
Total treatment duration: 4 weeks""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Patients were treated with acupuncture once a day and 6 times a week for a total of 4 weeks, with an intermittent rest for one day." .

