Combined acupuncture and auricular point sticking was significantly more effective than acupuncture alone (P<0.01) and the herbal formula group (P<0.05).
The combined intervention was effective compared to the control/sham groups: Yes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Total effective rate
Secondary outcome measures: Relapse rate, factors contributing to good recovery (fast needlingSensation, younger age,Shorter duration), alleviation of anxiety and depression""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Combined acupuncture and auricular point sticking was performed once every other day, with 7 sessions constituting a course of treatment." .

