tara-kb:S-112625-1497 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1497" ;
    dc:title "Clinical Observation of the Treatment of 87 Cases of Insomnia with Acupuncture to Regulate the Yingiao and Yanggiao Channels" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Main points along the Yinqiao channel: KI6, KI8, KI1
Main points along the Yangqiao channel: UB62, UB61, UB59, LI15, GB20
Auxiliary points:
For palpitations or upset: UB15, UB44, PC6
For stomachache, poor appetite, and fullness: ST36, UB20, UB21
For headache: DU20, DU24, ST8
Acupoint prescriptions: Paired points from both channels (e.g., KI6 with UB62, KI8 with UB61)
Manipulation:
Depth for Yinqiao channel: 0.3 0.5 cun
Depth for Yangqiao channel: 0.5 1 cun
Techniques: Reinforcing on inspiration, reducing on expiration; needles inserted perpendicularly and twirled or rotated gently""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Not specified (the study design is a controlled trial, but whether it is randomized or not is not explicitly stated)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 45 cases treated with Klonopin, with a dosage of 2 mg one hour before sleep every night in the first week, adjusted according to therapeutic effect and side effects." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
