Secondary outcome measure: ADL (Activities of Daily Living) scores""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: around 30 minutes to 1 hour
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "3 times/week for 4 weeks; every other day for 4 weeks; each session lasted around 30 min to Ih" .

tara-kb:S-112625-1529 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1529" ;
    dc:title "Effect of \"Phased Whole Acupuncture Therapy\" on Ability of Daily Life in 63 Cases of Cerebral Infarction induced Hemiplegia" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not mention specific needle locations or related acupoints)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 50 patients who were treated with traditional acupuncture. This group was used for comparison with the treatment group to evaluate the effectiveness of phased whole acupuncture." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0001170,
        MONDO:0002679 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1529 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1529 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 113
Treatment group: 63
Control group: 50""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide details on how the needles were stimulated or if any specific sensations were sought)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a specific TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cerebral infarction induced hemiplegia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"Patients in the treatment group obtained satisfactory therapeutic effects in ADL improvement and in lowering of deformed rate, which were superior to those in the control group."
"The phased whole acupuncture is an effective therapy in treating cerebral infarction induced hemiplegia, which can better improve the life quality of the patients."
"After the treatment, the BI scores in both groups were significantly elevated (P<0.01), but the elevation in the treatment group was obviously higher than that in the control group with significant difference (P<0.01), indicating that the 'phased whole acupuncture' was superior to the traditional acupuncture in elevating ADL."
"After the treatment significant difference was found (P<0.05), indicating that the 'phased whole acupuncture' was superior to the traditional acupuncture in lowering the deformed rate."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Improvement in the ability of daily life (ADL) as assessed by the Barthel Index (BI)Scoring method.
Secondary outcome measure: Lowering of the deformed rate, evaluated using BIScores.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide details on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of acupuncture treatments)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-153 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-153" ;
    dc:title "Effects of motion style acupuncture treatment in acute low back pain patients with severe disability: A multicenter, randomized, controlled, comparative effectiveness trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Pungbu (GV16), Haenggan (LR2), Gokji (LI11)
Selected based on traditional Chinese medicine theory (qi circulation) and previous clinical experience.
Location determined using World Health Organization guidelines.
Needles inserted to a depth of 10 to 15 mm.
Occasional manual stimulation at GV16.""" ;
