    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Ear Shenmen" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003470,
        MONDO:0005098 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1539 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1539 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 16
Real acupuncture group: 10
Sham acupuncture group: 6""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure involved identifying points with a Fluke Ohm meter.
Points for sham treatments were not traditional acupuncture points but areas of normal electrical resistance.
Sham procedure was likely non penetrating or involved minimal penetration to mimic real acupuncture without actual therapeutic effect.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Low frequency electrical stimulation (1 2 Hz) was used on the needles on selected points. No other types of stimulation were mentioned. No information on sought sensations is provided." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Post stroke paralysis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcome(s). The results indicated that significantly more patients had a good response following real acupuncture than sham acupuncture, with a p value of less than 0.013. The effectiveness was highly dependent on the CT scan lesion site, with lesions in less than half of the motor pathway areas showing a positive response." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome measure: Boston Motor Inventory test assessing isolated active range of motion for leg and arm movements.Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment period: Five days per week for four weeks
Duration needles were left in place: Twenty minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: Five days per week
Duration: Twenty minutes per session
Total treatments: Twenty""" .

tara-kb:S-112625-154 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-154" ;
    dc:title "Teasing apart quality and validity in systematic reviews: an example from acupuncture trials in chronic neck and back pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Traditional acupuncture points: Used in trials by Lundeberg et al. (1991), Kreczi and Klingler (1986), Petrie and Hazleman (1986), Lehmann et al. (1986), and Coan et al. (1980, 1981).
Non-traditional acupuncture points: Used in trials by Duplan et al. (1983), Garvey et al. (1989), Gunn et al. (1980), and Lopacz and Gralewski (1979).
Specific acupoints or areas: Not specified.
Criteria for choosing points: Not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham acupuncture
Sham TENS
Local anaesthetic spray and acupressure
Standard clinic therapy alone
Delayed treatment control group""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003418,
        HP:0030833 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-154 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-154 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 537 patients
Acupuncture group: 281 patients
Placebo group: 256 patients""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Duplan et al. (1983): Sham acupuncture on non-traditional points.
Garvey et al. (1989): Local anaesthetic spray and acupressure.
Lundeberg et al. (1991): Sham acupuncture (details not specified).
Mendelson et al. (1983): Sham acupuncture (details not specified).
Edelist et al. (1976): Sham acupuncture with randomly placed needles at non-acupuncture sites.
Petrie and Hazleman (1986): Sham TENS.
Lehmann et al. (1986): Sham TENS.
Gunn et al. (1980): No sham acupuncture details provided.
Lopacz and Gralewski (1979): No sham acupuncture details provided.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electro-acupuncture was used in some trials (e.g., Edelist et al., 1976; Lehmann et al., 1986).
Laser acupuncture was used in some trials (e.g., Kreczi and Klingler, 1986).
The paper does not specify the exact method of stimulation for each trial, but it does mention the use of electrical stimulation and laser acupuncture in some trials.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide TCM terminology for the conditions)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic back and neck pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Pain intensity, pain relief, global measures of treatment efficacy
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Petrie and Hazleman (1986): 20 minutes per session, 8 sessions over 4 weeks
Garvey et al. (1989): Not specified
Coan et al. (1980 and 1981): Not specified
Duplan et al. (1983): 20 minutes per session, 5 daily sessions over 5 days
Edelist et al. (1976): 30 minutes per session, 3 sessions over 6 days
Gallacchi et al. (1981): 10 minutes per session, 9 sessions over an unspecified period
Lundeberg et al. (1991): 40 minutes per session, single session
Lopacz and Gralewski (1979): 10 minutes per session, 4 sessions over an unspecified period
Mendelson et al. (1983): 30 minutes per session, multiple sessions over 4 weeks""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Petrie and Hazleman (1986): Twice weekly for 20 minutes over 4 weeks
Lundeberg et al. (1991): Single session of 40 minutes
Coan et al. (1980): Minimum 10 sessions, frequency not specified
Coan et al. (1981): Minimum 10 sessions, three to four times a week
Duplan et al. (1983): Five daily sessions, each lasting 20 minutes
Gallacchi et al. (1981): Nine sessions, twice weekly for 10 minutes
Mendelson et al. (1983): Twice weekly for 30 minutes over 4 weeks
Garvey et al. (1989): Single session, duration not specified""" .

