tara-kb:S-112625-1541 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1541" ;
    dc:title "Treatment of Apoplectic Movement Dysfunctions of Wrist and Ankle Joints with Local Penetrating Needling" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Local points: Yangxi (LI 5), Yangchi (SJ 4), Shenmen (HT 7), Daling (PC 6), Qiuxu (GB 40)
Auxiliary points:
Wind phlegm blocking the veins: Fengchi (GB 20), Yinlingquan (SP 9), Fenglong (ST 40)
Hyperactive liver yang: Taichong (LV 3), Taixi (KI 3), Yanglingquan (GB 34)
Phlegm heat and fu organ deficiency: Tianshu (ST 25), Fenglong (ST 40), Shangjuxu (ST 37)
Blood stasis due to qi deficiency: Qihai (RN 5), Zusanli (ST 36), Xuehai (SP 10)
Wind stirring due to yin deficiency: Taichong (LV 3), Taixi (KI 3), Ganshu (UB 18), Shenshu (UB 23)
Needle locations:
Outside Shenmen (HT 7): ulnar end of the transverse crease of the wrist, in the depression on the radial side of the tendon of the muscle flexor carpi ulnaris
Manipulation: Needles sized 30 32, 1.5 2 cun deep, punctured perpendicularly""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 20 cases who received non penetrating needling. The group was divided based on syndrome differentiation: 7 cases of wind phlegm blocking the veins, 4 cases of hyperactive liver yang, 2 cases of phlegm heat and fu organ deficiency, 5 cases of blood stasis due to qi deficiency, and 2 cases of wind stirring due to yin deficiency. The youngest was 44 years old and the oldest was 78 years old; their disease courses ranged from 2 weeks to 3 years." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "HT 7, PC 6, SJ 4, GB 40, LI 5, GB 20, SP 9, ST 40, LV 3, KI 3, GB 34, ST 25, ST 37, RN 5, ST 36, SP 10, UB 18, UB 23" ;
