    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 46
Treatment group: 26
Control group: 20""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not provide specific details on the sham procedure)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation: Needles were twisted slowly and equally for one minute after puncture. Reinforcement and reduction methods were used. Needles were rotated every 10 minutes to retain the \"qi sensation.\"" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Hemiplegia caused by the obstruction of qi and blood, with syndromes including wind and phlegm blocking the veins, hyperactive liver yang, phlegm heat and fu organ deficiency, blood stasis due to qi deficiency, and wind stirring due to yin deficiency." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Stroke (cerebral infarction at the right basal nuclei and corona radiata)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The therapeutic effects of the local penetrating needling group was better than those of the nonpenetrating needling group in dorsiflexion, palmar flexion, radial flexion and ulnar flexion of the wrist and dorsiflexion and metatarsal flexion of the ankle joint (P<0.05)."
"The therapeutic effect of local penetrating needling is better than that of non penetrating needling."
"Therapeutic effects were observed after several effective courses of treatment. Tables 2 3 4 5 6 7 shows that the curative effects of the treatment group were better than those of the control group to treat wrist and ankle joint dysfunction in stroke patients (P<0.05) The differences between the two groups were significant."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Improvements in range of motion (ROM) for dorsiflexion,Palmar flexion, radial flexion, ulnar flexion of the wrist, and dorsiflexion and metatarsal flexion of the ankle.
Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles retained for: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The patients were treated once daily, with each treatment course lasting 5 days, followed by a 2 day rest period. The total treatment duration was 6 courses." .

tara-kb:S-112625-1542 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1542" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture Medication Versus Medication Alone in Lowering Intracranial Pressure in Apoplectic Patients" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Renzhong (DU 26), Fengfu (DU 16), Fengchi (GB 20), Zhongchong (PC 9), Taichong (LR 3)
Hegu (LI 11). Used bilaterally.
Manipulation: lifting and thrusting, retained for 30 minutes, repeated every 10 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 21 cases, with 13 males and 8 females, aged 46 77 years, and a disease duration of 1.5 to 6 days. They received 20% mannitol 250 ml intravenously by drip, completed within 40 minutes, with a total infusion volume not exceeding 2500 ml per day, and were observed for 10 days." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "DU 26, DU 16, GB 20, PC 9, LR 3, LI 11" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0829128,
        TARA:2324295,
        TARA:3361967,
        TARA:5138859,
        TARA:6499349,
        TARA:8923096 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0829128\": \"GV 26\", \"TARA:3361967\": \"GV 16\", \"TARA:2324295\": \"GB 20\", \"TARA:5138859\": \"PC 9\", \"TARA:6499349\": \"LR 3\", \"TARA:8923096\": \"LI 11\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1542 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1542 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 60
Control group: 21
Observation group: 39""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation by lifting and thrusting the needles, repeated every 10 minutes for 30 minutes. No specific sensation was mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a specific TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cerebral apoplexy with acute increase of intracranial pressure" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The observation group (acupuncture plus medication) had a higher effective rate (92.31%) compared to the control group (medication alone) at 71.43%.
Statistical analysis showed significant differences between the groups (P < 0.05), indicating that acupuncture enhanced the effect of medication.
The paper provides specific p values for various outcomes, such as CSF pressure and intraocular pressure, showing significant improvements in both groups but with more pronounced effects in the observation group.
The clarity of optic papilla and blood pressure were improved more in the observation group than in the control (P < 0.01).
Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: CerebralSpinalPressure, clarity of opticPapilla
Secondary outcome measures:Symptoms andPhysicalSigns,SystolicPressure""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Frequency of sessions: Twice a day
Total treatment duration: 10 days""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice a day for 10 days, with each session lasting 30 minutes and manipulation repeated every 10 minutes." .

