    dc:title "Clinical observation on acupuncture therapy for cerebral hemorrhage" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Tongli (H 5) for aphasia.
Neiguen (P 6) and Xuehai (Sp 10) for tachycardia with ecchymonic purplish tongue.
Yinlingquan (Sp 9) and Pencong (42M), pelvic Plexuses, an extra point near Zhibian (UB 54) for disorders of defecation and urination.
Jiansanzhen points, Quchi (LI 11), Waiguan (SJ 5), Hegu (LI 4) for paralysis of the upper extremity.
Huan 10 tiao (GB 30), Zhibian (UB 54), Fengshi (GB 31), Yanglingquan (GB 34), Sanyinjiao (Sp 6) for paralysis of the lower extremity.
Fengfu and Yamen were exempt from puncture.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the study design)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received the same acupuncture treatment as the treatment group, with the exception of excluding Fengfu and Yamen points. Both groups received routine emergency care during the acute phase, and after stabilization, they received only acupuncture." ;
