tara-kb:S-112625-1547 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1547" ;
    dc:title "Effects of the Lifting Manipulation of Scalp Acupuncture for Raising Myodynamia of the Affected Limbs in Hemiplegic Patients Due to Cerebral Thrombosis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Area needled: The patient's head of the affected side, i.e., the opposite side of the hemiplegic limbs.
Lines selected: The middle vertex line (Ding Zhong Xian J√©itf 2) and the anterior oblique vertex temporal line (Dingnieqian Xiexian Jiii fi).
Specific acupoint: Xuanli (GB 6), upper 2/3 section.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was treated with scalp acupuncture using the twirling manipulation. This group is referred to as \"Group A\" in the paper. The treatment specifics for Group A include: posture supine position; area needled the patient's head of the affected side; lines selected the middle vertex line and the anterior oblique vertex temporal line; needles used No.30 32 stainless filiform needles; manipulation twirling manipulation to induce a needling sensation; retaining of the needle retained for 2 hours with no further manipulation; course of treatment once every other day, three times a week, 12 treatments constituting a therapeutic course." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GB 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0316650 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0316650\": \"GB 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0001170 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "25mm (1 cun)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1547 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1547 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 180
Group A (control): 60
Group B (treatment): 120""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not include a sham acupuncture group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Group A: Twirling manipulation to induce a needling sensation.
Group B: Lifting manipulation with swift lifting and slow insertion of the needle.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Hemiplegia due to cerebral thrombosis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "Both groups showed increased myodynamia, but with different cured and much relieved rates (86.67% in the treatment group and 5% in the control group, P<0.01)."
The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group: Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Improvement of myodynamia and comprehensive functions after the treatment.
Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Not specified
Duration needles were left in place: 2 hours""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was given once every other day, three times a week, with 12 treatments constituting a therapeutic course. Each treatment session lasted 2 hours with manipulations repeated every 30 minutes." .

