    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1565" ;
    dc:title "Observation on Acupuncture Treatment of Ischemic Apoplexy by Nourishing the Kidney and Regulating the Du Channel" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Treatment Group:
Main Points: Shenshu (BL 23), Fengfu (GV 16), Jinsuo (GV 8), Taixi (KI 3), Mingmen (GV 4), Dazhui (GV 14)
Adjunct Points: Waiguan (TE 5) or Hegu (LI 4) for upper limb, Fenglong (ST 40) or Guangming (GB 37) for lower limb
Control Group:
Points: Jianyu (LI 15), Quchi (LI 11), Shousanli (LI 10), Waiguan (TE 5), Hegu (LI 4), Huantiao (GB 30), Yanglingquan (GB 34), Zusanli (ST 36), Jiexi (ST 41), Kunlun (BL 60)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control group: Treated using an "ordinary method" based on points selected from a textbook for medical students for hemiparalysis caused by apoplexy.
Points used: Jianyu (LI 15), Quchi (LI 11), Shousanli (LI 10), Waiguan (TE 5), Hegu (LI 4), Huantiao (GB 30), Yanglingquan (GB 34), Zusanli (ST 36), Jiexi (ST 41), Kunlun (BL 60), excluding kidney and Du channel points.
Treatment duration: Once a day for 30 days.""" ;
