tara-kb:S-112625-1566 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1566" ;
    dc:title "Bilateral Alternating Point Penetration Method for 25 Cases of Ischemic Stroke Hemiplegia" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Treatment Group:
Upper limbs: Jianyu (L115) to Jiquan (HT1), Quchi (LI11) to Shaohai (HT3), Waiguan (SJ5) to Neiguan (PC6), Hegu (LI4) to Houxi (S13)
Lower limbs: Yanglingquan (GB34) to Yinlingquan (SP9), Xuanzhong (GB39) to Sanyinjiao (SP6), Kunlun (BL60) to Taixi (KI3), Taichong (LR3) to Yongquan (KI1)
Face: Shangguan (GB3) to Xiaguan (ST7), Dicang (ST4) to Jiache (ST6)
Dysphasia: Yamen (DUIS) to Shegeng (EX), Tongli (HT5) to Shenmen (HT7)
Control Group:
Upper limbs: Jianyu (L115), Quchi (LI11), Shousanli (L110), Waiguan (SJ5), Hegu (LI4)
Lower limbs: Huantiao (GB30), Yanglingquan (GB34), Zusanli (ST36), Jiexi (ST41), Kunlun (BL60)
Face: Dicang (ST4), Jiache (ST6)
Dysphasia: Yamen (DU15), Lianquan (RN23), Tongli (HTS)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control group: Routine acupuncture group
Acupoint selection: Based on therapeutic principles
Acupoints for upper limbs: Jianyu (L115), Quchi (LI11), Shousanli (L110), Waiguan (SJ5), Hegu (LI4)
Acupoints for lower limbs: Huantiao (GB30), Yanglingquan (GB34), Zusanli (ST36), Jiexi (ST41), Kunlun (BL60)
Acupoints for facial paralysis and distortion: Dicang (ST4), Jiache (ST6)
Acupoints for dysphasia: Yamen (DU15), Lianquan (RN23), Tongli (HTS)
Operation method: Perpendicular acupuncture with 1~1.5 inch filiform needles
Manipulation: Fast insertion, slow twisting, lifting, and thrusting
Retention time: 30 minutes with twisting every 10 minutes
Treatment frequency: Once a day for a defined course of treatment""" ;
