Study group: 34
Control group: 29""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group or procedure described)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The needles were stimulated using electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) with a G6805 II multipurpose health device. The stimulation involved a dense disperse wave with frequencies of 4Hz and 20Hz, an output voltage of 100v, and intensity adjusted to the patient's maximal tolerance. The needling sensation was directed to specific areas such as the kidney and lower abdomen." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "lumbago (yao tong), haematuria (xue niao), stone urine (siti lin)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Urinary calculi (kidney and ureter stones)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes of cure rates for renal and ureteral calculi, with statistical significance (p<0.05)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Cured rates for renal and ureteral calculi (45.4% and 91.6%, respectively)
Disappearance of clinicalSymptoms;Stones are discharged; X ray and abdominal ultrasound tests are negative
Secondary outcome measures:
ClinicalSymptoms are controlled;Stones move or break up; hydronephrosis disappears
Improvement inSymptomsSuch asPain and lassitude
Breaking ofStones intoSmallerPieces for easier discharge""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified (electrical stimulation lasted for 50 minutes)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Treatment was given once daily, with 6 treatments constituting one course and a one day break between courses. Alternatively, 10 sessions per course without breaks if no undue fatigue or pain. Each treatment lasted 20 minutes." .

