    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1584" ;
    dc:title "Clinical Observation on the Acupuncture Treatment in Patients with Urinary Retention after Radical Hysterectomy" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Zusanli (ST36): Needles inserted vertically with Deqi, manipulated every 5 minutes, retained for 30 minutes.
Sanyinjiao (SP6): Electroacupuncture.
Shuidao (ST28): Electroacupuncture.
Shenque (CV8): Warming moxibustion.
Scalp Reproduction Area: Acupuncture.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received acupoint injection with vitamin B, targeting Sanyinjiao and Zusanli points, with injections alternating between sides. Both groups also received usual care and bladder function exercises." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "ST 36, SP 6, ST 28, CV 8, Scalp Reproduction Area" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:4385250,
        TARA:5017471,
        TARA:6463344,
        TARA:9392275 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\", \"TARA:5017471\": \"ST 28\", \"TARA:9392275\": \"CV 8\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Scalp Reproduction Area" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0000016 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1584 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1584 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 80
Treatment group: 40
Control group: 40""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Needles at Zusanli (ST36) were inserted vertically with Deqi and manipulated every 5 minutes (manual stimulation).
Electroacupuncture was used on Sanyinjiao (SP6), Shuidao (ST28), and Scalp Reproduction Area (electrical stimulation).
Moxibustion was applied on Shenque (CV8) (thermal stimulation).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Urinary retention after radical hysterectomy (implied as related to TCM concepts of bladder function and urinary system health)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Urinary retention after radical hysterectomy" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"Within 1 course and 2 courses of treatment, the patients with bladder function recovery in the treatment group were 21 (21/40) and 36 (36/40), and those in the control group were 12 (12/40) and 29 (29/40), both with a significant difference (P<0.05)."
"After the first course and second course, residual urine volume for those who had voluntary micturition more than 200 mL in the treatment group was 91.7+17.5 mL and 93.5+ 15.5 mL, in the control group 102.4 + 13.7 mL and 102.5+15.7 mL, both with a significant difference (P<0.05)."
"Conclusions: Combination of acupuncture modalities was better than acupoint injection for the recovery of bladder function in urinary retention after radical hysterectomy."
The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group: Yes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Recovery of bladder function, Residual urine volume for those who had voluntary micturition more than 200 mL
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles left in place during a session: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Daily for 5 days, followed by a 2-day rest period, repeated every 7 days." .

tara-kb:S-112625-1585 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1585" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture's Effects on Relieving Symptoms for Postradiation Cystitis and Prostatitis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Verum Acupuncture Group:
Standard points: CV 4, 9, 14, 17; Ki3, 6, 21; LI 4, 11; Lu5, 95 TBS; Ht6, 7; St36, 40; Sp3, 6, 9, 10; Gb34; Liv3
Individualized points based on TCM diagnosis
Sham Acupuncture Group:
Non penetrating sham needles at points not located on any acupuncture channel
Specific points for TCM patterns:
Warming and supplementing kidney qi: Tai Xi (KI 3), Shinning Sea (K1 6), Youmen Kid (K1 21), Taibai (Sp 3), Sanyinjiao (Sp 6), Yinlingquan (Sp 9), Xuehai (Sp 10), Guanyuan (CV 4), Shuifen (CV 9), Shanzhong (CV 17)
Transforming phlegm: Tai Bai (Sp 3), Feng Long (St 40), Juque Ren (Cv 14), Taiyan (Lu 9), Tai Chong (Liv 3)
Clearing heat: Hegu (L1 4, Quchi (LI 22), Zhaohai Kid (Ki 6), Yanglingquan (Gb 34), Waiguan (TB 5), Shuifen (Cv 9), Xuehai (Sp 10, Zusanli (St 36)
Emotional causes: Yinxi (Ht 6), Shenmen (Ht 7), Taichong (Liv 3), Sanyinjiao (Sp 6), Fenglong (St 40), Juque (Cv 14)
Enriching kidney essence: Tai Xi (Ki 3), Zhaohai Kid (Ki 6), Sanyinjiao (Sp 6), Guanyuan Ren (Cv 4)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was a wait list control arm that continued with their standard care until week 17 and then received verum acupuncture. They did not receive any specific intervention during the study period." ;
