tara-kb:S-112625-1588 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1588" ;
    dc:title "The efficacy of acupuncture as an aid to stopping smoking" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Lung point: in the concha of the external ear
Hunger point: on the tragus
Auricular 'placebo' points: close to the shoulder and eye acupoints on the pinna
Ankle 'placebo' points: superior to the medial malleolus
Hoku (large intestine 4): on the hand
Tongue point: on the car""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """"Placebo" auricular points group: Auricular 'placebo' points were situated close to the shoulder and the eye acupoints on the pinna.
"Placebo" points at the ankle: Placed bilaterally on each person, at a site superior to the medial malleolus and devoid of any known acupuncture points.
"Cut off studs" group: A control group in which the 2 mm spike of the press needle was removed, resulting in no penetration; the remainder of the stud was taped over the appropriate 'placebo' or 'effective' auricular acupuncture points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "New Zealand" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Lung point, Hunger point, large intestine 4" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Hunger point",
        "Lung point" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0008575 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1588 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1588 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants initially treated: 405
Total participants analyzed after drop outs: 278
Gender distribution: Females 231, Males 174
Sample sizes for each group at different follow up periods: Not specified (refer to table for specific numbers)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Press needles with the 2 mm spike removed (non penetrating)
Quantity: Not specified
Size: 2 mm spike removed
Location: Non penetrating, taped over "placebo" or "effective" auricular acupuncture points
Penetration: Non penetrating
Other details: Part of a single blind design, subjects unaware of placebo points, effect attributed to "magnetic inductance\"""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) using a Grass sD9 Stimulator with a square wave of 0.05 msec duration at 1 Hz, maintained at twice motor threshold for 20 minutes. No specific sensation was mentioned as being sought. Needles were not manually manipulated or stimulated with heat or laser." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition related to smoking cessation)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Smoking cessation (nicotine addiction)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No (the study found that acupuncture can help a small percentage of smokers stop smoking, but the effectiveness compared to a control group is not clearly established due to the lack of significant differences between \"effective\" and \"placebo\" groups)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure:Percentage ofSubjects whoStoppedSmoking at three weeks, three months, andSix months.
Secondary outcome measure: Reduction in daily cigarette consumption at three weeks, three months, andSix months.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of needles being left in place: Three weeks
Duration of each acupuncture session: Not specified (except for electroacupuncture at Hoku, which was 20 minutes)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide details on the frequency of repeated treatments beyond the initial placement and a single electroacupuncture session)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-1589 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1589" ;
    dc:title "Effects of Acupuncture on Smoking Cessation or Reduction for Motivated Smokers'" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Test Group Acupoints:
Body Electroacupuncture: Lieque, Kongzui
Ear Acupuncture: Shenmen, Mouth, Lung, Trachea, Hunger, Endocrine
Ear Acupressure: Shenmen, Mouth, Lung, Trachea, Hunger, Endocrine
Control Group Acupoints:
Body Electroacupuncture: Shousanli, Sanyanglui
Ear Acupuncture: Knees, Lumbar vertebra, Neck
Ear Acupressure: Knees, Lumbar vertebra, Neck, Shoulder, Buttock""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group (CG) received acupuncture treatment at points assumed to have no effect for smoking cessation, referred to as \"sham acupoints.\"" ;
