    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1589 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 46
Test Group (TG): 26
Control Group (CG): 20""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "The sham acupuncture group (control group, CG) received treatment at acupoints assumed to have no effect on smoking cessation. The procedure involved body electroacupuncture, ear acupuncture, and ear acupressure at specific sham acupoints listed in Table 2. The treatment was similar in method to the test group but differed in the location of the acupoints. Real needles were used at these non-effective points." ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) with a sinus wave of 3 Hz frequency and amplitude of 170-200 V. Needles were also manually rotated every 5 minutes. No thermal or laser stimulation was mentioned. Acupressure involved non-invasive plant seeds." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Smoking addiction or nicotine dependence" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcome of reducing daily cigarette consumption and increasing smoking cessation rates." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: self-reported reduction in daily cigarette consumption, changes in serum/plasma concentrations of cotinine, thiocyanate, fibrinogen, and TBARS.
Secondary outcome measures: changes in taste of tobacco, desire to smoke.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes
Overall treatment period: 3 weeks, with sessions twice a week""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for 3 weeks, with each treatment lasting 20 minutes." .

