    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details about needle locations or related acupoints)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT) with a crossover design" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Not applicable (the study used a crossover design with different montages, but no traditional control group was included)" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States (specifically Utah)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "2-4 cm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-161 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-161 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total sample size: 72; Sample size within each group: 72" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham group or sham procedure was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) using a low-output battery-powered generator with specific parameters: 37 mA amplitude, asymmetric biphasic waveform, 0.7 ms pulse width, and continuous duty cycle. The intensity was adjusted to produce a maximal tolerable \"tapping\" sensation without muscle contractions." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the condition in terms of Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Low back pain (LBP)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Results: All four montages produced significant improvements in pain (42%-64%), physical activity (35%-51%), and quality of sleep (28%-46%). Montage II was significantly more effective than the standard and other montages.
Conclusion: The pattern of electrical stimulation influences PNT effects. Montage II was most effective.
Effectiveness: Yes (compared to other montages, not a control/sham group)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Acute analgesic response to PNT (assessed using VAS scores for pain)
Secondary outcome measures:
Improvements in physical activity (assessed using VAS scores)
Improvements in quality of sleep (assessed using VAS scores)
Reduction in daily oral analgesic usage
Health-related quality of life (assessed using SF-36 questionnaire)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place during a session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was three times per week, with each session lasting 30 minutes, conducted on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday afternoons for two consecutive weeks, followed by a one-week \"washout\" period between each modality." .

