    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1610 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 52
Combination treatment group: 22
TCA control group: 14
EA control group: 16""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual manipulation: Needles were twirled to evoke the "arrival of Qi" (soreness, numbness, tingling, tension, or heaviness).
Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture): Needles were attached to an electrical stimulator for 60 minutes, with intensity adjusted to prevent pain.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Infertility" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"All 3 acupuncture methods increased the success rate for IVF. There was a marked increase with the combination of TCA and EA (81.8% success twice the US average for IVF alone) (P < .01). The success rates for the control groups TCA and EA were 64.3% and 62.5%, respectively (P > .05)."
"The combination of TCA plus EA produced a higher success rate for IVF than either approach alone."
"The comparison of the combination group with the 2 control groups, by w 2 test yielded P < .01, a statistically significant difference."
"The success rate of the combination treatment group was 19.3% higher than the first control group, EA alone."
"The combination method, however, captures EA's ability to increase uterine arterial blood flow and TCA's ability to treat multiple conditions simultaneously."
"Thus, the combination of TCA plus EA produced a higher success rate for IVF than either approach alone."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome measure: Comparisons of IVF effectiveness rates for each method (success rates of IVF for each treatment group).Secondary outcome measure: NotSpecified." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 60 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 60 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly; minimum of 12 treatments; some patients received more than 13 treatments; each session lasted 60 minutes (30 minutes EA + 30 minutes TCA for combination group)." .

