tara-kb:S-112625-1624 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1624" ;
    dc:title "A randomized, controlled pilot study of acupuncture treatment for menopausal hot flashes" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """TCM Acupuncture: CV-4, KI-3, SP-6, BL-23, HT-6, KI-7 (standard points); additional points based on specific locations relative to GB-34, BL channels, navel, metacarpal-phalangeal joint, and toe web space.
Sham Acupuncture: Non-acupuncture point sites needled shallowly on both sides of the body.
Diagnostic categories and associated points: Not specified (summarized in Table 1).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT), Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Usual care (n = 19): Participants did not receive any new treatments for hot flashes but could continue with existing nonpharmacologic treatments.
Sham acupuncture (n = 18): Participants received shallow needling at nontherapeutic sites.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "CV 4, KI 3, SP 6, BL 23, HT 6, KI 7" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0992296,
        TARA:4362146,
        TARA:4385250,
        TARA:6421594,
        TARA:9881298,
        TARA:9921528 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:9921528\": \"CV 4\", \"TARA:4362146\": \"KI 3\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\", \"TARA:0992296\": \"BL 23\", \"TARA:6421594\": \"HT 6\", \"TARA:9881298\": \"KI 7\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0031217 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "0.5 to 3 cm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1624 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1624 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 56
Usual care group: 19
Sham acupuncture group: 18
Traditional Chinese Medicine acupuncture group: 19""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles (sterile, single-use, Vinco 34-gauge and 30-gauge)
Quantity: 12 needles (6 on each side of the body)
Size: 1-inch (0.22 √Ç 25 mm) and 1.5-inch (0.30 √Ç 40 mm)
Location: Nontherapeutic sites (not on traditional acupuncture points)
Penetration: Shallow needling (0.5 to 3 cm depth)
Other details: Did not attempt to elicit the de Qi sensation; sites chosen to have minimal effects on hot flashes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """For Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) acupuncture: Needles were stimulated to achieve a de Qi sensation.
For Sham acupuncture: Needles were inserted shallowly without attempting to elicit the de Qi sensation.
No other types of stimulation (e.g., manual manipulation, electrical stimulation, thermal stimulation) were mentioned.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Kidney yin deficiency; kidney yin deficiency and kidney yang deficiency; kidney yin and liver yin deficiency leading to liver yang rising; kidney and heart not harmonized" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Hot flashes in peri- and postmenopausal women" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Decrease in hot flash frequency and severity as measured by the Daily Diary of Hot Flashes.
Secondary outcomes: Hot flash interference (Hot Flash Related Daily Interference Scale), sleep (Women`s Health Initiative Insomnia Rating Scale), symptoms bothersomeness (Menopause-specific Quality of Life Questionnaire), mood (Psychological General Well-Being Index), and general quality of life (Medical Outcomes Study 36-Item Short Form Health Survey).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment: 8 weeks, with 16 sessions
Duration of each session: Approximately 30 minutes
Needles left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for 8 consecutive weeks, with a total of 16 treatment sessions, each lasting approximately 30 minutes." .

tara-kb:S-112625-1625 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1625" ;
    dc:title "A Randomized Controlled Trial of Single Point Acupuncture in Primary Dysmenorrhea" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Sanyinjiao (SP6): Located on the inside of the ankle, junction point of liver, spleen, and kidney meridians.
Xuanzhong (GB39): Unrelated acupoint.
Nonacupoint location: Fibular side of lower leg, at midpoint between stomach and gallbladder meridians, 3 B-cun above tip of external malleolus, anterior to GB39.
Size of acupuncture points: About 2 cm in diameter.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control Group: Sham acupuncture control group
Description: Mothers received three auricular press needles at the shoulder, wrist, and extraneous auricular point, which are not known to reduce anxiety.
Randomization: Computer-generated random number table
Blinding: Research assistants evaluating outcomes were blinded to group assignment
Communication: Minimal and standardized communication with parents
Baseline Characteristics: Comparable between groups""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "SP 6, GB 39" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:3770332,
        TARA:4385250 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\", \"TARA:3770332\": \"GB 39\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:1060206 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "10-30 mm perpendicularly" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1625 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1625 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 67 pairs of mothers and children
Intervention group: Not specified
Control group: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Auricular press needles
Quantity: Three needles
Location: Shoulder, wrist, and extraneous auricular point (non-acupuncture points)
Penetrating: Yes
Other details: The sham procedure was designed to mimic the intervention without using recognized acupuncture points for anxiety reduction.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation was through the insertion of auricular press needles, with a pinching sensation noted. No additional stimulation methods were mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Primary dysmenorrhea" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"Multivariable analysis examining maternal anxiety as a function of group found a group-by-time interaction (F 1,65 ‚Ä´ÿç‚Ä¨ 4.1, P ‚Ä´ÿç‚Ä¨ 0.04). That is, after induction, maternal anxiety in the acupuncture group was significantly lower (42.9 ÿé 10 vs. 49.5 ÿé 11; P ‚Ä´ÿç‚Ä¨ 0.014)."
"A multivariate model (F 1,65 ‚Ä´ÿç‚Ä¨ 4.8, P ‚Ä´ÿç‚Ä¨ 0.031) also showed that children whose mothers received the acupuncture intervention were significantly less anxious on entrance to the operating room (34.9 ÿé 20 vs. 47.4 ÿé 26; P ‚Ä´ÿç‚Ä¨ 0.03) and during introduction of the anesthesia mask (38.6 ÿé 25 vs. 55. 6 ÿé 31; P ‚Ä´ÿç‚Ä¨ 0.016)."
"Auricular acupuncture significantly decreased maternal anxiety during the preoperative period."
"Children of mothers who underwent acupuncture intervention benefitted from the reduction of maternal anxiety during the induction of anesthesia."
"In conclusion, we found that maternal auricular acupuncture in combination with maternal presence during induction of anesthesia reduced children's anxiety and increased children's compliance with the induction process."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes:
Subjective pain as measured by a 100-mm visual analog scale (VAS)
Cox retrospective symptom scale (RSS-Cox)
0-to 7-point verbal rating scale (VRS)
Secondary outcomes:
VAS score for average pain
Pain total time
Additional in-bed time
Proportion of participants using analgesics during three menstrual cycles""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Not specified
Duration needles were left in place during a session: At least 30 minutes
Duration needles were retained: Up to 24 hours""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper describes a single intervention session without specifying frequency or duration beyond this session)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-1626 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1626" ;
    dc:title "A randomised-controlled trial in Sweden of acupuncture and care interventions for the relief of inflammatory symptoms of the breast during lactation" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """HT 3: Used for its effect on the circulation of the thorax region.
GB 21: Used for relaxation effect.
SP 6: Considered a key point for gynaecological problems and has an oxytocin-like effect.
Points were used bilaterally unless a De Qi sensation was felt.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Group 1: essential care and the use of oxytocin spray as deemed necessary by the midwife" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Sweden" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "HT 3, GB 21, SP 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:2385378,
        TARA:4385250,
        TARA:5389461 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:2385378\": \"HT 3\", \"TARA:5389461\": \"GB 21\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0006849 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "3-5 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1626 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1626 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 205 mothers with 210 cases
Participants within groups: 70 in each of the three treatment groups""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the study was not placebo-controlled and did not include a sham acupuncture group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The needles were stimulated by manual manipulation, specifically by rotating them clockwise to 180 degrees for 30 seconds if the De Qi sensation did not occur spontaneously. The goal was to achieve a De Qi sensation. No other forms of stimulation like electroacupuncture, moxibustion, or laser were mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Mastitis (inflammatory symptoms of the breast during lactation)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "The use of acupuncture did not influence the number of contact days needed with health-care services in order that inflammatory symptoms of the breast during lactation should subside. However, significantly more mothers in the non-acupuncture group had higher scores for severity of symptoms on days 3 and 4 of contact."
Effectiveness: Maybe/Inconclusive""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Comparison between treatment groups for proportion of mothers with lowest possible SI (0) on contact days 3, 4, and 5
Number of contact days with midwives at the breast feeding clinic until recovery
Proportion of mothers with less favourable outcomes (‚â•6 contact days)
Numbers of mothers prescribed antibiotics
Numbers of mothers who developed a breast abscess
SI scores and mothers' satisfaction with breast feeding on contact days 3, 4, and 5
Proportion of mothers who experienced residual symptoms requiring renewed contact with health-care services
Care interventions suggested by the midwife at first contact
Secondary outcome measures:
Amount of bacteria in the breast milk in relation to erythema, breast tension, severity of pain, and SI level at first contact
Type of bacteria in relation to favourable/less favourable outcomes
Care interventions suggested by the midwives at first contact in relation to favourable/less favourable outcomes
Relationship between the occurrence of residual symptoms and the use of antibiotics""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Up to 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Up to 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Most mothers (88%) received one acupuncture treatment. Some received repeated treatments (2-4 times). Treatments could be given daily if necessary, with each treatment lasting up to 30 minutes." .

