tara-kb:S-112625-1633 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1633" ;
    dc:title "A Comparative Study on the Acupoints of Specialty of Baihui, Shuigou and Shenmen in Treating Vascular Dementia*" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Conventional points for hemiplegia: Jianyu (LI15), Quchi (LIll), Waiguan (SJ5), Hegu (LI4), Xuehai (SP10), Zusanli (ST36), Sanyinjiao (SP6), Taichong (LR3)
Specific acupoints: DU20 (Baihui), DU26 (Shuigou), HT7 (Shenmen)
Needle insertion details:
DU20: Inserted backwardly 0.8-1 cun, tip at galea aponeurotica
DU26: Inserted obliquely upward 0.2-0.3 cun
HT7: Inserted perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 cun
Needle specifications: Disposable stainless needles, gauge 30, 1 to 1.5 cun in length""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Group A: Conventional acupuncture for hemiplegia (control group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 15, LI 11, SJ 5, LI 4, SP 10, ST 36, SP 6, LR 3, DU 20, DU 26, HT 7" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0829128,
        TARA:0859695,
        TARA:2442762,
        TARA:3386254,
        TARA:4385250,
        TARA:6463344,
        TARA:6499349,
        TARA:7829474,
        TARA:8393005,
        TARA:8433932,
        TARA:8923096 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:7829474\": \"LI 15\", \"TARA:8923096\": \"LI 11\", \"TARA:8393005\": \"TE 5\", \"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:8433932\": \"SP 10\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\", \"TARA:6499349\": \"LR 3\", \"TARA:3386254\": \"GV 20\", \"TARA:0829128\": \"GV 26\", \"TARA:2442762\": \"HT 7\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0004648 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Baihui (DU20): 0.8-1 cun
Shuigou (DU26): 0.2-0.3 cun
Shenmen (HT7): 0.3-0.5 cun""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1633 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1633 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 50
Participants within groups: 10 per group""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation (even manipulation, thrusting, inserting, and twirling evenly) was used to stimulate the needles after achieving \"qi.\" The needles were stimulated every 5 minutes during the 20-minute retention period." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Dementia syndrome, gentle dementia, amnesia, mental disorder" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Vascular dementia (VD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcome of HDS-R scores, with significant increases in groups treated with DU20, DU26, and HT7 (P<0.01, P<0.05).
The ADL scores did not show significant changes, indicating no substantial impact on daily living activities.
The FAQ scores decreased significantly in groups B and E, indicating an improvement in social adapting abilities (P<0.05).
The combination of the three acupoints improved intelligence and social adapting abilities.
Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Hasegawa's dementia scale-recension (HDS-R)
Activities of daily living (ADL)
Functional activities questionnaire (FAQ)
Secondary outcome measures:
Clinical symptoms and signs (assessed using a self-developed criteria)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Not specified
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The patients received acupuncture treatment once a day, except on weekends. The treatment course lasted for four weeks, with 20 treatments administered during this period." .

tara-kb:S-112625-1634 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1634" ;
    dc:title "A clinical trial of acupuncture about time-varying treatment and points selection in primary dysmenorrhea" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Shiqizhui (EX-B8): Single point used for groups A and B.
Sanyinjiao (SP6): Junction point of spleen, liver, and kidney meridians; promotes qi and blood flow.
Diji (SP8): Xi-cleft Point of the spleen channel; regulates channel-qi and relieves pain.
Ciliao (BL32): Selected based on clinical experience for treating dysmenorrhea.
Needle depth: 0.5-1 cm for single point, 1-1.5 cm for multi-points.
Patient positions: Pronated for single point, supine or pronated for multi-points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Group E (n=200, no treatment)" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
