    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Group A and C: Once a day, approximately 3 to 7 days before menstruation (typically 5 days).
Group B and D: Once a day, as soon as pain occurred, continuing for 3 days.
Treatment duration: Three consecutive menstrual cycles.""" .

tara-kb:S-112625-1635 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1635" ;
    dc:title "A Clinical Pilot Study Comparing Traditional Acupuncture to Combined Acupuncture for Treating Headache, Trigeminal Neuralgia and Retro-auricular Pain in Facial Palsy" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Obligatory points: Korean Five Element Acupuncture points
Optional individual points: Ah-Shi points (tender points), local points, distal points, energetic points
Ear points (Fossion's theory): Master point of the head, allodynia point, nausea-sickness point, antitragus point, central point, cervical pain-extension point, pulsatile point
Selection criteria: TCM diagnosis, tender points, symptom-specific points
Specific locations: Nausea-sickness point on the midpoint of the auditory line; cervical pain-extension point on the upper part of the master point of the head""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study was the traditional acupuncture (TA) group, consisting of 15 participants. This group was used as a control to compare the efficacy of combined acupuncture (CA) in treating headache, trigeminal neuralgia, and retro-auricular pain." ;
