    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cardiac disorders (coronary heart disease and acute myocardial ischemia)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the manual acupuncture and electromagnetic field stimulation were effective compared to the nonstimulation group in modulating the autonomic nervous system, as indicated by statistically significant changes in HRV parameters. Laser acupuncture had a different effect, activating the sympathetic nervous system." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome measures: Heart rate variability (HRV) including low frequency (LF), high frequency (HF), and LF/HF ratio. Secondary outcome measures: Not specified." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration of stimulation: 20 to 25 minutes
Length of needles retained: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of treatment beyond a single experimental session)" .

