tara-kb:S-112625-1654 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1654" ;
    dc:title "Observation on Therapeutic Effects of Acupuncture and Tuina in Treatment of Sprains and Strains of Minor Joints at Four Extremities" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Needle locations: Bony cleft of the injured metacarpophalangeal (metatarsophalangeal) joint
Depth of insertion: About 1 cun into the first metatarsophalangeal joint, about 0.5 cun into other metacarpophalangeal (metatarsophalangeal) joints
Number of needles: One or two needles inserted according to the condition of the injury""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Acupuncture group: 30 cases treated by acupuncture at the bony clefts
Tuina group: 30 cases treated by tuina therapy""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0012531 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """First metatarsophalangeal joint: 1 cun
Other metacarpophalangeal (metatarsophalangeal) joints: 0.5 cun""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1654 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1654 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 90
Observation group: 30
Acupuncture group: 30
Tuina group: 30""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation (lifting thrusting and twisting methods) after arrival of qi; needles manipulated once every 10 minutes during 30 minute retention." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Sprains and strains of minor joints at the four extremities (metacarpophalangeal/metatarsophalangeal joints)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The cure rates of the observation group, the acupuncture group and the tuina group reached 50.0%, 20.0% and 16.7% respectively, and the total effective rates reached 93.4%, 70.0% and 73.3% respectively."
"There were statistical significance between the observation group and the acupuncture and tuina groups (P<0.05); while there was not a statistical difference between the acupuncture group and the tuina group."
"It was indicated that the therapeutic effect of the observation group was better than that of the acupuncture group and the tuina group."
"Acupuncture at the bony clefts in combination with tuina therapy is quite effective in the treatment of sprains and strains of metacarpophalangeal (metatarsophalangeal) joints."
"The difference in the total effective rate was statistically significant (P<0.05) by the Chi square test."
"In comparison with the observation and acupuncture group, the difference of the cure rate was statistically significant (P<0.05) by the Chi square test."
"In comparison with the observation group and tuina group, the difference of the cure rate was statistically significant (P<0.01)."
"The total effective rate and the cure rate of the observation group were higher than acupuncture and tuina group."
"Acupuncture at the bony clefts and tuina can decrease the intra articular pressure, improve the microcirculation, favor the absorption of the inflammatory exudates, and possess the obvious function to relieve pain."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Cure rate, Total effective rate
Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes (needles retained for 30 minutes, manipulated once every 10 minutes)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "6 times a week for 2 courses of treatments; each session lasted 30 minutes with manipulation every 10 minutes" .

tara-kb:S-112625-1655 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1655" ;
    dc:title "Effects of acupuncture on oxidative stress mechanisms, pain, and quality of life in fibromyalgia: A prospective study from T√ºrkiye" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """CV 6: supportive effect on general fatigue and weakness
GV 20: effective on sleep disturbance, headache, and memory impairment
EX-HN 3: used for headaches, sleep disorders, and psychological problems; improves well-being
Pc 6 (bilaterally): used in treatment of sleep disorders, depression, dizziness, and upper extremity pain
H 7 (bilaterally): used in treatment of sleep disorders, depression, dizziness, and upper extremity pain
LI 4: important pain relief point; effects on digestive system disorders, headaches, and immune system
CV 17: junction of respiratory energy; used in anxiety
LIV 3: effective in sleep disorders, chronic constipation, and gastrointestinal problems
ST 36: for gastrointestinal problems, sleep disorders, lower extremity pain
SP 6: effective in immune system, sleep disturbance, pain, and numbness in lower extremity
SI 3: for neck-low back pain, wrist pain, and tinnitus
GB 34: used for knee, neck, shoulder pain, and headache""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received sham acupuncture treatment on Helix (HX) points, which are considered inactive points remote from the inner ear area. This was used to control for placebo effects and compare outcomes with the treatment group receiving active auricular acupuncture points." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Turkey" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
