tara-kb:S-112625-1665 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1665" ;
    dc:title "Special Topic Study Clinical Observation on Acupuncture for Migraine" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Major points: Baihui (GV 20), Hegu (LI 4), Taichong (LR 3)
Adjunct points: Zulinqi (GB 41), Fenglong (ST 40), Yinlingquan (SP 9), Xuehai (SP 10), Zusanli (ST 36)
Method: Retain the needle at Baihui (GV 20) after qi arrival. Perform 2 min lifting, thrusting and rotating at Hegu (LI 4), Taichong (LR 3) and other adjunct points and then retain for 10 min. Then re manipulation for 2 min and continue to retain the needles for 10 min.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was treated with oral Sibelium (Flunarizine Hydrochloride capsules), 10 mg once a day before going to bed, for 40 days." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the country where the study was conducted)" ;
