tara-kb:S-112625-1667 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1667" ;
    dc:title "Clinical Observation of Combined Acupuncture and Herbs in Treating Chronic Pelvic Inflammation" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Main acupoints: Zhongji (CV 3), Guanyuan (CV 4), Shuidao (ST 28), Guilai (ST 29), Dahe (KI 12), Qixue (KI 13)
Additional acupoints based on TCM diagnosis:
Dampness heat accumulation: Ligou (LR 5), Baihuanshu (BL 30), Yinlingquan (SP 9)
Qi blood stagnation: Zhongdu (LR 6), Xuehai (SP 10), Diji (SP 8)
Yin deficiency and blood stasis: Taixi (KI 3), Shenshu (BL 23), Fuliu (KI 7), Zusanli (ST 36), Zhongwan (CV 12), Sanyinjiao (SP 6)
Anatomical locations:
Zhongji (CV 3) and Guanyuan (CV 4): Crossing acupoints of Conception Vessel and three foot yin meridians
Shuidao (ST 28) and Guilai (ST 29): Acupoints of stomach meridian
Dahe (KI 12) and Qixue (KI 13): Crossing acupoints of kidney meridian and Thoroughfare Vessel""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 43 participants who were treated with Fu Ke Qian Jin Jiao Nang (Female Herbal Capsule), produced by Zhuzhou Qianjin Pharmaceutical Company Limited. The dosage was 0.4 g per capsule, taken two capsules at a time, three times a day, starting after the menstrual period ended. The treatment consisted of three courses, each lasting thirty days." ;
