    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1669 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 80
Scalp acupuncture group: 27
Body acupuncture group: 25
Control group: 28""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Scalp acupuncture: Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) using G6805 electric stimulator with sparse wave pattern.
Body acupuncture: Manual manipulation using even reinforcing reducing techniques.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Deficiency of the brain marrow" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Vascular dementia (VD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The total effective rate in the scalp acupuncture group was 92%, versus 89% in the body acupuncture group and 83% in the control group, showing a statistical significance (P<0.01).
After the treatments, the MMSE and BI scores showed significant differences in all three groups (P<0.01).
After the treatment, the MMSE and BI scores in the scalp acupuncture and body acupuncture groups showed statistical significances compared with the control group (P<0.05).
Conclusion: Scalp acupuncture based therapy can substantially improve MMSE and BI scores and thus obtain a more remarkable effect for vascular dementia.
Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Mini MentalState Examination (MMSE), Barthel Index (BI)
Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Once a day (except for Sunday), for 30 days" .

tara-kb:S-112625-167 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-167" ;
    dc:title "Effect of electroacupuncture on muscle state and infrared thermogram changes in patients with acute lumbar muscle sprain" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Houxi (SI 3): Inserted towards Hegu (LI 4) at a depth of 20 to 30 mm.
Jiaji (EX-B2): Three to five points chosen and stimulated.
Ashi points: Three to five points chosen and stimulated.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study is the medication group, which received diclofenac sodium as a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory analgesic drug." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "SI 3, EX-B2, Ashi" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0220496,
        TARA:3734471 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0220496\": \"SI 3\", \"TARA:3734471\": \"Huatuojiaji\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Ashi" ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "20-30 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-167 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-167 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 120
Sample size in EA group: 60
Sample size in medication group: 60""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used was electroacupuncture (EA) with an EA device providing continuous waves at a frequency of 10 to 25 Hz and a current intensity of 2 mA. Manual manipulation was also used with a mild reinforcing-reducing method. Local soreness and distention were sought as part of the needling sensation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Injuries of muscles and tendons" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Acute lumbar muscle sprain (soft tissue laceration)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The cure rate was 63.3% in the EA group and 53.3% in the medication group."
"The total efficacy in the EA group (93.3 %) was not significantly different from that in the medication group (86.6 % , P = 0.204)."
"After treatment, the mean FDV of the lumbar muscle significantly increased in both groups (P < 0.05 for both groups); the FDV increase in the EA group was significantly higher than in the medication group (P = 0.015)."
"The temperature index was also significantly increased in both groups (P < 0.05 for both groups); the infrared thermogram in the EA group indicated significantly greater recovery compared to the medication group (P = 0.026)."
"Both EA and diclofenac sodium markedly improved acute lumbar sprain, but EA better improved the rehabilitation and regeneration of FDVs and temperature index of infrared thermogram of the muscle."
"The results reflect only an immediate effect of EA, and the long-term effect needs to be further observed."
The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s): Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Force-displacement value (FDV) of muscle state, Temperature index of infrared thermogram
Secondary outcome measure: Curative effects based on traditional Chinese medicine criteria""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes
Total treatment duration: 7 days""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Daily for 7 days, with each session lasting 20 minutes." .

