tara-kb:S-112625-169 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-169" ;
    dc:title "Effect of a Traditional Chinese Medicine combined therapy on adolescent idiopathic scoliosis: a randomized controlled trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper describes acupotomology locations but not traditional acupuncture points)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study is the brace group (CG), where patients were treated with a Milwaukee brace for at least 22 hours every day, with adjustments and counseling as part of the treatment protocol." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005488 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-169 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-169 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 120
TCMG: 60 (initial), 58 (completed)
CG: 60 (initial), 49 (completed)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham group or sham procedure was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not mention needle stimulation or any form of stimulation)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Adolescent idiopathic scoliosis (AIS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The Cobb angle significantly decreased in both groups after 12 months of treatment compared with before treatment (P < 0.05)."
"The percentages of original Cobb angle in TCMG and CG were 51.4% and 47.8% (P > 0.05) after 12 months and 62.5% and 34.7% (P < 0.05) after 24 months, respectively."
"Pulmonary function significantly improved after 12 months in TCMG (P < 0.05) but significantly decreased in CG (P < 0.05)."
"The AEMG ratio was significantly lower (P < 0.01) and tended to remain at 1 after stopping treatment in TCMG, but increased in CG (P < 0.05)."
"TCM combined therapy can prevent the progression of scoliosis."
"The AEMG ratio is a promising index that could replace radiography in the evaluation of treatment effect and progression in scoliosis."
"TCM combined therapy can significantly decrease the Cobb angle, partially correct scoliosis, and can improve the muscle imbalances on either side of scoliosis."
"This therapy also showed good compliance and safety."
"Pulmonary function improved significantly in TCMG (P < 0.05, Table 3) after 12 months of treatment, while pulmonary function diminished in CG (P < 0.05) because of limitations caused by the brace to lung development."
"There was a significant reduction in AEMG ratio, which tended to remain at 1 in TCMG after 6, 12, 18, and 24 months of treatment (P < 0.05, Figure 2)."
"In contrast, the AEMG ratio significantly increased in CG (P < 0.05)."
"These results suggest that the imbalances in muscle tension from scoliosis improved with the combined therapy and tended to remain balanced even if treatment was stopped."
"The muscle imbalance in CG was aggravated, which could result in further development of scoliosis."
"No adverse reactions were found in either group."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Cobb angle
Secondary outcome measures: Pulmonary function, Average electromyogram (AEMG) ratio""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific information about the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Tuina: Twice a week for 12 months
Acupotomology: Once a week for ten treatments
Daoyin: Twice a day until skeletal maturity (duration not specified)
Milwaukee brace: At least 22 hours every day for 12 months""" .

