    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Hegu Large Intestine 4: Located in the middle of the first interosseous of hand, needle insertion depth of 1-2 cun.
Sanyinjiao Spleen 6: Located 3 cun above the medial malleoli, needle insertion depth of 1.5-2.5 cun.
Zhusanli Stomach 36: Located 3 cun above the tip of the medial malleolus on the medial border of the tibia, needle insertion depth of 1-2 cun.
Yanglingquan Gold Bladder 34: Located in the depression anterior and inferior to the head of the fibula, needle insertion depth of 1-2 cun.
Thaichong Liver 3: Located in the foot, between the first and second toe, needle insertion depth of 0.2-0.5 cun.
Neiguan Pericardium 6: Located on the palmar side of the forearm 2 cun above the transverse crease.
Shenmen Heart 7: Located on the outer side of the wrist, between the ulna and the pisiform bones.""" ;
