    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Prolonged pregnancy" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No, the acupuncture intervention was not effective compared to the control group in reducing the rate of labor induction for prolonged pregnancy. However, there was a trend for earlier delivery and a significant increase in the length of the second stage of labor in nulliparous women." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome: The rate of women submitted to labor induction for prolonged pregnancy at week 41 √æ 5.
Secondary outcomes: The rate of induction for other indications and the length of first and second stage of labor.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30-40 minutes" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Acupuncture sessions were administered every odd day from randomization until 41 weeks plus 4 days, with each session lasting 30-40 minutes." .

