tara-kb:S-112625-17 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-17" ;
    dc:title "Analgesic Effect of Electroacupuncture in Postthoracotomy Pain: A Prospective Randomized Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Hegu (LI 4): Dorsal aspect of the palm, midway between first and second metacarpal, midpoint of the lateral aspect of the second metacarpal. Therapeutic effects: Numbness and paralysis of upper limbs, cough, pain relief. Depth: 0.5‚Äì1 inches.
Yanglingquan (GB 34): Indentation of skin just below the head of fibula. Therapeutic effect: Shortness of breath. Depth: 1‚Äì1.5 inches.
Sanyangluo (TE 8): Dorsal aspect of forearm, midway between ulna and radius, 4 cm caudal to the proximal wrist crease. Therapeutic effect: Upper limbs pain relief. Depth: 0.5‚Äì1 inches.
Waiqiu (GB 36): 7 inches caudal to the lateral malleolus, along the anterior border of the fibula. Therapeutic effect: Chest wall pain relief. Depth: 0.3‚Äì0.5 inches.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study; Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture (SA) using a special blunt-tip needle and pseudostimulation from the electrostimulator as a placebo control." ;
