    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual manipulation: Needles were inserted with a twisting reducing and reinforcing technique.
Electroacupuncture (EA): Used at SP6, KI3, and GB34 with alternating frequencies of 50 and 100 Hz for 30 minutes.
Moxibustion: Used at CV8 Shenque for 30 minutes at night.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Secondary osteoporosis in patients with spinal cord injury (SCI)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Acupuncture significantly reduced TNFŒ± and IgM levels compared to the control group (p=0.028 for TNFŒ±, p=0.002 for IgM).
No significant change in IgG levels.
BMD increased more in the acupuncture group, but the difference was not statistically significant (p=0.253 and p=0.314 for L2-3 lumbar spine and intertrochanteric femur, respectively).
Acupuncture was effective in reducing TNFŒ± and IgM, but not in significantly improving BMD compared to the control group.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Concentrations of IgG, IgM, and TNFŒ± in serum; Bone mineral density (BMD) of the lumbar spine and intertrochanteric femur.
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration of electroacupuncture (EA) treatment: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The acupuncture treatments were administered every other day, with each course lasting 10 days followed by 2 days of rest, for a total of 10 courses. Each standard treatment session lasted 20 minutes, and electroacupuncture sessions lasted 30 minutes. Moxibustion was applied for 30 minutes at night." .

