    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation was achieved using a seed-embedding method with Wangbuliuxingzi seeds and hard beads fixed with adhesive to provide continual pressure at the auricular acupoints. No specific type of sensation was mentioned. No needles were used." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Hypertension" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The study found significant improvements in body pain (p = .03) and mental health (p = .002) aspects of QoL for patients with hypertension who received auricular acupressure compared to the control group.
There were no significant differences in HRV parameters, heart rate, blood pressure, or overall QoL between the experimental and control groups.
The intervention was effective in improving physical pain and mental health aspects of QoL but not in physiological benefits.
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Heart Rate Variability (HRV), Quality of Life (QoL)
Secondary outcomes: Heart rate, Blood pressure, High frequency (HF), Low frequency (LF), LF/HF ratio""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupressure session: 2 minutes per acupoint, 3 times a day
Total duration of the intervention: 10 weeks
Duration needles/beads left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Duration: 10 weeks
Frequency: 3 times per day, 2 minutes each time""" .

