    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Acupoint group: Received acupuncture at Sanyinjiao (SP6) specifically designed to treat primary dysmenorrhea.
Unrelated acupoint group: Received acupuncture at Xuanzhong (GB39), an unrelated acupoint.
Nonacupoint group: Received needle insertion at a nonacupoint location, serving as a sham acupuncture control.
No acupuncture group: Did not receive any acupuncture treatment, serving as a control group.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0004169,
        MONDO:1010182 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1722 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1722 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 200
Acupoint group: 50
Unrelated acupoint group: 50
Nonacupoint group: 46
No acupuncture group: 48""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham details: The sham procedures involved two types:
1. Unrelated acupoint: Needles were inserted at Xuanzhong (GB39), which is not typically used for treating primary dysmenorrhea.
2. Nonacupoint: Needles were inserted at nonacupoint locations (lateral side of lower leg, 3 inches above the tip of external malleolus, 1.5 inches behind anterior crest of the tibia).
Needle type: Real needles were used for all groups.
Quantity and size: Needles were 0.25 mm ¬• 40 mm.
Location: Sham procedures involved either unrelated acupoints or nonacupoint locations.
Penetrating or non penetrating: Penetrating.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation type: Electro acupuncture
Stimulation method: Bipolar stimulating electrodes with alternating frequency mode (2/100 Hz)
Sensation sought: "De Qi" (radiating feeling)
Duration of stimulation: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Liver depression and Qi stagnation; dysfunction of the Liver" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Premenstrual syndrome (PMS) and premenstrual dysphoric disorder (PMDD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, acupuncture was effective compared to the control group (no acupuncture) in reducing pain, but its effectiveness was similar to sham acupuncture, suggesting nonspecific effects." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcome Measures:
Rate of improvement (%)
End-of-treatment scores
Percentage of reduction in symptom scores
Secondary Outcome Measures:
Menstrual Distress Questionnaire (MDQ)
Menstrual Symptoms Severity List (MSSL)
Premenstrual Syndrome Diary (PMSD)
Daily Symptom Rating (DSR)
The Premenstrual Tension Syndrome Self-Rating Scale (PMTS)
Premenstrual Assessment Form (PAF)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Acupuncture and sham acupuncture were administered once daily for 3 days, with each session lasting 30 minutes." .

tara-kb:S-112625-1723 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1723" ;
    dc:title "Effect of Combined Acupuncture and Medication for Hypertension due to Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus and Plasma Neuropeptide Y" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Major points: Bilateral Taichong (LR 3) and Fengchi (GB 20)
Adjunct points:
For yin deficiency of the liver and kidney: Taixi (KI 3) and Sanyinjiao (SP 6)
For hyperactivity of liver yang: Quchi (LI 11) and Xingjian (LR 2)
For internal phlegm dampness: Fenglong (ST 40) and Zusanli (ST 36)
For blood stasis: Xuehai (SP 10)
Manipulation techniques:
Reducing manipulation: Taichong (LR 3), Fengchi (GB 20), Quchi (LI 11), Xingjian (LR 2), Fenglong (ST 40), Xuehai (SP 10)
Reinforcing manipulation: Taixi (KI 3)
Reinforcing reducing manipulation: Zusanli (ST 36), Sanyinjiao (SP 6)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 30 patients with hypertension due to type 2 diabetes, who received oral extended release nifedipine tablets alone. The group had 16 males and 14 females, with an average age of 58.0¬±6.0 years and a mean duration of 5.4¬±1.6 years." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
