tara-kb:S-112625-1727 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1727" ;
    dc:title "Efficacy of Acupuncture for Acute Migraine Attack: A Multicenter Single Blinded, Randomized Controlled Trialp me_1376 623..630" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Obligatory points: DU20 (Baihui), DU24 (Shenting), ST8 (Touwei), GB8 (Shuaigu), GB20 (Fengchi)
Additional points based on syndromes:
Shaoyang headache: SJ5 (Waiguan), GB34 (Yanglingquan)
Yangming headache: LI4 (Hegu), ST44 (Neiting)
Taiyang headache: BL60 (Kunlun), SI3 (Houxi)
Jueyin headache: LR3 (Taichong), GB40 (Qiuxu)
Nausea and vomiting: PC6 (Neiguan)
Dysphoria and susceptibility to rage: LR3
Needle insertion method:
DU20, DU24, ST8, GB8: Oblique then horizontal
Other points: Perpendicular
Sham points: Selected near elbow and knee joints, unrelated to headache treatment, randomly assigned to subgroups""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study was the sham acupuncture group. This group received acupuncture at points unrelated to headache, chosen to avoid therapeutic effects, and was used as a comparison to the verum acupuncture group." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "DU 20, DU 24, ST 8, GB 8, GB 20, SJ 5, GB 34, LI 4, ST 44, BL 60, SI 3, LR 3, GB 40, PC 6" ;
