tara-kb:S-112625-1731 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1731" ;
    dc:title "Effects of electroacupuncture on stress-related symptoms in medical students: a randomised placebo-controlled study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """ST36: 2 cm deep, manipulated to obtain contraction of the tibialis anterior muscle
PC6: 0.5 cm deep, inserted obliquely towards distal
GB14: Inserted subcutaneously 1 cm towards the midpoint of the eyebrow
Shenmen: Connected to GB14 on the left
Heart point: Connected to GB14 on the right
GV20: Needles inserted 0.5 cm under the scalp
Four Sishencong points: Directed caudally or rostrally and interconnected
Sham TENS: Same points on limbs (ST36 and PC6), GB14 bilaterally connected to the ipsilateral region of the neck under the mastoid process""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 34 students who did not receive any intervention (untreated control group)." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Brazil" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "ST 36, PC 6, GB 14, Ear Shenmen, Heart point, GV 20, Sishencong points" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:3386254,
        TARA:4311153,
        TARA:6463344,
        TARA:9987270 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\", \"TARA:9987270\": \"GB 14\", \"TARA:3386254\": \"GV 20\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Ear Shenmen",
        "Heart point",
        "Sishencong points" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0000716,
        MONDO:0011918,
        MONDO:0100081 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """ST36: 2 cm deep
PC6: 0.5 cm deep
GB14: subcutaneously 1 cm deep
GV20 and Sishencong points: 0.5 cm under the scalp""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1731 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1731 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 82
EA group: 30
Sham TENS group: 18
Control group: 34""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Sham TENS
Needle type: Non-penetrating (wired electrodes)
Quantity and size: Not specified
Location: Similar sites as real acupuncture points (ST36, PC6, GB14) but connected to different areas (e.g., neck under the mastoid process)
Penetrating or non-penetrating: Non-penetrating
Other details: Electrodes attached to skin with microporous medical tape, connected to an electrostimulation device emitting a beeping sound.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation in the study was electroacupuncture (EA), involving electrical stimulation at a continuous frequency of 2 Hz for 20 minutes. The needles were connected to an electrostimulator, and the amplitude was set to be comfortable for the patient. Some manual manipulation was used to obtain muscle contraction, but the primary stimulation was electrical. The stimulation was intended to be painless." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Stress-related symptoms (sleep disorders, anxiety, depression, burnout)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcome Measures:
Mini-Sleep Questionnaire (MSQ)
Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index (PSQI)
Epworth Sleepiness Scale (ESS)
Beck Depression Inventory (BDI)
Beck Anxiety Inventory (BAI)
Maslach Burnout Inventory-Student Survey (MBI-SS)
Quality of Life Questionnaire -abbreviated version (WHOQOL-bref)
Secondary Outcome Measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Once a week for 20 minutes, with 8 sessions planned (6 sessions in 2012 due to interruption)" .

