    dc:title "Effect of Electroacupuncture on Visceral and Hepatic Fat in Women with Abdominal Obesity: A Randomized Controlled Study Based on Magnetic Resonance Imaging" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Main acupoints: Huaroumen (ST-24), Tianshu (ST-25), Wailing (ST-26), Shuidao (ST-28), Fujie (SP-14), Daheng (SP-15), Zusanli (ST-36), Fenglong (ST-40)
Additional acupoints: Guanyuan (RN-4), Shuifen (RN-9), Yanglingquan (GB-34), Neiting (ST-44), Zhigou (SJ-6)
Technique: Needles adjusted along meridian direction, inserted into fat layer
Electrical stimulation: Applied to specific pairs of points to create an electrical circuit
Emphasis on de qi with continuous weak electric current stimulation at abdominal points and meridians""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group did not receive any intervention and maintained their normal diet and usual exercise habits. They did not undergo electroacupuncture (EA) treatment and served as a baseline for comparison with the treatment group." ;
