tara-kb:S-112625-1741 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1741" ;
    dc:title "Effect of acupuncture on experimentally induced itch" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Lu 3: on the medial aspect of the upper arm, about 9 cm below the end of the axillary fold, on the radial side of m. biceps brachii.
Lu 4: on the medial aspect of the upper arm, about 3 cm below Lu 3, on the radial side of m. biceps brachii.
Lu 1: below the acromial extremity of the clavicle.
Lu 2: in the depression below the acromial extremity of the clavicle.
Liv 5: about 15 cm above the tip of the medial malleolus, on the medial aspect and near the medial border of the tibia.
Liv 6: about 21 cm above the tip of the medial malleolus, on the medial aspect and near the medial border of the tibia.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was the unstimulated control site, where no acupuncture or electro-acupuncture was applied after the histamine injection." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Lu 3, Lu 7, Liv 5, Liv 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0780558,
        TARA:3515622,
        TARA:3888808,
        TARA:8267317 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:3888808\": \"LU 3\", \"TARA:3515622\": \"LU 7\", \"TARA:0780558\": \"LR 5\", \"TARA:8267317\": \"LR 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0000989 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "0.5-1.2 cm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1741 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1741 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 10
Gender distribution: 7 males, 3 females
Participants within groups: All 10 participants were part of each treatment group (placebo-acupuncture, acupuncture, 2 Hz electro-acupuncture, 80 Hz electro-acupuncture)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Stainless steel acupuncture needles
Quantity: Two needles
Size: 38 cm long
Location: Lu3 and Lu4 (real points)
Penetration: Superficial insertion
Sensation: No specific sensation experienced by patients""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Acupuncture: Needles inserted to a depth of 0.5-1.2 cm, manually manipulated by rotating back and forth to elicit sensations of numbness, distension, heaviness, tingling, or radiating sensations (de Qi).
Electro-acupuncture: Electrical stimulation at 2 Hz or 80 Hz, with needles connected to an acupuncture pulse stimulator, intensity adjusted to twice the perception threshold level.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not mention a specific disease or condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Pruritus (itch)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, acupuncture and electro-acupuncture at 2 Hz and 80 Hz were effective in reducing subjective itch intensity when applied intrasegmentally, with statistical significance (p < 0.01 for 80 Hz and p < 0.05 for 2 Hz)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Maximal itch intensity (Mil), Itch duration (ID)
Secondary outcome measure: Total itch index (Til)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 5 minutes (post-induction), 5 minutes and 20 minutes (pre-induction)
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on how often acupuncture treatments were administered in terms of frequency per week or month)" .

