tara-kb:S-112625-1750 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1750" ;
    dc:title "Influence of Acupuncture on Remodeling of Swallowing Functions for Patients with Pseudobulbar Palsy after Cerebral Infarction" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Major acupoints:
Fengchi (GB 20): Located in the dip between the sternocleidomastoid muscle and the trapezius muscle, at the level of Fengfu (GV 16).
Yiming (Ex HN 14): Located midway between Yifeng (TE 17) and Fengchi (GB 20) at the nape.
Gongxue (Extra): Located 1.5 cun directly below Fengchi (GB 20).
Zhiqiang (Extra): Located in the depression between the laryngeal protuberance and the hyoid bone.
Tunyan (Extra): Located between the hyoid bone and the laryngeal protuberance, in the depression 0.5 cun lateral to the midline.
Fayin (Extra): Located 0.5 cun below the laryngeal protuberance and 0.3 cun lateral to the midline.
Lianquan (CV 23): Located superior to the laryngeal protuberance, at the midpoint of the upper border of the hyoid bone.
Jinjin (Ex HN 12) and Yuye (Ex HN 13): Inside of the mouth, on the veins bilateral to the glossodesmus.
Adjunct acupoints: Sanyinjiao (SP 6), Taichong (LR 3), Fenglong (ST 40), Hegu (LI 4)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received routine neurological therapies for 42 days (8 weeks), which is equivalent to usual care without any specific intervention like acupuncture." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GB 20, Ex HN 14, Extra, Extra, Extra, Extra, CV 23, Ex HN 12, Ex HN 13, SP 6, LR 3, ST 40, LI 4" ;
