tara-kb:S-112625-1757 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1757" ;
    dc:title "Effect of Acupuncture or Acupressure on Quality of Life of Patients with Chronic Obstructive Asthma: A Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Zhongfu (Lung 1): Alarm point of the lung and meeting point of the lung and spleen.
Dazhui (Du Mai 14): Meeting point of several Yang meridian connections in the neck and upper chest.
Dingchuan (Extra 17): Extra point for asthma relief, located 1 cm away from Dazhui.
Neiguan (Pericardium 6): Connecting point confluent to Yinwei and near Yangchi (Sanjiao 4).
Zusanli (Stomach 36): Uniting point with a homeostatic effect on the stomach meridian.
Zhongfu, Neiguan, and Zusanli were used bilaterally.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study, Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received standard care alone, which included oral medication and chest physiotherapy, as well as instructions on relaxation techniques and exercises. They did not receive any additional interventions like acupuncture or acupressure." ;
