tara-kb:S-112625-176 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-176" ;
    dc:title "Hypothalamus-Related Resting Brain Network Underlying Short-Term Acupuncture Treatment in Primary Hypertension" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """GV20 (baihui): Located in the center of the head.
GV23 (shangxing): Not specified.
EX-HN1 (sishencong): Includes four acupoints located around GV20, each about 3 cm to GV20.
ST9 (renying): Located in the neck, beside the Adam's apple, in the midpoint of the leading edge of the sternocleidomastoid.
LI11 (quchi): Located in the outer end of the elbow stripes.
PC6 (neiguan): Located in the volar forearm, about 6 cm above the wrist stripes between tendon and radial measured wrist flexor tendon.
LI4 (hegu): Located in the back of the hand, between the first and second metacarpal, radial side of the midpoint of the second metacarpal.
ST36 (zusanli): Located in the anterolateral leg, between the tibialis anterior muscle and extensor digitorum longus, about 10 cm below the knee, about 1.5 cm from the tibia leading edge.
SP6 (sanyinjiao): Located in the medial leg, about 10 cm above the medial condyle tip.
LR3 (taichong): Located in the dorsal foot and the first metatarsal gap rear depression.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group did not receive acupuncture treatment and continued with their original treatment programs (usual care or medication). They participated in fMRI scans and 24-hour ABPM, and completed quality of life questionnaires (SF-36)." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GV 20, GV 23, EX-HN 1, ST 9, LI 11, PC 6, LI 4, ST 36, SP 6, LR 3" ;
