    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Zhongwan (CV 12): Located in the epigastric region, regulates middle jiao and ascending/descending ability.
Xiawan (CV 10): Located in the epigastric region, regulates middle jiao and ascending/descending ability.
Qihai (CV 6): Sea of qi, fosters kidney and strengthens constitution.
Guanyuan (CV 4): Fosters kidney and strengthens constitution.
Huaroumen (ST 24): Bilateral, dredges meridian, regulates qi and blood.
Wailing (ST 26): Bilateral, dredges meridian, regulates qi and blood.
Shangfengshidian (Extra): Related to Xun trigram wind, dominates liver and middle jiao.
Baihui (GV 20): Wakes up brain, opens orifices, balances yin and yang.
Yintang (GV 29): Calms mind, wakes up brain, soothes heart, benefits wisdom.
Neiguan (PC 6): Dilates chest, relieves depression.
Taichong (LR 3): Soothes liver, relieves depression.""" ;
