Duration needles were left in place: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of acupuncture treatment varied across studies. In one study, acupuncture was administered once a day for 7 days. In another study, treatments were conducted once a week for 3 weeks a month, over 3 months. Overall, the frequency and duration were not consistently specified across all studies." .

tara-kb:S-112625-1768 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1768" ;
    dc:title "Fifteen-day Acupuncture Treatment Relieves Diabetic Peripheral Neuropathy" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Hegu (LI4), Fenglong (ST40), Quchi (LI11), Zusanli (ST36), San Yin Jiao (SP6)
Identified by an experienced acupuncturist using traditional methods
Position determined by anatomic landmarks and proportional measurements
Precise position refined by palpation
Depth of insertion:
LI4: 1.20-1.53 cm
ST40: 1.82-2.25 cm
LI11: 1.38-1.50 cm
ST36: 2.11-2.30 cm
SP6: 1.73-2.00 cm
Needles rotated every 5 minutes to achieve "De qi"
Same acupoints used for sham acupuncture with shallower insertion and no manipulation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT) and Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture group: The control group consisted of 21 participants who received sham acupuncture. In this procedure, the same acupoints were punctured with the same acupuncture needles, but the needle was inserted to a depth of only 0.3 cm, and no manipulation of the needle was performed to avoid De qi." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
