tara-kb:S-112625-1771 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1771" ;
    dc:title "Phantom Acupuncture: Dissociating Somatosensory and Cognitive/Affective Components of Acupuncture Stimulation with a Novel Form of Placebo Acupuncture" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Acupoint: PC6
Location: Left acupoint on the medial side of the right forearm
Specific location: 2 cun (approximately 5 cm) proximal to the transverse wrist crease, between the tendons of the palmaris longus and flexor carpi radialis muscles
Innervation: Median and antebrachial cutaneous nerves
Clinical use: Useful for cardiac conditions, controlling nausea and vomiting, modulating autonomic function, and inducing robust acupuncture sensation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Controlled Trial (Crossover Design)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control group: Phantom acupuncture (PHNT), which is a visual manipulation that mimics the acupuncture needling ritual without actual somatosensory stimulation.
Subgroups: PHNTc (credible) and PHNTnc (not credible) based on subjects' belief in the credibility of the phantom acupuncture.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "South Korea" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "http://dx.doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.1094881" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "PC 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:4311153 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper provides the length of the needle but does not explicitly state the depth of insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1771 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1771 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 20
PHNTc (credible): 11
PHNTnc (non-credible): 9""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Phantom acupuncture
Description: Visual manipulation mimicking acupuncture needling ritual without somatosensory tactile stimulation
Method: Acupuncturist approaches acupoint without tactile input; video clip of real acupuncture needling is replayed to create illusion
Purpose: To control for needling credibility without somatosensory afference""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation of stainless steel needles at acupoint PC6; for PHNT, no actual needle stimulation occurred, only a visual illusion of needle insertion and stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state a primary medical condition or disease in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the paper discusses acupuncture in general terms and its effects on pain, but does not specify a primary medical condition or disease)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the effectiveness of the acupuncture intervention compared to the control/sham group in terms of statistical significance or primary outcomes)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Physiological measures: Heart rate (HR), skin conductance (SC), pupil size (PS)
Psychophysical responses: Subjective ratings of needle sensation, MASS index (MI), individual sensation intensities
Secondary outcome measures:
Influence of needling credibility on physiological and psychophysical responses
Comparison between real and phantom acupuncture effects""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Approximately 7.5 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 2 minutes (post-stimulation resting period)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of treatment sessions over time)" .

