tara-kb:S-112625-1780 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1780" ;
    dc:title "Electrical acupoint stimulation of the affected arm in acute stroke: a placebo-controlled randomized clinical trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """GB20: Located on either side of the occiput.
LI15: On the affected arm contralateral to the side of brain lesion.
LI11: On the affected arm contralateral to the side of brain lesion.
LI10: On the affected arm contralateral to the side of brain lesion.
LI4: On the affected arm contralateral to the side of brain lesion.
These points are commonly used in traditional Chinese medicine to manage acute stroke and associated arm weakness.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT) Double-blind, placebo-controlled" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 23 subjects who received conventional rehabilitation only, which included daily physiotherapy, occupational therapy, and consultations from speech therapists and/or dieticians as needed." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Hong Kong" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GB 20, LI 15, LI 11, LI 10, LI 4" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0742938,
        TARA:0859695,
        TARA:2324295,
        TARA:7829474,
        TARA:8923096 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:2324295\": \"GB 20\", \"TARA:7829474\": \"LI 15\", \"TARA:8923096\": \"LI 11\", \"TARA:0742938\": \"LI 10\", \"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005098 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not applicable (the study uses surface electrodes, not needle insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1780 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1780 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 73
Electrical stimulation group: 29
Placebo-electrical stimulation group: 21
Control group: 23""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Placebo-electrical stimulation (placebo-ES)
Details: The placebo-ES group received identical treatment to the ES group, but the electrical circuits were disconnected internally, so no actual electrical stimulation was delivered.
Location: Same acupoints as the ES group (GB20, LI15, LI11, LI10, and LI4)
Method: Non-penetrating, using surface electrodes
Other details: The machines' lights and dial appeared to work normally when switched on, but no actual stimulation was delivered.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electrical stimulation applied to acupoints using surface electrodes. The parameters included square direct current pulses of 200 Œºs duration at 20 Hz and maximum tolerable intensity without causing pain. A mild tingling sensation was expected. Needles were not used; instead, surface electrodes were employed." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Acute stroke with associated arm weakness" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Acute stroke with moderate to severe weakness in the arm contralateral to the side of the stroke" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the electrical stimulation intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes of hand grip and pinch strength, with significant p-values of 0.015 and 0.007, respectively. The placebo-electrical stimulation group did not differ significantly from the control or ES groups." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Hand grip strength, Pinch strength
Secondary outcome measure: Action Research Arm Test (ARAT)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each session: 60 minutes
Frequency: Five sessions a week
Total duration: Four weeks
Needles left in place: Not applicable (electrical stimulation used)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "60 minutes a day, five days a week, for four weeks" .

