    dc:title "Wrist-Ankle Acupuncture for Pain After Transcatheter Arterial Chemoembolization in Patients with Liver Cancer: A Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Point 1 at the left ankle
Points 1 and 2 at the right ankle
Needling points are chosen based on the location of pain: upper body pain is treated at the wrist, lower body pain at the ankle.
The body is divided into six longitudinal zones, with one needling point per zone at the wrist or ankle.""" ;
