tara-kb:S-112625-1794 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1794" ;
    dc:title "Warm Needling Therapy for Sciatica: A Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Major acupoints: Bilateral Jiaji (Ex B 2) points of L 4 and L 5, Dachangshu (BL 25), Zhibian (BL 54), Huangtiao (GB 30), Yanglingquan (GB 34) on the affected side.
Adjuvant acupoints: Ciliao (BL 32) for lumbosacral pain, Weizhong (BL 40) and Chengshan (BL 57) for posterior calf pain, Kunlun (BL 60) and Shenmai (BL 62) for ankle pain.
Dachangshu (BL 25) is located on the lumbosacral region, regulating meridian qi in loin and tonifying the kidney.
Yanglingquan (GB 34) is the lower He Sea point of the Gallbladder Meridian, also a tendon joint.
Huantiao (GB 30) regulates and promotes qi and blood in Foot Taiyang and Foot Shaoyang Meridians.
Zhibian (BL 54) and Huantiao (GB 30) strengthen yang, dispel cold, drive away dampness, relieve impediment, kill pain, and dredge meridians and collaterals.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received ordinary acupuncture therapy, with the same acupoints, operation, and treatment schedule as the treatment group, but without the warm needling component." ;
