tara-kb:S-112625-18 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-18" ;
    dc:title "Electroacupuncture in Reduction of Discomfort Associated with Barostat-Induced Rectal Distension-A Randomized Controlled Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Hegu (LI4): Located on the dorsum of the hand, between the first and second metacarpal bones.
Neiguan (PC6): Located on the palmar aspect of the forearm, 2 cun above the transverse crease of the wrist between the flexor carpi radialis and palmaris longus tendons.
Zusanli (ST36): Located on the anterior aspect of the leg, 3 cun below the knee cap and one fingerbreadth from the anterior crest of the tibia.
Chosen for their roles in reducing abdominal pain (LI4 and PC6) and regulating colorectal muscle contractility (ST36).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study; Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture (SA) group: This group received sham acupuncture with a short stud instead of a needle to mimic the procedure of electroacupuncture (EA) without actual needle insertion." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Hong Kong" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4, PC 6, ST 36" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:4311153,
        TARA:6463344 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "15 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-18 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-18 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total sample size: 40; EA group: 20; SA group: 20" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Blunt-tip acupuncture needles
Quantity: Not specified
Size: 10 mm in length, 0.22 mm in diameter
Location: Same points as real acupuncture (Hegu, Neiguan, and Zusanli)
Penetration: Non-penetrating
Electrical stimulation: No electrical output despite connected stimulator""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electroacupuncture (EA) group: Electrical stimulation using a six-channel programmable electrical stimulator at 1-10 Hz, with an intensity sufficient to provoke muscle contraction.
Sham acupuncture (SA) group: No electrical stimulation; blunt-tip needles inserted without penetrating the skin.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the study focuses on reducing colorectal discomfort during colonoscopy, not a specific disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes:
Reduction of colorectal discomfort caused by Barostat-induced rectal distension
Pressure at which rectal discomfort is reported
Maximal tolerable pressure
Secondary outcomes:
Number of subjects who could tolerate higher rectal distension pressures
VAS scores for discomfort
Increase in beta-endorphin levels""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "45 minutes; Needles were left in place during the entire Barostat procedure, removed at the end or when maximum tolerable pressure was reached." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper only describes a single session of EA or SA lasting 45 minutes, with no information on frequency or repeated treatments)" .

