Liu et al: Not specified
Orellana Molina et al: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1806 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1806 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide a total sample size for all participants across the included studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Shallow needling at two unrelated points on the sole.
Needle type: Real needles used for shallow needling.
Quantity: Two points.
Size: Not specified.
Location: Unrelated points on the sole.
Penetrating: Yes, but shallow.
Electroacupuncture: Minimal, below threshold of perception.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual stimulation: Slight rotation and thrusting to elicit de qi (dull, numb or heavy); periodic manual stimulation.
Electrical stimulation: Electroacupuncture with frequencies of 5/80 Hz to tolerance.
Thermal stimulation: Pyrogenic herbal dressing and heat application.
Sensation sought: De qi (dull, numb or heavy).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Plantar heel pain (PHP)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to control/sham groups based on primary outcomes such as pain reduction and improvement in function. Statistical significance was reported in several studies, including p<0.05 for Karagounis et al. and p<0.0009 for Tillu and Gupta." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Pain scales such as VAS and PFPS
Secondary outcome measures: Assessments of function and tenderness""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Liu et al: Retained 20 minutes
Karagounis et al: Retained 20-30 minutes
Zhang et al: Retained 30 minutes
Vrchota et al: Retained 20 minutes
Orellana Molina et al: Retained 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Liu et al: Daily for 30 sessions, 20 minutes per session
Orellana Molina et al: Daily for 10 sessions, 20 minutes per session
Vrchota et al: Not specified
Karagounis et al: Twice a week for 16 sessions, 20-30 minutes per session
Zhang et al: Daily for 10 sessions, 30 minutes per session""" .

