    dc:title "Therapeutic Effect Observation on Combined Acupuncture and Chinese Medicine for Reflux Esophagitis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Neiguan (PC 6): Puncture 1 1.5 cun perpendicularly, use reducing manipulation by lifting, thrusting, and rotating at a frequency of 150 200 times/min, enabling the needling sensation to radiate to the shoulder.
Gongsun (SP 4): Puncture 1 1.5 cun perpendicularly, use even reinforcing reducing manipulation by lifting, thrusting, and rotating at a frequency of 60 70 times/min.
Yanglingquan (GB 34): Puncture 1.5 2 cun perpendicularly, use same manipulation and frequency as Gongsun (SP 4), enabling the needling sensation to radiate to the shoulder.
Retention time: 20 minutes.
Treatment frequency: Once a day.""" ;
