    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total participants: 36; Participants within groups: EA=12, MA=12, SA=12" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture was non-invasive.
A plastic guide tube was tapped at ST36 and ST40 to create a sensation.
Bent needles with adhesive bandages were taped to the skin surface, not inserted.
Manipulations involved pressing the bent needles to create a pressure sensation.
A non-functioning electrical stimulator was used for visual effect.
De qi sensations were avoided.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual Acupuncture (MA): Needles were inserted to a depth of 20-25 mm and rotated 180-360¬∞ at 3-5 Hz to produce De qi sensations.
Electroacupuncture (EA): Needles were inserted and connected to an electrical stimulator delivering square waves at 2 and 100 Hz to produce De qi sensations.
Sham-Acupuncture (SA): Non-invasive method using a plastic guide tube and bent needles taped to the skin to produce a pressure sensation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Bi syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Knee Osteoarthritis (OA)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention (EA) was effective compared to the control/sham group (SA) based on the primary outcomes (SPT and TST)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Pain relief scores
Secondary outcome measure: Computerized infrared thermography (IRT) scores""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 25 minutes
Needles left in place during a session:
MA: 25 minutes
EA: 25 minutes
SA: Not applicable (needles not inserted)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper only describes a single session of acupuncture treatment without specifying frequency or duration beyond this session)" .

