tara-kb:S-112625-1826 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1826" ;
    dc:title "Randomized-controlled study of treating attention deficit hyperactivity disorder of preschool children with combined electro-acupuncture and behavior therapy ‡¨ù" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Head points:
Shen-Ting (GV 24): located on the midline, 0.5 cun posterior to the anterior hairline.
Bilateral Ben-Shen (GB 13): located in the frontal region, 0.5 cun within the anterior hairline, on a sagittal line ascending from the lateral canthus of the two eyes.
Yin-Tang (EX-HN 3): located at the midway between the medial ends of the eyebrows.
Bilateral Tai-Yang (EX-HN 5): located at the left and right temples, respectively, in a depression about 1 cun posterior to the midpoint between the lateral end of the eyebrow and the outer canthus of the eye.
Si-Shen-Cong (EX-HN 1): a group of four points, at the vertex, 1 cun posterior, anterior and lateral to Bai-Hui (GV 20) point.
Bai-Hui (GV 20): located on the midsagittal line, at the intersection of a line connecting the right and left ear apices.
Body points:
Gan-Yu (BL 18): located on the middle back, 1.5 cun lateral to the lower border of the spinous process of the ninth thoracic vertebra (T9).
Shen-Yu (BL 23): located on the lower back, 1.5 cun lateral to the lower border of the spinous process of the second lumbar vertebra (L2).
Bilateral Tai-Xi (KI 3): located on the medial ankle, at the midpoint between the prominence of the medial malleolus and Achille's Tendon.
Pi-Yu (BL 20): located on the middle back, 1.5 cun lateral to the lower border of the spinous process of the eleventh thoracic vertebra (T11).
Bilateral Tai-Chong (LR 3): located on the dorsum of the foot, between the first and second metatarsal bones, approximately 2 cun superior to the web margin.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received sham electro-acupuncture and behavior therapy. Sham electro-acupuncture involved the same needle insertion and positioning as the experimental group but without manipulation or electrical stimulation. Behavioral therapy was identical to that received by the experimental group." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GV 24, GB 13, EX-HN 3, EX-HN 5, EX-HN 1, GV 20, BL 18, BL 23, KI 3, BL 20, LR 3" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0992296,
        TARA:3135569,
        TARA:3283628,
        TARA:3386254,
        TARA:4362146,
        TARA:4994509,
        TARA:6499349,
        TARA:7679931,
        TARA:9534465,
        TARA:9610280,
        TARA:9655874 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:7679931\": \"GV 24\", \"TARA:4994509\": \"GB 13\", \"TARA:3135569\": \"Yintang\", \"TARA:9534465\": \"Taiyang\", \"TARA:9610280\": \"Sishencong\", \"TARA:3386254\": \"GV 20\", \"TARA:9655874\": \"BL 18\", \"TARA:0992296\": \"BL 23\", \"TARA:4362146\": \"KI 3\", \"TARA:3283628\": \"BL 20\", \"TARA:6499349\": \"LR 3\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0007743 ;
