Participants within groups: Not specified (implied equal distribution within subtypes)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Same as experimental group
Quantity: Same as experimental group
Size: Same as experimental group
Location: Same acupoints as experimental group
Penetrating: Yes, needles were inserted
Other details: No manipulation to induce "de qi" sensation, no electrical stimulation (0 mA)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electro-acupuncture: Manual manipulation (lifting, thrusting, rotating) to achieve de qi sensation, followed by electrical stimulation (15 Hz frequency, 2-4 V voltage, 3-5 mA current intensity).
Sham electro-acupuncture: No manual manipulation, no electrical current (0 mA).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "- Effulgent gallbladder fire - Yin-Yang disharmony - Noninteraction of heart and kidney - Congenital constitutional insufficiency - Postnatal loss of nourishment - Affect-mind dissatisfaction and trauma - Liver-kidney Yin vacuity - Vacuity fire frenetic stirring - Phlegm-heat harassing the inner body - Internal static blood obstruction" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Change in core symptoms of ADHD (evaluated by disappearance of symptoms)
Secondary outcome measure: Relapse rate (evaluated after a half-year follow-up)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was administered once a day, with each course lasting 6 days and a 1-day interval between courses. Patients underwent 12 courses over 12 weeks." .

