    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 162
Participants within groups: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure involved "dummy studs" with a ring but no needle, indicating they were non-penetrating.
Sham studs were placed halfway between the upper and lower border of the spinous processes T2 to T10, approximately 0.5 cun from the spine.
Leg studs were placed 2 cun posterior to GB-34 on the lower leg.
No studs were placed in the ear; instead, sham studs were placed on the anterior arm, 3 cun proximal and 3 cun medial to the midpoint of the antecubital crease.
Sham studs were placed at non-acupuncture points to prevent tactile stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation was provided by the physical presence of the intradermal needles (studs) penetrating the epidermis. No additional stimulation methods such as manual manipulation, electrical stimulation, or thermal stimulation were used. The type of sensation sought is not specified." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Postthoracotomy pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Brief Pain Inventory (BPI) pain intensity score at day 30 after the operation.
Secondary outcome measures:
BPI scores at different time points (e.g., 60 and 90 days).
Numeric rating scale of pain.
Total opioid use.
Medication Quantification Scale (MQS) scores.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment: 4 weeks
Duration needles were left in place: ST-36 and Shenmen: 1 week
Back: 3 weeks
Duration of each acupuncture session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment involved an initial placement of intradermal needles before the operation, with an exchange of new needles 1 week later. The total duration of the intervention was 4 weeks. No regular frequency like \"twice weekly\" or \"daily\" is specified." .

