tara-kb:S-112625-1837 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1837" ;
    dc:title "Pilot, Randomized, Modified, Double Blind, Placebo Controlled Trial of Acupuncture for Cancer Related Fatigue" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Ki 3: Medial side of the ankle region, midway between the most prominent aspect of the medial malleolus and the Achilles tendon, in a depression immediately posterior to the pulsation of the posterior tibial artery.
Sp 6: Medial side of the leg, posterior to the medial margin of the tibia, 3 cun above the prominence of the medial malleolus.
LI 4: Dorsum of the first interosseus space of the hand, at the level of the midpoint of the shaft of the second metacarpal bone, on the belly of the first interosseus dorsalis muscle.
St 36: Superolateral aspect of the anterior surface of the leg, 3 cun distal to the apex of the patella and one fingerbreadth lateral to the tibial tuberosity.
Ren 6/CV 6: Umbilical region, on the anterior midline, 1.5 cun inferior to the umbilicus.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot, Randomized, Modified, Double Blind, Placebo Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture using the Park Sham Device, which is a telescoping blunt edged needle validated to be indistinguishable from true acupuncture." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Ki 3, Sp 6, LI 4, St 36, Ren 6/CV 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:4362146,
        TARA:4385250,
        TARA:6463344 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4362146\": \"KI 3\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\", \"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Ren 6/CV 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0012378,
        MONDO:0004992 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific measurements or descriptive terms for the depth of needle insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1837 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1837 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 23
Participants in true acupuncture group: 16
Participants in sham acupuncture group: 11""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Park Sham Needle (telescoping blunt edged, non penetrating)
Quantity: Same points as true acupuncture (Ki 3, Sp 6, LI 4, 5t 36, and Ren 6/CV 6)
Location: Same points as true acupuncture
Penetration: Non penetrating
Other details: Mimicked true acupuncture procedure with disconnected wires for electrostimulation; used plastic apparatus to hold needles; involved acupressure at active points""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved low frequency electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) at Ki 3 and St 36 points, with an attempt to elicit a \"needle grab\" sensation and potential for \"de qi\" (soreness, aching, or numbness)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM equivalent for the condition being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cancer related fatigue" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No (the differences between true and sham acupuncture were not statistically significant)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Cancer related fatigue (CRF) as measured by the 13 item Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy FatigueSubscale (FACIT F)
Secondary outcome measures: Quality of life and CRF distress as measured by theShort Form 36 (SF 36) and the Cancer Related Fatigue DistressScale (CRFDS)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles left in place during a session: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: Once to twice per week
Duration: 30 minutes per session""" .

