tara-kb:S-112625-1852 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1852" ;
    dc:title "Effectiveness of dry needling techniques in patients with knee osteoarthritis: A systematic review and meta-analysis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Myofascial trigger point dry needling (MTrP DNT): Needling hyperirritable spots in skeletal muscles or fascia.
Periosteal stimulation (PST): Needling over the periosteum.
Intramuscular electrical stimulation (IMES): Stimulation over motor points, regional, and paravertebral musculature.
Specific acupuncture points or locations: Not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham MTrP DN: Used a simulated device over the same MTrPs without penetrating the skin.
Control PST: Involved inserting needles in the same points as PST without electrical stimulation and 2 needles at nonperiosteal points with brief stimulation.
Sham IMES: Same electrode placement as active IMES but with the output current disconnected.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0005086 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1852 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1852 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide a total sample size or detailed participant numbers within groups)" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """MTrP dry needling sham: Simulated device over MTrPs without penetrating the skin.
Periosteal stimulation sham: Needles inserted at same points as active group without electrical stimulation; additional needles at nonperiosteal points with brief stimulation.
Intramuscular electrical stimulation sham: Same electrode placement as active group but with output current disconnected.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Myofascial trigger point dry needling (MTrP DNT): Manual stimulation to produce a local twitch response.
Periosteal stimulation (PST): Manual stimulation to stimulate sympathetic nerves.
Intramuscular electrical stimulation (IMES): Electrical stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not use Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology to describe the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Knee Osteoarthritis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Periosteal stimulation (PST) is effective compared to control/sham groups for pain and function immediately post-treatment (p < 0.00001).
Intramuscular electrical stimulation (IMES) shows significant effects on pain (p = 0.03), but with marked heterogeneity.
Dry needling may provide short-term relief in pain for KOA patients.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcomes:
Pain: WOMAC (Western Ontario and McMasters University Osteoarthritis Index), KOOS (Knee Injury and Osteoarthritis Outcome Score), NPRS (Numerical Pain Rating Scale), VAS (Visual Analogue Scale)
Function: WOMAC, KOOS
Secondary Outcomes:
Quality of life: EQ-5D (EuroQol Group 5-Dimension Self-Report Questionnaire), SF-36 (Short-Form Health survey)
Balance: TUG (Timed Up and Go test)
Improvement in function: GROC (Global Rating of Change)
Psychological factors: SPPB (Short Physical Performance Battery)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper provides information on the number and duration of sessions but does not specify the frequency of treatment sessions)" .

