tara-kb:S-112625-1857 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1857" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for polycystic ovarian syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control Acupuncture Group (CAG): Received non-specific acupuncture stimulation at Touwei (ST8), Pianli (LI6), and Zusanli (ST36).
Migraine Group (MG): Received no treatment.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Australia, China, Sweden, US" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0008487 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1857 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1857 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 30
Sample size within groups: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham group: Control Acupuncture Group (CAG)
Needle type: Sterile single-use acupuncture needles (25-40 mm in length and 0.30 mm in diameter)
Quantity: Three points (Touwei, Pianli, and Zusanli)
Location: Yangming meridians (non-traditional points for migraine treatment)
Penetrating: Yes
DeQi sensation achieved through manipulations""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Needles were stimulated using both manual manipulation (lifting and thrusting or twirling and rotating) and electro-acupuncture.
Electro-acupuncture was performed using a Han's acupoint nerve stimulator with a frequency of 2/100 Hz and intensity varying from 0.1 to 1.0 mA.
The goal was to achieve DeQi sensation (soreness, numbness, distention, and heaviness).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Kidney deficiency" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Polycystic ovarian syndrome (PCOS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"Traditional acupuncture treatment was more effective for pain reduction than control acupuncture treatment."
"The VAS of pain intensity was significantly reduced in the TAG (P = 0.0005) and CAG (P = 0.008) groups after AS compared with before (paired two-tailed t-test with threshold at P <0.01)."
"The reduction of pain intensity appeared greater in the TAG than in the CAG."
"There was no significant reduction in pain intensity in the MG (P = 0.047)."
"Acupuncture stimulation of different points on similar body regions in migraine patients reduced pain and induced different levels of cerebral glucose metabolism in pain-related brain regions."
"Our findings demonstrated that acupoints did have some specificity in migraine treatment."
Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes:
Live birth rate
MultiplePregnancy rate
Ovulation rate
Secondary outcomes:
ClinicalPregnancy rate
Restored regular menstrualPeriod
Miscarriage rate
Adverse events""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes; Duration needles were left in place: Not specified (implied to be for the duration of the session, 30 minutes)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on how often acupuncture treatments were administered)" .

