    dc:title "Therapeutic Efficacy Observation on Acupuncture for Post withdrawal Syndrome of Heroin Dependence" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Neiguan (PC 6): One of the eight Confluent points and the Luo Connecting Point of the Pericardium Meridian.
Shenmen (HT 7): Both the Yuan Primary and Shu Stream Point of the Heart Meridian.
Method for Shenmen (HT 7): Puncture by 0.5 1.0 cun using disposable needles (with tube) of 0.22 mm in diameter and 25 mm in length, with even reinforcing reducing manipulation upon arrival of qi.
Locations based on the National Standard of the People's Republic of China, GB12346 90.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received no intervention. It was used as a comparison to assess the effects of acupuncture at Neiguan and Shenmen points on post withdrawal symptoms and anxiety. The control group consisted of 20 participants." ;
