    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The initiating time of analgesia was shorter while the sustaining time of analgesia was longer in Group A and B than those in Group C (all P<0.01)."
"The efficacy of analgesia was higher in Group B than that in Group A, and a better effect was shown in Group B in reducing serum uric acid level than that in Group A (P<0.01), which was near that in Group C (P>0.05)."
"Conclusion; EA is an effective treatment for AGA, and low frequency (2 Hz) EA showed a better efficacy."
Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes for AR: symptomatic relief (sneezing, rhinorrhoea, nasal congestion, nasal itchiness), effectiveness rate
Primary outcomes for asthma: pulmonary function (FEV1, FEV1%, PEF, PEF%), quality of life (6 min walking distance, Dyspnoea Visual Analogue Scale, Modified Borg Scale, St George's Respiratory Questionnaire, Bronchitis Emphysema Symptom Checklist)""" ;
