tara-kb:S-112625-1876 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-1876" ;
    dc:title "Warm Needling Therapy for the Third Lumbar Transverse Process Syndrome: A Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Intensive acupuncture: Conducted on the affected side, in a circle with the lateral end of the third lumbar transverse process as the center and radius of 3 cm.
Needles inserted into the lateral edge of the transverse process of the third lumbar (L3), evenly from the top to the end of the edge till touching the bone.
Tender points: An obvious tender point around the transverse process of L3 was used as the inserting point for the needle knife therapy.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received small needle knife therapy. The treatment involved inserting a needle knife in parallel with the vertical axis of the body, cutting and peeling, and then pulling it out after ensuring no obstruction. Local anesthesia was used during the procedure." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "The depth is described as until the needle reaches the bone." ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-1876 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-1876 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 120
Treatment group: 68
Control group: 52""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Thermal stimulation (moxibustion) using moxa sticks attached to the needles. Needles were retained for 30 minutes. No manual manipulation or electrical stimulation mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Bi Impediment syndrome (third lumbar transverse process syndrome)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "The third lumbar transverse process syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group. The therapeutic effects were similar between the two groups, but the acupuncture intervention had a lower relapse rate. However, the differences were not statistically significant (P>0.05)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Therapeutic effects (cured, effective, invalid)
Secondary outcome measure: Relapse rate""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Frequency of sessions: Every 3 days, 3 times as a treatment session
Total number of sessions: Generally 1 session, no more than 2 sessions""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was administered every 3 days, with each session consisting of 3 treatments. Patients generally received one treatment session, with a maximum of two sessions in total." .

