tara-kb:S-112625-194 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-194" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture to Treat Sleep Disorders in Postmenopausal Women: A Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Body acupuncture based on Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) was used in eight studies.
Ear acupuncture was used in one study.
Mixed protocols combining body and ear acupuncture were used in two studies.
Acupoints varied significantly across studies; no specific pattern or preferred treatment option was observed.
Some studies used fully individualized treatments, while others used partially individualized or identical treatments for all participants.
Specific acupoints and detailed criteria for selection are not explicitly listed in the paper; they are likely detailed in tables referenced but not quoted here.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Not applicable (the paper is a systematic review, not a single trial)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control groups used in the studies included sham acupuncture, no treatment groups, and other interventions like diet and self-massage training. Specific details for each study can be found in the tables at the end of the paper." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0007147,
        MONDO:0013600 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "0.5 to 1.5 inches (approximately 1.27 to 3.81 cm) and 0.5 to 3 cm; not specified for other studies" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-194 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-194 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide a cumulative sample size for all participants across the 12 articles)" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Some studies used sham points proximate to treatment points but not considered active.
Others used Streitberger placebo needles in 4-5 points.
Sham procedures varied across studies; not all studies used a sham group.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific information on the stimulation methods used in the studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Deficiency of yin leading to blood and qi stagnation and compromising the balance of kidney, heart, and liver." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Insomnia and Obstructive Sleep Apnea Syndrome (OSAS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Maybe/Inconclusive (the paper suggests some effectiveness of acupuncture in improving sleep complaints, but notes limited evidence and inconsistent results across studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Improvements in sleep-related variables such as reduced latency to sleep, increased total sleep time, and sleep efficiency (Hachul et al., 2013 [35]; Kung et al., 2011 [36])
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific information on the duration of each acupuncture session or needle retention time)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency of treatment: Weekly to three times a week
Number of sessions: Ranged from nine to 36 sessions
Duration of treatments: Varied across studies, e.g., 10 sessions over 12 weeks, twice a week for eight weeks, nine sessions over seven weeks""" .

