Group A: 50
Group B: 50""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual stimulation: Seven star needles (plum blossom) in the dorsal region C7-T5 for 5 minutes; stimulation of three lines in the shoulder blades with average intensity.
Electroacupuncture: Disposable metal needles for 30 minutes.
No thermal or laser stimulation mentioned.
Sensation sought: Not explicitly mentioned, but "average intensity" implies controlled stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Insufficiency of the yin of the kidney accompanied by a flare-up of the fire of the liver, deficiency of yang of the kidney or general deficiency of the kidney, stagnation of the blood and accumulation of phlegm and stagnation of the qi of the liver, and disharmony of the heart and kidney." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Hot flushes in menopause" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Mean change in frequency and/or intensity in menopause-related symptoms.
Secondary outcome measures: Hot flushes, sudden sweating, sleep disorders, irritability, bone pain, feeling depressed, headache, chest pain, memory loss, vaginal dryness, skin changes, urinary tract problems, and genital itching.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment: 6 weeks, twice weekly
Duration of each acupuncture session: First visit: 45 minutes (history, examination, self-massage teaching)
Subsequent sessions: Needle insertion: 15-20 minutes
Electroacupuncture: 30 minutes
Plum blossom treatment: 5 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for 6 consecutive weeks; 12 sessions in total. Each session consisted of 15-20 minutes for needle insertion, 30 minutes for electroacupuncture, and 5 minutes for plum blossom treatment." .

