tara-kb:S-112625-198 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-198" ;
    dc:title "A randomized trial of acupuncture for vasomotor symptoms in post-menopausal women" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Acupuncture points were selected based on TCM patterns: Kidney Yin Deficiency, Kidney and Liver Yin Deficiency with Liver Yang rising, Kidney Yin and Yang Deficiency, Kidney yin and Spleen deficiency, Kidney and Heart not communicating, Heart Blood Deficiency, and Liver Qi Stagnation.
Specific points used: UB 23 (Shenshu), UB 20 (Pishu), UB 15 (Xinshu), UB 17 (Geshu), Du 9 (Zhiyang), Du 4 (Mingmen), Sp 9 (Yinlingquan), Sp 6 (Sanyinjiao), right Lu 7 (Lieque), left Ki 6 (Zhaohai), Ki 3 (Taixi), Ki 7 Fuliu), H 6 (Yinxi), H 7 (Shenmen), Liv 3 (Taichong), Du 24 (Shenting), GB 20 (Fengchi).
Electroacupuncture: Bilateral UB 23 (Shenshu) and SP 6 (Sanyinjiao) at 2 Hz.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study was the shallow needle (sham) acupuncture group, which used non-piercing needles to mimic the sensation of acupuncture without actual penetration of the skin." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
