    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Non-penetrating, blunted needles developed by Streitberger and Kleinhenz.
Quantity: 6 needles.
Size: Not specified.
Location: Away from traditional acupuncture meridians, specifically on the back, lower legs, and forearms.
Penetration: Non-penetrating.
Other details: Connected to a disabled acupuncture device; some needles rotated slightly during treatment; removed after 25 minutes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture): Four needles were connected to an electroacupuncture device and stimulated at a frequency of 2 Hz.
Manual manipulation: Remaining needles were stimulated manually after 15 minutes.
Sensation sought: De Qi, a sensation of heaviness or soreness around the needle.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Kidney Yin Deficiency, with additional patterns including Kidney and Liver Yin Deficiency with Liver Yang rising, Kidney Yin and Yang Deficiency, Kidney yin and Spleen deficiency, Kidney and Heart not communicating, Heart Blood Deficiency, and Liver Qi Stagnation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Vasomotor symptoms in post-menopausal women" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Maybe/Inconclusive (both verum and sham acupuncture showed improvement, but no significant difference was found between them)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Number of hot flashes recorded by participants in their diaries.
Secondary outcome measures: Greene Climacteric Scales, Beck Depression Inventory, Beck Anxiety Inventory.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 25 minutes
Needles retained for: 25 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: Two 25-minute treatments per week for the first 4 weeks, followed by one treatment per week for the next 8 weeks.
Total treatments: 16 treatments over 12 weeks.""" .

