tara-kb:S-112625-2 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-2" ;
    dc:title "Electrical stimulation of acupuncture points for analgesia during bone marrow aspiration and biopsy: A randomized double-blind placebo-controlled trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """LI-4 (Hegu): Located in the middle of the angle between the first and second metacarpus.
LI-11 (Quchi): Located at the lateral end of the elbow crease, midway between the biceps brachii tendon and the lateral epicondyle of the humerus.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was the placebo group, where patients received sham electrical stimulation of acupoints LI-4 and LI-11 with the electro acupuncture instrument off." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Iran" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4, LI 11" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:8923096 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:8923096\": \"LI 11\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0012531 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not applicable (the study used skin electrodes for electrical stimulation, not needle insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-2 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-2 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 50
Sample size per group: 25 (AES group), 25 (placebo group)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Placebo electrical stimulation with the instrument off.
Location: Same acupoints as the active group (LI-4 and LI-11).
Type: Non-penetrating (electrodes placed on skin without actual stimulation).
Quantity and size: Not specified.
Other details: A cloth was used to blind the physician to the patient's group.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) of acupoints LI-4 and LI-11, applied bilaterally for 25 minutes starting 15 minutes before the BMA/BMB procedure. The intensity was set to the maximum voltage and frequency each patient could tolerate, indicating a sought sensation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Pain during bone marrow aspiration and biopsy (BMA/BMB)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcome of pain reduction as measured by VAS scores (P < 0.001)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Pain level caused by BMA/BMB measured using the Visual Analog Scale (VAS)
Secondary outcome measures:
Changes in systolic and diastolic blood pressure
Changes in pulse rate
Patient satisfaction and willingness to undergo the procedure again
Duration of the procedure
Frequency of non-successful BMA/BMB before the successful one
Sweating""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "The duration of each acupuncture session was 25 minutes, starting 15 minutes before the BMA/BMB procedure. Not applicable for needle retention as the study used electrical stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper describes a single session of AES during BMA/BMB, with no information on repeated treatments or frequency)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-20 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-20" ;
    dc:title "The effect of auricular acupuncture on anaesthesia with desflurane" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Shen Men: Located at the superior and central part of the Triangular Fossa on the right ear.
Thalamus Point (subcortex): Located at the base of the Concha Wall behind the Antitragus on the right ear.
Tranquiliser Point: Located at the inferior Tragus where it meets the face on the right ear.
Master Cerebral: Located where the ear lobe meets the face on the right ear.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of the same volunteers on days when they did not receive acupuncture, meaning no needles were inserted. This was part of a crossover design where each participant served as their own control." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the country where the study was conducted)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
