tara-kb:S-112625-203 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-203" ;
    dc:title "Efficacy of Acupuncture for Bell's Palsy: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific needle locations or related acupoints)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Eight RCTs used drug therapy as a control.
One RCT used an electrotherapeutic apparatus as a control.
One RCT used Chinese traditional manipulation as a control.
One RCT used stellate ganglion block therapy as a control.
Five studies compared acupuncture plus drug therapy against drug therapy alone.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005665 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper describes needle insertion as \"shallow\" but does not provide specific measurements or further details on depth)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-203 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-203 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 1541
Sample sizes for each study: Not specified in text, but detailed in tables at the end of the paper""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the included studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Conventional stimulation: Manual manipulation of needles to elicit "de qi."
Electric acupuncture stimulation: Electroacupuncture with an electric current applied to the needles.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Bell's palsy" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, but with significant limitations due to heterogeneity and bias." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Total effective rate of patients after acupuncture therapy
Secondary outcome measures: Mean therapy time, skills with acupuncture, adverse effects, incidence of complications during manipulation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20-30 minutes
Frequency and number of sessions: Varies across studies; examples include daily sessions for 5-10 sessions, sessions every other day for 10 sessions, and sessions several times a week for multiple weeks""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Daily sessions: 30min/d√ó5 treatment sessions for acute stage, 30min/d√ó10 treatment sessions for resting and restoration stages.
Weekly sessions: 30min/d√ó6 treatment sessions/week, 20min√ó5‚Äì10 treatment sessions/week for inpatients, 20min√ó2‚Äì5 treatment sessions/week for outpatients.
Other frequencies: 20min/d√ó5 days/week, electroacupuncture 20-30min/other day√ó10 sessions for a cycle.
Duration: Typically 20-30 minutes per session.
Cycles and rest periods: Varied, with some studies specifying rest periods between cycles.""" .

