tara-kb:S-112625-208 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-208" ;
    dc:title "Efficacy of Acupuncture as a Treatment for Tinnitus A Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Hansen et al: Points on the affected side (face and hand) and foot points tailored to personality type.
Marks et al: Electroacupuncture on points in the hand, arm, and face.
Podoshin et al: Points in the tragus and retroauricular region.
Axelsson et al: Points in the face, hand, and leg.
Vilholm et al: Points on the head and around the ear.
Furugard et al: Points on the head, hands, and legs.
Sham control in Vilholm et al: Randomly selected nonacupuncture points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham acupuncture: subcutaneous insertion of needles (Hansen et al), pricking the skin and immediately removing the needle (Marks et al), needling at randomly selected nonacupuncture points (Vilholm et al)
Placebo biofeedback and placebo cinnarizine tablets (Podoshin et al)
Sham electroacupuncture: electrical stimulator with audible and visible signals (Axelsson et al)
Individualized physiotherapy (Furugard et al)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the country or countries where the studies were conducted)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0700322 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-208 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-208 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 185
Participants receiving acupuncture: 112""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Hansen et al: Sham control involved inserting needles subcutaneously into the same points.
Marks et al: Sham control consisted of pricking the skin and immediately removing the needle without the patient's knowledge.
Axelsson et al: Sham control involved an electrical stimulator generating pulses at a low frequency (2 Hz) with audible and visible signals.
Vilholm et al: Sham control involved needling at randomly selected non-acupuncture points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual acupuncture: Needles were manually manipulated.
Electroacupuncture: Needles were stimulated with alternating low (6-10 Hz) and high (100 Hz) frequencies.
No thermal or laser stimulation mentioned.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term or description for tinnitus)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Tinnitus" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Visual analog scale scores for loudness, annoyance, and awareness of tinnitus; subjective severity scale scores for tinnitus; Nottingham Health Profile scores.
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Hansen et al: Not specified
Marks et al: Not specified
Podoshin et al: 30 minutes
Axelsson et al: 30 minutes
Furugard et al: Not specified
Vilholm et al: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Hansen et al: 6 sessions of manual acupuncture
