tara-kb:S-112625-209 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-209" ;
    dc:title "A comparative study on the effects of systemic manual acupuncture, periauricular electroacupuncture, and digital electroacupuncture to treat tinnitus: A randomized, paralleled, open-labeled exploratory trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """MA: Nine acupoints selected according to Traditional Chinese Medicine meridian system theory; five in the periauricular region (TE17, TE21, SI19, GB2, GB8), two in the upper limbs (TE3, TE9), and two in the lower limbs (ST36, ST37).
PE: Two periauricular acupoints (TE17, TE21) chosen to maximize the effect of EA on tinnitus.
DE: Four distal acupoints; two in the upper limbs (TE3, TE9) for tinnitus, and two in the lower limbs (ST36, ST37) for balance between body and mind.""" ;
