    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Nepp et al., 1998: Local point (GB1, UB2, ST5, and Ex2YinTang), specific points for the eyes and mucosa (LI4, SI3, Li3, Kd6, and TH5)
Granlund et al., 2004: ST2, ST8, ST36, GB1, GB14, BL2, and LI4
He et al., 2004: Thermal burn Yin: ST2, LI20, LI11, LI4, SP6, OR Phlegm and blood stasis mutual: ST2, SP10, SP9, SP6, ST36, and KI6
Wang et al., 2005: Thermal burn Yin: LI11, LI4, SP6, KI3, LI20, and ST2 Phlegm and blood stasis mutual: SP10, SP9, ST36, ST40, SP6, and ST2
Tseng et al., 2006: Ex-HN, SJ23, GB14, ST2, and SP6
Shi and Miao, 2012: DU20, BL1, ST1, Taiyang, SJ23, LI4, and ST36
Kim et al., 2012: Bilateral BL2, GB14, TE23, Ex1, ST1, GB20, LI4, LI11, and single GV23""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Artificial tears were used as the control group in this study. The control group consisted of 185 patients who were treated with artificial tears, which were compared to the acupuncture group consisting of 198 patients." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0006733 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Not specified for most studies
0.6‚Äì3 cm for points at the face and head, 3-4 cm for points on the hand and arm (Kim et al., 2012)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-217 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-217 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 383
Acupuncture group: 198
Artificial tears group: 185""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details on the stimulation methods used in the acupuncture treatments)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Dry eye syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Tear break-up time (BUT), Schirmer I test (SIT)
Secondary outcomes: Cornea fluorescein staining (CFS), Visual Analogue Scale (VAS) for self-assessment of ocular discomfort and ocular symptoms""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place during a session)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Nepp et al., 1998: Once per week
Gr√∂nlund et al., 2004: Once to twice per week
He et al., 2004: Once in 2 days, 10 times/course, 3 courses, 10 days‚Äô rest after a course
Wang et al., 2005: Once in 2 days, 10 times/course, 3 courses, 10 days‚Äô rest after a course
Tseng et al., 2006: Twice a week, 2 to 3 day apart, for 8 weeks
Shi and Miao, 2012: Three times a week, for three weeks
Kim et al., 2012: Three times per week, for four weeks""" .

tara-kb:S-112625-218 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-218" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for treating dry eye: a systematic review" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Wang et al. (2005): (A) Individualized by pattern classification: Quchi (LI 11), Hegu (LI 4), Sanyinjiao (SP 6), Taixi (KI 3), Sibai (ST 2), Yingxiang (LI 20)
(B) Standardized local acupoints: Cuanzhu (BL 2), Sizhukong (TE 23), Yangbai (GB 14), Chengqi (ST 1)
He et al. (2004): Individualized by pattern classification: Sibai (ST 2), Yingxiang (LI 20), Quchi (LI 11), Hegu (LI 4), Sanyinjiao (SP 6)
Pang et al. (2003): Fixed classic acupuncture: Sibai (ST2), Zanzhu (BL2), Chengqi (ST1), Yingxiang (LI20), Baihui (GV20), Shaoze (SI1), Houxi (SI3)
Tseng et al. (2006): Fixed classic acupuncture: Taiyang (Ex-HN), Sizhkong (TE 23), Yangbai (GB 14), Sibai (ST 2), Sanyinjiao (SP 6)
Gronlund et al. (2004): Fixed classic acupuncture: ST2, ST8, ST36, GB1, GB14, BL2, LI4
Nepp et al. (1998): Fixed classic acupuncture: Local points: GB1, BL2, ST5, EX2 (Yintang); Specific points for the eyes and mucosa: LI4, SI3, LI3, KI6, TE5""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Artificial tears (used as a control group in studies comparing acupuncture with artificial tears)
Artificial tears alone (used as a control group in studies comparing acupuncture plus artificial tears with artificial tears alone)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China, Sweden, Austria" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0006733 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-218 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-218 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size across all studies: Not specified
Sample sizes for each study:
Wang et al. (2005): 45 participants
He et al. (2004): 32 participants
Pang et al. (2003): 60 participants
Tseng et al. (2006): 43 participants
Gronlund et al. (2004): 25 participants
Nepp et al. (1998): 114 participants
Participants within groups for each study:
Wang et al. (2005): 15 in acupuncture group, 15 in control group
He et al. (2004): 16 in acupuncture group, 16 in control group
Pang et al. (2003): 30 in acupuncture group, 30 in control group
Tseng et al. (2006): 17 in acupuncture group, 9 in control group
Gronlund et al. (2004): 12 in acupuncture group, 13 in control group
Nepp et al. (1998): 30 in acupuncture group, 22 in control group""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the included trials)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide details on how the needles were stimulated or manipulated)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM term for the condition being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Dry eye" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes (acupuncture showed significant improvements in some outcomes compared to artificial tears), but the evidence is limited due to methodological issues and mixed results in other comparisons." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Tear break-up time (BUT), Schirmer test scores, response rates, cornea fluorescent staining (CFS)
Secondary outcomes: Frequency of artificial tear usage""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Wang et al. (2005): 20‚Äì25 min
He et al. (2004): 20‚Äì25 min
Pang et al. (2003): 30 min
Tseng et al. (2006): 20 min
Gronlund et al. (2004): 30 min
Nepp et al. (1998): 30 min
How long the needles were left in place during a session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Wang et al. (2005): Once every 2 days for 10 times, with 10 days rest, totaling three sessions.
He et al. (2004): Once every 2 days for 10 days, with 10 days rest, totaling three sessions.
Pang et al. (2003): Daily for 10 times, totaling three sessions.
Tseng et al. (2006): Two times weekly for 8 weeks.
Gronlund et al. (2004): Once or twice weekly for a total of 10 sessions.
Nepp et al. (1998): Once weekly for 10 weeks.""" .

