tara-kb:S-112625-220 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-220" ;
    dc:title "Adjunctive Effect of Acupuncture to Refractive Correction on Anisometropic Amblyopia One-Year Results of a Randomized Crossover Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """GV20 (baihui): On top of the head, 7 cun above the occipital hairline and 5 cun behind the frontal hairline; perpendicular or oblique insertion; 1‚Äì2 mm depth.
EX-HN5 (taiyang): At the temporal fossa and 1 cun behind the midpoint of a line from the lateral end of the eyebrow to the external canthus; perpendicular or oblique insertion; 6‚Äì10 mm depth.
BL2 (cuanzhu): In the supraorbital notch and at the median end of the eyebrow; perpendicular or oblique insertion; 2‚Äì6 mm depth.
LI4 (hegu): At the dorsum of the hand and between the first and second metacarpals, midway down the second metacarpal; perpendicular insertion; 10‚Äì15 mm depth.
BL59 (fuyang): 3 cun above the site between the Achilles tendon and lateral malleolus; oblique insertion; 10‚Äì15 mm depth.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Crossover Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control group: Spectacles alone (Group 1; n = 42)
Intervention group: Spectacles + Acupuncture (Group 2; n = 41)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
