tara-kb:S-112625-221 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-221" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for slowing the progression of myopia in children and adolescents" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Auricular acupoints: Yan (Eye), Gan (Liver), Shenmen (Gate of Spirit), Mu1 (Vision 1), Pi (Spleen), Xin (Heart), Mu2 (Vision 2), Shen (Kidney), Pizhixia (Subcortex)
Meridian points: zanzhu (UB.2), jingming (UB.1), chengqi (St.1), sibai (St.2), taiyang (Ex.2), baihui (Du.20), fengchi (GB.20), hegu (LI.4)
Selection criterion: Visual observation by an experienced doctor
Sequence and laterality adjustment: Changed every month and week to avoid allergy""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control group 1: Treated with 0.25% atropine eyedrops (0.25A group) and 0.5% atropine eyedrops (0.5A group) only.
Control group 2: No intervention.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Taiwan" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0001384 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not applicable (the study uses auricular acupressure without needle insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-221 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-221 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 131
Trial 1: 71 participants (22 in 0.25A group, 23 in 0.5A group, 26 in 0.25A+E group)
Trial 2: 83 participants (35 in each group after attrition)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the included studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation methods: Auricular acupoint stimulation using a 1 mm alloy ball and a seed-embedding method for acupressure.
Sensation sought: Activation of De Qi (numbness or tingling).
Needle stimulation: Not specified if needles were stimulated manually or electrically.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition related to myopia)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Myopia (near-sightedness or short-sightedness)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Myopia progression (defined as one diopter mean change)
Proportion of children/adolescents whose myopia increased by one diopter per year
Secondary outcome measures:
Mean change in axial length measured by any method
Mean change in corneal radius of curvature measured by any method""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: At least 1 minute to 3 to 5 minutes per time
Frequency of sessions: Three times a day
Duration of treatment: At least 6 months""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was three times a day for at least six months. Additionally, interactive multimedia instruction was provided every Thursday morning during the 15-week intervention period." .

