Acupuncture vs. sham acupuncture: 636 participants
Acupuncture vs. medication: 916 participants""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture was used as a control in several trials.
Non-acupuncture points were used for sham procedures.
Specific details:
Trial [42]: Sham points in different innervation area from the acupuncture group.
Trial [43]: Non-acupuncture points, three in upper limbs and one near ST36.
Trial [45]: Non-acupuncture points near the main acupoints of EA group.
Trial [46]: Non-acupuncture points, 1 cm away from the classical acupoints of MA group.
Trial [49]: Non-acupuncture points, three in upper limbs and one near ST36.
Trial [50]: Non-acupuncture points near the main acupoints of MA group.
No details on needle type, quantity, size, or whether penetrating or non-penetrating.""" ;
