    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0002014,
        HP:0002019,
        MONDO:0005052 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "20-25 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-238 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-238 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants initially: 85
Total participants after dropouts: 81
EA group: Initially 42, completed 38
Mox group: Initially 43, completed 43""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electroacupuncture (EA): Needles were stimulated with electrical stimulation using the HANS Acupoint Nerve Stimulator at a frequency of 2 Hz and intensity of 3.0 mA. The sensation sought was "Qi" (soreness, numbness, distension, and heaviness).
Moxibustion (Mox): Needles were not used; instead, warm moxibustion was applied with lit moxa placed 1-2 cm above the acupoints, maintaining a surface temperature of 46 ¬± 1 ‚ÑÉ for 30 minutes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) - specifically diarrhea-predominant (IBS-D) and constipation-predominant (IBS-C) types" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, both EA and Mox were effective in relieving abdominal pain and improving gastrointestinal symptoms in IBS patients. Mox was more effective for IBS-D, while EA was more effective for IBS-C. Statistical significance was noted for improvements in abdominal pain (P < 0.001) and stool features (P < 0.01 for EA in IBS-D, P < 0.001 for Mox in IBS-D and EA in IBS-C)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Primary gastrointestinal symptoms (abdominal pain, stool form)
Expression of substance P (SP) and vasoactive intestinal peptide (VIP) in colonic mucosa
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles left in place during a session: Not specified (implied to be for the duration of the session, 30 minutes)
Overall treatment duration: Once per day, six times per week, for 4 consecutive weeks""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was administered once a day, six times per week, for 4 consecutive weeks." .

tara-kb:S-112625-239 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-239" ;
    dc:title "Effect and Safety of Deep Needling and Shallow Needling for Functional Constipation A Multicenter, Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Bilateral ST25, located according to the World Health Organization Standardized Acupuncture Points Location" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study is the lactulose-controlled group, where participants took lactulose orally for 16 continuous weeks. This group serves as a comparison to evaluate the effectiveness and safety of deep and shallow needling for functional constipation." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "ST 25" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:5717468 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:5717468\": \"ST 25\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0002019 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Deep Needling: approximately 20 to 60 mm until they pierced into the muscle layer of the abdominal wall for 1 to 2 mm.
Shallow Needling: approximately 3 to 5 mm into the fat layer.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-239 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-239 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 455
Deep needling group: 237
Shallow needling group: 119
Lactulose-controlled group: 119""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the study did not include a sham acupuncture group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electroacupuncture (EA) with a dilatational wave of 2/15 Hz and a current intensity of 0.1 to 1 mA. The stimulation was applied for 30 minutes, and a mild shivering sensation around the acupoints was sought to indicate the proper dose." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide the condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Functional Constipation" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The primary outcome of mean weekly SBMs improved in all groups compared to baseline (P < 0.01).
During week 1 to 4, no significant difference was observed between acupuncture groups and lactulose (P > 0.05).
At week 8 and week 16, deep and shallow needling showed sustained effects superior to lactulose (P < 0.05).
Lactulose was better for stool consistency and time to first SBM, but acupuncture had lower emergency drug usage.
Acupuncture was effective but not superior to lactulose during treatment; however, it showed sustained effects post-treatment.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome: Change from baseline of mean weekly spontaneous bowel movements (SBMs) during week 1 to 4, with additional assessments at weeks 8 and 16.
Secondary outcomes:
Weekly SBMs at each assessing week
Change from baseline of mean scores of straining, incomplete evacuation, stool consistency, and abdominal distention over week 1 to 4
Change from baseline of mean weekly Cleveland Clinic Scores (CCS) over week 1 to 4
Time to the first SBM
Percentage of emergency drug usage
Proportion of adverse effects""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Frequency of sessions: 5 times a week for 4 weeks
Depth of needle insertion: approximately 20 to 60 mm
Duration needles were left in place: for the duration of the session (30 minutes)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: 5 times a week
Duration: 30 minutes per session
Total duration: 4 weeks""" .

tara-kb:S-112625-24 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-24" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture facilitates neuromuscular and oculomotor responses to skin incision with no influence on auditory evoked potentials under sevoflurane anaesthesia" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Chosen for general analgesic potency according to traditional Chinese principles of EA under anaesthesia." ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study was the sham group, where electrodes were taped onto the skin without needle insertion or connection to the EA device, serving as a comparison to the EA intervention." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Sweden" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4, PC 6, ST 36, SP 9, LR 3, SP 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:3553465,
        TARA:4311153,
        TARA:4385250,
        TARA:6463344,
        TARA:6499349 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:3553465\": \"SP 9\", \"TARA:6499349\": \"LR 3\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "5-15 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-24 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-24 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants initially randomized: 45
Participants in EA group: 22
Participants in sham group: 23
Total participants analyzed for AEP signals: 32
Participants in EA group analyzed for AEP signals: 16
Participants in sham group analyzed for AEP signals: 16""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Sham (no needle insertion)
Quantity: Same points as acupuncture group
Size: Not applicable (no needle insertion)
Location: Same points as acupuncture group
Penetrating or non-penetrating: Non-penetrating
Other details: Electrodes taped onto skin, not connected to EA device""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved the insertion of stainless steel acupuncture needles intramuscularly to a depth of 5-15 mm. The needles were stimulated using an ACUS II stimulator with a square pulse pattern of alternating polarity, duration of 180 ms, intensity of 2 mA, and a burst frequency of 2 Hz including 80 Hz frequency pulse-trains. The stimulation was bilateral and applied at specific acupuncture points. The sham group did not receive needle insertion. The stimulation was continued for approximately 20 minutes." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not mention a specific disease or condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the study focuses on physiological responses during laparoscopic sterilization, not a specific disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Results: More acupuncture than sham patients responded to skin incision with movement (77% vs. 43%; P = 0.021), pupil dilatation (77% vs. 39%; P = 0.001), and eye axis divergence (72% vs. 39%; P = 0.023). No difference in AEP activity.
Conclusion: Acupuncture facilitates physiological responses to nociceptive stimulation under sevoflurane anesthesia without reducing the depth of anesthesia.
Effectiveness: No (acupuncture did not reduce pain or provide an antinociceptive effect; it facilitated physiological responses).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Movement (neck or limb movements)
Dilatation of the pupils
Divergence of the eye axes
Activity of auditory evoked potentials (AEPs)
Secondary outcome measures:
Changes in mean arterial pressure
Changes in heart rate""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Approximately 20 minutes (21 minutes for acupuncture, 23 minutes for sham)
Duration needles were left in place: Approximately 20-21 minutes for acupuncture, 23 minutes for sham""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not mention the frequency of treatment, only the duration of a single session)" .

