tara-kb:S-112625-247 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-247" ;
    dc:title "The effectiveness of acupuncture in postoperative gastroparesis syndrome -A systematic review and meta-analysis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """ST36: He-Sea point of the Stomach Meridian, command point of the abdomen
CV12: Front-Mu point of the stomach, converging point of the fu-organs, crossing point of the Conception vessel and small intestine, San Jiao (triple energiser) and Stomach Meridian
PC6: Luo-connecting point of the Pericardium, calms shen, harmonises stomach, relieves nausea vomiting and regulates qi
SP6: Crossing point of Spleen, Kidney and Liver Meridians
ST40: Luo-Connecting point of Stomach Meridian, activates the meridian and relieves pain
SP9: He-Sea point of Spleen Meridian, resolves dampness (especially Lower Jiao) and regulates spleen
LV3: Yuan-Source point and Shu-Stream point of the Liver Meridian, regulates liver qi, subdues liver yang, nourishes liver yin and calms shen
ST37: Lower He-Sea point of Large Intestine Meridian, regulates intestines, stomach and spleen
SP10: Invigorates, moves and cools the blood, treats blood stasis and heat in the blood""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control groups: Usual care/medication
Specific interventions in control groups: Metoclopramide, Domperidone, Mosapride, "Da cheng qi tang\"""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Mainland China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0006769 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-247 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-247 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 370 (188 intervention, 182 control)
Participants within groups: Intervention 188, Control 182""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the studies reviewed)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation techniques such as lift thrust, twirl rotation, and rapidly in slowly out were used. Moderate to strong stimulation was applied. No electrical or thermal stimulation methods were mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Dyssplenism, stomach downward propelling disorders, injuries to arteries and vein, energy stagnancy and blood stasis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Postoperative gastroparesis syndrome (PGS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, but with limitations due to low quality of trials. The paper provides statistical evidence of acupuncture's effectiveness compared to control groups, but notes that a definitive conclusion cannot be drawn due to trial quality issues." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome: Efficacy of acupuncture for the treatment of PGS and common acupoint(s) selection.
Secondary outcomes: Technique of manipulation, adverse events, impact to the use of rescue anti-emetics.
Outcome measures: Clinical symptoms, gastric drainage volume, X-ray, esophageal endoscopy, ultrasound assessment, occurrence of complications, effect index.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes (most common), 15 minutes (in one study)
Needle retention time: 30 minutes (most common), 15 minutes (in one study)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: Once daily
Duration: Needle retention times ranged from 15 minutes to 30 minutes
Number of treatments: Most patients achieved satisfactory results after 10 treatment sessions""" .

