tara-kb:S-112625-250 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-250" ;
    dc:title "Electro-acupuncture to prevent prolonged postoperative ileus: A randomized clinical trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """SJ-6: Located 3 cun proximal to the dorsal crease of the wrist, on the line connecting Yangchi (SJ-4) and the tip of olecranon, between the radius and ulna, on the radial side of the extensor digitorum communis muscle. Chinese name: Zhigou.
GB-34: Located in the depression anterior and inferior to the head of the fibula. Chinese name: Yanglingquan.
ST-36: On the lateral surface of the leg, 3 cun distal to the lower border of the patella, one finger's breadth from the tibia tuberosity between the tibia digitorum tibialis anterior muscle and the tendon of longus pedis. Chinese name: Zusanli.
ST-37: Located 3 cun below Zusanli (ST-36) and one finger's breadth (middle finger) from the anterior border of the tibia. Chinese name: Shangjuxu.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received standard postoperative care with no acupuncture. This is described as \"usual care\" and is used as a comparison to the acupuncture intervention." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "SJ 6, GB 34, ST 36, ST 37" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:5918799,
        TARA:6463344,
        TARA:7510801,
        TARA:8758950 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:7510801\": \"TE 6\", \"TARA:8758950\": \"GB 34\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:5918799\": \"ST 37\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0004567 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-250 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-250 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants initially recruited: 90
Participants randomized into groups: 85 (Acupuncture: 44, Control: 41)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation was applied using an electro-acupuncture stimulator at a frequency of 2 Hz." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Prolonged postoperative ileus (PPOI)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: time to first flatus, time to first bowel movement, electrogastroenterography
Secondary outcomes: quality of life measures including pain, nausea, insomnia, abdominal distension/fullness, sense of well-being""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: approximately 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: approximately 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Once daily, starting on postoperative day 1, for up to six consecutive days or until the first bowel movement, with each session lasting approximately 20 minutes." .

tara-kb:S-112625-251 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-251" ;
    dc:title "A Single-Blinded, Randomized Pilot Study Evaluating Effects of Electroacupuncture in Diabetic Patients with Symptoms Suggestive of Gastroparesis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Zusanli (ST 36): Located between the tendon of the extensor digitorum longus pedis and the tibialis anterior muscle, 1 fingerbreadth lateral to the lower border of the tibial tuberosity.
Hegu (LI 4): Located on the dorsum of the hand, approximately at the midpoint of the second metacarpal bone, in the belly of the first interosseus dorsalis muscle.
Sham EA points: 2 cm lateral to ST 36 and 2 cm away from LI 4.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study with a randomized, single-blinded design" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham electroacupuncture (EA) group: The sham EA was applied with true shallow needling into the subcutaneous layer horizontally at nonacupuncture points around true points. This group consisted of 10 patients who received 4 sessions of sham EA treatment over a 2-week period." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Taiwan" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "ST 36, LI 4" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:6463344 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0006769 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """ST 6 acupoint: 1 body-inch
LI 4 acupoint: 0.5 body-inch""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-251 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-251 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total participants: 19; EA group: 9; Sham EA group: 10" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: True shallow needling into the subcutaneous layer horizontally at nonacupuncture points around true points.
Location: 2 cm lateral to the ST 36 point and 2 cm away from the LI 4 point.
Penetration: Penetrating but shallow.
Electrode connections and electrical stimulation: Same as the real EA group.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation method: Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture)
Frequency: 2 Hz
Intensity: Adjusted according to patient tolerance, up to 10 mA
Sensation sought: De qi (needling sensation associated with acupuncture)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly translate diabetic gastroparesis into Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Diabetic Gastroparesis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Reduction in symptom severity of gastroparesis as measured by the Gastroparesis Cardinal Symptom Index (GCSI).
Secondary outcome measure: Shortening of solid gastric half-emptying time as measured by scintigraphy.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place during a session: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for 2 weeks, with each session lasting 30 minutes, for a total of 4 sessions." .

