tara-kb:S-112625-254 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-254" ;
    dc:title "Components of placebo effect: randomised controlled trial in patients with irritable bowel syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details about the needle locations or related acupoints, as it was a sham treatment)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Waiting list (observation): Participants had neither placebo treatment nor interaction with a healthcare practitioner.
Limited: Participants received placebo acupuncture alone with minimal interaction with the practitioner.
Augmented: Participants received placebo acupuncture with a patient-practitioner relationship augmented by warmth, attention, and confidence.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005052 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the sham acupuncture device does not pierce the skin, so no depth is applicable)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-254 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-254 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 262 participants
Participants within groups: Not specified (groups were well balanced)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham device: Validated sham acupuncture device that is indistinguishable from real acupuncture.
Needle type: Dummy needles that retract into a hollow handle, creating an illusion of penetration.
Quantity: Six to eight dummy needles per session.
Location: Non-acupuncture points on the arms, legs, and abdomen.
Penetration: Non-penetrating; the needles retract into a hollow handle.
Frequency: Twice a week for 20 minutes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not stimulated (sham acupuncture device used, no physical stimulation of needles)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide TCM terminology for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The study found that the placebo effect can be separated into components and progressively combined to produce incremental clinical improvement in patients with irritable bowel syndrome.
The patient-practitioner relationship was the most robust component of the placebo effect, with significant statistical and clinical improvements.
The study did not directly compare acupuncture to a control group but rather examined its role as a therapeutic ritual within the placebo effect.
The acupuncture intervention was part of the placebo treatment and showed significant improvements when combined with a supportive patient-practitioner relationship.
Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcomes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Global improvement scale, adequate relief of symptoms
Secondary outcome measures: Symptom severity score, quality of life scale""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly, with each session lasting 20 minutes and involving the placement of six to eight dummy needles. Participants received an additional six sham treatments beyond the initial three weeks." .

tara-kb:S-112625-255 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-255" ;
    dc:title "Clinical trial: acupuncture vs. doubling the proton pump inhibitor dose in refractory heartburn" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Per.6 Neiguan: located two cun proximal to the wrist crease, between the tendons of the muscles palmaris longus and flexor carpi radialis, 0.5-0.8 cun depth
St.36 Zusanli: located one cun lateral to the tibial tubercle, 0.5-1.2 cun depth
Liv.3 Taichong: on the dorsum of the foot in a depression distal to the junctions of the 1st and 2nd metatarsal bones, 0.5-0.8 cun depth
CV12 Zhangwan: midway between the umbilicus and xiphoid process, 0.3-0.5 cun depth
CV17 Shan Zhong: on the sternum (level of the 4th intercostal space), 0.2-0.3 cun depth
Sp.9 Yinlingquan (additional point for 'dampness'): on the lower border of the medial condyle of the tibia in the depression posterior and inferior to the medial condyle of the tibia, 0.5-1.0 cun depth""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Not applicable (the study compares two active interventions without a control group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
