    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group (doubling the PPI dose) based on the primary outcomes of daytime heartburn, night-time heartburn, and acid regurgitation. The paper reports significant improvements in these symptoms for the acupuncture group compared to baseline and compared to the double-dose PPI group." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Efficacy of adding acupuncture vs. doubling the proton pump inhibitor dose in controlling GERD-related symptoms
Reduction in symptoms: daytime heartburn, night-time heartburn, acid regurgitation, dysphagia, chest pain
Secondary outcome measures:
Improvement in general health score
Quality of life assessed by SF-36""" ;
