Acupuncture vs. sham acupuncture: 281 patients (4 RCTs)
Quality of life: 253 patients (3 RCTs)
Acupuncture vs. pharmacological therapy: 449 patients (5 studies)
Acupuncture vs. no specific therapy: 181 patients (2 studies)
Acupuncture as adjuvant: 466 patients (4 studies)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture: Needles either do not penetrate the skin or are placed at non-acupuncture points.
Sham points: 2 to 3 cm away from traditional points, not on a meridian, with an insertion depth of 1 to 2 mm.
Sham moxibustion: Burning moxa pole held 8 inches above and 2 to 3 cm away from traditional points for 2 minutes.
Use of Streitberger needles: Validated sham device that does not pierce the skin but creates an illusion of doing so.
Sham points: Chosen from areas that do not correspond to recognized acupuncture points, deemed to have no therapeutic value.""" ;
