tara-kb:S-112625-263 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-263" ;
    dc:title "Is acupuncture effective in the treatment of pain in endometriosis?" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Lower back/pelvic-abdominal area, Shank, Feet, Hands
Specific points: BL32, ST29, ST36, SP6, CV3, LR3, LR8, SP9, SP10, KI10, Jing well points in hands and feet, Back shu points, Sacral area, Ear (auricular acupuncture)
Case 1: CV4, CV6, ST38, ST36, SP6, SP10, KI3, GB43, PC6, EX1 (tai yang), BL23
Case 2: CV4, CV6, SP6, SP10, KI3, PC6, LU7
Control points: SI9, GB31, LU1, ST8
Non-acupuncture points near SP4, SP6, S10, PC6""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType """Two studies: Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT) with one having a crossover design
One study: Retrospective observational case series study""" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Rubi-Klein et al: Non-specific acupuncture points located on the head, shoulder, chest, and thigh, stimulated less than active points.
Wayne et al: Non-penetrating Streitberger needles attached to the skin over non-acupuncture points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005133 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Intracutaneous to intramuscular
1‚Äì2 mm, 10‚Äì20¬∞""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-263 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-263 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total: 99; Specific group sizes: Not specified in the text, but detailed in Table 7" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Rubi-Klein et al: Non-specific acupuncture points on the head, shoulder, chest, and thigh; subcutaneous neutral needling technique.
Wayne et al: Non-penetrating Streitberger needles attached to the skin over non-acupuncture points close to defined points in the forearm, shank, and foot.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation: Mainly manual with a focus on deQi sensation in two studies and an "echo" sensation in one study.
Thermal stimulation: Moxa was used as a possibility.
Other types of stimulation: Not specified (no mention of electrical or laser stimulation).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Blood stagnation due to Qi/yang deficiency, Qi stagnation, cold, blood deficiency, phlegm." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Endometriosis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes (Rubi-Klein et al showed systematic effects favoring acupuncture; Wayne et al's results were inconclusive)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Patient-rated pain intensity
Secondary outcome measures:
Rated pain disability
Patients' treatment expectation
Take home baby rate
Number of absent days
Analgesic intakes
Perceived symptom severity
Perceived stress
Health-related quality of life (HRQOL)
Symptoms of greatest concern
Social activity and attendance in school activity""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 15-25 minutes
Needle retention time: 15-25 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was one to two times per week, with the number of treatments ranging from nine to 16 sessions. The needle retention time was 15-20 minutes per session." .

