        TARA:9946635 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:6742407\": \"BL 32\", \"TARA:5873796\": \"ST 29\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:0022762\": \"CV 3\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\", \"TARA:7867167\": \"LI 3\", \"TARA:8455793\": \"LI 8\", \"TARA:3553465\": \"SP 9\", \"TARA:8433932\": \"SP 10\", \"TARA:8716769\": \"KI 10\", \"TARA:2187225\": \"SI 9\", \"TARA:5264783\": \"GB 31\", \"TARA:0913913\": \"LU 1\", \"TARA:9946635\": \"ST 8\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005133 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper describes the depth as intracutaneous to intramuscular for the verum group and subcutaneous for the control group, but does not provide specific measurements in mm or cm)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-272 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-272 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 101
Group 1: 47
Group 2: 54
Participants analyzed: 83""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Single application needles type Fa JW (0.18 √Ç 0.25) from China
Quantity and size: Same as verum group
Location: Non-specific points SI 9, Gb 31, Lu 1, St 8
Technique: Constant subcutaneous (neutral) needling""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual manipulation: The insertion depth varied from intracutaneous to deeper intramuscular, and the Chinese needle sensation (deqi) was evoked individually.
Thermal stimulation (moxibustion): Moxa treatment was applied for patients with a TCM diagnosis of cold.
No electrical or laser stimulation mentioned.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "blood stagnation due to Qi/ yang deficiency, Qi stagnation, cold, blood deficiency, phlegm" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Endometriosis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcome of pain intensity reduction. The study found statistically significant reductions in pain intensity in both groups when they received verum-acupuncture, with p-values of <0.0001. Additionally, there were significant improvements in quality of life measures. However, the study suggests that further confirmation is needed." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Pain intensity by VAS during verum treatments compared to control treatments
Secondary outcome measures: Quality of life (assessed using SF 36 and PDI), take-home-baby rate, number of absentee days""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice a week for five weeks, with two units of 10 treatments each." .

