"T a b l e 2 t h a t t h r o u g h t te s t , t h e d y s m e n o r r h e a s c o r e a f t e r t r e a tm e n t w a s o b v i o u s l y r e d u e e d i n e o m P a r i s o n w ith t h a t b e f o r e t r e a t m e n t i n th e g r o u P o f e a r a c u P i m e t u r e th e r a Py ( P < 0 . 0 5 )"
"t h e d if f e r e n e e o f ÂàÄE P l e v e l s i n the P a ti e n ts w it h m ild Âãø s m e n o r r h e a b e t w e e n Pr e ‰∏Ä a n d P o s t ‰∏Ä t r e a tm e n t s h o w s n o s ta ti s t i e a l 5 1 , if i c a n e e ( Â§ñ 0 C o m p a n so n w ith the ËÑö Âè© o f n o r m a l e o n t r o l , Âèñ 0 . 0 5 : a n d 0 e o m p Ê∂å s o n b e t w e e n p r e ‰∏Ä a n d p o s t ‰∏Ä tre a t m e n t i n th e e a r a c u P u n c t u r e th e r a P y g r o u P , Â∞∏‰∏à 0 f f e e ts f o r t h e s e v e re e a s e s i n t h e g r o u P o f e a r a c u P u n c t u r e t h e r a Py 1 5 m a r k e d ly b e t t e r th a n t h a t i n t h e g r o u P o f C h i n e s e d r u g s ( P < 0 . OS )"
"T h e e a r a c u P u n e t u r e t h e r a P y e a n a l s o e l e v a t e r r h e a . U te r u s 1 5 a ta r g e t o r g a n o f ÂàÄE P w h i e h 1 5 i n v o l v e d i n th e r e g u l a tio n o f u t e r i n e a e ti v ity Z , su g g e s ti n g tha t e a r a c Âç≥ u n e t u r e th e r a P y m a y Pl a y a n a n a lg e s i e a c ti o n thr o u g h t h e e l e v a tio n o f ÂàÄ ‰∏Ä E P l e v e l i n P e r i Ph e r a l Pl a s m a a n d t h e e o o r d i n a t i o n o f u t e r i n e a c t i v ity ."
The acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcome(s).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Therapeutic effects of ear acupuncture therapy (EAT) compared to Chinese drugs (CD), reduction in dysmenorrheaScores.
Secondary outcome measures: Œ≤ EP levels, cured and markedly effective rates.""" ;
