    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Quote: "Directly after OPU, the EA group reported signi¬Æcantly higher mean and maximum pain, and `pain now' than the CMA group."
Quote: "At 30 min after OPU and thereafter, no signi¬Æcant differences were found between the groups regarding abdominal pain."
Quote: "Despite a per-operative difference in pain rating, EA, given a few minutes prior to OPU, is a good alternative to CMA."
Quote: "The procedure is well tolerated by the patients, with a shorter hospitalization time and lower costs."
The acupuncture intervention was not as effective as the control group in terms of immediate pain relief but became comparable over time. It offered benefits in terms of shorter hospitalization times and lower costs.
Effectiveness: Maybe/Inconclusive""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Pain relief
Secondary outcome measures: Costs, time to discharge, clinical outcome parameters""" ;
