tara-kb:S-112625-297 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-297" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture Reflexotherapy in the Treatment of Sensory Urgency That Persists After Transurethral Resection of the Prostate: A Preliminary Report" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """CV1 (Huiyin): 40-mm needle inserted deeply in the perineal musculature between the anus and scrotum.
CV2 (Qugu): 40-mm needle inserted 1.5 cm deep in the superior margin of the pubic symphysis.
CV4 (Guanyuan): 40-mm needle inserted 1.5 cm deep approximately 3 cm below the umbilicus.
CV5 (Shimen): 40-mm needle inserted 1.5 cm deep approximately 2 cm below the umbilicus, at the level of the iliac crests.
BL21 (Weishu): 25-mm needle inserted 1.5 cm deep, lateral to the inferior margin of the spinous apophysis of the 12th dorsal vertebra.
BL23 (Shenshu): 25-mm needle inserted 1.5 cm deep, lateral to the spinous margin of the 2nd lumbar vertebra.
BL32 (Ciliao): 40-mm needle inserted in the 2nd sacral foramen.
Auricular points: "prostate" and "external genitalia" with specific locations on the ear.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 14 patients who received placebo for 3 months. This group served as a control for the other interventions, allowing for comparison of the effects of oxybutynin and acupuncture reflexotherapy against a baseline where no active treatment was administered." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "CV 1, CV 2, CV 4, CV 5, BL 21, BL 23, BL 32, Prostate, External Genitalia" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0992296,
        TARA:1205186,
        TARA:4839095,
        TARA:6742407,
        TARA:6969962,
        TARA:8693603,
        TARA:9921528 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:8693603\": \"CV 1\", \"TARA:6969962\": \"CV 2\", \"TARA:9921528\": \"CV 4\", \"TARA:1205186\": \"CV 5\", \"TARA:4839095\": \"BL 21\", \"TARA:0992296\": \"BL 23\", \"TARA:6742407\": \"BL 32\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "External Genitalia",
        "Prostate" ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """CV1: 40-mm-long needle inserted deeply in the perineal musculature
CV2: 40-mm needle inserted 1.5 ^2 cm deep
CV4: 40-mm needle inserted 1.5 ^2 cm deep
CV5: 40-mm needle inserted 1.5 ^2 cm deep
BL21: 25-mm needle inserted 1.5 ^2 cm deep
BL23: 25-mm needle inserted 1.5 ^2 cm deep
BL32: 40-mm needle inserted in the 2nd sacral foramen
Auricular points: 15-mm-long needle inserted tangentially""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-297 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-297 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 42
Participants within groups:
Placebo: 14
Oxybutynin: 15
Acupuncture reflexotherapy: 13""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved electrostimulation by acupuncture reflexotherapy at a low frequency (5 to 10 Hz) and at the highest intensity that did not cause pain. The somatic points were connected bilaterally and stimulated in alternating sessions, while auricular points were stimulated in each session." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Sensory urgency persisting after transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Changes in International Prostate Symptom Score (I-PSS) and I-PSS Quality of Life (IPSS QoL) scores.
Secondary outcome measures: Changes in maximum flow rate (Qmax) and voiding diary parameters (daytime and nocturnal voidings).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "12 sessions over 4 weeks, 3 sessions per week, 20 minutes each session; maintenance sessions every fortnight up to 3 months" .

