tara-kb:S-112625-306 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-306" ;
    dc:title "Somatic Acupuncture Versus Ear Acupuncture in Migraine Therapy: A Randomized, Controlled, Blind Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Somatic Acupuncture: LR 3 (on the dorsal surface of the foot, in the depression distal to the joint between the first and second metatarsal bones)
Ear Acupuncture:
Aggressiveness point: on the ear lobule, below the intertragic notch, 3-4 mm from the attachment of the lobule to the face
Lung point: in the center of cavum conchae, delimited by the crms of helix, the antitragus and the external auditory canal
Thalamus point: in the cavum conchae, close to the antitragus, which has to be pulled back in order to reveal this point
Other points chosen by electrical and manual detection, focusing on the most painful points upon manual stimulation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
