tara-kb:S-112625-307 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-307" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for Migraine: A Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Waiting list: Used in three trials.
Sham acupuncture: Used in eleven trials.
Pharmacotherapies: Used in thirteen studies.
Other sham procedures: Used in two studies (placebo injection and mock TEnS).
Non pharmacological therapies: Used in two studies, but not fully analyzed due to methodological issues.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005277 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """10‚Äì30 mm (multiple studies)
2‚Äì20 mm (one study)
Not specified (other studies)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-307 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-307 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 3004 patients
Acupuncture vs. sham acupuncture: 1324 patients
Acupuncture vs. waiting list: 434 patients
Acupuncture vs. pharmacotherapy: Not specified (13 studies)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Sham acupuncture involved superficial needling 2 3 cm away from true acupuncture points, with patients blinded. The needles were inserted at non acupoints on the arm, back, and thigh, with a 3 mm insertion depth and no stimulation. In some cases, blinding was not fully effective." ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit details on needle stimulation methods)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Migraine" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "The current evidence suggests that acupuncture is significantly superior to waiting list and at least as good as sham acupuncture, and of comparable efficacy to several proven drug therapies for the treatment and prevention of migraine. Maybe/Inconclusive regarding effectiveness compared to sham acupuncture." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Number of days with headachePer month in the last follow upPeriod
Secondary outcome measures: Intensity ofPain, duration and frequency of headache attacks, medication use, global response to treatment or frequency of headache (defined as at least 33% improvement from baseline)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details about the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Median treatment period: 8 weeks with 8 sessions (range = 1 16 sessions)
