tara-kb:S-112625-338 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-338" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture in patients with tension-type headache: randomised controlled trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Basic points: Forearm: 1 cun ulnar of the proximal third of the line between heart (HE) 3 and HE 7
Scapula: 1 cun laterally of the lower scapular edge
Spina iliaca: 2 cun above spina iliaca anterior superior in vertical line to the arch of left ribs
Back I: 5 cun laterally of the spine of lumbar vertebrum IV
Back II: 5 cun laterally of the spine of lumbar vertebrum V
Upper leg I: 6 cun above the upper edge of the patella (between the spleen and stomach meridians)
Upper leg II: 4 cun above the upper edge of the patella
Upper leg III: 2 cun dorsally of GB 31 (avoiding bladder meridian)
Additional points could be chosen individually based on specific criteria.
Minimal acupuncture involved needling at non-acupuncture points superficially.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Minimal acupuncture: superficial needling at non-acupuncture points, serving as a sham intervention.
Waiting list control: no prophylactic treatment for headaches for 12 weeks after randomization.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
