tara-kb:S-112625-339 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-339" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for tension type headache: a multicentre, sham controlled, patientand observer blinded, randomised trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details about the locations or names of the acupoints used in either the verum or sham groups)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control Group: Group TM
Description: Conservative treatment with tramadol (1.5 mg/kg) 30 minutes before lithotripsy and midazolam (0.06 mg/kg) as sedo-analgesic 5 minutes before ESWL.
Demographics: 8 females, 10 males; median age 43 years (range 18-55)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0012228 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Verum acupuncture: 2 30 mm
Sham acupuncture: 1 3 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-339 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-339 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 35
EA group: 17
TM group: 18""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual stimulation: until the patient felt the sensation of qi as numbness.
Electrical stimulation: 2-4 Hz frequency, intensity up to the tolerance level of each patient, for 20 minutes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the TCM term for tension type headache)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Tension type headache (TTH)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The primary outcome regarding pain reduction showed lower VAS scores in the EA group compared to the TM group, but the difference was not statistically significant (P=0.245).
Both treatments were effective in providing sedation and analgesia, with no significant difference in stone-free rates (P=0.658).
EA was found to have no side effects, making it a favorable alternative.
The effectiveness of EA compared to the control group is inconclusive due to the lack of statistical significance in pain reduction.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: >50% reduction in number of headache daysPer four weeks from baseline to 6 months.
Secondary outcome measures: Von Korff chronicPain gradeScale
SF 12 for health related quality of life
Patient global assessment of therapy effectiveness
Medication use
Headache days
Pain intensity
Quality of life measures""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes (preparation and initial application)
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper only describes a single application of EA treatment)" .

