    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Migraine without aura" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcome of pain reduction as measured by VAS scores, with statistical significance (p < 0.001)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Changes in pain intensity measured using a Visual Analogue Scale (VAS) at various times during the study.
Secondary outcome measures: Number of patients achieving at least a 50% reduction in pain score and number of patients totally pain free at 120 minutes after needle insertion.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
