tara-kb:S-112625-341 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-341" ;
    dc:title "Role of the needling per se in acupuncture as prophylaxis for menstrually related migraine: a randomized placebo-controlled study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """GB8: above apex of ear
GB20: medial to mastoid process
LI4: first dorsal interosseus of upper limbs
Liv3 = LR3: first dorsal interosseus of lower limbs
SP6: above medial malleolus
GB14: above middle of eye-brow (for frontal pain)
Taiyang = Extra 2: between eye-brow and external canthus (for temporal pain)
Bl10 = UB10: insertion of trapezius at external protuberantia occipitalis (for occipital pain)
Acupoints were used bilaterally.
Selected based on previous studies, recommendations from manuals, and advice from the University of Traditional Chinese Medicine in Shanghai.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study is the TENS (Transcutaneous Electrical Nerve Stimulation) group, which was used as a conservative physical therapy control intervention." ;
