    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Performed with the validated Park Sham Device.
Location: Placed on the skin at standardized points on all four extremities (Achilles tendon and lateral head of the triceps) to avoid standard acupuncture meridians and points.
Penetration: Non-penetrating.
Other details: The sham procedure might not have been inert, implying potential effects despite being a sham.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """True acupuncture: Bilateral points stimulated with electroacupuncture (EA) at Bladder 23, Bladder 28, Spleen 6, and Spleen 9.
True acupuncture: Manual stimulation at Pericardium 6, Triple Energizer 5, and Governor Vessel 20.
Sham acupuncture: No stimulation intended; used the validated Park Sham Device.""" ;
