    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Difference in the number of days with headache of at least moderate intensity between baseline (month 1) and month 7.
Secondary outcome measures: Health related quality of life (SF 36), depression (ZungSelf ratingScale), headache diary entries, days headache inhibited usual activities or work.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for the first four weeks, followed by once weekly for an additional four weeks. Total intervention duration: 2 months. Part of a 5-month protocol." .

tara-kb:S-112625-346 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-346" ;
    dc:title "Needle acupuncture in tension-type headache: a randomized, placebo-controlled study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """GB20: medial to the mastoid process
LI4: first dorsal interosseus muscle of the upper limbs
LR3: first dorsal interosseus muscle of the lower limbs
GB8: above the tip of the ear
GB14: above the middle of the eye-brow
GB21: over the middle of upper border of the trapezius
GB41: lateral to the tendon of the extensor digiti longus V
UB2: medial end of the eye-brow
UB10: insertion of the trapezius at the external protuberantia occipitalis
UB60: middle between the external malleolus and the tendon of the gastrocnemius
LU7: between the tendon of the extensor pollicis and the radius
TW5: between the radius and ulna proximal to the wrist
ST8: in the angle of forehead and temple
ST36: lateral to the tibia at the level of the tuberositas tibiae
ST44: between the second and third toe in the fold
DU20: middle of the skullpan
Extra1: middle between the eye-brows""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group used in this study was a placebo acupuncture group. The placebo method involved using blunt needles that did not puncture the skin, inserted through a cube-shaped elastic foam to obscure the patients' vision on the insertion point. This was designed to be indistinguishable from the verum (actual acupuncture) treatment, serving as a control to assess the efficacy of acupuncture in tension-type headache." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
