    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Tapping a blunted cocktail-stick in a guide tube against bony prominences.
Locations: Four standard areas (occipital protuberances, spines of scapula, vertex of skull, spinous process of 6th cervical vertebra, and middle of 2nd metacarpal bone of each hand) and one individually chosen area.
Avoided areas: Site of pain, tender areas, and known acupuncture points.
Method: Gentle pressure with rotation for 15 seconds at each point.
Non-penetrating.""" ;
