tara-kb:S-112625-357 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-357" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture inhibits vagal gastric acid secretion stimulated by sham feeding in healthy subjects" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Bladder 21: lateral to the lower edge of the spiny process of the 12th thoracic vertebra
Stomach 36: lateral to the edge of the tibia below the knee joint gap
Knee joint 12: unpaired, in the middle of the line joining the tip of the sternum and the umbilicus
Sham acupuncture points: medial to the insertion of the deltoid muscle, caudal to the iliac crest in the gluteus maximus muscle""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control period: Sham feeding without acupuncture.
Sham acupuncture: Acupuncture performed at points not known to have an effect, with electrical stimulation applied.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "BL 21, ST 36, KJ 12, medial to the insertion of the deltoid muscle, caudal to the iliac crest in the gluteus maximus muscle" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:4839095,
        TARA:6463344 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4839095\": \"BL 21\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "KJ 12",
        "caudal to the iliac crest in the gluteus maximus muscle",
        "medial to the insertion of the deltoid muscle" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0002020 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Stomach 36: 3-4 cm deep
Bladder 21: 1-3 cm deep
Knee joint 12: 1 cm, then 2-3 cm caudad""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-357 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-357 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total participants initially: 8; Participants analyzed: 7; Distribution within groups: Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Performed at points not recognized as effective acupuncture points.
Location: Medial to the insertion of the deltoid muscle, caudal to the iliac crest in the gluteus maximus muscle.
Needle type: Real needles were used for sham procedure.
Penetration: The sham procedure involved penetrating the skin with needles.
Stimulation: Electrical stimulation was applied during the sham procedure.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electroacupuncture: Electrical stimulation using a device to produce a 'De-Qi' sensation (soreness, numbness, or distension).
Classic needle acupuncture: Manual manipulation by rotating or wiggling the needles every 10 minutes for 10 seconds.
Laser acupuncture: No manual or electrical stimulation; used a laser device operating at 20 Hz.
Transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation: Used adhesive electrodes and a stimulation device to produce a tingling sensation.
Sham acupuncture: Insertion at non-acupuncture points with electrical stimulation; no significant effect on gastric acid secretion.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper focuses on physiological responses rather than a specific TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Gastric acid secretion" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, electroacupuncture and transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation were effective in reducing gastric acid secretion compared to the control/sham group, with statistical significance (p<0.05)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Effect of different forms of acupuncture on gastric acid secretion stimulated by sham feeding, measured by comparing gastric acid secretion during the first and second 30-minute periods after sham feeding, as well as peak acid output.
Secondary outcome measure: Duration of the effect of electroacupuncture and transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation; effectiveness of different types of acupuncture (electroacupuncture, transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation, classic needle acupuncture, laser acupuncture, and sham acupuncture) on gastric acid secretion.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes (duration of each acupuncture session); Needles were left in place for 30 minutes during each session." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of acupuncture treatments beyond the duration of each session)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-358 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-358" ;
    dc:title "A Controlled Trial of Placebo Versus Real Acupuncture" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Large Intestine 4 (LI4) acupoint
Located at the highest point of the adductor pollicis muscle between the thumb and index finger
Used for treating head and neck pain""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control Group: Placebo Acupuncture Group
Description: Placebo acupuncture was performed by administering a blunted acupuncture needle through a foam pad at the Large Intestine 4 acupoint. The blunted needle touched but did not penetrate the skin.
Demographics: 25 subjects, male-to-female ratio of 15:10, average age of 29.04 years.
Real Acupuncture Group
Description: Real acupuncture was performed by administering an acupuncture needle through a foam pad at the Large Intestine 4 acupoint. The needle pricked and penetrated the skin to a depth of 10 to 20 mm.
Demographics: 24 subjects, male-to-female ratio of 14:10, average age of 28.83 years.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper does not mention any dataset link or availability of datasets)" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4" ;
