tara-kb:S-112625-369 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-369" ;
    dc:title "The efficacy of acupuncture in human pain models: A randomized, controlled, double-blinded study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """H√©g≈´ (Large intestine 4): Eases pain, disperses wind and regenerates yang, regulates the defensive qi. Important in acupuncture analgesia; Against pain of head, teeth, the 4 extremities, sinews and bones; Especially used to treat pain of arms.
Sh√©nm√©n (Heart 7): Calms mind, regulates and tones the heart. Relieves agitation, sleeplessness, and pain.
Quchi (Large intestine 11): Activates the meridian, relieves pain, clears heat and fire, regulates qi and blood. Relieves pain of abdomen, against painful stasis syndrome caused by wind; Good in combination with H√©g≈´.
Yanglingquan (Gallbladder 34): Relieves pain, activates the meridian, dispenses liver qi, clears humid heat in liver and gallbladder. Relieves pain in muscles of calves or bones, for illnesses of the gallbladder.
Taichong (Liver 3) (double-sided): Dispenses liver qi, suppresses liver yang, deletes wind, nourishes liver blood and liver yin, clears the head and eyes, regulates menorrhea. Relieves tension and pain in many regions of the body (eg, head, heart), against sleeplessness and fear.
Fengfu (Governing vessel 16): Eliminates wind, nourishes the sea of pulp, supports head and neck, calms mind. Relieves pain and swelling of the neck, against wind-induced stasis syndrome, relieves pain of the head, against ‚Äústiff neck‚Äù.
Xuehai (Spleen 10): Strengthens blood, removes stasis, cools down blood, harmonizes menorrhea, supports skin. Against pruritus, painful hot lesion, urticaria, problems with menorrhea.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Laser acupuncture (n = 17)
Needle acupuncture (n = 15)
Sham laser stimulation (n = 16)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4, HT 7, LI 11, GB 34, LR 3, GV 16, SP 10" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:2442762,
        TARA:3361967,
        TARA:6499349,
        TARA:8433932,
        TARA:8758950,
        TARA:8923096 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:2442762\": \"HT 7\", \"TARA:8923096\": \"LI 11\", \"TARA:8758950\": \"GB 34\", \"TARA:6499349\": \"LR 3\", \"TARA:3361967\": \"GV 16\", \"TARA:8433932\": \"SP 10\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0012531 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit information on the depth of needle insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-369 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-369 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 48
Laser acupuncture: 17
Needle acupuncture: 15
Sham laser stimulation: 16""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Sham laser stimulation
Device: Identical appearance and function to active laser device but with an inactivated laser beam
Penetration: Non penetrating
Location: Not specified (as it was a sham laser stimulation)
Needle type: Not applicable (no sham needling was used)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Needle stimulation: Manual manipulation (twirling 180 degrees during insertion), no further stimulation.
Low level laser stimulation: Infrared semiconductor laser device, 1 minute per point.
Sham stimulation: Inactivated laser beam.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Pain disorders (general) Not specified (TCM terminology not explicitly provided)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Auricular laser acupuncture: No
Needle acupuncture: Maybe/Inconclusive""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Reduction of mean pain intensity during 3 minutes of the cold-pressor test or within 10 minutes after capsaicin injection.
Secondary outcome measures: Pain reduction during different phases of both tests; time when pain became P70 during the CP test; time when pain became <10 in the capsaicin model; area of hyperalgesia; area of allodynia; neurogenic flare after capsaicin injection; area under the curve (AUC) for pain ratings.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 to 45 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: up to 40 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Daily sessions lasting between 30 to 45 minutes until the end of withdrawal." .

