tara-kb:S-112625-371 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-371" ;
    dc:title "Electro-Acupuncture at the Zusanli, Yanglingquan, and Kunlun Points Does Not Reduce Anesthetic Requirement" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Zusanli: 6 cm below the lower margin of the patella and 3 cm lateral to the tibia
Yanglingquan: in the depression just at the anterior edge of the round head of the fibula in the angle of the lower edge of the head of the tibia and posterior edge of the insertion of the extensor digitorum longus muscle
Kunlun: in the hollow between the lateral malleolus and the Achilles tendon""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control Group: Each participant served as their own control on a separate day.
Description: On control days, electrodes were connected without the acupuncture needles, meaning no actual acupuncture stimulation was applied.
Purpose: To compare the effects of electro-acupuncture on anesthetic requirement with a condition where no acupuncture was applied.""" ;
