    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation was electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) with 2-Hz and 100-Hz currents alternated at 2-s intervals. The initial intensity was increased until muscular twitching was observed. Needles were stimulated electrically, and the stimulation was started after anesthesia induction to prevent volunteers from sensing the tingling sensation." ;
