tara-kb:S-112625-374 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-374" ;
    dc:title "Crossover Clinical Trial to Determine the Effect of Manual Acupuncture at Siguan Points (Bilateral LI4 and LR3) on Intestinal Motility in Healthy Subjects" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """LI4: Located on the dorsum of the hand, between the first and second metacarpal bones, in the middle of the second metacarpal bone on the radial side.
LR3: Located on the dorsum of the foot, in the depression distal to the junction of the first and second metatarsal bones.
Sham points: On the dorsum of the hand, in the middle of the junction of the capital bone and the third metacarpal bone; on the dorsum of the foot, in the middle of the junction of the lateral cuneiform bone and the third metatarsal bone.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT) with a crossover design" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture (SA) group" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "South Korea" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4, LR 3" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:6499349 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:6499349\": \"LR 3\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """LI4: 1 cm
LR3: 1.2 cm
Sham points: 0.5 cm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-374 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-374 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total sample size: 20; Participants within groups: 20 (crossover design)" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham points: Located on the dorsum of the hand and foot, not traditional acupuncture points.
Needle type: Same as real acupuncture (stainless steel, gauge 32, diameter 0.25 mm).
Quantity: Same as real acupuncture.
Size: Same as real acupuncture.
Location: Non-traditional points on the hand and foot.
Penetration: Superficial and transverse insertion.
Other details: Needles not manipulated after insertion, retained for 30 minutes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation (rotation of needles 90¬∞ clockwise five times) at Siguan points; no manipulation at sham points." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a specific disease or condition in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the study focuses on normal intestinal motility in healthy subjects rather than a specific disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Effect of manual acupuncture on intestinal motility, evaluated through the distribution and speed of radio-markers in different parts of the digestive tract.
Secondary outcome measures: Frequency of defecation, changes in blood pressure, and complete blood counts (CBC).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration Retained: 30 minutes
Length of treatment: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Acupuncture treatments were administered every 12 hours, with four treatments in each session. Each treatment lasted for 30 minutes. There were two sessions with a 2-week washout period in between." .

