    dc:title "Effect of bidirectional rotation of an acupuncture needle at LI10 on acupuncture needle sensation and experimentally-induced contact heat pain in healthy human volunteers" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """LI10: Located on the non-dominant forearm, inserted to a depth of approximately 15-25 mm.
LI4: Mentioned as a point used during familiarization, not part of the actual experiment.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was the mock bidirectional needle rotation intervention, which involved inserting the needle without any actual rotation to control for non-specific effects of receiving an intervention." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United Kingdom" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 10, LI 4" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0742938,
        TARA:0859695 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0742938\": \"LI 10\", \"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "15-25 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-393 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-393 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total participants: 22; Participants within groups: Not specified (crossover design)" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Mock rotation
Needle type: Empty guide tube (no actual needle)
Quantity: One guide tube
Size: Not specified
Location: LI10 (same as real acupuncture)
Penetration: Non-penetrating
Other details: Guide tube rotated behind a screen to mimic needle rotation without touching the skin.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved bidirectional rotation of the acupuncture needle inserted at LI10, with the needle rotated approximately 360¬∞clockwise followed by 360¬∞anticlockwise at approximately two rotations per second (2 Hz) for 30 seconds, followed by 30 seconds of no rotation, repeated for 10 minutes. The study sought to elicit acupuncture needle sensations, which include both painful and non-painful sensations." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the study focuses on experimental heat pain in healthy volunteers rather than a specific disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention with bidirectional needle rotation was effective compared to the control/sham group (mock rotation) in increasing heat pain thresholds and needle sensation intensity, with statistical significance (p<0.001)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Effects on acupuncture needle sensations (assessed using MASS and VAS) and experimentally-induced contact heat pain (measured as heat pain thresholds).
Secondary outcome measure: Comparison between bidirectional needle rotation and mock rotation to isolate specific effects of the intervention.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place during a session: 15 minutes (10 minutes of manipulation + 5 minutes before removal)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: Two sessions with a washout period of at least 72 hours.
Duration: Each session lasted 30 minutes, with the acupuncture intervention lasting 15 minutes.
Note: The paper does not specify the frequency of treatment in a clinical setting or over a longer period.""" .

