    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Hegu (LI-4): 15 mm
Sanyinjiao (SP-6): 20 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-406 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-406 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total: 36; Electro-acupuncture group: 18; Control group: 18" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The needles were stimulated using electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) with a frequency of 2-100 Hz and an electric current of 14-30 mA. A dense-and-disperse waveform was used, and a sore and distending sensation was sought." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM condition or terminology for labor pain)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Labor pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The electro-acupuncture group was found to exhibit a lower pain intensity and a better degree of relaxation than the control group (p ¬º 0.018; p ¬º 0.031)."
"There existed a significant difference in the concentration of b-EP and 5-HT in the peripheral blood between the two groups at the end of the first stage (p ¬º 0.037; p ¬º 0.030)."
"Electroacupuncture was found to be an effective alternative or complementary therapy in the relief of pain during labor."
"The benefit of electro-acupuncture for relieving labor pain may be based on the mechanism of producing a synergism of the central nervous system (CNS) with a direct impact on the uterus through increasing the release of b-EP and 5-HT into the peripheral blood."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Assessments of pain intensity and degree of relaxation during labor.
Secondary outcome measures: Concentration of b-endorphin (b-EP) and 5-hydroxytryptamine (5-HT) in the peripheral blood.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Needles left in place during a session: 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Treatment was administered at the beginning of the active phase in the first stage of labor.
A second treatment was performed when 7 to 8 cm of cervical dilation was present.
Each treatment session lasted 20 minutes.
Frequency of treatment outside of labor is not specified.""" .

