tara-kb:S-112625-412 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-412" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture During Labor Can Reduce the Use of Meperidine: A Controlled Clinical Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Acupuncture points were selected based on patient needs such as degree of pain, localization of pain, stage of labor, and restlessness and anxiety.
Specific points mentioned include BL32 for back pain, GV20 + Sishencong, BL60, BL62, and BL67.
Needles were inserted to achieve de-qi, with depth varying based on subcutaneous adipose tissue.
Needles were manually rotated to achieve de-qi.
Duration of needling varied with different points and patient responses.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of patients selected from the labor ward protocol, matching the parity of the patients in the no acupuncture group. They did not receive acupuncture and were used for comparison purposes. The study did not use a placebo control." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (hints towards Norway due to pharmaceutical companies' addresses, but not explicitly stated)" ;
