Fifth study: 94 participants
Sixth study: 60 participants""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Sham acupuncture was defined as superficial needling of nonacupuncture points without needle manipulation, done either proximally or distally to the true acupuncture points, or both. Details on needle type, quantity, size, and whether it was penetrating or non-penetrating are not provided." ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual manipulation to achieve de qi
Electroacupuncture (electrical stimulation)
Strong stimulation during insertion and withdrawal""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Labor pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Maybe/Inconclusive (the paper reports mixed results with some studies showing significant differences in favor of acupuncture, but overall, the poor quality of the trials precludes firm conclusions)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Pain relief in labour (100-mm visual analogue scale or numeric rating scale), use of other analgesia (number of women requiring meperidine, EDA, or other pain relief)
Secondary outcomes: Maternal satisfaction with pain relief in labour, satisfaction with childbirth experience, duration of labour, augmentation of labour, mode of delivery; Fetal Apgar score at 5 minutes, birthweight, umbilical cord blood pH; Adverse events""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Study 1: 30 minutes
Study 2: 30 minutes
Study 3: 20 minutes
Study 4: 30 minutes
Study 5: 20 minutes
Study 6: 2 minutes (for control group), 30 minutes (for experimental group)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """First study: Once daily for three courses, each course lasting 15 days, with 4-day intervals between courses.
Fourth study: Once daily for six courses, each course lasting 5 days, with 2-day intervals between courses.
Fifth study: Once daily for four courses, each course lasting 5 days, with 2-day intervals between courses.
Sixth study: Once daily for 21 days.""" .

