    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-445" ;
    dc:title "The Effect of Acupuncture on Working Memory and Anxiety *" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Sishencong (EX-HN1): benefits the eyes and ears; calms the spirit; indicated for poor memory.
Shenting (GV24): benefits the brain; calms the spirit.
Yintang (EX-HN3): calms the Shen; indicated to calm anxiety and agitation.
Shenmen (Ht 7): calms the spirit; regulates and tonifies the heart; indicated for poor memory, fear and fright.
Neiguan (PC 6): indicated for poor memory, apprehension, fear and fright.
Taixi (Kd 3): chosen for its association with the brain and balancing effect on upper body points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group involved participants lying on a treatment table for 20 minutes with acupoints touched and swabbed with alcohol but no needles inserted. Participants were unaware they were in the control group until the end of the study." ;
