tara-kb:S-112625-450 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-450" ;
    dc:title "The benefit of combined acupuncture and antidepressant medication for depression: A systematic review and meta-analysis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Frequently used points: Baihui (GV20), Yingtang (EX-HN3)
Points on extremities: Shenmen (HT7), Sanyinjiao (SP6), Hegu (LI4), Neiguan (PC6)
Points on trunk: Baihui (GV20), Yingtang (EX-HN3), Dazhui (GV14), Sishencong (EX-HN1), Shenting (GV24), Fengfu (GV16), Fengchi (GB20)
Some studies used fixed acupoints, while others used flexible selection based on symptoms.
All studies used body or scalp acupuncture.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in the studies included in the meta-analysis was typically the group receiving antidepressant medications alone. This is evident from the repeated comparisons made between acupuncture combined with antidepressants and antidepressants alone throughout the paper and in the tables." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany, China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0000716 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-450 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-450 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 1046
Sample size range for individual studies: 29 to 160
Number of participants in the 6-week endpoint score analysis: 339 (162 in acupuncture combined SSRIs group, 177 in SSRIs-only group)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not provide details on sham acupuncture procedures)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual Acupuncture (MA): Needles twisted back and forth by practitioner until DeQi is achieved (numbness, soreness, or heaviness).
Electroacupuncture (EA): Needles connected to an electrical stimulator delivering high or low frequency impulses.
Acupuncture plus moxibustion: Thermal stimulation used in addition to needle stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide TCM terminology for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Depression" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Endpoint scores of the 17-item Hamilton rating scale for depression
Therapeutic response rates
Secondary outcome measures:
Treatment Emergent Symptoms Scale (TESS)
HAMD-24
Clinical Global Impressions (CGI) Scale
Health Resources and Services Administration (HRSA)
Side Effect Rating Scale (SERS)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Number of treatment sessions: 9 to 36 sessions
Duration of therapy: Most periods lasted for six weeks
Frequency of treatment sessions per week: Varied across studies (see tables on pages 4 and 5 for specific details)""" .

