    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 71
Treatment group (TG): 45
Control group (CG): 26""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the study did not include a sham acupuncture group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation involving lifting-thrusting and rotating the needle with light and smooth stimulation to achieve de qi needling sensation. Amplitude: 1-2 mm; needle rotation angle <90¬∞; frequency: 60-100 times per minute for 1-2 min." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Depression (TCM patterns: Liver depression and Spleen deficiency, Liver Qi stagnation, Heart and Spleen deficiency, Liver and Kidney Yin deficiency)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Depression" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The mean (SD) baseline total HDRS scores were 22.2 (0.60) and 22.1 (0.33) in the TG and CG, respectively."
"After the first week of treatment the HDRS score for the TG was reduced to 15.6 (0.81), significantly different from the score of 18.3 (0.55) for the CG, p<0.05."
"This significant difference was maintained to the end of the 6-week treatment period, when HDRS scores had fallen to 6.3 (0.49) and 8.2 (0.35) for the TG and CG, respectively."
"Acupuncture combined with an SSRI showed a statistically significant benefit for patients with depression in hospital over the 6-week period compared with SSRIs alone."
"A statistically significant reduction in mean HDRS score was found for the TG compared with the CG receiving SSRIs only."
"Acupuncture plus SSRIs showed a reduction of 17 total scores ( p<0.05) after 6 weeks (-1.83, 95% CI -2.07 to -1.58) and this difference was evident from the first week of intervention (-2.52, 95% CI -2.14 to -2.92)."
"Acupuncture combined with SSRIs shows a statistically significant benefit over a 6-week period compared with SSRI administration only."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome measure: 17-item Hamilton Depression Rating Scale (HDRS-17). Secondary outcome measures: Not specified." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment period: 6 weeks
Duration of needle retention:
GV14 and GV4: 5 minutes
Other points: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Daily in the mornings, 5 days a week for 6 weeks. Each session involved specific techniques and retention times, with the total number of needles used varying from six to ten." .

