tara-kb:S-112625-459 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-459" ;
    dc:title "Comparative Study Treating Attention Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) Patients Using the New Multiphase Hand Acupuncture Microsystem and Koryo Hand Therapy System" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """KHT: Somatotopic projection of the brain on the distal phalanx of the middle fingers, Shoa Yin/Tai Yang micro meridian, Kidney cerebral circulation on the hand.
Multiphase: Somatotopic projections of the brain in Phases 1, 2, and 3, specifically targeting the frontal brain, corpus callosum, and pineal gland.
Selection based on tenderness.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Group 1: Koryo Hand Therapy (KHT) treated with KHT micro meridians and somatotopic projection of the brain on the distal phalanx of the middle fingers.
Group 2: Multiphase treatment treated through needling the brain somatotopic projections in Phases 1, 2, and 3 of the Three Phase hand acupuncture microsystem.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0007743 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "1 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-459 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-459 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 40
Group 1 (Koryo Hand Therapy): 20
Group 2 (Multiphase treatment): 20""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Needles were not stimulated. They were inserted to a depth of 1 mm and left without any stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Attention Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the Three Phase hand acupuncture microsystem was found to be more effective than Koryo Hand Therapy, with 85% of patients showing statistically significant improvement compared to 50% in the KHT group. The primary outcome was measured by parents' assessment of ADHD symptoms using a numerical rating scale biweekly. No p values are explicitly mentioned in the paper." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome measure:Parents assessed ADHDSymptoms using a numerical ratingScale biweekly.Secondary outcome measures: Overall improvement, 60%‚Äì80% improvement over baseline, <50% improvement over baseline, <20% improvement over baseline." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles were left in place without stimulation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Once weekly for 30 minutes over 20 weeks" .

