tara-kb:S-112625-464 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-464" ;
    dc:title "Sedative effect of acupuncture during cataract surgery Prospective randomized double-blind study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Sham acupuncture points: volar aspect of the hand, interdigital membrane between the first and second finger on the dorsal aspect of the hand, medial aspect of the forearm 6 cm above the wrist, medial aspect of the forearm 6 cm below the elbow, scaphoid fossa of the ear, dorsum of the foot distally to the joint between the third and fourth metatarsal bone.
True acupuncture points: Not specified (chosen based on TCM criteria for sedation and analgesia, distant from ophthalmic operative field, not on the back).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Group A: No intervention, patients left alone in a quiet room for 20 minutes.
Group C: Sham acupuncture, performed in areas traditionally devoid of an acupuncture effect.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Italy" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005129 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-464 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-464 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 75
Participants per group: 25 (Group A), 25 (Group B), 25 (Group C)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture was performed in areas traditionally devoid of an acupuncture effect.
Locations included: volar aspect of the hand, interdigital membrane between the first and second finger on the dorsal aspect of the hand, interdigital membrane between the first and second finger on the medial aspect of the forearm, 6 cm above the wrist, 6 cm below the elbow, scaphoid fossa of the ear, and dorsum of the foot distally to the joint between the third and fourth metatarsal bone.
No details on needle type (real vs. sham), quantity, or size are provided.
No information on whether the procedure was penetrating or non-penetrating.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual stimulation was applied to the needles until the needling sensation (De Qi) was evoked." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the disease/condition in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cataract" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, acupuncture was found to be effective in reducing anxiety compared to the control/sham groups, as indicated by significant differences in preoperative and postoperative anxiety VAS scores (P Z.001, A versus B; P Z .003, A versus B)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Reduction of anxiety in patients undergoing cataract surgery under topical anesthesia, measured by a VAS postoperative anxiety evaluation of 6.
Secondary outcome measures: Preoperative anxiety VAS score, postoperative anxiety VAS score.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Throughout surgery (approximately 15 minutes on average)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper only describes a single session of acupuncture during cataract surgery)" .

