    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 91
Participants within groups: 27 per group (as calculated for the study design)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real (occlusive press needles)
Quantity: Three needles
Size: Pyonex-small
Location: Non-traditional points with no documented effect on anxiety
Penetrating: Yes
Other details: Needles were placed on the nondominant side of the external ear for 30 minutes without stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The needles were not stimulated. They were occlusive press needles placed without any stimulation. No type of sensation was sought." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state a primary medical condition or disease in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the study focuses on preoperative anxiety rather than a specific disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group for the Relaxation group (P = 0.01), but not for the TCM group (P = 0.28)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome measure: State-Trait Anxiety Inventory (STAI), specifically the state anxiety subscale (STAIS). Secondary outcome measures: Not specified." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes; Needles were left in place for the entire 30-minute session." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not mention the frequency of treatment, only the duration of a single session)" .

