    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-471 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 151
Specific acupuncture intervention: 50
Nonspecific acupuncture intervention: 49
Waitlist: 52""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used; instead, an active nonspecific acupuncture intervention was used as a control)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual stimulation; de qi sensation sought; needles retained for 20 minutes." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM term for the condition being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Major Depressive Disorder (MDD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The primary outcome measure was the HAM-D 17, which showed a significant decrease in depression severity across all subjects (p < .001).
Both SPEC and NONSPEC acupuncture groups showed greater decreases in severity compared to the waitlist group (p < .001), but did not differ from each other (p > .2).
Response rates: SPEC 22%, NONSPEC 39%, waitlist 17% (p < .05).
Remission rates: SPEC 16%, NONSPEC 33%, waitlist 8% (p < .01).
Acupuncture was effective compared to the control group, but there was no differential efficacy between SPEC and NONSPEC interventions.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Hamilton Rating Scale for Depression (HAM-D 17)
Secondary outcome measure: Beck Depression Inventory (BDI)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "20 minutes (needles retained for 20 minutes)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for the first 4 weeks, then once weekly for the next 4 weeks; 12 sessions in total over 8 weeks." .

tara-kb:S-112625-472 a TARA:6701896,
