    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Core features of ASD (social interaction, communication, behavioral problems) as measured by Aberrant Behavior Checklist (ABC), Ritvo-Freeman Real Life Rating Scale (RFRLRS), Autism Treatment Evaluation Checklist (ATEC), and Autism Diagnostic Observation Scale (ADOS).
Secondary outcome measures: Global functioning (Pediatric Evaluation Disability Inventory (PEDI), Functional Independence Measure for Children (WeeFIM)), Quality of life (WHOQOL-BREF), Frequency of adverse effects (needle pain, tiredness, bleeding, faintness, syncope, pneumothorax).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes (for acupoints stimulation), 50 minutes (for electroacupuncture)
Frequency of sessions: Daily for 3 days/week for 8 weeks (for acupoints stimulation), once daily, 5 sessions/week for 2 months (for electroacupuncture)
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """In one study, acupuncture was administered daily for 3 days a week, with each session lasting 30 minutes, over a period of 8 weeks.
In another study, electroacupuncture was applied once daily, with sessions lasting 50 minutes, five times a week, for two months.
In a third study, treatment lasted 45 minutes per session, administered daily for five days a week, over a period of 6 to 9 months.""" .

