tara-kb:S-112625-484 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-484" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for Alzheimer's disease: a systematic review" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "GV20, Sishenchong (EX), GB20, BL23, HT7, PC6, SP6, KI3, ST36, ST40, LR3, Yintang (EX), GV14" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review of Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Donepezil alone
Conventional drug therapy
Herbal mixture
Psychological consultation
Nimodipine""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0004975 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-484 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-484 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the total sample size or specific numbers for each group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not provide specific details about sham acupuncture procedures)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) was used in some studies. Other forms of stimulation are not specified." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide TCM terminology for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Alzheimer's disease (AD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"Acupuncture combined with donepezil showed a significant difference in effectiveness rate [RR=1.45, 95% CI (1.19, 1.77), P=0.0002] compared with donepezil."
"On the comparison of mini-mental state examination (MMSE) score and Alzheimer's disease assessment scale cognitive subscale (ADAS-Cog) score there was no difference."
"However, after one trial with severe AD patients was removed, acupuncture combined with donepezil showed better effect than donepezil alone."
"Acupuncture combined with donepezil could work on AD at the early stage or being mild, implying that acupuncture could be a complementary therapy for AD at the early stage or being mild."
"Besides, scalp acupuncture seems to be more effective on improving cognitive function."
"However, this conclusion must be considered cautiously, given the small sample size and lack of trials with high quality."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Mini Mental Status Examination (MMSE), activities of daily living (ADL)
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Study 1: 30 minutes
Study 2: 40 minutes (15 minutes continuous wave + 25 minutes longitudinal wave)
Study 3: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit information on the frequency of acupuncture treatments)" .

