Needle type: Sham PN had no needle.
Quantity and size: Not specified in detail, but sham PN was designed to mimic active PN without actual penetration.
Location: Not specified, but likely applied at the same points as active PN to maintain blinding.
Other details: Sham PN was used to create a double-blind, placebo-controlled design.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation was provided by press needles (PN) that were left in place for 72 hours to continuously stimulate the targeted acupoints. No additional stimulation methods like manual manipulation, electrical stimulation, or thermal stimulation were mentioned." ;
