Reduction in the severity of depression (measured by self-rating scales like Beck Depression Inventory or clinician-rated scales like Hamilton Rating Scale for Depression)
Improvement in depression (defined as remission versus no remission)
Secondary outcomes:
Quality of life indices (e.g., Short Form 36 Health Status questionnaire)
Change in use of medication or use of other support systems
Adverse events
Acceptability of acupuncture (assessed by participant questioning or satisfaction measures)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 53 minutes (average overall contact time)
Needle retention time: 20 minutes (median), range 1-60 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit details on the frequency of treatment sessions, such as how often they were administered per week or month)" .

