    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 56
Acupuncture group: 29
Sham control group: 27""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham auricular acupuncture was performed at non-acupuncture points (Wrist, Shoulder, and Extraauricular sham points).
The same type of needles (sterile, single-use, sticker press needles, 0.25 mm œ´ 2 mm) was used for both real and sham auricular acupuncture.
Sham body acupuncture was performed at the same points as real acupuncture (Bilateral Liver 3 and Large Intestine 4) but with very superficial insertion (1-2 mm).
No electrical stimulation was delivered to the sham group.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) with specific parameters: frequency of 2 Hz, voltage of 25 V, and a pulse width of 4 milliseconds. The waveform was symmetrical biphasic with spikeshaped waves. The sham group did not receive electrical stimulation. Some sensation, possibly vibration, was expected or sought during the stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Kidney stones (renal or upper ureteral calculi)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes:
Preprocedural anxiety
Intraprocedural alfentanil consumption
Visual analogue scale for pain
Secondary outcomes (implied):
Pain scores at discharge (assessed by SF-MPQ)
Fentanyl requirements in the recovery room""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper describes a single session of acupuncture during lithotripsy but does not specify the frequency of treatment over time)" .

