tara-kb:S-112625-501 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-501" ;
    dc:title "Combination of Acupuncture and Fluoxetine for Depression: A Randomized, Double-Blind, Sham-Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Verum Acupuncture (VA) Group: GV20 (Baihui), EX-HN1 (Sishencong), EX-HN3 (Yintang), GV26 (Shuigou), P6 (Neiguan), H7 (Shenmen), Liv3 (Taichong), LI4 (Hegu)
Sham Acupuncture (SA) Group: Nonspecific locations near the above points, not recognized as true acupoints or meridians""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study was the SA (sham acupuncture) group, which received sham acupuncture and 20-30 mg/day fluoxetine. Sham acupuncture involved needling at nonspecific locations to mimic real acupuncture without actual therapeutic effect." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GV 20, EX-HN 1, EX-HN 3, GV 26, P 6, H 7, Liv 3, LI 4" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0829128,
        TARA:0859695,
        TARA:2442762,
        TARA:3135569,
        TARA:3386254,
        TARA:4311153,
        TARA:6499349,
        TARA:9610280 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:3386254\": \"GV 20\", \"TARA:9610280\": \"Sishencong\", \"TARA:3135569\": \"Yintang\", \"TARA:0829128\": \"GV 26\", \"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\", \"TARA:2442762\": \"HT 7\", \"TARA:6499349\": \"LR 3\", \"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0002009 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """GV20 and EX-HN1: 13 mm (oblique)
GV26: 13‚Äì25 mm (oblique)
P6 and H7: 25 mm (perpendicular)
Liv3 and LI4: 13‚Äì25 mm (perpendicular)
EX-HN3: 5‚Äì15 mm (perpendicular)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-501 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-501 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 80
VA group: 40
SA group: 40""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles were used for sham acupuncture.
Quantity: Not specified.
Size: Not specified.
Location: Nonspecific locations in the neighborhood of real acupoints, not recognized as true acupoints or meridians.
Penetration: Superficial insertion, 1-4 mm deep.
Other details: Shallow insertion with minimal manual stimulation to minimize needle sensation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation to achieve a good needle sensation described as soreness, numbness, heaviness, or distension." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Major Depressive Disorder (MDD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The primary outcome measure (therapeutic response rate based on HRSD score change) did not show a statistically significant difference between the VA and SA groups (p = 0.07).
Acupuncture was effective in improving anxiety symptoms and reducing antidepressant side-effects compared to sham acupuncture (p = 0.01 and p < 0.001, respectively).
The intervention was considered effective for patients with severe anxious symptoms or intolerable side-effects.
The overall rate of adverse events due to acupuncture was low (8.75%).
Conclusion: Acupuncture is as effective as a recommended dose of fluoxetine when added to low-dose fluoxetine, particularly for patients with severe anxious symptoms or intolerable side-effects.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Therapeutic response rate based on the rate of total score change in the 17-item Hamilton Rating Scale for Depression (HRSD)
Secondary outcome measures:
Changes in HRSD scores
Changes in Hamilton Rating Scale for Anxiety (HRSA) scores
Evaluation of antidepressant side effects using the Asberg Rating Scale for Side Effects (SERS)
Evaluation of acupuncture-specific side effects using a predefined checklist""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment: 6 weeks
Frequency: 5 times a week
Duration retained (VA group): 30 minutes
Duration retained (SA group): Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "5 times a week for 6 weeks" .

