    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "sweating syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Spontaneous polyhidrosis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group. The total effective rate for acupuncture was 96.7% compared to 57.7% for western medicine, with a significant difference (P<0.01)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Total effective rate (cured or improved)
Secondary outcome measures: Amount and frequency of abnormal sweating (implied by definitions of cured and improved)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes (duration of each session); Needles retained for 30 minutes during each session" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was given once daily. Each course of treatment lasted for ten days, with a one-day interval between courses. The total duration of treatment was three courses." .

