tara-kb:S-112625-510 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-510" ;
    dc:title "Pharmacopuncture in Korea: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """12 meridian points and/or extra points (used in 19 studies)
Ashi points (used in 2 studies)
Tender points (used in 4 studies)
Dr. Dong's acupuncture point (used in 1 study)
Abdomen (approximate area mentioned in 1 study)
Area between the flexor carpi radialis tendon and the median nerve (approximate area mentioned in 1 study)
Left and right sides of four points inferior to and four points superior to the navel points on the stomach and the spleen and gallbladder meridians (approximate area mentioned in 1 study)
Specific acupoints listed in tables at the end of the paper (not specified in text)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Placebo or sham interventions: injections of normal saline or distilled water into pharmacopuncture points or nonacupuncture points.
Other interventions: tuina manual treatment, acupuncture, herbal/western medicine, cupping, physical therapy (including hot pack, TENS, ICT, ultrasound, massage, and exercise).
Control procedures categorized into four types:
1. Comparison with normal saline or distilled water.
2. Comparison with tuina manual treatment.
3. Comparison with acupuncture.
4. Comparison of pharmacopuncture plus other interventions versus other interventions alone.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Korea" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419,
        MONDO:0011122 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "5 to 30 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-510 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-510 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 1,211
Range of participants in pharmacopuncture group: 10 to 37
Range of participants in control group: 9 to 46
Median sample sizes per arm: Pharmacopuncture group = 17, Control group = 18""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not describe a sham acupuncture procedure with needles)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper focuses on pharmacopuncture involving herbal injections and does not explicitly mention needle stimulation techniques)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "- Obesity - Musculoskeletal conditions (including low back pain and cervicalgia) - Bell's palsy" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, pharmacopuncture was found to be effective compared to control groups in reducing weight and waist circumference for obesity and in reducing pain intensity for musculoskeletal conditions. However, the evidence is limited by methodological flaws and small sample sizes." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Intensity of discomfort (visual analogue scale, numeric rating scale), quality-of-life-related scales, Yanagihara score for Bell's palsy, neck disability index for cervicalgia, Oswestry disability index for low back pain.
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each pharmacopuncture session or the retention time of the needles)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment varied from 3 to 16 sessions over 6 days to 8 weeks. Specific details about the frequency (e.g., daily, twice weekly) are not explicitly stated in the text but are likely detailed in the tables." .

tara-kb:S-112625-511 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-511" ;
    dc:title "Clinical Observation on Acupuncture Treatment of Alopecia Areata" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Major acupoints: Shenshu (BL 23), Ganshu (BL 18), Taixi (KI 3), Sanyinjiao (SP 6), Xuehai (SP 10), Geshu (BL 17), Zusanli (ST 36), Fengchi (GB 20), Baihui (GV 20), Shangxing (GV 23), Shuaigu (GB 8)
Adjunct acupoints: Neiting (ST 44) for alopecia above the forehead, Taichong (LR 3) for alopecia on the vertex, Waiguan (TE 5) for alopecia on the sides of the head, Houxi (SI 3) for alopecia on the occiput
Functions: Ganshu and Shenshu for nourishing yin and replenishing blood, Sanyinjiao for regulating liver, spleen, and kidney, Zusanli for strengthening digestive functions
Locations: Not specified in the paper""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 35 cases treated with oral administration of Cystine tablets, Vitamin B1, and topical application of Minoxidil Solution." ;
