    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation (twisting technique for tonify and sedation, reinforcing technique) with needling sensation sought; needles retained for 30 min and manipulated every 10 min." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Oil Wind" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Alopecia areata" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"The curative effect and total effective rate were 58.1% and 97.7% in the treatment group, and 34.3% and 77.1% in the control group respectively, with statistical differences in the curative rate and total effective rate between the two groups (both P<0.05)."
"Conclusion: Acupuncture is better than medications in the treatment of alopecia areata."
"The findings indicate that the therapeutic effect is better in the treatment group than in the control group."
"By statistical management, the comparison of curative rate showed œá 2 =4.40, P<0.05 between the two groups, with statistical difference. By the statistical management, the comparison of the effective rate showed œá 2 =6.08, P<0.05 between the two groups, with statistical difference too."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Curative effect: New hair all grew out, with dense distribution and normal color, negative in the hairPulling test.
Total effective rate: Includes cure, remarkable effect, and effect based onSpecific criteria related to hair growth and density.
Secondary outcome measures:
Hair growth and density (implicitlyStated through the definitions of cure, remarkable effect, and effect)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles retained for: 30 minutes
Manipulation frequency: Once every 10 minutes
Treatment frequency: Once every 2 days
Number of sessions per course: 10""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was administered once every 2 days, with each course consisting of 10 sessions. The therapeutic effects were assessed after 4 courses." .

