    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "Local pressure pain sensitivity at baseline and during conditioned pain modulation decreased significantly more following acupuncture compared with relaxation (time ¬• group interactions: p < 0.001), both in the neck and at a site distinct from the painful region."
Effectiveness: Yes (for local pressure pain sensitivity), No (for conditioned pain modulation and temporal summation)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Immediate activation of endogenous analgesia (pressure pain sensitivity and conditioned pain modulation)
Secondary outcome measures: Pain relief and reduced disability level""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Each patient received two treatment sessions, one with acupuncture and one with relaxation, with each session lasting 20 minutes. There was a 1-week wash-out period between the sessions." .

tara-kb:S-112625-523 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-523" ;
    dc:title "Neck Pain Treatment With Acupuncture: Does the Number of Needles Matter?" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Group A: Houxi-SI3 (proximal to the head of the V metacarpal, C8 dermatome), Waiguan-TE 5 (2 cm above the transverse bend on the dorsal side of the wrist, C6 to C7 to C8 myomere and C7 dermatome), Shenmai-BL62 (depression below the lateral malleolus, S1 dermatome), Fengchi-GB20 (neck below the occipital bone, C2 to C3 to C4 myomere and C-2 dermatome), Dazhui-GV14 (between the 7th cervical vertebrae and the spinal process of the 1st thoracic vertebrae, C8 dermatome), and two most painful trigger points.
Group B: Houxi-SI3 (proximal to the head of the V metacarpal, C8 dermatome), Dazhui-GV14 (between the 7th cervical vertebrae and the spinal process of the 1st thoracic vertebrae, C8 dermatome), and two most painful trigger points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Not applicable (the study compared two different acupuncture protocols without a control group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Italy" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
