tara-kb:S-112625-533 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-533" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture plus Acupoint Injection for Treatment of Cervical Spondylosis of VertebroarterialType" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Jiaji points: Located between the Governor Vessel and Gallbladder Channel of Foot Taiyang, along the neck and back.
Fengchi (GB 20): Expels wind and clears collaterals, promotes local qi activity and blood supply to the neck and back.
Taixi (KI 3): Strengthens the kidney and replenishes its essence.
Sanyinjiao (SP 6): Supplements qi and blood.
Zusanli (ST 36): Supplements qi and blood, strengthens the spleen to remove phlegm.
Taichong (LR 3): Inhibits liver yang.
Fenglong (ST 40): Strengthens the spleen to remove phlegm.
Dazhui (GV 14): Enhances yang and improves immune function.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received simple acupuncture. The control group consisted of 33 cases, with 13 males and 20 females, aged from 35 to 70 years, and the duration of illness was 7 120 months with an average of 31.0¬±76.9 months." ;
