    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 24
Test group (TG): Not specified
Control group (CG): Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham group: Control Group (CG)
Electroacupuncture: No voltage applied, but instrument produced a beep
Body Acupuncture: Needles inserted 10-40 mm distal to real acupoints
Ear Acupressure: Applied 4-6 mm below real acupoints
Penetrating vs. Non-penetrating: Penetrating needles used at non-acupoints""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) with a sinus wave lasting 100 ms and an amplitude of 170-200 V, at a frequency of 5 Hz, lasting 30 minutes. Needles were also rotated every 5 minutes as part of the manual manipulation. No thermal or laser stimulation was mentioned. The control group did not receive any electrical stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM condition or disease)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic neck and shoulder pain and related headache" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Reduction in chronic neck and shoulder pain, related headache, intensity and frequency of pain, degree of headache, pain threshold (PPT) measurements.
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 45 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Three treatments per week for 3-4 weeks, with each treatment lasting 45 minutes. Additionally, subjects performed ear acupressure several times daily." .

tara-kb:S-112625-537 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-537" ;
    dc:title "Tension neck syndrome treated by acupuncture combined with physiotherapy: A comparative clinical trial (pilot study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Chinese acupuncture: Body points selected based on TCM syndromes (e.g., LR.3, LI.4, SP6, ST.36, K.3, Ex.HN.3).
YNSA: Kinetic points B and C in the forehead; Ypsilon points Y1, Y4, Y5 in the temporal region.
Selection criteria: TCM syndromes for body points; YNSA-ND for scalp points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Placebo acupuncture: Used in three RCTs to compare with acupuncture.
Conventional medication: Used as a control or comparison group in RCTs assessing acupuncture adjunctive to conventional drugs.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Brazil" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0030833 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Body points: 10-15 mm
Scalp points (kinetic points): 1-2 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-537 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-537 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide a total sample size for all participants or a breakdown of participants within groups across all studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure involved nonacupoints acupuncture or electroacupuncture.
Park et al.'s study used nonacupoints acupuncture as a sham.
Chae et al.'s study used covert and overt placebo sham acupuncture at acupoint GB34.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation methods included needle acupuncture, electroacupuncture, and bee venom acupuncture.
Electroacupuncture was used with varying frequencies and durations, such as 50 Hz for 30 minutes and 4 Hz for 20 minutes.
Manual manipulation and thermal stimulation (moxibustion) are not specified as being used.
Specific sensations sought during stimulation are not mentioned.
Needles were stimulated using electroacupuncture in some studies.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Liver-Qi-Stagnation associated with Kidney-Yin-Deficiency" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Tension Neck Syndrome (TNS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Pain intensity (VAS pain), muscular tension (VAS mt), functional disability (NDI-BR), isometric neck muscle strength (INMS)
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Park et al. (2007): 15 minutes
Cho et al. (2012): Needle acupuncture 15 minutes; Bee venom acupuncture 20 minutes
Huang et al. (2009 and 2010): Electroacupuncture 30 minutes
Shulman et al. (2002): 2 hours
Ha et al. (2003): Not specified
Kang et al. (2004): Not specified
Cristian et al. (2005): Not specified
Eng et al. (2006): Not specified
Jung et al. (2006): Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Park et al.: Twice weekly for 4 weeks
Huang et al.: Six times weekly for 5 weeks
Cho et al.: Twice weekly for 8 weeks
Ha et al.: Twice weekly for 8 weeks
Kang et al.: Twice weekly for 8 weeks
Eng et al.: Once weekly for 24 weeks""" .

