tara-kb:S-112625-539 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-539" ;
    dc:title "Forty six Cases ofthe Nerve Root Involved Cervical Spondylopathy Treated by Needling the Sitian Points" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Primary acupoints: Tianyou (SJ 16), Tianrong (SI 17), Tianchuang (SI 16), Tianding (LI 17), Lieque (LU 7)
Additional points based on symptoms:
Jianzhongshu (SI 15) and Jianwaishu (SI 14) for heaviness and pain in the back
Yangxi (LI 5), Yangchi (SJ 4), and Yanggu (SI 5) for pain and numbness in the fingers
Dazhui (GV 14) and Shangxing (GV 23) for pain while bending forward and stretching backward
Location: Sitian points are in the sternomastoid muscle area
Meridian associations: Tianding (LI 17)Hand Yangming Meridian, Tianchuang (SI 16) and Tianrong (SI 17)Hand Taiyang Meridian, Tianyou (SJ 16)Hand Shaoyang Meridian""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 22 cases treated by needling at cervical Jiaji points (C3 C7)." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "SJ 16, SI 17, SI 16, LI 17, LU 7, SI 15, SI 14, LI 5, SJ 4, SI 5, GV 14, GV 23, C3 C7 Jiaji" ;
