        TARA:3515622,
        TARA:5246417,
        TARA:5677319,
        TARA:7690229,
        TARA:8452754,
        TARA:9834019 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:9834019\": \"TE 16\", \"TARA:3389422\": \"SI 17\", \"TARA:5246417\": \"SI 16\", \"TARA:2260412\": \"LI 17\", \"TARA:3515622\": \"LU 7\", \"TARA:2976260\": \"SI 15\", \"TARA:3226024\": \"SI 14\", \"TARA:5677319\": \"LI 5\", \"TARA:1594912\": \"TE 4\", \"TARA:0669306\": \"SI 5\", \"TARA:8452754\": \"GV 14\", \"TARA:7690229\": \"GV 23\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "C3 C7 Jiaji" ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Tianyou (SJ 16): 1 1.5 cun
Tianrong (SI 17) and Tianchuang (SI 16): 1 1.5 cun
Tianding (LI 17): 1 1.5 cun
Lieque (LU 7): 0.5 cun
Cervical Jiaji points: 1 1.5 cun""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-539 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-539 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 68
Treatment group: 46
Control group: 22""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not include a sham acupuncture group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved manual manipulation using a pecking maneuver (lifting and thrusting with small amplitude) at specific frequencies to elicit a needling sensation that radiates to specific areas. The needles were manipulated once during a 30 minute retention period." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Nerve root involved cervical spondylopathy" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The results showed that the markedly effective rate was 78.3% and 54.5%, respectively in the treatment group and the control group, with a significant difference (P<0.05).
Needling at "Sitian" points was more effective than needling at cervical Jiaji points in improving clinical symptoms, physical signs, and pain.
Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Visual AnalogueScale (VAS) for painSensation,Semeiographic format for clinicalSymptoms, working and living ability, hand functions, and physicalSigns.
Secondary outcome measures: Therapeutic effects categorized as clinically cured, markedly effective, improved, and failed.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "30 minutes" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The treatment was given once every other day, with 10 sessions constituting a therapeutic course. The therapeutic effects were evaluated after 2 therapeutic courses." .

