tara-kb:S-112625-540 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-540" ;
    dc:title "The Therapeutic Effects of Acupuncture on Patients with Chronic Neck Myofascial Pain Syndrome: A Single-Blind Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Fenhchi (GB20); Jianliao (TE14); Houxi (SI3).
Chosen based on meridian theory of Traditional Chinese Medicine, focusing on the governor vessel (GV) and the connection of Houxi acupoints to the GV.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Single-Blind Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Placebo injection: Used as a control group to compare the effectiveness of acupuncture and sumatriptan.
Note: The study lacks a sham acupuncture control group.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Taiwan" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GB 20, TE 14, SI 3" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0220496,
        TARA:2324295,
        TARA:5894876 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:2324295\": \"GB 20\", \"TARA:5894876\": \"TE 14\", \"TARA:0220496\": \"SI 3\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0030833 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Acupuncture Group (AG): Not specified (depth in cun, no conversion provided)
Sham Acupuncture Group (SG): About 2 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-540 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-540 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 179
Acupuncture group: 60
Sumatriptan group: 58
Placebo group: 61""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the study did not include a sham acupuncture control group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation to achieve a numb, warm feeling around the acupuncture point (de qi)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic neck myofascial pain syndrome (MPS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"A full migraine attack was prevented in 21 of 60 (35%) patients receiving acupuncture, 21 of 58 (36%) patients receiving sumatriptan and 11 of 61 (18%) patients receiving placebo (relative risk of having a full attack 0.79 (95% CI, 0.64 0.99) for acupuncture versus placebo, and 0.78 (95% CI, 0.62 0.98) for sumatriptan versus placebo)."
"The difference between acupuncture and placebo was statistically significant (Fisher's exact test, P = 0.028)."
"In this trial acupuncture and sumatriptan were more effective than a placebo injection in the early treatment of an acute migraine attack."
"When an attack could not be prevented, sumatriptan was more effective than acupuncture at relieving headache."
"In conclusion, our trial provides evidence that both s.c. sumatriptan and acupuncture are more effective than a placebo injection in the early treatment of acute attacks in a population of hospitalized migraine sufferers."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Quality of life as assessed with Short Form-36 (SF-36)
Secondary outcome measures:
Neck range of motion (ROM)
Motion-related pain (assessed with a visual analogue scale, VAS)
Short-Form McGill Pain Questionnaire (SF-MPQ)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Median 1.5 hours (range, 0.5 2.1 hours)
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of acupuncture treatments in terms of how often they were administered over time)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-541 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-541" ;
    dc:title "Analysis on the Effect of Acupuncture in Treating Cervical Spondylosis with Different Syndrome Types" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Treatment Group: Dazhui (DU14), Bailao (Ex-HN15), Jianzhongshu (SI15)
Control Group: Points 1 cm apart laterally from Bailao and Jianzhongshu
Needle Size: Treatment Group 40 mm length, 0.3 mm diameter; Control Group 40 mm length, 0.22 mm diameter
Depth of Insertion: Treatment Group to muscular layer; Control Group to subcutaneous layer""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 58 patients who received sham acupuncture. Sham acupuncture involved needling at points 1 cm apart from actual acupoints, with superficial insertion and no manipulation, serving as a placebo control to compare with the actual acupuncture treatment." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "DU 14, EX-HN 15, SI 15" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:2976260,
        TARA:5153816,
        TARA:8452754 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:8452754\": \"GV 14\", \"TARA:5153816\": \"Bailao\", \"TARA:2976260\": \"SI 15\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0008480 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Treatment group: reaching the depth of the muscular layer
Control group: superficially reaching the subcutaneous layer (just penetrating the epidermal layer)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-541 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-541 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants enrolled: 117
Treatment group: 59
Control group: 58
Participants analyzed after dropouts: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture was used in the control group.
Needles were 40 mm in length and 0.22 mm in diameter.
Needling was done at points 1 cm apart laterally from acupoints Bailao and Jianzhongshu.
Needles were inserted superficially, only reaching the subcutaneous layer.
Needles were kept in place for 20 minutes without further manipulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Treatment group: Manual manipulation to achieve "Deqi" sensation.
Control group: No stimulation (sham acupuncture).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Cervical spondylosis differentiated into 5 syndrome types: windcold-damp type (A), qi-stagnancy with blood-stasis type (B), phlegm-dampness blocking Collateral type (C), Gan-Shen insufficiency type (D), and qi-blood deficiency type (E)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cervical spondylosis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, acupuncture was found to be effective compared to the control/sham group in the short term, with statistically significant differences in NPQ and VAS scores (P<0.05). However, its long-term effect was not satisfactory. The effectiveness varied by syndrome type, with significant influence on VAS scores but not on NPQ scores." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Northwick Park Neck Pain Questionnaire (NPQ), Visual Analogue Scale (VAS)
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration retained (needles left in place): 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The acupuncture treatments were administered once every other day, with a total of 9 treatments in 18 days constituting one therapeutic course." .

tara-kb:S-112625-542 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-542" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture versus Placebo for the Treatment of Chronic Mechanical Neck Pain A Randomized, Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Needle sizes: 13 mm ~ 0.25 mm, 25 mm ~ 0.25 mm, 40 mm~0.25 mm
Point selection based on individualized western acupuncture techniques and clinical consensus
Points chosen based on pain distribution and palpation for ah-shi points
Six points on average per side for bilateral pain, with at least one distal point
Specific points:
Primary local neck points: GB 20, 21; GV 14
Secondary alternative local neck points: SI 12, 13, 14; BL 9, 10; ST 11; SI 15, 16; BL 11, 41, 15, 17; GB 29; TE 16, 17; GV 15, 16, 17
Primary distal points: LI 4, SI 3, GB 34, TE 5
Secondary alternative distal points: LI 11; SI 8; TE 10, 36, 39, 40; BL 60; extra Luozhen""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received mock transcutaneous electrical stimulation of acupuncture points using a decommissioned electroacupuncture stimulation unit. This sham intervention involved the use of visual and audio signals but did not deliver any actual electrical current to the patients." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United Kingdom" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly provide a dataset link or mention the availability of a dataset)" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0030833,
        MONDO:0002253,
        MONDO:0005178 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-542 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-542 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 124
Acupuncture group: 70
Placebo group: 65""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Mock transcutaneous electrical stimulation of acupuncture points
Device: Decommissioned Noma FM-4 electroacupuncture stimulator
Electrodes: Reusable, connected to severed cables to prevent actual stimulation
Stimulation: No actual electrical stimulation; visual and audio signals only
Needle type: Not applicable (no needles used)
Quantity and size: Not applicable (no needles used)
Location: Same as real acupuncture points for appearance, but no actual stimulation
Penetrating or non-penetrating: Non-penetrating (electrodes on skin surface)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation to achieve deqi sensation" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM equivalent for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic Mechanical Neck Pain (associated with cervical spondylosis and osteoarthritis)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "For the primary outcome (weeks 1 to 5), a statistically significant difference in visual analogue scale score in favor of acupuncture (6.3 mm [95% CI, 1.4 to 11.3 mm]; P ‚Ä´ÿç‚Ä¨ 0.01) was observed between the 2 study groups, after adjustment for baseline pain and other covariates."
Effectiveness: No (statistically significant but not clinically significant)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome: Pain score 1 week after treatment, measured using a visual analogue scale (VAS).
Secondary outcomes:
Pain scores at other time points (measured using VAS).
Score on the Neck Disability Index (NDI).
Score on the Short Form-36 (SF-36).
Use of analgesic medications.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "20 minutes; needles were left in place for the duration of the session" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Patients were treated twice per week for 4 weeks. Each treatment session lasted 20 minutes." .

