    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size initially enrolled: 160
Total sample size analyzed: 127
Group TA: 32
Group RMA: 30
Group SMA: 31
Group R: 34""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """RMA (Ritualized Mock Acupuncture): Non-penetrating, using a small foam cylinder on the skin with blunted needles to simulate needle insertion. Needles touched but did not penetrate the skin. Simulated "arrival of Qi" with slight pressure and rotation.
SMA (Standard Mock Acupuncture): Used real acupoints with a Western approach. Method of insertion was the same as RMA, implying non-penetrating, but details are not explicitly provided.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """True Acupuncture (TA): Manual manipulation with large rotations (>360¬∞) for reducing method and small rotations (<360¬∞) for reinforcing method, repeated 3 times at 5-minute intervals.
Ritualized Mock Acupuncture (RMA): Simulated stimulation with blunted needles touching but not penetrating the skin, with slight pressure and rotation within a foam cylinder to simulate "arrival of Qi.\"""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly translate the condition into Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Dizziness/Vertigo of suspected cervical origin" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Effects of different therapies on dizziness/vertigo
Effects of different therapies on cervical pain
Effects of different therapies on cervical kinesthetic sensibility
Use of a 100 mm visual analogue scale (VAS) for dizziness and neck pain
Ability to perceive position of the head with respect to the trunk
Secondary outcome measures:
Duration of dizziness/vertigo complaints
Cervical range of motion""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration of needles left in place during a session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice a week, 2 courses of 10 acupuncture applications each, with a 1-week rest between courses. Each session lasted 30 minutes." .

