    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles were used for both groups, but the sham group received needles at non-traditional points.
Quantity and size: Not specified in detail, but the same type of needles were likely used for both groups.
Location: Sham points were used, which were 10-40mm distal to actual acupuncture points for body acupuncture and 4-6mm below actual points for ear acupressure.
Penetrating vs. non-penetrating: The sham procedure involved penetrating needles at non-traditional points, but non-penetrating electrostimulation (no voltage applied).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) was used. The stimulation was given through flat electrodes with a pulse width of 100¬µs and an amplitude of 170-200V, followed by a reversed current decaying exponentially over 10ms. The stimulation was applied for 30 minutes at 5Hz. Needles were inserted bilaterally in three body points to a depth of 10-30mm after starting electrostimulation." ;
