    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """True Acupuncture Group: Electroacupuncture (EA) with manual manipulation to achieve de qi sensation; electrical stimulation at 10 Hz with intensity adjusted to patient tolerance (max 10 mA).
Sham Acupuncture Group: No stimulation; needles inserted superficially without manipulation or electrical stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a specific TCM term for the condition being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting (CINV)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No (the study found no significant difference in the primary outcome measure between acupuncture and control/sham groups, and concluded that it was not possible to determine the effectiveness of acupuncture due to low incidence of CINV)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Change in Functional Living Index Emesis (FLIE) score from day 1 to day 7.
Secondary outcome measures: Nausea scores, number of vomits, toxicity of acupuncture, FLIE score on days 1, 4 and 7, change in FLIE score from day 1 to day 4, nausea score change between days 1 and 2 and days 1 and 4, difference in the number of vomits between days 1 and 2 and days 1 and 4, adverse events.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was twice: once on day 1 for 30 minutes and again on day 3 for 30 minutes." .

