tara-kb:S-112625-560 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-560" ;
    dc:title "Randomized, Placebo-Controlled Trial of K1 Acupoint Acustimulation to Prevent Cisplatin-Induced or Oxaliplatin-Induced Nausea" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """K1 acupoint: Located on the sole of the foot in the depression when the foot is in plantar flexion, at the junction of the anterior one-third and the posterior two-thirds of the line connecting the base of the second and third toes with the heel.
Placebo point: Center part of the heel (not an acupoint).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Group B: Patients received tropisetron and electrostimulation at a placebo point on the heel." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "https://clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/NCT00430313" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "K 1" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:4512048 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4512048\": \"KI 1\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0002691 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not applicable (the study used electrostimulation with surface electrodes, not needle insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-560 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-560 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 103
Group A: 51
Group B: 52""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Electrostimulation at a placebo point on the center part of the heel.
Equipment: G9805-C low-frequency electric pulse treatment device.
Electrode placement: Positive electrode on one foot, negative electrode on the other.
Non-penetrating surface electrostimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) using circular self-adhesive electrodes with a continuous wave mode at a frequency of 4 Hertz and a duration pulse width of 0.15 to 0.3 milliseconds. Stimulation intensity was adjusted to the highest level the patient could comfortably withstand." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Liver cancer (primary or metastatic)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No (the acupuncture intervention was not effective in preventing nausea and vomiting compared to the control group, but it did transiently improve quality of life)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Rate, intensity, and duration of nausea and vomiting
Secondary outcome measures: Quality of life assessed using MD Anderson Symptom Inventory and EuroQoL scale""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each electrostimulation session: 30 minutes
Needles left in place: Not applicable (electrostimulation used instead of needles)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Daily for 6 consecutive days, with each session lasting 30 minutes. Treatments were administered approximately 1 to 2 hours before TAI on the first day and between 7 AM and 9 AM for the following days." .

tara-kb:S-112625-561 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-561" ;
    dc:title "Electroacupuncture for Fatigue, Sleep, and Psychological Distress in Breast Cancer Patients With Aromatase Inhibitor-Related Arthralgia: A Randomized Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """EA group: At least 4 local points around the joint with the most pain; at least 4 distant points for nonpain symptoms (depression/anxiety and fatigue).
SA group: Streitberger nonpenetrating needles at nonacupuncture, nontrigger points at least 5 cm from the joint where pain was perceived to be maximal.
Specific acupuncture points or areas: Not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Waitlist Control (WLC): Participants did not receive any intervention during the study period but were allowed to receive real acupuncture treatments after 12 weeks of follow-up.
Sham Acupuncture (SA): Participants received sham acupuncture using nonpenetrating needles at nonacupuncture points to mimic the sensation of acupuncture without actual treatment.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper provides a clinical trial identifier but does not specify a dataset link)" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper provides needle length but not specific insertion depth)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-561 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-561 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 67
EA group: 21
SA group: 20
WLC group: Not specified (implied to be 26 based on total sample size and numbers in EA and SA groups)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Streitberger nonpenetrating needles
Quantity and size: Not specified
Location: Nonacupuncture, nontrigger points at least 5 cm from the joint where pain was perceived to be maximal
Penetrating or non-penetrating: Non-penetrating
Other details: Avoided eliciting "De Qi" sensations; mock electrical stimulation setup with TENS unit""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electroacupuncture (EA): 2-hertz electrostimulation using a TENS unit; brief manual manipulation at the beginning and end of therapy; aimed to elicit "De Qi" sensation.
Sham Acupuncture (SA): No electrical stimulation; minimal manipulation to avoid "De Qi" sensation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM diagnosis or terminology for the condition being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the paper focuses on symptoms related to breast cancer and aromatase inhibitors but does not specify a single primary medical condition or disease)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Pain intensity and interference, measured by the Brief Pain Inventory (BPI)
Secondary outcome measures: Fatigue, sleep, and psychological distress""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles left in place during a session: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The acupuncture treatments were administered twice weekly for 2 weeks, then weekly for 6 more weeks, for a total of 10 treatments over 8 weeks. Each treatment session lasted 30 minutes with brief manipulation at the beginning and the end of therapy." .

