    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Lu 2012: 10 mm
Chen 2013: 25 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-574 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-574 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 285
Alimi 2003: 90 participants (3 groups)
Chen 2008: 66 participants (groups based on pain severity)
Chen 2013: 60 participants (electroacupuncture: n = 30, placebo: n = 30)
Lu 2012: 21 participants (electroacupuncture: n = 11, sham electroacupuncture: n = 10)
Dang 1998: 48 participants (3 treatment groups)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure involved non-penetrative needles.
Needles were inserted to a depth of less than 0.2 mm.
Sham procedure was performed at non-acupuncture points.
Electroacupuncture unit was switched off during sham procedure.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual acupuncture: Not specified
Electroacupuncture: Used in studies like Lu 2012 with electrical stimulation at 20 Hz to 25 Hz; Chen 2013 used electroacupuncture but specifics not detailed.
Thermal (moxibustion): Not mentioned
Laser: Not mentioned
Needle sensation: 'De qi' or strong sensation of paraesthesiae ('pins and needles') sought in some studies.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention TCM terminology for the conditions being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cancer-related pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Maybe/Inconclusive (the paper concludes that there is insufficient evidence to judge the effectiveness of acupuncture for cancer pain in adults)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Patient-reported pain intensity using validated scales (e.g. visual analogue scales (VAS), numerical rating scales)
Secondary outcome measures: Pain relief as measured by validated pain scales (e.g. VAS); patient satisfaction; quality of life; analgesic consumption and changes in concurrent treatments; hospital attendance/admission (including Hospice admission); adverse events (major or minor)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Alimi 2003: Duration determined by time needles/seeds remained in place; not specified
Chen 2013: 30 minutes per session, daily for 3 days
Lu 2012: 30 minutes per session
Dang 1998: 20 minutes per session""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Chen 2013: Daily for three days, 30 minutes per session.
Lu 2012: Two to three sessions per week, 10 sessions in total.
Dang 1998: Continuously for two weeks, then a gap of two to three days; frequency varied by pain severity.
Chen 2008: Not specified.""" .

