    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, acupuncture was effective in reducing the frequency of acute vomiting and the dose of rescue medication compared to the control group. Acupressure was effective in decreasing the frequency of nausea. However, acupuncture did not reduce acute nausea severity or frequency, and acupressure did not affect acute vomiting or delayed symptoms." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
