Depth of insertion: Limited to 0.2 mm
Needle manipulation: None
Electro-acupuncture: Deactivated machine used
Heat lamp: Positioned to minimize warming effect
Visual barrier: Used to maintain blinding
Interaction: Scripted to maintain sham nature""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation: Manual and electrostimulation
Electrostimulation: AWQ-104L electro-acupuncture machine at 20-25 Hz on ST36 and SP6
Thermal stimulation: TDP CQ-27 infrared heat lamp placed above the feet""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Ovarian cancer" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the sham group based on the primary outcomes of higher median leukocyte values and reduced incidence of grade 2-4 leukopenia. However, further confirmation is needed from larger trials." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: WBC count, ANC at nadir and second recovery day, feasibility of patient recruitment and acupuncture protocols
Secondary outcome: Influence of acupuncture on endogenous G-CSF levels""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "2-3 times per week for a total of 10 sessions, with each session lasting 30 minutes." .

