    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "France" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:6000040 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "The maximum diameter of the part of the needle that enters the skin is 0.7 mm. The length of the needle is 3.4 mm." ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-582 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-582 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 90
Auricular acupuncture group: 29
Placebo auricular acupuncture group: 30
Placebo auricular seed group: 31
Analyzed sample size: 79""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Two placebo groups were used.
First placebo group: Steel implants were inserted at non-acupuncture points (points with no electrodermal signal).
Second placebo group: Auricular seeds were fixed at non-acupuncture points with an adhesive patch.
Needle type: Identical single-use sterile steel implants were used for the first two groups.
Needle size: 3.4 mm long, cylindrical head with 1.2 mm diameter and height, maximum diameter of the part entering the skin is 0.7 mm.
Location: Non-acupuncture points (outside areas of projected pain).
Penetration: First placebo group was penetrating; second placebo group was non-penetrating.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide details on how the needles were stimulated beyond their insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Neuropathic pain in cancer patients" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Pain intensity at D60 measured on the VAS
Secondary outcome measures: Pain intensity at D30, average electrical potential differences at D60, average electrical potential differences at D30""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 44 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 1 to 34 days (average 12 days)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Two courses of auricular acupuncture were administered, approximately one month apart. Each treatment session lasted about 44 minutes." .

