tara-kb:S-112625-584 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-584" ;
    dc:title "Manual Acupuncture Improved Quality of Life in Cancer Patients with Radiation-Induced Xerostomia" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """St 6 (jiache): located on the cheek, 1 middle finger breadth anterior and superior to the mandibular angle
Li 4 (hegu): located on the dorsum of the hand, between the 1st and 2nd metacarpal bones
St 36 (zusanli): located on the leg, 1 finger breadth lateral to the tibia's anterior crest
Sp 6 (sanyinjiao): located 10 cm directly above the tip of the medial malleolus on the posterior border of the tibia
Sham acupuncture points: non-acupoints 2 cm away from the real acupoints""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study (Randomized Controlled Trial)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 5 participants who received a sham acupuncture treatment. This involved the insertion of needles just under the skin at non-acupuncture points with minimal intensity, mimicking the real EA treatment to provide a similar sensation. This sham treatment was used to control for placebo effects and allow for comparison with the intervention group." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "South Korea" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper does not mention the availability of or provide a link to related datasets)" ;
