    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Body acupuncture: Treating disease through points along the channels of the human body.
Electroacupuncture: Combining acupuncture with electrical stimulation.
Scalp acupuncture: Using needles on the surface of the head.
Elongated needle: A special long needle for dredging and activating the meridian.
Fire needling: A technique using a burnt metal needle for subcutaneous tissue needling.
EX-CA1: Involves heating and handling the acupuncture needle with moxa.
Specific acupoints: Not specified.""" ;
