    dc:title "Clinical Study on Acupuncture Treating Thalamic Pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Body Acupuncture Points:
Ji anyu (L1 15) and Ji anliao (TE 14) for shoulder pain
Quchi (L1 II) and Tianj in g (TE 10) for elbow pain
Wai guan (TE 5) and Yangehi (TE 4) for wrist pain
Huantiao (G B 30) and Biguan (ST 3 1) for hip pain
Chengfu (BL 36) and Fengshi (GB 31) for thigh pain
Dubi (ST 35) and Heding (Ex LE 2) for knee pain
Qiuxu (GB 40) and Shcnmai (BL 62) for ankle pain
Scalp Acupuncture Point:
The Posterior Oblique Tempo ropaielal Line (sensory zone of scalp)
Located on the temporoparietal region, crossing through the Governor Vessel, Three Foot Yang Meridians, and Triple Energizer Meridian
Fengfu (GV 16) mentioned in relation to scalp acupuncture""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 40 patients who received single body acupuncture treatment using the same acupoints as the treatment group but without scalp acupuncture." ;
