tara-kb:S-112625-599 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-599" ;
    dc:title "Scalp Acupuncture for Parkinson's Disease: A Systematic Review of Randomized Controlled Trials" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state specific acupuncture points or areas used in the trials)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control groups: Medication alone (e.g., Madopa, Artane, Levodopa)
Specific details: Medication dosages and durations varied by study (e.g., Madopa 125 mg √ó 3 times a day for 5 weeks; Artane 2 mg √ó 2‚Äì3 times every other day for 20 days)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005180 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-599 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-599 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 184 PD patients
Sample sizes within groups:
UPDRS assessment: 60 cases
Webster scale assessment: 154 cases
Individual study sample sizes:
Huang (2009): 30 cases
Jiang (2006): 30 cases
Yang (2004): 60 cases
Zhang (2002): 64 cases""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not provide details on the sham acupuncture procedure)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Two trials used electrical stimulation.
Two trials used hand manipulation.
Deqi sensation was sought in all trials.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the disease or condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Parkinson's disease (PD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "In total, 4 RCTs met the inclusion criteria. As assessed by the Unified PD Rating Scale (UPDRS), 2 RCTs showed that SA combined with CTs proved superior to CTs alone [60 cases; weighted mean difference, -3.94; 95% confidence interval (CI), -6.05 to -1.84, P=0.01; I 2 =0%]."
Direct quote: "Based on the Webster scale, however, 3 RCTs showed no superior effect of SA when combined with CTs with high heterogeneity (154 cases; risk ratio, 1.29; 95% CI, 0.79 to 2.12, P=0.30; I 2 =84%)."
Direct quote: "The result of our systematic review and meta-analysis suggested that the effectiveness of SA for PD is promising, however, the evidence is not convincing."
Direct quote: "In conclusion, the evidence that SA is effective for PD is not strong enough to be determined, although SA is being explored as a possible supportive or alternative treatment for PD."
Effectiveness: Maybe/Inconclusive""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Unified PD Rating Scale (UPDRS), Webster scale, Hoehn and Yahr (H&Y), Schwab and England (S&E), Columbia University Rating Scale (CURS)
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit information on the duration of each acupuncture session or needle retention time)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Once a day, 6 times a week, for 5 weeks
Once a day, 5 times a week, for 6 weeks
Once every other day, for 3 months
Once every other day, for 20 d Once every 5-7 d, for 50 d""" .

