    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-6" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for Pain Relief After Total Knee Arthroplasty A Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Body acupoints: SP10, ST34, BL40, LR7, ST36, sensory area of the scalp acupuncture, GV20, GV24
Auricular acupoints: ear Shen men (shemen, TF4), knee point (xi, AH4), sympathesis point (jiaogan, AH6a), subcortex point (pizhixia, AT4)
Electroacupuncture stimulation: SP10-LR7, ST36-ST34""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received sham auricular acupuncture (AA) under general anesthesia, where the ear needles were bent and did not penetrate the skin, serving as a placebo control." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper mentions registration in ClinicalTrials.gov but does not provide a direct link to a dataset)" ;
