    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-6 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 60
Participants in the study group: 30
Participants in the control group: 30""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Sham auricular acupuncture (AA)
Needle type: Sham needles with bent tips to prevent skin penetration
Quantity and size: Same as real acupuncture group
Location: Same ear acupoints as in the study group
Penetration: Non-penetrating
Duration: Retained in situ for 3 days after surgery""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electroacupuncture, which involved electrical stimulation using a transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation device. The stimulation was applied to specific acupoints with alternating frequencies of 100 and 10 Hz for 20 minutes, inducing muscle twitch as a sought sensation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the condition in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Degenerative osteoarthritis leading to total knee arthroplasty (TKA)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcomes. The fentanyl requirement was lower (P = 0.002), time to first fentanyl request was longer (P < 0.001), and pain intensity was lower in the first 24 hours. Additionally, nausea and vomiting were less frequent in the acupuncture group (P = 0.002)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Requirement for postoperative fentanyl in the first 48 hours after TKA.
Secondary outcome measures:
Time to the first PCA request.
Pain intensity assessed by patients on the VAS-100 at rest, recorded at 2, 4, 8, 12, 24, 36, and 48 hours after the operation.
Incidence of analgesia-related adverse effects: nausea and vomiting, respiratory depression, hypotension, urine retention, pruritus, and sedation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 3 days""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "1 session of acupuncture and AA under general anesthesia, lasting 20 minutes, with ear needles retained for 3 days after surgery." .

