    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-602" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for Promoting Intelligence of Children -An Observation on 37 Cases with Mental Retardation" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Main points: Sishenchong (EX-HN1), Baihui (GV 20), Naohu (GV 17), Benshen (GB 13), Fengchi (GB 20), Neiguan (PC 6), Hegu (LI 4), Zusanli (ST 36)
Additional points based on symptoms:
Glossolalia: Yamen (GV 15), Lianquan (CV 23)
Slow reaction: Xinshu (BL 15), Shenmen (HT 7)
Restlessness: Taichong (LR 3), Sanyinjiao (SP 6)
Enuresis: Shenshu (BL 23), Guanyuan (CV 4)
Salivation: Dicang (ST 4), Yinlingquan (SP 9)
Feeble neck: Tianzhu (BL 10), Dazhui (GV 14)
Points based on syndrome differentiation:
Weakness of spleen and stomach: Pishu (BL 20), Qihai (CV 6)
Deficiency of liver and kidney: Ganshu (BL 18), Shenshu (BL 23)
Obstruction of meridians by phlegm: Zhongwan (CV 12), Fenglong (ST 40)
Needle insertion techniques: transcutaneous, oblique, perpendicular
Needle manipulation: reinforcing, reducing, even""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 50 children with mental retardation who received Naofukang Capsule orally, with dosages of 0.2 g for ages 1-3, 0.4 g for ages 4-5, and 0.6 g for ages 6-12, three times a day for four weeks as one course. Only 36 cases had complete data records. The total effective rate in the control group was 30.56%." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
