tara-kb:S-112625-607 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-607" ;
    dc:title "Traditional needle acupuncture treatment for insomnia: A systematic review of randomized controlled trials" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Shenmen (HT7) on the wrists
Neiguan (PC6) on the wrists
Shenting (GV24) on the head
Baihui (GV20) on the head
Sishenchong (EX-HN1) on the head
Sanyinjiao (SP6) on the legs
Average of 8.8 acupoints per session""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Benzodiazepines (used in 18 studies)
Sleep hygiene counseling (used in 1 study)
Non-invasive sham acupuncture (used in 1 study)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China, Brazil, Korea" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0013600 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-607 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-607 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 1956 subjects
Range of sample sizes for individual studies: 30 to 190 participants
Specific sample sizes for some studies are provided in the table on page 5, but not for all studies.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Non-invasive sham acupuncture
Needle type: Real needles used but not inserted
Quantity: Same as active treatment group
Location: Real acupoints
Penetration: Non-penetrating
Other details: Needles held in place by surgical tape without skin penetration""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual stimulation was used in 12 studies.
Electrostimulation (electroacupuncture) was used in 4 studies.
No other types of stimulation (e.g., thermal, laser) were mentioned.
No specific sensations sought during stimulation were mentioned.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Insomnia (disharmony of Yin and Yang)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Insomnia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Maybe/Inconclusive (the paper suggests that while TNA may be more effective than benzodiazepines, the findings are compromised by methodological shortcomings, making it inconclusive)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Effective rate (proportion of subjects with improvement in sleep problems)
Secondary outcome measure: Self-reported rating scales""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details on the duration of each acupuncture session or needle retention time)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of acupuncture treatment was mostly once per day. The course of treatment ranged from 2 to 56 days. The exact duration was not mentioned in two studies." .

tara-kb:S-112625-608 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-608" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture and Chinese Patent Drugs For Chronic Fatigue Syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Baihui (GV20), Sishencong (EX HN1), bilateral Zusanli (ST36), bilateral Sanyinjiao (SP6)
Incoordination between the liver and spleen: Yanglingquan (GB34), Taichong (LR3)
Qi insufficiency of the spleen and stomach: Pishu (BL20), Weishu (BL21)
Deficiency of both the heart and spleen: Xinshu (BL15), Pishu (BL20)
Yin deficiency of the liver and kidney: Ganshu (BL18), Shenshu (BL23)
Yang insufficiency of the spleen and kidney: Pishu (BL20), Shenshu (BL23)
Locations and effects:
Baihui (GV20): Located in the head where all channels gather; removes mental cloudiness and clears the eyes.
Sishencong (EX HN1): Located one cun around Baihui (GV20); removes mental cloudiness and clears the eyes.
Zusanli (ST36): He (sea) point of the Stomach Channel of Yangming; strengthens the spleen and regulates the stomach.
Sanyinjiao (SP6): Located where the three yin channels meet; strengthens the spleen, nourishes the liver and tonifies the kidney.
Yinlingquan (SP9) and Taichong (LR3): Soothe the liver and regulate the circulation of qi.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control Group: 42 cases treated with Chinese patent drugs.
Treatment based on TCM differentiation:
Incoordination between the liver and kidney: Xiaoyao San (Ease Powder)
Qi insufficiency of the spleen and stomach: Xiangsha Liujunzi Wan (Pill of Six Noble Ingredients with Cyperus and Amomum)
Deficiency of both the heart and spleen: Guipi Wan (Pill for Invigorating the Spleen and Nourishing the Heart)
Yin deficiency of the liver and kidney: Liuwei Dihuang Wan (Bolus of Six Drugs Including Rehmanniae)
Yang insufficiency of the spleen and kidney: Sishen Wan (Pill of Four Miraculous Drugs)
Administration schedule: Twice daily, with 5 days constituting a course and 2 days interval between courses.
Evaluation: Therapeutic effects evaluated after 4 courses of treatment.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GV 20, EX HN 1, ST 36, SP 6, GB 34, LR 3, BL 20, BL 21, BL 15, BL 18, BL 23" ;
