    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "1. Incoordination between the liver and spleen 2. Qi insufficiency of the spleen and stomach 3. Deficiency of both the heart and spleen 4. Yin deficiency of the liver and kidney 5. Yang insufficiency of the spleen and kidney" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic Fatigue Syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No (the acupuncture intervention was not found to be significantly more effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcome)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Cured: Disappearance ofSymptoms with no recurrence in a 3 month follow up
Markedly effective:Symptoms improved by 70%
Effective:Symptoms improved by 50%
Ineffective: No obvious improvement inSymptoms
Secondary outcome measures: NotSpecified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Acupuncture: Once daily, 5 days per course, 2 days interval between courses, evaluated after 4 courses.
Auricular seed embedding therapy: Twice a week, patients press points 4 5 times daily, evaluated after 4 weeks.""" .

tara-kb:S-112625-609 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-609" ;
    dc:title "A Systematic Review of Acupuncture and Moxibustion Treatment for Chronic Fatigue Syndrome in China" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """GV20, CV6, CV4, ST36, Back-shu points, CV8, Back areas of GV meridian, Bladder meridians, Huatuojiaji points
Points on extremities: ST36, SP6, PC6, HT7, LI4
Points on trunk: CV4, CV6, CV17, CV12, CV8, Backshu points, GV14
Points on head region: GV20, Sischencong (EX), Taiyang (EX), Yintang (EX)
Selection based on TCM theories and symptom presentation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Cortisone: Used in 3 studies as a control treatment, with dosages specified (e.g., 5 mg once daily in the morning).
Adenosine Triphosphate (ATP): Used in 1 study as a control treatment, with dosages specified (2 tablets 3 times a day for 15 days).
Herbs: Used as a control in some studies, comparing acupuncture and moxibustion with herbal treatments.
Tuina and music therapy: Used as part of combined treatments compared with acupuncture alone or herbal medicine alone.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005404 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-609 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-609 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 2,266
Specific sample sizes for each study or detailed breakdowns of participants within groups: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the studies reviewed)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual stimulation: Needles were inserted into different parts or points of the body.
Thermal stimulation: Moxibustion involved the use of burning moxa.
Physical stimulation: Cupping and tapping were used until local erythematous changes were noted.
Manual manipulation: A mild reinforcing-reducing method was applied during needling.
Not specified: Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) or laser stimulation were not mentioned.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a specific TCM disease or condition name for CFS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic Fatigue Syndrome (CFS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcome Measures:
Improvement in CFS symptoms
Standardized measures: Fatigue Assessment Instrument (FAI), Symptom Checklist-90 (SCL-90), Chronic Fatigue/Immune Dysfunction Syndrome Disability Scale (CFIDS Disability Scale)
Secondary Outcome Measures:
Changes in immune substances: IgG, IgA, IgM, C3, C4, CD+3, CD+4, CD+8, NK cells, IL-2""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles left in place during a session: Not specified beyond the session duration""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Treatments were administered once daily for 2 to 3 courses, with each course consisting of 10 sessions, and each session lasting 30 minutes." .

