tara-kb:S-112625-611 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-611" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for Spinal Cord Injury and Its Complications: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Functional recovery: 48 points (36 meridian, 1 extra, 8 ear, 2 scalp, 1 Ashi); 62.5% in upper and lower extremities, 37.5% in head and back.
Bladder dysfunction: 18 points (17 meridian, 1 extra); 77.8% in lower back.
Pain control: 30 points (29 meridian, 1 Ashi); 93.3% in shoulder area.
Rationale: Primarily based on Traditional Chinese Medicine theory.
Point selection: Fixed points in 10 trials, fixed plus individualized in 5 trials, individualized by symptoms in 1 trial.
Specific points listed in tables at the end of the paper.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Conventional treatments alone (for functional recovery)
Conventional treatments such as intramuscular neostigmine methylsulfate, intermittent catheterization, and bladder training (for bladder dysfunction)
Sham acupuncture (for pain control)
The Trager Approach (for pain control)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China, Taiwan, USA" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0043797 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-611 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-611 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: Not specified
Sample sizes for specific conditions:
Functional recovery: Not specified
Bladder dysfunction: n=264 (for total efficacy rate)
Pain control: Not specified
Sample sizes for individual studies: Not specified (information likely contained in tables)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Manual acupuncture with no manipulation at sites located at least 1 cun (1 Chinese anatomic inch, approximately 2.5 cm) away from the established meridian and extra points.
Penetrating: Yes
Needle type, quantity, and size: Not specified
Location: Non-acupuncture points
Other details: No manipulation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """14 studies used electrical stimulation with acupuncture (electroacupuncture).
2 studies used needling acupuncture alone (no additional stimulation).
No other forms of stimulation (e.g., manual manipulation, thermal, laser) were mentioned.
No specific sensation was sought during stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a specific TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Spinal Cord Injury (SCI) and its complications: functional recovery, bladder dysfunction, and pain control" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes (for functional recovery and bladder dysfunction), No (for pain control)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes:
Motor ASIA scores
Total FIM scores
Total efficacy rate for bladder dysfunction
Secondary outcomes:
Not explicitly mentioned, but possibly includes other measures related to complications of SCI such as bladder function scales and pain scores.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
How long the needles were left in place during a session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Dyson-Hudson [18] (2001): AT (1 session = 20~30 min, twice a week, total 10 treatments)
Cheng [14] (1998): EA (20‚Äì30 Hz, 30‚Äì50 mA, 1 session = 15 min, 4~5 sessions each week, till their bladders were balanced)
Gu [15] (2005)b: EA (continuous wave, 1 session = once a day, 30 min for 2 weeks, total 14‚Äì56 treatments)
Liu [16] (2009): EA (1 session = once a day, 30 min for 15 days, total 60 treatments)
Dyson-Hudson [17] (2007): AT (1 session = 20 min, twice a week, total 10 treatments)
Gu [8] (2005)a: EA (1 Hz, 3‚Äì5 V, 1 session = once a day, 30 min for 1 month, 1 week rest, total 150 treatments)
Ma [9] (2005): EA + AT (scalp EA; 5 min, body AT; 25 min, once a day, total 168 sessions)
Sheng [10] (2009): EA (1 session = once a day, 30 min for 10 days, 2 days‚Äô rest, total 70 treatments)
Huang [11] (2002): EA (continuous wave, 1 session = 30 min, for 5 days, 3 days‚Äô rest, total 5‚Äì20 treatments)
Zhang [12] (2008): EA (2 Hz, 6 V, 1 session = once a day, 30 min for 2 weeks, total 12 treatments)
Zhou [13] (2007): EA (continuous wave, 80 Hz, 20 mA, 1 session = once a day for 15 days, 5 days‚Äô rest, total 30 treatments)
Chen [3] (1995): EA (1-2 Hz, 1 session = once a day, 30 min, 6 times a week, total 48 treatments)
Wong [4] (2003): EA + AA (75 Hz, 10 mV, 1 session = 30 min, 5 times a week, till discharge)
Cui [5] (2004): EA (1 session = once a day, 30 min for 1 month, total 90 or 180 treatments)
Xu [6] (2004): EA (1 Hz, 1 session = once a day, 30 min for 1 month, 7 days‚Äô rest, total 150 treatments)
Chen [7] (2005): EA + AA (EA; 1‚Äì5 Hz, 1 session = once a day, 30 min, 6 days a week for 3 months, session interval 1-2 weeks, till discharge, AA; 1 session = once a day, 10 times, total 2-3 session, each ear alternately)""" .

