tara-kb:S-112625-616 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-616" ;
    dc:title "Stimulation of Acupoint ST-34 Acutely Improves Gait Performance in Geriatric Patients During Rehabilitation: A Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Verum treatment: Acupuncture point ST-34 (stomach 34), located 2 cun proximal to the superior lateral border of the patella.
Control treatment: Nonspecific skin point with no direct relation to any conduit (meridian) between the gallbladder meridian and the lateral posterior border of the femur, at the same height as the verum point.
Selection criteria: Chosen according to the theory of Chinese Medicine as described by the Heidelberg Model of TCM.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received nonacupoint skin stimulation, which is a sham acupuncture treatment performed at a nonspecific skin point with no direct relation to any traditional Chinese medicine meridian." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "ST 34" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:8773594 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:8773594\": \"ST 34\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "0.5 cm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-616 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-616 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 60
Intervention group: Not specified
Control group: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Commercially available sterile standard disposable injection needles (BD Micro-Fineœ©, 0.30mm [30G] œ´ 8mm)
Quantity: Bilateral needling
Size: 0.30mm [30G] œ´ 8mm
Location: Nonspecific skin point with no direct relation to any conduit (meridian) between the felleal conduit (gallbladder meridian) and the lateral posterior border of the femur
Penetration: Penetrating with a depth of 0.5 cm
Technique: Sparrow-pecking technique with 5 rapid skin penetrations""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved manual manipulation using the \"sparrow-pecking technique,\" which consists of 5 rapid skin penetrations with disposable needles. No additional stimuli like laser or electrical stimulation were used." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition name, but it focuses on improving gait performance and addressing leg weakness)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Gait disorders/mobility limitations in geriatric patients" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Maximal gait speed
Secondary outcome measures: Other temporal and spatial gait performances related to dynamic postural control and performance-based measures""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Single application (once)" .

