Secondary outcome measures: Disease Assessment Scale (DAS), tender and swollen joint count, morning stiffness, Health Assessment Questionnaire (HAQ), visual analogue scale (VAS) of pain, physician global assessment of activity disease, physician and patient global assessment of treatment, and inflammatory markers (erythrocyte sedimentation rate and C-reactive protein).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Acupuncture group (AC): 40 minutes per session (20 minutes in supine position, 20 minutes in ventral position)
Control group (controlAC): 20 minutes per session (10 minutes in supine position, 10 minutes in ventral position)
Needle retention duration: Not specified for AC group; up to 2 mm insertion for controlAC group""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for 5 consecutive weeks, with a total of 10 sessions. Each session lasted 40 minutes (20 minutes in supine position and 20 minutes in ventral position)." .

tara-kb:S-112625-620 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-620" ;
    dc:title "Traditional Chinese Medicine for Treatment of Fibromyalgia: A Systematic Review of Randomized Controlled Trials" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details about needle locations or related acupoints used in the trials)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """No treatment
Sham acupuncture
Conventional medications""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the country or countries where the studies were conducted)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005546 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-620 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-620 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 1516
Sample size within groups: varied from 10 to 38 participants, with an average of 25 patients per group""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Sham laser acupuncture
Details: Non-penetrating, no actual needle insertion
Trials: Lautenschlager J 1989, Sprott H 1998""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture), including transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation (TENS). Other forms of stimulation are not specified." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Fibromyalgia (FM) is mainly caused by emotional upsets affecting the Liver, leading to stagnation of qi and Blood stasis, which causes pain." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Fibromyalgia (FM)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Acupuncture is effective compared to conventional medications for reducing pain and tender points (Yes).
Acupuncture is not significantly effective compared to sham acupuncture for pain reduction (No).
Combination of acupuncture and cupping therapy is effective compared to conventional medications for pain reduction and improving depression scores (Yes).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Reduction in severity of pain
Reduction in number of tender points
Improvement of QoL
Reduction of relapse rate
Secondary outcome measures:
Depression (assessed using Hamilton Depression Scale)
Anxiety (assessed using Hamilton Anxiety Scale)
Quality of life (measured using SF-36 and QoL scale)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes, 30 minutes
Frequency of sessions: Twice a week, once a day
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: Twice weekly (2X/week), daily (1X/day)
Duration: 20 minutes, 30 minutes
Treatment period: 12 days to 12 weeks""" .

tara-kb:S-112625-621 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-621" ;
    dc:title "Randomized Controlled Trial of Traditional Chinese Medicine (Acupuncture and Tuina) in Cerebral Palsy: Part 1-Any Increase in Seizure in Integrated Acupuncture and Rehabilitation Group Versus Rehabilitation Group?" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Acupoints were selected based on TCM diagnosis using the "Eight-Principle Differentiation" model.
Needling of body points and scalp acupuncture areas to address pattern differentiation and regulate channels.
Acupoints were chosen on affected limbs and scalp areas.
Channels involved: Foot and Arm Yang-Ming (Stomach/Large Intestine) and Shao-Yang (Gall Bladder/Triple Heater).
Specific acupoint names not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control session: A session without acupuncture needles, used as a baseline to compare the effects of acupuncture.
Pseudoacupuncture session: A session where needles were inserted to avoid recognized acupuncture points, serving as another control or comparison group.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China, United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0006497 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper describes a \"secure depth\" but does not provide a specific numerical value or descriptive term)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-621 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-621 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total sample size: 12; Group sizes: 6 in each group (genuine acupuncture and pseudoacupuncture sessions)" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles
Quantity: Two needles inserted bilaterally
Size: Inserted to a depth of 2 0 to 2 5 cm
Location: Non acupuncture points (avoiding recognized points)
Penetration: Penetrating
Electrical stimulation: Yes, from a 6 V battery stimulator""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) applied using a 6 V battery stimulator to induce local fasciculation at a maximum comfortable intensity. The stimulation was applied during specific intervals between heat stimulus trials." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cerebral Palsy (CP)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, acupuncture was found to be effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s). The study concluded that acupuncture is significantly more effective than suggestion in raising pain thresholds and has substantial support for its effectiveness in increasing tolerances. Statistical significance was reported with p values: P < 0.05 for thresholds and P < 0.02 for tolerances." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome measure: Change in baseline seizure frequency in children with cerebral palsy undergoing acupuncture treatment. Secondary outcome measures: Not specified in this part of the study, but mentioned as part of a future report: gross motor function, fine motor function, range of motion of 6 joints, and function as assessed by the primary caregiver." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 1 hour
Duration needles were left in place: Approximately 35 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper only describes the frequency of experimental sessions, not ongoing treatment frequency)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-622 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-622" ;
    dc:title "A randomized controlled trial of acupuncture added to usual treatment for fibromyalgia" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Ex-HN-3: Bilateral LR3, LI4, PC6
GB34, SP6
Needle penetration: 10-30 mm
