tara-kb:S-112625-632 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-632" ;
    dc:title "Electroacupuncture in fibromyalgia: results of a controlled trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """First dorsal interosseous muscle of the hand
Anterior tibial muscle (5 cm beneath the inferior margin of the patella and 1 cm below the anterior crest of the tibia) on both sides
Additional sites chosen based on patient's symptoms and pain pattern, and empirical efficacy in pain treatment
Traditional acupuncture points used, with special attention to areas used in analgesia experiments
Tender points avoided due to observed worsening of pain""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group underwent a sham procedure where needles were inserted 20 mm away from the points used in real electroacupuncture, with a shallower depth and a weaker electric current, to serve as a comparison to the electroacupuncture group." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Switzerland, Sweden" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005546 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Electroacupuncture group: 10 25 mm
Control group: 3 4 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-632 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-632 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 70
Control group: 34
Electroacupuncture group: 36""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles were used for both real and sham procedures.
Quantity: A similar number of needles were used in both groups.
Size: The size of the needles was not specified, but they were likely the same as those used in the real procedure.
Location: Needles were inserted 20 mm away from the points used in real electroacupuncture.
Penetration: Needles were penetrating but to a shallower depth (3 4 mm) compared to the real procedure.
Other details: The electric current was weaker, and there was no muscular contraction.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation in the study was electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) using an electrostimulator with a rectangular current and a frequency of 1 99 Hz. The intensity was set to induce a visible muscular contraction and a \"needling sensation\" as indicated by the patient." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Fibromyalgia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure:Pain threshold
Secondary outcome measures: Number of analgesic tablets used, regionalPainScore,Pain recorded on visual analogueScale,Sleep quality, morningStiffness,Patient's appreciation, evaluatingPhysician's appreciation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Six sessions of electroacupuncture spread over three weeks. The exact frequency (e.g., daily or twice weekly) is not specified." .

