    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture was performed using points located 2 cun laterally to true acupuncture points, between the main channels.
The cun was calculated based on individual measurements using the width of the distal interphalangeal joint of the thumb.
The "Leopard spot technique" was used for sham treatments, involving sterile disposable needles (30G, 0.30 ‚Ä¢ 8 mm) and letting out drops of blood by quickly stabbing the skin.
The sham procedure was penetrating but at non-traditional points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation involved manual manipulation using the \"Leopard spot technique,\" where needles were quickly stabbed into the skin to let out some drops of blood. No other forms of stimulation like electrical or thermal were mentioned." ;
