    dc:title "Effects of Transcutaneous Electrical Acupoint Stimulation on Motor Functions and Self-Care Ability in Children with Cerebral Palsy" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Shousanli (LI10): Located 2 cun (6.7 cm) below the lateral end of the transverse cubital crease when the elbow is flexed and the forearm is pronated.
Waiguan (SJ5): Located 2 cun (6.7 cm) above the transverse wrist crease on the dorsal surface of the forearm, between the radius and the ulna.
Electrode placement: Anode on Waiguan (SJ5), cathode on Shousanli (LI10).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 11 children who received sham TEAS (with the device kept open and current set to 0 mA) plus exercise therapy." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
