    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-641 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total: 23; Control Group: 11; Therapeutic Group: 12" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Sham TEAS
Details: Electrodes placed at Shousanli (LI10) and Waiguan (SJ5) but with no current applied (0 mA)
Non-invasive
Mimicked appearance of TEAS without actual electrical stimulation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation type: Transcutaneous Electrical Acupoint Stimulation (TEAS)
Method: Electrical stimulation using electrodes placed on acupoints Shousanli (LI10) and Waiguan (SJ5)
Parameters: Pulse frequency at 2 Hz, pulse width at 200 ms, current adjusted to individual's maximum tolerated level
Sensation sought: De qi sensation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM term for cerebral palsy)" ;
