Traditional Chinese Acupuncture (TCA) group: 12
Sham Acupuncture group: 12""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles used for sham procedure
Quantity: Not specified
Size: Not specified
Location: Not specified (real points vs. non-points/off-meridian)
Penetrating or non-penetrating: Non-penetrating (skin punctured to 2 mm and then withdrawn)
Other details: Cube of foam used to hide needle tip, connected to electrical current generator without current passing through, intermittent non-specific manual twirling applied""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electroacupuncture (EA): Needles stimulated by an electrical current (dense wave at 4 HZ and disperse wave at 20 HZ) and intermittent non-specific manual twirling.
Traditional Chinese acupuncture (TCA): Needles stimulated by intermittent specific manual twirling.
Sham acupuncture: No stimulation; skin punctured to a depth of 2 mm and then the needle was quickly withdrawn.
Sensation sought: "de Qi" (heaviness, soreness, or numbness) in EA and TCA groups.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Bi syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Rheumatoid Arthritis (RA)" ;
