    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 120
Sample size per group: 30""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the study does not involve acupuncture with needles; the control group serves as a sham by receiving no stimulation)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Control group: No stimulation.
Vibration group: Vibration applied to acupuncture points using transducers at frequencies of 32 Hz, 48 Hz, and 64 Hz.
Music group: Music played through earphones.
Complete group: Combination of music and vibration applied to acupuncture points using transducers at frequencies of 32 Hz, 48 Hz, and 64 Hz.
Stimulation pattern: Intermittent, with 1 minute of vibration followed by a 10-second pause.
Sensation sought: Activation of skin mechanoreceptors (Meissner and Paccinian corpuscles).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM term for fibromyalgia)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Fibromyalgia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the combined intervention of music and vibration was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes of FIQ and HAQ scores, with significant p-values (p < 0.001 for FIQ and p < 0.004 for HAQ)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Fibromyalgia Impact Questionnaire (FIQ), Health Assessment Questionnaire (HAQ)
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each session: 30 minutes
Needles left in place: Not applicable (no needles used)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was three times a week, on every Tuesday, Thursday, and Saturday in the morning, for a total of five sessions. The exact duration of each session is not specified." .

