    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed for AR: 160
Total participants analyzed for asthma: 101
Sample sizes per study:
Chen and Qi: 50
Gan and Tu: 30
Liu: 30
Maa et al: 23 (T1)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupressure group was used in the studies reviewed)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not applicable (acupressure does not involve needle stimulation)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Parkinson's disease (PD)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Acupressure had greater effects on relieving nasal symptoms of allergic rhinitis compared to 1% ephedrine nasal drop plus thermal therapy.
Acupressure plus salbutamol showed significantly greater improvements in pulmonary function for asthma compared to salbutamol only.
No significant differences were found in other studies.
No reliable conclusions can be drawn due to small number of trials and high/unclear risk of bias.
Effectiveness: Maybe/Inconclusive""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcome Measures:
Balance assessment: COG ML/AP sway, ankle-to-hip sway
Unified Parkinson's Disease Rating Scale (UPDRS)
Secondary Outcome Measures:
Quality of life
Concerns for fall
Pain questionnaires
Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE) for cognition status
Hoehn and Yahr staging for disease stage""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment: 10 days to 3 months
Duration of each session: Chen and Qi: 2 minutes per point
Gan and Tu: 5 minutes per point
Liu: 1-2 minutes per point
Maa et al: 30 seconds to 2 minutes per point
Needles left in place: Not applicable (acupressure uses finger pressure, not needles)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Daily treatments; duration per point varied from 30 seconds to 5 minutes; overall treatment periods ranged from 10 days to 3 months." .

tara-kb:S-112625-674 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
