    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Insomnia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Results: A higher educational level and greater baseline ISI score were predictive of a better response to acupuncture for insomnia. The number of years spent in full-time education was an independent predictor of treatment response (OR 1.21, 95% CI 1.06 to 1.38, p<0.01).
Conclusion: Acupuncture was effective in reducing insomnia severity for some patients, particularly those with higher educational levels and baseline ISI scores.
Effectiveness compared to control/sham group: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Insomnia Severity Index (ISI)
Secondary outcome measures: Sleep diary, actigraphy, Hamilton Depression Rating Scale (HAMD), Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS), Credibility of the Treatment Rating Scale (CTRS)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Frequency and total duration: Three times a week for three consecutive weeks""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Three times per week for three consecutive weeks; each session lasted 30 minutes." .

