tara-kb:S-112625-689 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-689" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture or acupressure for induction of labour (Review)" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Spleen 6 (SP6): on the inner ankle; Large intestine 4 (LI4): in the webbing between thumb and forefinger; Bladder 67 (BL67): on the outer edge of the little toe; ST36; LR3; ; UB23; GV20; CV4; UB20; UB18; KI3; GVl4; HT7; UB15; LU7; PC6; TH6; BL32; BL60. Sham points: on the sacral area, hand, foot, a point below the knee, and lower leg." ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham control: Needles inserted at non-acupuncture points or with minimal insertion and stimulation.
Usual care: Standard medical care without specific intervention.
Sweeping of fetal membranes: Used as a control in one trial.
Misoprostol: Administered intravaginally as a control in one trial.
Routine healthcare services: Used as a control in acupressure trials.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Norway, Australia, Denmark, USA, Germany, UK" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """True acupuncture: 15 to 20 mm
Sham acupuncture: 1 to 1.5 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-689 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-689 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total sample size: 3456 pregnant women; Specific sample sizes for each group or trial: Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure involved invasive shallow needle insertion at non-acupuncture points on the hands, legs, and lower back, bilaterally, with needles retained for 30 minutes.
Sham procedure used noninvasive Park sham needle at real acupuncture points BL67, LI4, SP6, GV20.
Sham procedure involved minimal insertion and stimulation at non-acupuncture points on the sacral area, hand, foot, a point below the knee, and lower leg.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual stimulation: Needles were stimulated intermittently and irregularly by hand for 30 minutes to attain a "de qi" sensation.
Electro-acupuncture: Points were stimulated by an electrical stimulator with 2-Hz pulses of 0.5 millisecond duration for 30 minutes, sufficient to cause non-painful muscle contractions.
Electro-acupuncture also used 2 distinct frequencies (5 and 50 Hz) that alternated every 7 pulses for 30 minutes.
Sham group: Minimal insertion and stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Induction of labour" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes:
1. Vaginal delivery not achieved within 24 hours
2. Uterine hyperstimulation with fetal heart rate (FHR) changes
3. Caesarean section
4. Serious neonatal morbidity or perinatal death
5. Serious maternal morbidity or death
Secondary outcomes:
1. Cervix unfavourable/unchanged after 12 to 24 hours
2. Oxytocin augmentation
3. Uterine hyperstimulation without FHR changes
4. Uterine rupture
5. Spontaneous vaginal delivery""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes (multiple studies)
Duration needles were left in place: 30 minutes (multiple studies)
Treatment duration: 20 minutes (one study)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Weekly from 36 weeks until delivery
Up to 2 times over a 1-week period (every 3 days)
