tara-kb:S-112625-700 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-700" ;
    dc:title "Modulation of the Sleep State-Dependent P50 Midlatency Auditory-Evoked Potential by Electric Stimulation of Acupuncture Points" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Pericardium 6 (PC6): Located 2cm above the wrist between the tendons of the palmaris longus and flexor carpi radialis.
Heart 3 (HT3): Located near the medial epicondyle at the medial end of the transverse cubital crease when the elbow is fully flexed.
Liver 3 (LR3): Located on the dorsal foot in the hollow distal to the junction of the first and second metatarsal bones.
Control points: Gall Bladder 34 (GB34), Large Intestine 11 (LI11), Small Intestine 3 (SI3)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """No-stimulation group: Subjects were fitted with electrodes but not stimulated.
Control points group: Stimulation at Gall Bladder 34, Large Intestine 11, Small Intestine 3.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "PC 6, HT 3, LR 3, GB 34, LI 11, SI 3" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0220496,
        TARA:2385378,
        TARA:4311153,
        TARA:6499349,
        TARA:8758950,
        TARA:8923096 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:4311153\": \"PC 6\", \"TARA:2385378\": \"HT 3\", \"TARA:6499349\": \"LR 3\", \"TARA:8758950\": \"GB 34\", \"TARA:8923096\": \"LI 11\", \"TARA:0220496\": \"SI 3\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not applicable (the study uses surface electroacupuncture without needles)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-700 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-700 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 80
Investigation 1 (men vs women): 31
Investigation 2 (bilateral low stimulation): 31
Investigation 3 (bilateral medium stimulation): 16
Investigation 4 (bilateral high stimulation): 11
Investigation 5 (control stimulation): 8
Investigation 6 (unilateral stimulation): 7
Investigation 7 (repeated stimulation): 7""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the study used surface electroacupuncture and did not include a sham acupuncture group with needles or non-penetrating sham needles)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electroacupuncture, which involved the use of surface electrodes to stimulate specific acupuncture points bilaterally. The stimulation was adjusted to elicit a \"tingling\" sensation. Needles were not used in this study." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a disease/condition in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the paper discusses potential applications for disorders of hypervigilance but does not specify a primary medical condition or disease being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"Electroacupuncture at specific points decreased P50 potential amplitude versus electroacupuncture at control points (Pœ≠.006) or versus no stimulation (PœΩ.001)."
"The optimal effective frequency was 5Hz (PœΩ.05 at 5Hz, Pœæ.05 at 60 and 100Hz), and unilateral electroacupuncture was not as effective as bilateral electroacupuncture (Pœ≠.007)."
"Repeated episodes of bilateral electroacupuncture showed additive effects (PœΩ.05)."
"Electroacupuncture may be effectively used to decrease arousal levels, perhaps as adjunct therapy for disorders of hypervigilance."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: P50 auditory evoked potential latency, amplitude (measure of level of arousal), and habituation (measure of sensory gait)
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "20 minutes" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not mention how often acupuncture treatments were administered)" .

