tara-kb:S-112625-703 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-703" ;
    dc:title "An fMRI Study Comparing Brain Activation Between Word Generation and Electrical Stimulation of Language-Implicated Acupoints" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """SJ 8: Located in the forearm at mid-position between the distal ulna and the distal radius and at 4 cm above the carpoulnar junction.
Du 15: Located in the depression below the spinous process of the first cervical vertebra at 1.5 cm above the midpoint of the posterior hairline.
Other acupoints related to language disorders mentioned in the paper: small Intestine 19, sanjiao [SJ] 21, GB 2, extra point of head and neck (EX-HN) 12, EX-HN 13, and EX-HN 14.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Not specified (the study design is not explicitly stated in the paper)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "control group: stimulation of adjacent non-acupoints (used as a control condition to compare with the active acupuncture task)" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Taiwan" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "SJ 8, Du 15, Small Intestine 19, SJ 21, GB 2, EX-HN 12, EX-HN 13, EX-HN 14" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:1698911,
        TARA:1772472,
        TARA:2849795,
        TARA:3361879,
        TARA:3641900,
        TARA:4427404,
        TARA:7471145,
        TARA:7596288 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:1698911\": \"TE 8\", \"TARA:4427404\": \"GV 15\", \"TARA:1772472\": \"SI 19\", \"TARA:3361879\": \"TE 21\", \"TARA:2849795\": \"GB 2\", \"TARA:3641900\": \"Jinjing\", \"TARA:7471145\": \"Yuye\", \"TARA:7596288\": \"Yiming\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-703 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-703 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 17
Participants in language task: 17
Participants in electro-acupuncture:
SJ 8: 11
Du 15: 6""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles used for both actual and sham procedures
Quantity: Two needles inserted over non-acupoints
Size: Not specified
Location: Non-acupoints at 1 cm lateral to SJ 8 and Du 15
Penetrating: Yes, needles were inserted into the skin""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) was used for the acupoints SJ 8 and Du 15. The stimulation was bipolar at 2 Hz, with intensity set at a mid-level between barely perceptible and maximally tolerable. Subjects closed their eyes during stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Not specified (the paper focuses on language disorders but does not specify a particular Western medical condition or disease)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Results: Significant activation was seen in specific brain regions during word generation and acupoint stimulation, but acupoint stimulation did not activate typical language areas in the left inferior frontal cortex.
Conclusion: Acupuncture at SJ 8 or Du 15 may improve certain language disorders by activating other brain areas, but it does not activate typical language areas.
Effectiveness: Not specified (the study does not provide a direct comparison with a control group or statistical significance for primary outcomes).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Comparison of brain activation patterns during word generation and electrical stimulation of language-implicated acupoints (SJ 8 and Du 15) using fMRI.
Secondary outcome measures: Activation of specific brain regions such as the inferior frontal gyri (BA 44, 45, 46) and superior temporal gyri (BA 22, 42) during these tasks.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the duration of each acupuncture session or how long the needles were left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency or duration of acupuncture treatments)" .

