tara-kb:S-112625-707 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-707" ;
    dc:title "Neuronal Specificity of Acupuncture Response: A fMRI Study with Electroacupuncture" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Real EA: Gallbladder 34 (GB34), Yanglinquan, located at the intersection of lines from the anterior and inferior borders to the head of the fibula.
Sham EA: Nonmeridian points, 4‚Äì5 cm from GB34, lateral area of the left leg.
Minimal EA: Nonmeridian points, 4‚Äì5 cm from sham point, lateral area of the left leg.
Other referenced acupoints: LI4 (Hegu), ST36 (Zusanli), GB37, Bladder 67, GB43.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Mock EA: No stimulation was applied.
Minimal EA: Superficial and light stimulation at nonmeridian points.
Sham EA: Same stimulation as real EA but applied at nonmeridian points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the country where the study was conducted)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GB 34, GB 37, GB 43" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:6320058,
        TARA:8758950,
        TARA:8885103 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:8758950\": \"GB 34\", \"TARA:6320058\": \"GB 37\", \"TARA:8885103\": \"GB 43\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0012531 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Real EA: 2‚Äì3 cm
Sham EA: 2‚Äì3 cm
Minimal EA: 0.3‚Äì0.5 cm
Mock EA: No needle insertion""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-707 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-707 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 15
Sham EA: 15
Real EA: 15
Mock EA: 7
Minimal EA: 8""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham EA was performed at nonmeridian points.
The location was 4‚Äì5 cm from the real acupoint GB34.
The needle depth and current were the same as those for real EA.
The sham EA was penetrating and used real needles.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electroacupuncture (EA) at the Gallbladder 34 (GB34) acupoint. The study included four models of stimulation: mock EA (no stimulation), minimal EA (superficial and light stimulation), sham EA (same stimulation as real EA but at nonmeridian points), and real EA (stimulation at GB34). The stimulation intensity was measured in terms of electric current, with real EA and sham EA using higher currents than minimal EA. The study aimed to elicit a sensation known as DeQi." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper focuses on analgesia and pain management but does not specify a particular TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Pain (musculoskeletal pain/disorders of muscle and tendon)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Activation of brain regions in response to electroacupuncture (EA) as measured by fMRI.
Specificity of neuronal expression by comparing different types of EA (real, sham, minimal, mock).
Secondary outcome measure:
Self-reported DeQi sensation scores to assess subjects' response to EA stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 5 minutes (1 minute per block √ó 5 blocks)
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of treatment sessions over time)" .

