tara-kb:S-112625-716 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-716" ;
    dc:title "A randomized controlled trial of acupuncture for initiation of labor in nulliparous women" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """LI4 (large intestine 4 or Hegu): located on the hands, inserted to a depth of 5 mm
SP6 (spleen 6 or Sanyinjiao): located on the legs, inserted to a depth of 10 mm
UB31 (urinary bladder 31 or Shangliao): located on the lower back, inserted to a depth of 30-50 mm
UB32 (urinary bladder 32 or Ciliao): located on the lower back, inserted to a depth of 30-50 mm
Low-voltage electrical stimulation used between UB31 and UB32 with current at 2 Hz during the 30-minute treatment""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Conventional treatment group: 2 4 weeks of medication with antibiotics, corticosteroids, 0.9% sodium chloride solution, and local decongestants.
Sham control group: Minimal acupuncture at non acupoints.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4, SP 6, BL 31, BL 32" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:2465151,
        TARA:4385250,
        TARA:6742407 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:4385250\": \"SP 6\", \"TARA:2465151\": \"BL 31\", \"TARA:6742407\": \"BL 32\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """LI 4: 5 mm
SP 6: 10 mm
UB 31: 30-50 mm
UB 32: 30-50 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-716 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-716 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 66
Conventional treatment group: 21
Traditional Chinese acupuncture group: 25
Minimal acupuncture at non acupoints group: 19""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Minimal acupuncture at non acupoints
Needle type: Real needles, but smaller (0.5 cun, √ò 0.25 mm, length 13 mm)
Location: Non acupoints, outside the meridians
Penetration: Shallow, maximum depth 0.25 cun
Duration: Needles left in place for 25 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation; a good needle sensation described as soreness, heaviness, or distension was sought." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM term for the condition being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Difficulties in labor initiation (post-term pregnancies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"In the conventional treatment group, sinus soft tissue swelling was reduced over 4 weeks (p = 0.04), and HRQoL improved over 12 weeks (p = 0.01 0.05)."
"Only a non significant difference in symptom score change over 4 and 12 weeks was shown between conventional medication and traditional Chinese acupuncture."
The acupuncture intervention was not found to be effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s): No""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Time elapsed from the time of randomization to delivery.
Secondary outcome measures: Rates of cesarean section, induction of labor, mode of delivery, frequency of spontaneous labor, neonatal complications, change in Bishop score, and cervical dilation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment period: 4 weeks
Duration of each acupuncture session: 25 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was approximately twice weekly for 4 weeks, with each treatment session lasting 25 minutes." .

