tara-kb:S-112625-725 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-725" ;
    dc:title "Manual Acupuncture for Analgesia During Electromyography: A Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Large Intestine 4 (LI-4, He Gu): Located on the dorsum of the first interosseous space of the hand, at the level of the midpoint of the shaft of the second metacarpal bone, on the belly of the first interosseous dorsalis muscle.
Liver 3 (LR-3, Tai Chong): Located on the dorsum of the foot, on the first interosseous space of the metatarsus, in a depression distal to the intermetatarsal joint between the first and second metatarsal bones.
Needles were inserted about 1cm deep bilaterally.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT), Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received telescopic sham needles as a placebo control. These needles were used to mimic real acupuncture needles but did not penetrate the skin, serving as a comparison to assess the placebo effect." ;
