tara-kb:S-112625-727 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-727" ;
    dc:title "Needling Therapies in the Management of Myofascial Trigger Point Pain: A Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details about needle locations or related acupoints)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control groups varied across studies, often involving comparisons between different needling techniques (e.g., wet vs. dry needling).
Some studies used potentially active interventions in control groups, rather than a true placebo.
Specific control groups included:
Subcutaneous water injection over trigger points (Byrn et al.)
Subcutaneous saline injection over trigger points (Byrn et al.)
Sham needling plus metoprolol (Hesse et al.)
Superficial acupuncture, sham IP cords, sham heat (Birch and Jamison)
Occlusal splint (Johansson et al.)
No treatment control (Johansson et al.)
Physical therapy (Kisiel and Lindh)
Dry needling at unselected points (Chu)
Supf saline injection plus supf dry needling (double placebo) (McMillan et al.)""" ;
