tara-kb:S-112625-73 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-73" ;
    dc:title "Effectiveness of Acupuncture as Adjunctive Therapy in Osteoarthritis of the Knee A Randomized, Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Acupuncture point selections based on Traditional Chinese Medicine meridian theory to treat knee joint pain ("Bi" syndrome).
Same points treated for each affected leg; 9 needles inserted in each leg if both knees were affected.
Needle insertion depth: approximately 0.3 to 1.0 inch.
Electrical stimulation at knee points Xiyan: low frequency (8 Hz), square biphasic pulses (0.5-ms pulse width) for 20 minutes.
Specific acupoints not explicitly listed in the paper.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham Acupuncture: Participants received 23 sham acupuncture sessions over 26 weeks. The procedure involved tapping guiding tubes at sham points without needle insertion to mimic the real treatment.
Education Control: Participants received 6 two-hour group sessions based on the Arthritis Self-Management Program, taught by an experienced educator.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0005086 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "approximately 0.3 to 1.0 inch" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-73 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-73 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 570
True acupuncture group: 190
Sham acupuncture group: 191
Education control group: 189""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles were used for sham points, but no actual insertion occurred at true points.
Quantity: 2 needles were inserted into sham points in the abdominal area.
Size: Not specified.
Location: Sham points were in the abdominal area, approximately 3 cm lateral to and slightly above the umbilicus bilaterally.
Penetrating vs. non-penetrating: Non-penetrating at true points; penetrating at sham points.
Other details: Mock plastic needle guiding tubes were used to create sensation at true points without insertion. Needles were attached to the skin with adhesive tape without insertion at true points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) was used in the true acupuncture group at knee points Xiyan with low frequency (8 Hz) and square biphasic pulses (0.5-ms pulse width) for 20 minutes. The sham group had a mock electrical stimulation unit. No other forms of stimulation were mentioned. The \"De-Qi\" sensation was achieved in the treatment group." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Bi syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Osteoarthritis of the knee" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcomes: Western Ontario and McMaster Universities Osteoarthritis Index (WOMAC) pain and function scores
Secondary outcomes: 36-Item Short-Form Health Survey (SF-36) physical component score, patient global assessment, 6-minute walk time""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Not specified
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Total sessions: 23 true acupuncture sessions
Frequency: First 8 weeks: 2 treatments per week
Next 2 weeks: 1 treatment per week
Next 4 weeks: 1 treatment every other week
Last 12 weeks: 1 treatment per month
Adherence: Mean of 22.7 sessions received out of 25 possible sessions""" .

