    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in Taras I Usichenko's study received invasive needle control, where non-acupuncture points were used as a sham acupuncture technique. This involved inserting needles into non-acupuncture points to stimulate neural pathways without the specific effects of acupuncture. The purpose was to compare the postoperative analgesic effect of auricular acupuncture with this control procedure." ;
