    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: 67
Participants within groups: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Streitberger (non-penetrating)
Quantity: Between 8 and 12 needles
Location: Non-traditional acupuncture points, at least 5 cm from the joint where pain was perceived to be maximal
Penetration: Non-penetrating
Electro-stimulation: Not used
Manipulation: Minimal to avoid eliciting sensations""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Electro-acupuncture (EA): 2 Hz electro-stimulation delivered by a TENS unit; needles inserted until 'De Qi' sensation was reported; brief manual manipulation at the beginning and end of therapy.
Sham acupuncture (SA): Minimal manual manipulation to avoid 'De Qi' sensation; no electrical stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Bi Syndrome" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Arthralgia (joint pain) related to aromatase inhibitor use in breast cancer patients" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group(s) based on the primary outcome(s)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Change in pain severity score as measured by the Brief Pain Inventory (BPI) at Week 8 between EA and WLC.
Secondary outcome measures:
Pain-related interference domain of the BPI.
Western Ontario and McMasters Universities Osteoarthritis (WOMAC) Index.
Quick Disability of Arm, Shoulder, Hand (DASH) scale.
Physical Performance Test (PPT).
Patient's Global Impression of Change.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Needles left in place during a session: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: Twice weekly for the first 2 weeks, then weekly for the next 6 weeks.
Number of treatments: 10 treatments over 8 weeks.
Duration of each treatment: 30 minutes.""" .

tara-kb:S-112625-761 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-761" ;
    dc:title "Two-Dimensional Ultrasound and Ultrasound Elastography Imaging of Trigger Points in Women with Myofascial Pain Syndrome Treated by Acupuncture and Electroacupuncture: A Double-Blinded Randomized Controlled Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Gallbladder meridian 20 (GB20)
Gallbladder meridian 21 (GB21)
Large intestine four (LI4)
Liver meridian three (LV3)
Ashi points in the upper trapezius (painful points not predicted on meridians)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received general anesthesia with enflurane alone for inducing and maintaining. The group consisted of 28 males and 2 females, with an average age of 51.08 years and an average body weight of 59.03 kg. Anesthesia was carried out by tracheotomy under local analgesia, with muscle relaxation using fentanyl, mizodiazepam, vecuronium bromide, and disoprofol, and connected to an anesthesia machine for respiratory control. Vecuronium bromide was administered every 25 minutes, and enflurane concentration was adjusted to maintain BP and HR within +10% of baseline." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Brazil" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "GB 20, GB 21, LI 4, LV 3, Ashi" ;
