    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Ashi" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0006862 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit information on the depth of needle insertion for the EA and AC groups)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-761 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-761 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 60
Control group: 30
Tested group: 30""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation was electrical in nature, conducted using electrodes placed on bilateral Hegu (LI4) and Neiguan (PC6) acupoints, linked to a HANS device with specific parameters (2 Hz with 0.6 ms wave width and 100 Hz with 0.2 ms wave width, 10 13 mA in strength). The stimulation was adjusted to the optimal degree that patients could tolerate, suggesting some form of sensation was sought." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Myofascial Pain Syndrome (MPS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcomes of reduced MACen and enflurane dosage, as well as less pronounced changes in HR and BP. The study found significant differences between the groups (P<0.01 for MACen and enflurane dosage, P<0.05 or P<0.01 for HR and BP changes)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Intensity of pain assessed by visual analogue scale (VAS), mean area of myofascial trigger points (MTrP) measured by 2D US and UE.
Secondary outcome measure: Strain ratio (SR) measured by UE.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Duration of each acupuncture session: 15 30 minutes; Needles left in place: Throughout the anesthesia process" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of acupuncture treatments outside of the operation)" .

