    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Wang et al.: Experimental group (n = 19), Control group (n = 17)
Lewis et al.: Total (n = 11)
Mann: Experimental group (n = 50), Control group (n = 50)
Usichenko et al. (pilot): Experimental group (n = 11), Control group (n = 9)
Usichenko et al. (larger): Experimental group (n = 61), Control group (n = 59)
Usichenko et al. (THA): Experimental group (n = 31), Control group (n = 30)
Sator-Katzenschlager et al.: Experimental group 1 (n = 32), Experimental group 2 (n = 32), Control group (n = 30)
Michalek-Sauberer et al.: Experimental group 1 (n = 76), Experimental group 2 (n = 37), Control group (n = 36)
Likar et al.: Experimental group (n = 21), Control group (n = 20)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Usichenko et al. (2005): Sham acupuncture consisted of inserting needles in non-acupuncture points on the helix.
Usichenko et al. (2005): Same methodology as previous study.
Usichenko et al. (2007): Sham procedure involved four non-acupuncture points of the helix.
Sator-Katzenschlager et al. (2006): Sham procedure involved adhesive tapes applied to the ear without needles or electrostimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Wang et al.: Electroacupuncture (EAA) with electrical stimulation at 2-20 Hz.
Lewis et al.: Not specified.
Mann: Not specified.
Usichenko et al.: Fixed indwelling needles without additional stimulation.
Sator-Katzenschlager et al.: Electroacupuncture with and without electrical stimulation.
Michalek-Sauberer et al.: Electroacupuncture with and without electrical stimulation.
Likar et al.: Electroacupuncture.""" ;
