    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Placebo acupuncture
Needle type: Nonpenetrating needles
Quantity: Not specified
Size: Diameter of 0.16 mm
Location: Real acupuncture points (ST44, LI4, ST7, ST6, and TE17)
Penetration: Nonpenetrating
Other details: Nonpenetrating needles were designed to mimic the sensation of skin puncture and tissue penetration without actual penetration.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Active acupuncture: manual rotation of penetrating needles at 0, 15, and 30 minutes. Placebo acupuncture: non-penetrating needles with sensation similar to skin puncture and tissue penetration, no additional stimulation mentioned." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not mention any Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) terminology or conditions)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Post-surgical pain after third molar surgery" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The study found no specific effect of active acupuncture compared to placebo acupuncture (P = .240).
There was a significant nonspecific effect of placebo acupuncture (P < .001).
Patients who believed they received active acupuncture had significantly lower pain levels than those who believed they received placebo acupuncture (P < .001).
Expected pain levels accounted for significant variance in pain ratings (up to 69.8%).
The effectiveness of acupuncture is largely due to nonspecific factors such as patient perception and expectations.
The acupuncture intervention was not effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcome(s): No""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Pain intensity at different time points (√Ä2, 13, and 28 minutes)
Pain unpleasantness at different time points (√Ä2, 13, and 28 minutes)
Secondary outcome measures:
Expected pain intensity levels
Expected pain unpleasantness levels
Perceived treatment allocation""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "The duration of each acupuncture session was 30 minutes. The needles were left in place for the entire 30 minutes, as they were removed at the end of the session." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper only describes a single session of acupuncture treatment lasting 30 minutes, with no information on frequency or multiple sessions)" .

