    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture point: Binao (LI14)
Needle type: Real needles with superficial insertion less than 3 mm
Location: Non-acupuncture point (LI14)
Stimulation: No manual or electrical stimulation
Duration: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Sanyinjiao (SP6), Shuidao (ST28), and Epangxian III (MS4) were stimulated with electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) using a continuous wave at a frequency of 4 Hz.
Zusanli (ST36) was not stimulated electrically.
The sensation sought was "De Qi," characterized by numbness, distention, soreness, and heaviness.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention TCM terminology for the disease or condition)" ;
