    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-780 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 20
Participants within groups: Not specified (ideally 10 in each group based on 1:1 ratio)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Non-invasive sham acupuncture
Needle type: Streitberger's placebo needles (blunt)
Quantity and size: Not specified
Location: Same acupoints as real electroacupuncture
Penetration: Non-penetrating
Other details: Simulated puncturing sensation, held by surgical tape or hair pins, connected to electric stimulator""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electroacupuncture, involving electric currents via inserted acupuncture needles. The needles were stimulated with a 6-volt, biphasic triangular, brief-pulse stimulus at a frequency of 2 Hz. The needles were also manipulated to achieve \"deqi,\" an irradiating feeling considered indicative of effective needling. The stimulation lasted for 30 minutes." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Postpartum depression" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Results: Both electroacupuncture and non-invasive sham acupuncture were effective for postpartum depression, with significant reductions in HDRS 17 scores. There was no significant between-group difference in any outcome measures.
Conclusion: Both interventions were effective, but their efficacy was equivalent, suggesting that the effectiveness of electroacupuncture compared to sham acupuncture is not conclusively established.
Effectiveness compared to control/sham: Maybe/Inconclusive""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcome Measures:
HDRS 17 (Hamilton Depression Rating Scale)
EPDS (Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale)
HADS (Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale)
CGI (Clinical Global Impression scale)
Secondary Outcome Measures:
SDS (Sheehan Disability Scale)
CTRS (Credibility of Treatment Rating Scale)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment: 4 weeks
Frequency of sessions: Twice a week
Duration of each session: 30 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for four weeks, with a minimum interval of two days between sessions." .

