tara-kb:S-112625-783 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-783" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture To Treat Nausea and Vomiting in Early Pregnancy: A Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Traditional Acupuncture Group: Points based on traditional Chinese medicine diagnosis, including:
Stomach meridian: ST19, ST20, ST21
Kidney meridian: K21, K20
Conception vessel points: CV14, CV13, CV12
Specific conditions:
Liver qi stagnation: CV12, P6, GB34, CV13, K21, ST34, ST36
Stomach or spleen qi deficiency: ST36, P6, CV12
Stomach heat: ST44, CV11, ST34, ST21, P6, PC3
Phlegm: ST40, SP9, ST19, BL20, K21
Heart qi deficiency: H5, P6, ST36, CV14
Heart fire: P6, CV14, BL15
P6 Acupuncture Group: P6 point located on the anterior surface of the forearm
Sham Acupuncture Group: Needles inserted close to but not on actual points:
Between pericardium and lung meridian at 6 cun
Between stomach and gallbladder meridians on the ankle
Between third and fourth metatarsals on the foot
Below ST36 on the lower leg""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham acupuncture: Acupuncture needles inserted into areas close to but not on actual acupuncture points.
No acupuncture (control): No active treatment, with weekly telephone calls to assess well-being and encourage compliance.""" ;
