    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Huatojiaji points" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0003419,
        HP:0034267 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-786 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-786 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 18
fTCD: 17
fMRI: 1""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Stimulation at eight placebo points (non-acupoints) using laser needles.
Type of sham needles: Laser needles (non-invasive, non-penetrating).
Location: Non-acupoint locations.
Design: Randomized controlled double-blind cross-over study.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Laser needle acupuncture using red light in cw-mode with an output power of 30-40 mW per laser needle (wavelength: 685 nm). The stimulation is absolutely painless and does not involve any tactile sensation. The study was conducted as a double-blind trial." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide TCM terminology for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Low back and pelvic pain during pregnancy" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The study found a trend towards an increase in mean blood flow velocity in the PCA during laser needle acupuncture, but this was not statistically significant.
Significant changes in brain activity were observed in the occipital and frontal gyri using fMRI.
The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group based on the significant changes in brain activity observed with fMRI.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Pain intensity using a numerical rating scale (NRS) for current pain, average pain over the previous 14 days, and maximum pain over the previous 14 days.
Secondary outcome measures:
Functional capacity: ability to perform general activities, work, and walk.
Use of analgesic drugs (paracetamol).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes; Needles were not left in place beyond irradiation time." ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on how often acupuncture treatments were administered over time)" .

