tara-kb:S-112625-795 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-795" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture and assisted conception" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review of Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham acupuncture points (Benson 2006; Craig 2007; Domar 2006; Paulus 2002; Westergaard 2006)
Sedative pre-medication (Gejervall 2005)
Alfentanil and paracervical block (Stener-Victorin 1999; Stener-Victorin 2003)
Standard analgesia with remifentanil (Sator-K 2006)
Benzodiazepine pre-medication (Humaidan 2004)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Sweden, Austria" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0000789 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-795 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-795 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 2209
Specific sample sizes:
Impact on miscarriage: 409 participants
Live birth rates: 403 participants
Live birth rates in specific trials: 57/207 (acupuncture), 34/196 (control)
Ongoing pregnancy rates: 57/207 (acupuncture), 32/196 (control)
Miscarriage rates: 30/207 (acupuncture), 18/196 (control)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture was performed by needling areas that are not recognized acupoints.
Sham needles that do not penetrate the skin were used, such as the Streitberger placebo needle.
In Paulus 2003, a placebo needle set was used without penetrating the skin.
The sham procedure was non-penetrating.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Needles can be stimulated by manual twirling or with a small electric current as electro-acupuncture (EA).
Some acupuncturists attempt to produce a sensation called 'de Qi', which is a sign of correctly stimulating the acupuncture point.
The source of stimulation could be the hand, fine needle, moxibustion with warming needle, or electrical stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state a primary TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Subfertility" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, but with caution due to potential placebo effect. The meta-analysis suggests that acupuncture may increase live birth rates with IVF, but the findings are not conclusive due to possible placebo effects." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure "Primary outcome: Live birth rate (LBR); Secondary outcomes: Ongoing pregnancy rate, Clinical pregnancy rate, Miscarriage rate" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 10 to 30 minutes
How long the needles were left in place during a session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific information on the frequency or duration of acupuncture treatment sessions)" .

tara-kb:S-112625-796 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-796" ;
    dc:title "The Role of Acupuncture in in vitro Fertilization: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details about the needle locations or related acupoints used in the studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham acupuncture: using superficial needling and blunt (placebo) needles on the true acupuncture points, using acupuncture on other places such as thighs and arms, or using laser sham acupuncture.
No intervention: participants did not receive any acupuncture or sham acupuncture.
Mock transcutaneous electrical acupoint stimulation: used as a control in some studies.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Denmark, Brazil, Germany, China, USA, UK, Australia" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0000789 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-796 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-796 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 5,428
Participants in trials around ET: 3,971
Participants in trials before/after and around ET: 1,457
Detailed sample sizes for individual trials: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Sham acupuncture was performed using various methods: superficial needling and blunt (placebo) needles on true acupuncture points, acupuncture on non-traditional points such as thighs and arms, and laser sham acupuncture. In some studies, placebo needle sets were used without penetrating the skin but at the same acupoints and after the same scheme (e.g., Paulus et al.), and Streitberger placebo needles were used at the same acupoints and time (e.g., Zhang et al.)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Traditional needle acupuncture: Manual manipulation (not explicitly stated but implied by the use of traditional needle acupuncture)
Electroacupuncture: Used in some studies (So et al., Zhang et al.)
Laser stimulation: Used in sham controls
Thermal stimulation (moxibustion): Not mentioned
Sensation sought: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM term for the condition being studied, but it is related to infertility and subfertility)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Infertility/Subfertility" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Acupuncture did not significantly improve clinical pregnancy rates when performed only at the time of ET.
Acupuncture was effective when performed at follicle phase and 25 min before and after ET, or 30 min after ET and during the implantation phase.
No significant difference was found when comparing acupuncture to no acupuncture or sham acupuncture controls around the time of ET.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Clinical pregnancy rate (CPR)
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 25 minutes before and after ET (multiple studies)
30 minutes after ET (Zhang et al. [34], Dieterle [33])
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """On the day of ET: 25 minutes before and after ET
At follicle phase: daily or twice weekly for 2 weeks
Specific studies:
di Villahermosa et al. (2013): on the 1st and 7th day of ovulation induction, day before ovarian puncture, and day after ET
Zhang et al. (2011): 30 minutes after ET
Dieterle (2006): 30 minutes after ET and again 3 days later
Smith (2006): on day 9 of stimulating injections, before ET, and after ET
Cui (2006): daily during mid-follicular phase until oocyte revival
Ho (2009): twice a week for 2 weeks""" .

