tara-kb:S-112625-804 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-804" ;
    dc:title "The role of acupuncture in the management of subfertility" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "The specific acupoints mentioned in the paper include LI4 for inhibiting uterine motility. The paper also references studies by Paulus et al. for additional acupoint information, which is detailed in the tables at the end of the paper. These tables likely contain comprehensive lists of acupoints used in various studies, but the exact details are not specified in the text itself." ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not provide detailed descriptions of the sham procedures used in the studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink """Acupuncture may help restore ovulation in patients with polycystic ovary syndrome, but there is not enough randomized evidence to validate this.
There is insufficient evidence to support the role of acupuncture in male subfertility.
Acupuncture is effective for pain relief during oocyte retrieval for those who cannot tolerate conventional sedation.
The pregnancy rate of IVF treatment is significantly increased when acupuncture is administered on the day of embryo transfer (OR 1.42, 95% CI 1.17-1.72).
Yes, acupuncture is effective compared to control/sham groups for improving pregnancy rates when administered on the day of embryo transfer.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0000789 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Electric stimulation (electroacupuncture) was used, involving lowand high-frequency stimulations.
Manual stimulation was also used, particularly in body acupuncture.
Auricular acupuncture was used, but the specific method of stimulation is not detailed.
Thermal (moxibustion) and laser stimulation are not mentioned.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-804 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-804 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "The control groups in the studies varied: some received conventional analgesia (including premedication), others received no acupuncture, and some received sham acupuncture at nontherapeutic points." ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Twice weekly for 5 weeks, with each session lasting 25 minutes.
Twice weekly for 8 weeks, with each session lasting 25 minutes.
Twice weekly for 10 weeks, with acupuncture sessions lasting 25 minutes and moxibustion sessions lasting 20 minutes.
Immediately after ET and 3 days later.
Twice weekly for 6 weeks, with each session lasting 20 minutes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the condition in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Subfertility" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Not specified (the paper does not provide a comprehensive list of specific acupoints used in the studies)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Restoration of ovulation in patients with polycystic ovary syndrome, increase in pregnancy rate of IVF treatment when acupuncture is administered on the day of embryo transfer.
Secondary outcome measure: Pain relief during oocyte retrieval.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Stener-Victorin et al. (65): 150 patients
Humaidan and Stener-Victorin (66): 200 patients
Gejervall et al. (24): 160 patients
Sator-Katzenschlager et al. (67): 94 patients
Paulas et al. (70): 160 patients
Westergaard et al. (74): 300 patients
Total sample size: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Duration of each acupuncture session: 25 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" .

