Secondary outcome measures:
Implantation rate (proportion of embryos transferred resulting in an intrauterine gestational sac)
Clinical pregnancy rate (one or more intrauterine gestational sacs on scanning or histological confirmation of gestational product in miscarriages)
Ongoing pregnancy rate (pregnancies beyond 10 weeks of gestation)
Live birth rate (baby born after 24 weeks of gestation)
Cortisol concentration
Anxiety level""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Frequency: 2 times/week for 12 weeks
Duration retained (how long needles were left in place): Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """True acupuncture: 30 minutes, 2 times/week for 12 weeks
Low-frequency electroacupuncture: Twice weekly for 2 weeks, once weekly for 6 weeks, and once every other week for 8 weeks, for a total of 14 treatments over 16 weeks""" .

tara-kb:S-112625-812 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-812" ;
    dc:title "In vitro fertilization and acupuncture: Clinical efficacy and mechanistic basis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Not specified (the paper does not provide specific details on the needle locations or related acupoints used in the studies reviewed)" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT), Controlled Trial, Case Series, Observational Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham acupuncture controls were used in two RCTs (Dieterle et al and Smith et al).
Standard IVF procedure without acupuncture was used as a control in the study by Paulus et al.
No acupuncture was used as a control in the studies by Westergaard et al and Balk et al.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0000789 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-812 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-812 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Paulus et al: 160 women (n=80 each group)
Dieterle et al: 225 women (n=116 real acupuncture, n=109 sham acupuncture)
Smith et al: 228 women (n=110 real acupuncture, n=118 sham acupuncture)
Westergaard et al: 262 women (n=87 no acupuncture, n=95 ACU 1, n=80 ACU 2)
Balk et al: 10 women
Emmons and Patton: 6 women
Johnson: 22 women
Narrative case studies: 13 women""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Non acupuncture points were used.
Needle type: Non insertive Streitberger needle.
Quantity and size: Not specified.
Location: Non acupuncture points.
Penetration: Non penetrating.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation methods: Manual manipulation, Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture)
Specific studies:
Paulus et al: Electroacupuncture (EA)
Dieterle et al: Manual acupuncture
Balk et al: Electroacupuncture (EA)
Sensation sought: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Kidney deficiency (TCM)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Infertility" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes (acupuncture found to be effective in improving IVF success rates in some studies, but results are inconclusive due to methodological limitations)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Clinical pregnancy rates, implantation rates, biochemical pregnancy rates, ongoing pregnancy rates
Secondary outcome measures: Quality of life (QOL),Safety""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Paulus et al: EA sessions 25 minutes before and after embryo transfer (total session duration: 50 minutes)
Dieterle et al: Two manual acupuncture treatments given 30 minutes and 3 days after ET (duration of each session not specified)
Smith et al: Three acupuncture treatments (duration of each session not specified)
Balk et al: EA twice a week for 4 weeks (duration of each session not specified)
Emmons and Patton: Twice weekly manual acupuncture for 3 or 4 weeks (duration of each session not specified)
Johnson: Introductory treatment followed by 3 full treatments prior to ET and 2 treatments 25 minutes before and after ET (duration of each session not specified)
Duration of needles left in place during a session: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Two manual acupuncture treatments were given 30 minutes and 3 days after ET.
Three acupuncture treatments on day 9 of stimulating injections and immediately before and after ET.
EA twice a week for 4 weeks prior to ET.
Twice weekly manual acupuncture for 3 or 4 weeks.
Introductory treatment followed by three full treatments before ET and two treatments around ET.""" .

