    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture involved minimal acupuncture at nonacupuncture points.
Needles were inserted 1-1.5 cm away from actual acupuncture sites.
Needles were inserted to a depth of 3-5 mm using a shallow needling technique to avoid de-qi.
The practitioner rotated the needle once for patient blinding.
Other factors like needle size, retention time, treatment frequency, and number of treatments were identical to the active acupuncture group.""" ;
