tara-kb:S-112625-827 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-827" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for persistent allergic rhinitis: a randomised, sham-controlled trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Key acupoints: Yingxiang (LI 20), Yintang (Extra point), Fengchi (GB 20)
Supplementary acupoints based on Chinese medicine syndrome differentiation:
Hegu (LI 4) for lung qi deficiency syndrome
Zusanli (ST 36) for spleen qi deficiency syndrome
Qihai (CV 6) for kidney qi deficiency syndrome
Sham acupuncture: Insertion sites 1-1.5 cm from real acupoints, shallow needling technique (3-5 mm)
Needle insertion depth: 10-30 mm, depending on the acupoint""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Not applicable (the study compares two types of acupuncture without a non-acupuncture control group)" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Australia" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 20, Yintang, GB 20, LI 4, ST 36, CV 6" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:2324295,
        TARA:3135569,
        TARA:6463344,
        TARA:6681003,
        TARA:8833337 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:6681003\": \"LI 20\", \"TARA:3135569\": \"Yintang\", \"TARA:2324295\": \"GB 20\", \"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:8833337\": \"CV 6\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0011786 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Real acupuncture: 10-30 mm
Sham acupuncture: 3-5 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-827 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-827 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 35
Group A (Somatic Acupuncture): 18
Group B (Ear Acupuncture): 17""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (no sham acupuncture group was used in the study)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual stimulation (manual manipulation) was used for both somatic and ear acupuncture groups. A 250 g pressure palpeur was used for manual detection. No specific sensation was mentioned as being sought during stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the disease or condition in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Persistent Allergic Rhinitis (PAR)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"On the basis of the migraine index, pain at the end of therapy was significantly lower than before the treatment, being residual pain 54.83% and 63.43%, respectively for somatic and ear acupuncture."
"On the contrary, a significant difference between the 2 groups was clear during the follow up: in fact, after 6 months residual pain was 16.80% and 48.83% for somatic and ear acupuncture, respectively (p=0.038)."
"This study, despite the limited number of patients, confirms the effectiveness of acupuncture for treatment of migraine without aura."
The study found both somatic and ear acupuncture to be effective in reducing pain, with somatic acupuncture showing a significant advantage in long-term follow-up.
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Nasal obstruction, sneezing, rhinorrhoea, nasal itch, and total nasal symptom score (TNSS)
Secondary outcome measure: Use of PAR relief medication""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Once a week for 8 weeks, with each session lasting 20 minutes." .

tara-kb:S-112625-828 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-828" ;
    dc:title "Effect of Acupuncture in the Treatment of Seasonal Allergic Rhinitis: A Randomized Controlled Clinical Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Primary acupoints: Yingxiang (LI 20), Yintang (Extra point), Fengchi (GB 20)
Supplementary acupoints based on syndrome differentiation:
Lung Qi Deficiency Syndrome: Feishu (BL 13), Taiyuan (LU 9)
Spleen Qi Deficiency Syndrome: Pishu (BL 20), Zusanli (ST 36)
Kidney Qi Deficiency Syndrome: Shenshu (BL 23), Qihai (CV 6)
Details of acupoints (direction, depth, needle technique) are provided in the table on page 4.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture group: Thirty subjects were randomly assigned to two groups with 17 and 13 subjects respectively and treated with real or sham acupuncture (three times per week) for four consecutive weeks and then a crossover for treatments for a further four weeks without a washout period." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Australia" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 20, Extra point, GB 20, BL 13, LU 9, BL 20, ST 36, BL 23, CV 6" ;
