tara-kb:S-112625-830 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-830" ;
    dc:title "A Randomized Treatment-Placebo Study of the Effectiveness of Acupuncture for Benign Vocal Pathologies" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Experimental Group:
Renyin (Stomach Channel 9): Front edge of sternocleidomastoid muscle, ~2 cm lateral to the upper edge of laryngeal prominence.
Lieque (Lung Channel 7): ~2 cm above the wrist crease in the depression below the radial styloid.
Zhaohai (Kidney Channel 6): In the depression inferior to the inferior border of the medial malleolus.
Placebo Group:
Houxi (Small Intestine Channel 3): At the ulnar end of the proximal crease of the fifth metacarpophalangeal joints.
Kunlun (Bladder Channel 60): Midpoint between the prominence of lateral malleolus and the Achilles tendon.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Control Group: Placebo group receiving sham acupuncture on acupoints Houxi (Small Intestine Channel 3) and Kunlun (Bladder Channel 60), which are not related to voicing." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "China" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "ST 9, Lieque, Zhaohai, Houxi, Kunlun" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0220496,
        TARA:2108622,
        TARA:3515622,
        TARA:5047947,
        TARA:6890771 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:6890771\": \"ST 9\", \"TARA:3515622\": \"LU 7\", \"TARA:2108622\": \"KI 6\", \"TARA:0220496\": \"SI 3\", \"TARA:5047947\": \"BL 60\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0001618 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Renyin: 3 cm
Lieque: 2 cm
Zhaohai: 2 cm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-830 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-830 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total participants analyzed: 24; Experimental group: 12; Placebo group: 12" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Acupuncture on acupoints Houxi (Small Intestine Channel 3) and Kunlun (Bladder Channel 60), which are not related to voicing.
Needle type: Real needles made of stainless steel, 40 mm in length, and 0.32 mm in diameter.
Quantity and size: Same as the experimental group.
Location: Non-points/off-meridian related to voicing.
Penetrating: Yes, needles were inserted until subjects reported a sensation.
Duration: Each session lasted 30 minutes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) was used on the Renyin (Stomach Channel 9) acupoint. The stimulation was adjusted to achieve a sensation reported by the subjects." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Hyperfunctional dysphonia associated with yin deficiency and excessive yang leading to phlegm-heat accumulation" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Dysphonia; Hyperfunctional Dysphonia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Acoustic analysis of voice range profile (phonetogram recording)
Perceptual analysis of voice quality (sentence recording task for breathiness and roughness)
Self-perceptions of quality-of-life (QOL) measurement (Voice Activity and Participation Profile VAPP)
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment period: 20 days
Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was once every 2 days, with a total of 10 intensive acupuncture sessions administered within a 20-day period." .

