        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-832" ;
    dc:title "A systematic review of the clinical effectiveness of acupuncture for allergic rhinitis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """ST36 and LI4 were used in one study.
24 different acupoints were used across five studies.
Specific criteria for selecting acupoints (e.g., TCM diagnosis, tender points) are not specified.
Detailed list of all 24 acupoints is not provided in the text.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture treatment involving needling away from the active site or needling at a more shallow depth with shorter needles to avoid stimulating the acupoint." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the country or countries where the study was conducted)" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0011786 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified (the paper describes the placebo treatment as involving shallower needle insertion but does not provide specific measurements or descriptive terms for depth)" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-832 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-832 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants in meta-analysis: Intervention arm = 160, Control arm = 188
Total participants after sensitivity analysis: Intervention arm = 172, Control arm = 169
Specific sample sizes for each study are not explicitly stated in the text or tables.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure involved needling away from active sites or at a more shallow depth with shorter needles.
Specific studies:
Wolkenstein et al.: Placebo needle placed away from defined acupoints.
Langer & Hauswald: Control with inactive laser.
Ng et al.: Control needling at less depth.
Magnusson et al.: Control acupuncture away from intervention acupoints and shallow needling.
Williamson et al.: Control needling on the patella.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Stimulation methods included needle acupuncture with electrostimulation and laser acupuncture.
The comparator involved needling away from the active site or at a more shallow depth to avoid stimulation.
Specific sensations sought during stimulation are not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Allergic Rhinitis (AR)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Symptom severity score measured on a visual analogue scale (VAS)
Secondary outcome measures: Medication use, serum IgE levels, plasma cytokine levels
Other outcomes: Quality of life (QoL), days off work or school""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of sessions: One study: 25 minutes
Another study: 30 minutes
Another study: 5 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment sessions ranged from one to five per week, with a total of two to 16 sessions overall." .

