tara-kb:S-112625-836 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-836" ;
    dc:title "Comparison of traditional Chinese acupuncture, minimal acupuncture at non acupoints and conventional treatment for chronic sinusitis ‡¨ù" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Traditional Chinese Acupuncture (TCA) points:
For retention of damp in the Yangming channel: LI 4 Hegu, LI 11 Quchi, ST 40 Fenglong, ST 44 Neiting.
For retention of Phlegm in the Shaoyang channel: GB34 Yanglingquan, LR 2 Xingjian, LI 4 Hegu, LR 3 Taichong.
Local acupoints around the affected sinuses.
EX HN5 Taiyang for symptoms affecting the lateral area of the eyes.
Sham points:
On each shoulder between LI 15 and TE 14.
On each thigh 3 cun above the midpoint of the patella.
Two bilateral points 2.5 cun lateral to the umbilicus.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group consisted of 14 patients who received the same treatment as the experimental group except for the acupuncture. They did not receive any acupuncture intervention and were used as a comparison to assess the effects of electroacupuncture (EA) on pregnancy rates and uterine artery pulsatility index (PI)." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Norway" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 4, LI 11, ST 40, ST 44, GB34, LR 2, LR 3,Taiyang" ;
