    dc:title "Acupuncture in children and adolescents with bronchial asthma: A randomised controlled study ‡¨ù" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Standard points: BL 13 (both sides, parallel to skin surface, depth of penetration 5 mm), CV 17 (about 45¬∞ angle of inclination to skin surface, depth of penetration 2 4 mm), Lu 7 (both sides, perpendicular to body surface, depth of penetration 2 3 mm)
Additional points based on TCM diagnosis:
Mucous symptoms: St 40 (10 15 mm)
Kidney Qi deficiency: Ki 6 (2 3 mm)
Lung Yin deficiency: LI 11 (10 mm)
Stomach heat: St 41 (5 mm)
Grief, worries, anxieties: BL 42 (5 mm)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received a placebo treatment known as mock TENS (sham transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation), which involved the application of electrodes to the upper back without any actual electrical stimulation." ;
