tara-kb:S-112625-841 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-841" ;
    dc:title "A Double-Blind, Randomized, Placebo-Controlled Trial of Acupuncture for the Treatment of Childhood Persistent Allergic Rhinitis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Yin tang (EX-HN3): midpoint between the medial ends of the supraciliary arches
Shang ying xiang (EX-NH8): upper end of the nasolabial fold
Zu san li (ST36): 4 fingerbreadths below the depression lateral to the patella and 1 fingerbreadth lateral to the anterior border of the tibia
Needle sizes and penetration depths:
EX-HN3: 0.3-mm-diameter, 50-mm-long needle, 0.7-to 1.2-cm penetration, oblique direction
EX-NH8: 0.25mm-diameter, 13-mm-long needle, 0.7-to 1.2-cm penetration, oblique direction
ST36: 0.3-mm-diameter, 50-mm-long needle, 1.2-to 2.4-cm penetration, perpendicular direction
Technique: Needles rotated alternately in a clockwise or counterclockwise manner every 5 minutes for 20 minutes
Selection criterion: Commonly reported to be useful in traditional Chinese medicine journals""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture was used as the control group in this study. It involved puncturing the same acupoints as active acupuncture but with minimal needle penetration and no manipulation to avoid the sensation of qi. This allowed for a comparison of the efficacy of active acupuncture versus a placebo-like intervention." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Hong Kong" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "EX-HN 3, EX-NH 8, ST 36" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:3135569,
        TARA:6463344 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:3135569\": \"Yintang\", \"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "EX-NH 8" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0011786 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Active Acupuncture:
EX-HN3: 0.7 to 1.2 cm
EX-NH8: 0.7 to 1.2 cm
ST36: 1.2 to 2.4 cm
Sham Acupuncture: 0.3 cm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-841 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-841 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants initially recruited: 85
Active acupuncture group: 35
Sham acupuncture group: 37
Total sample size analyzed: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure used the same acupoints as active acupuncture: yin tang (EX-HN3), shang ying xiang (EX-NH8), and zu san li (ST36).
Same type of needles used for sham as for active acupuncture.
Needles inserted to a depth of only 0.3 cm for sham procedure.
No manipulation of the needle was performed during sham procedure.
Sham procedure was penetrating but shallow.
Frequency and duration: 2 sessions per week for 8 weeks.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Active Acupuncture: Manual manipulation (rotation of needles in a clockwise or counterclockwise manner every 5 minutes for 20 minutes); sensation of "qi" (paresthesia) sought.
Sham Acupuncture: No stimulation (needles inserted to a depth of only 0.3 cm with no manipulation).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM classification for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Persistent Allergic Rhinitis" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcomes of daily rhinitis scores and symptom-free days." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: daily rhinitis scores, symptom-free days
Secondary outcome measures: visual analog scale scores of immediate improvement after each treatment, relief medication scores, side effects, treatment preferences of participants at the end of the study, blood eosinophil counts, nasal eosinophil counts, serum IgE levels""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Frequency of sessions: Twice per week
Total duration of treatment period: 8 weeks (16 sessions)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for 8 weeks, totaling 16 sessions." .

tara-kb:S-112625-842 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-842" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for dyspnea in advanced cancer: a randomized, placebo-controlled pilot trial [ISRCTN89462491]" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """True acupuncture points:
ST36: Below the knee, 3 cun inferior to Dubi ST35, one finger breadth lateral to the anterior crest of the tibia.
Ren17: On the anterior midline, at the level with the fourth intercostal space, midway between the nipples.
Auricular lung point: Medial and distal aspect of the tragus.
Auricular kidney point: Medial and proximal aspect of the cymba conchae.
Sham points:
Sham1: Posterior wrist, between radius & ulna, 1 cun distal to radial & ulnar heads.
Sham2: Anterior arm, 3 cun proximal and 3 cun medial to the antecubital crease.
Ear Sham: Adjacent to the "finger point", just below the helix of the auricle, at the apex.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study (Randomized Controlled Trial)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham acupuncture: Sham acupuncture was carried out by the same physicians as verum acupuncture and was standardized to 8 needles at defined non-acupuncture points, 4 needles above the medial part of the tibia bilaterally, with depth of needle insertion less than 5 mm.
Conventional conservative orthopaedic treatment (COT): Patients received conventional orthopaedic therapy with 50 mg diclofenac daily. Additionally, 15 treatment sessions were individually selected from physiotherapy, physical exercise, heat or cold therapy, ultra-sonic treatment, and TENS.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper does not mention the availability of or provide a link to related datasets)" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "ST 36, Ren 17, Auricular lung point, Auricular kidney point" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:3472408,
        TARA:6463344 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:6463344\": \"ST 36\", \"TARA:3472408\": \"CV 17\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Auricular kidney point",
        "Auricular lung point" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0002094 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "0.5 cm -1.5 cm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-842 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-842 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total participants analyzed: 424; Verum group: 154; Sham group: 135; COT group: 135" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles
Quantity: 8 needles
Location: Non-acupuncture points above the medial part of the tibia bilaterally
Penetration: Penetrating but shallow (less than 5 mm)
Other details: Standardized procedure performed by the same physicians as verum acupuncture""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation to achieve a feeling of heat and numbness around the acupuncture point (Deqi)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Dyspnea (shortness of breath)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Subjective sensation of dyspnea assessed with a 0-10 numerical rating scale immediately before and after acupuncture treatment and daily for a week thereafter.
Secondary outcome measure: Mean of seven day breathlessness diary.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration of needles being left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was one to three times per week, with a total of 15 treatments administered over 6 weeks. Each treatment session lasted for 20 minutes." .

tara-kb:S-112625-843 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-843" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture and Chinese herbal medicine in the treatment of patients with seasonal allergic rhinitis: a randomized-controlled clinical trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """TCM group: Standardized treatment with additional acupoints selected based on individual symptoms.
Specific acupoints mentioned: L.I. 4, L.I. 20, GB 20, Lu 7, Liver 3.
Control group: Non-acupuncture points distant from meridians.
Sham acupuncture points: Forearm, foot, lower leg, and other non-traditional points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Control Group: Received sham acupuncture applied to non-acupuncture points.
Sham Acupuncture Points: Ulnar side of the forearm, inner and outer side of the calcaneus, half distance between medial edge of patella and calcaneus internus, four fingers above the tip of the calcaneus internus, half between the inner side of the elbow and the axillae.
Non-specific Chinese Herbal Formula: Consisted of Semen coicis, Radix glycyrrhizae, Poria alba, Humulus lupulus, Fructus oryzae germ., Fructus hordei germ., Fructus crataegi, Massa medicata fermentata.""" ;
