tara-kb:S-112625-845 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-845" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for nasal congestion: A prospective, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled clinical pilot study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Specific verum acupoints were chosen based on the Chinese medical diagnosis according to the "Heidelberg model" of TCM.
The acupuncture points are listed and described in Figs. 2 and 3 (not provided in the text).
Five acupuncture needles were used: two on each side and Rg20 or Ex1.
Needles penetrated the skin to a depth of 1 cm and were kept in place for 15 minutes.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pilot Study (Randomized Controlled Trial)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received \"control acupuncture,\" which involved using nonspecific acupoints not related to the TCM diagnosis. This was designed to be less effective than verum acupuncture by avoiding known verum points and meridians. The control group showed some improvement in VAS but deterioration in NAF." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
