    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Asthma" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Results: No improvement in respiratory function; significant improvement in AQLQ scores and reduction in bronchodilator use.
Conclusion: Acupuncture may offer subjective benefits in quality of life and bronchodilator use, likely due to a placebo effect.
Effectiveness: No (based on objective respiratory outcomes), but yes for subjective quality of life and bronchodilator use.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Respiratory function tests (e.g., FEV1, FVC), Asthma Quality Life Questionnaire (AQLQ)
Secondary outcome measure: Reduction in the usage of bronchodilators""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "20 minutes" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide details on the frequency of acupuncture treatments beyond the initial and second sessions)" .

