tara-kb:S-112625-852 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-852" ;
    dc:title "Health-related quality of life in a trial of acupuncture, sham acupuncture and conventional treatment for chronic sinusitis" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Traditional Chinese Acupuncture (TCA) group: Not specified (points chosen based on individual TCM diagnoses)
Sham group: One point on each shoulder between LI 15 and TE 14
One point on each thigh 3 cun above the midpoint of the patella
Two bilateral points 2.5 cun lateral to the umbilicus""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Type: Minimal acupuncture at non-acupoints
Quantity: Ten treatments
Needle type: Real needles, but smaller (0.5 cun, √ò 0.25 mm, length 13 mm)
Location: Non-acupoints outside the meridians (shoulders, thighs, near umbilicus)
Penetration: Shallow, superficial insertion (maximum depth 0.25 cun)
Duration: Needles left in place for 25 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Norway" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0006031 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Traditional Chinese Acupuncture (TCA): Needles were stimulated manually using reducing or reinforcing methods to achieve a good needle sensation.
Sham Acupuncture: Minimal needle sensation was emphasized with shallow insertion, indicating no significant stimulation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-852 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-852 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Conventional medical therapy: 2-4 weeks of medication with antibiotics, corticosteroids, 0.9% sodium chloride solution, and local decongestants.
Sham acupuncture: minimal acupuncture at non-acupoints outside the meridians.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Ten treatments over 4 weeks, with each treatment lasting 25 minutes. The exact frequency per week is not specified, but it can be inferred as approximately twice a week." ;
