    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 97
Intervention group: 48
Control group: 49""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Retractable needles
Quantity: Not specified
Size: Not specified
Location: Same points as real acupuncture group
Penetrating or non-penetrating: Non-penetrating
Other details: Needles were supported by small adhesive cylinders and did not perforate the skin.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The needles were stimulated using electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture) with a WQ-10D1 electrostimulator. The sensation of Deqi was sought to ensure correct placement and stimulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM condition or terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Osteoarthritis of the knee" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"In the intention to treat analysis, the WOMAC index presented a greater reduction in the intervention group than in the control group (mean difference 23.9, 95% confidence interval 15.0 to 32.8)"
"The reduction was greater in the subscale of functional activity."
"The same result was observed in the pain visual analogue scale, with a reduction of 26.6 (18.5 to 34.8)."
"The PQLC results indicate that acupuncture treatment produces significant changes in physical capability (P = 0.021) and psychological functioning (P = 0.046)."
"Acupuncture plus diclofenac is more effective than placebo acupuncture plus diclofenac for the symptomatic treatment of osteoarthritis of the knee."
"Acupuncture as a complementary therapy to pharmacological treatment of osteoarthritis of the knee is more effective than pharmacological treatment alone, in terms of reducing pain and rigidity, and improving physical functioning and health related quality of life."
"According to the criterion that an improvement in quality of life requires changes in at least two of the variables measured by the PQLC, the acupuncture provided to the intervention group was more effective than the placebo treatment in improving patients' quality of life."
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
WOMAC index
Pain visual analogue scale
Dosage of diclofenac accumulated
Profile of quality of life in the chronically ill (PQLC) instrument
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of treatment program: 12 weeks
Duration of each acupuncture session: Approximately 29.4 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper does not provide information on the frequency of acupuncture treatments within the 12-week period)" .

