tara-kb:S-112625-866 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-866" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture and rehabilitation of the painful shoulder: study protocol of an ongoing multicentre randomised controlled clinical trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol "Tiaokou ST38 point, located equidistally from the flexion fold of the knee and the vertex of the lateral malleolus and 1 inch laterally from the tibial crest, to a depth of 4.5 -5.0 cm, towards the Chengshan UB57 point." ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Control group: TENS-placebo + physiotherapy" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Spain" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "ST 38" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:3182190 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:3182190\": \"ST 38\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0030834,
        MONDO:0002471,
        MONDO:0004857 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "4.5 -5.0 cm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-866 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-866 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 465
Experimental group: 226
Control group: 239""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the control group received a TENS-placebo, not sham acupuncture)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation: The needles were stimulated through vigorous broad bidirectional rotation movements to produce the sensation of Deqi. The needles were manipulated for 1 minute every 5 minutes during the 20-minute session." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM diagnosis or terminology for the condition being studied)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Painful shoulder caused by subacromial syndrome (rotator cuff tendinitis and subacromial bursitis)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Not specified (the paper is a study protocol and does not include results or conclusions)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Change produced on Constant's Shoulder Function Assessment (SFA) Scale
Secondary outcome measures:
Changes in diurnal pain intensity on a visual analogue scale (VAS)
Changes in nocturnal pain intensity on the VAS
Doses of non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) taken during the study period
Credibility scale for the treatment
Degree of improvement perceived by the patient
Degree of improvement perceived by the evaluator""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Needles left in place during a session: 20 minutes
Frequency of sessions: Once a week for three weeks""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Acupuncture treatments are administered once a week for three weeks. Each session lasts 20 minutes with manipulations every 5 minutes." .

tara-kb:S-112625-867 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-867" ;
    dc:title "German Randomized Acupuncture Trial for chronic shoulder pain (GRASP) -A pragmatic, controlled, patient-blinded, multi-centre trial in an outpatient care environment" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Locus dolendi (Ahshi) points
Local and distal points:
Ventral: Lung 1, 2
Ventrolateral: Large Intestine 4, 11, 14, 15
Lateral: Sanjiao 5, 13, 14
Dorsal: Small Intestine 3, 9
Distal points on the homolateral leg: Stomach 38, Gallbladder 34, Bladder 58
Needles inserted unilaterally to a depth of 1-2 cm
Needle manipulation to achieve Deqi""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Pragmatic Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Nurse-led supportive care was used as the control group, where patients received supportive care from a palliative care nurse for a similar length of time as the acupuncture sessions." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper mentions additional data available online but does not provide a direct link to a dataset)" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Lung 1, Lung 2, Large Intestine 4, Large Intestine 11, Large Intestine 14, Large Intestine 15, Sanjiao 5, Sanjiao 13, Sanjiao 14, Small Intestine 3, Small Intestine 9, Stomach 38, Gallbladder 34, Bladder 58" ;
