    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, acupuncture was found to be effective compared to the sham group in reducing migraine attack frequency, with significant differences reported (p<0.001)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Change in the Constant-Murley Score (CMS) at 4 weeks after randomization.
Secondary outcome measures:
Change in CMS at 3, 6, and 12 months after randomization.
Patients' self-reported improvement.
Improvement perceived by the evaluator.
Daytime and night-time intensity of shoulder pain (NRS).
Number of new episodes of pain and their duration.
Number and duration of days' sick leave.
Consumption of analgesic drugs and/or NSAIDs.""" ;
