tara-kb:S-112625-872 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-872" ;
    dc:title "Remote Influences of Acupuncture on the Pain Intensity and the Amplitude Changes of Endplate Noise in the Myofascial Trigger Point of the Upper Trapezius Muscle" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Wai-guan: Located in the extensor indicis muscle, on the dorsal forearm, between the radius and ulna, 3 cm superior to the dorsal transverse wrist crease.
Qu-chi: Located in the extensor carpi radialis longus muscle, on the lateral side of the cubital crease with elbow in full flexion.
Selected based on extensive review of acupuncture literature and clinical experience.
Confirmed as MTrPs (Ah-Shi points) by palpation examination.
Sequence of treatment: Wai-guan first, then Qu-chi, followed by simultaneous manipulation of both points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received sham acupuncture, where the acupuncture needle was inserted into a rubber connector, allowing the patient to feel the needle tip but without actual penetration into the skin." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "TE 5, LI 11" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:8393005,
