Sham acupuncture: Puncturing the skin outside acupoints or inserting needles at nonacupoints.
Conventional pharmacologic medications: Used as a control group in two RCTs.
No treatment: Used as a control group in one study.
Routine care: Used as a control group in one study.""" ;
