    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants analyzed: n = 152 (perennial AR), n = 193 (acupuncture vs. drug therapy)
Participants within groups: Not specified (except for small sample sizes in some trials)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture was defined as acupuncture with or without penetration at acupoints or nonacupoints.
Eight RCTs used penetrating sham acupuncture at nonacupoints.
One RCT used sham acupuncture at acupoints.
Nonpenetrating sham acupuncture was mentioned but not detailed further.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual acupuncture was used in 11 trials.
Electroacupuncture was used in 1 trial.
Needle stimulation causing a typical needle sensation (de-qi) was considered in 7 RCTs.
One trial reported use of the manipulation method only.""" ;
