    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-878 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-878 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total number of studies: 24
Types of studies: 16 RCTs, 6 prospective observational studies, 2 case reports
Sample sizes for specific conditions:
Dermatitis, urticaria, and pruritus: 559 participants
Acne: 185 participants
Chloasma: 180 patients
Breast inflammation: 205 breastfeeding women
Hyperhidrosis: 56 patients
Facial elasticity: 27 women
Detailed sample sizes within groups for each study: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not provide specific details on how the sham acupuncture was performed)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the method of stimulation or if any specific sensation was sought)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly translate the conditions into Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "- Atopic dermatitis - Urticaria - Pruritus - Acne - Chloasma - Neurodermatitis - Dermatitis herpetiformis - Hyperhidrosis - Human papillomavirus wart - Breast inflammation - Facial elasticity" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Atopic dermatitis: Visual analogue scale (VAS) for itch severity, mean wheal or flare size
Urticaria: Rate and duration of urticarial episodes
Acne: Clearance of acne lesions
Chloasma: Clearance of chloasma and normal skin pigmentation
Hyperhidrosis: Reduction in sweating
HPV wart: Clearance of the wart
Facial elasticity: Changes in Moire topography
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Ohlsen 2011: 45-min sessions, 3 times per week for 12 consecutive weeks
Weiying 2006: 30 d
Kvist 2007: Maximum 30-min sessions, 1‚Äì4 sessions total
Ursini 2011: 58 thirty-min sessions over 19 mo
Wang 2008: Daily 30-min sessions
Yun 2013: Five 10-min sessions over 3 wk
Salameh 2008: 35-min sessions twice a week for 12 wk
Iraji 2005: 3 wk
Tao 2009: 25-min sessions every other day for 0.5 mo to 3 mo
Zhao 2006: 2 courses, each consisting of 30-min sessions daily for 10 d
Chou 2005: 1-h sessions 3 times per week for 1 mo
Gao 2002: 30-min sessions twice a week for 4 wk
Jiang 2010: 30-min session
Pfab 2010: 10-min session
Pfab 2011: 20-min sessions twice per week, for 10 sessions
Pfab 2012: 20-min session
Hou 2002: 1‚Äì5 sessions, each session 3‚Äì5 times per day
Kim 2012: 8 sessions twice a week for 4 weeks
Liu 2008: 1‚Äì3 courses, each consisting of 30-min sessions 2‚Äì3 times per week, repeated 10 times
Feng 2010: Ten 30-min sessions performed every other day
Shi 2010: 40-minute daily sessions for first week, then twice a week for 3 mo
Xun 2003: 4 courses, each consisting of fifteen 2to 3-min sessions
Lee 2012: 3-min sessions 3 times per week for 4 wk
Pfab 2005: 15-min session""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Atopic dermatitis: Not specified in text, but details in tables.
Urticaria: Not specified in text, but details in tables.
Hyperhidrosis: Daily 30-min sessions.
HPV wart: 58 thirty-min sessions over 19 months.
Facial elasticity: Five 10-min sessions over 3 weeks.
Dermatitis herpetiformis: 45-min sessions 3 times per week for 12 consecutive weeks.
Breast inflammation: Maximum 30-min sessions, 1‚Äì4 sessions total.""" .

