    dc:title "The effect of acupuncture in the treatment of patients with primary Sjo √àgren's syndrome A controlled study" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Needles placed intramuscularly in the regions of the parotid, submandibular, and labial glands.
Specific acupuncture points stimulated:
Segmentally localized: ST 6, ST 7, TE 23, BL 2, CV23, CV24, GV20, GV26, Biantao, Quianzheng.
Non-segmentally localized: ST 36, LI 4, KI 3.
Bilateral stimulation: ST 6, ST 7, TE 23, BL 2, Biantao, Quianzheng.
Unilateral stimulation: Remaining points.
Criteria for choosing points: Not explicitly mentioned in terms of TCM diagnosis or tender points; points chosen based on localization in affected gland tissue and efficacy for pain and xerostomia.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group was a waitlist control group that did not receive active treatment during the initial 10 weeks. After this period, they received acupuncture treatment." ;
