tara-kb:S-112625-881 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-881" ;
    dc:title "Influence of acupuncture on type I hypersensitivity itch and the wheal and flare response in adults with atopic eczema -a blinded, randomized, placebo-controlled, crossover trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Verum Acupuncture Points:
Quchi: Located on the elbow at the midpoint of the line joining the lateral end of the transverse cubital crease and the lateral epicondyle of the humerus.
Xuehai: Located on the medial thigh two patient's thumb widths superior to the superomedial angle of the patella, on the vastus medialis muscle.
Placebo Acupuncture Points:
Arm: Located at the midpoint of the acromial part of the deltoid muscle.
Leg: Located on the frontal thigh four patient's thumb widths superior to the middle of the upper patella border, on the rectus femoris muscle.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Verum acupuncture (VA): Acupuncture at points Quchi and Xuehai on the dominant side.
Placebo-point acupuncture (PA): Acupuncture at non-classical acupoints in the same dermatomes as the verum points.
No acupuncture (NA): No acupuncture intervention.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Germany" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "LI 11, SP 10" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:8433932,
        TARA:8923096 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:8923096\": \"LI 11\", \"TARA:8433932\": \"SP 10\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0004980 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "2-3 cm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-881 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-881 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 30
Participants by gender: Female: 16, Male: 14
Participants by allergen sensitivity: Grass pollen: 13, Dermatophagoides pteronyssinus: 17
Participants in each group: All 30 participants were part of all three groups (verum acupuncture, placebo-point acupuncture, no acupuncture)
Analyzed sample size: 29 (after excluding one patient)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Placebo-point acupuncture
Location: Arm (midpoint of the acromial part of the deltoid muscle) and leg (frontal thigh four patient's thumb widths superior to the middle of the upper patella border, on rectus femoris muscle)
Needle type: Real needles
Quantity and size: Not specified
Penetration: Penetrating
Other details: Performed in the same manner as verum acupuncture but at non-traditional points""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation for 5 seconds; no further stimulation after initial manipulation." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention the condition in Traditional Chinese Medicine terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Atopic eczema" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes" ;
