tara-kb:S-112625-90 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-90" ;
    dc:title "Comparison of the effect of two types of acupuncture on quality of life in secondary progressive multiple sclerosis: a preliminary single-blind randomized controlled trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Chinese medical acupuncture: Points were commonly needled bilaterally with insertion depths ranging from 0.5 to 1.5 cun. Specific points like Stomach 34 and Spleen 10 were considered due to their location in the quadriceps muscle.
Minimal acupuncture: Points were located away from real acupuncture points and those important in treating multiple sclerosis. Needles were inserted just through the skin.
Points were selected based on traditional Chinese medical patterns identified through a questionnaire.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Preliminary single-blind randomized controlled trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Minimal acupuncture was used as a comparison group to Chinese medical acupuncture. It involved superficial needling away from true acupuncture points and was designed to be less effective. This is not a traditional control group but rather a comparison intervention." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper does not mention the availability of or provide a link to related datasets)" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Stomach 34, Spleen 10" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:8433932,
        TARA:8773594 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:8773594\": \"ST 34\", \"TARA:8433932\": \"SP 10\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0000450 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Chinese medical acupuncture: 0.5 to 1.5 cun
Minimal acupuncture: Just through skin (subcutaneous)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-90 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-90 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 14
Participants in Chinese medical acupuncture group: 7
Participants in minimal acupuncture group: 7""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles (Chinese Kangnian)
Quantity: Mean number of points needled was 4
Size: Length 13 mm, gauge 0.20
Location: Away from true acupuncture sites
Penetration: Just through the skin
Other details: No 'De Qi' elicited, no stimulation of needles""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Chinese medical acupuncture: Manual stimulation of needles at 5-minute intervals; needles remained in situ for 25 minutes. De Qi was elicited.
Minimal acupuncture: No stimulation of needles; needles inspected visually at 5-minute intervals.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "- Spleen-Qi Deficiency and Damp - Painful Bi-Syndrome - Liver-Blood Deficiency and Wind - Kidney-Yang Deficiency - Heart-Blood Deficiency" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Secondary progressive multiple sclerosis (SPMS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """Direct quote: "Participants receiving minimal acupuncture demonstrated statistically significant greater improvement in the Multiple Sclerosis Impact Scale 29 psychological subscale compared with those receiving Chinese medical acupuncture in an intention-to-treat analysis (P ¬º 0.04), with mean change in Chinese acupuncture group of 6.0 (SD 13.9) and in minimal acupuncture group of 23.0 (SD 21.0)."
Effectiveness: Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Multiple Sclerosis Impact Scale 29 (MSIS-29)
Secondary outcome measures: Fatigue Severity Scale, General Health Questionnaire 12""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "25 minutes (duration of each session); 25 minutes (needles left in place)" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Twice weekly for five consecutive weeks; 10 treatments in total, each lasting 25 minutes." .

tara-kb:S-112625-900 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-900" ;
    dc:title "Treatment of moderate obstructive sleep apnea syndrome with acupuncture: A randomised, placebo controlled pilot trial q" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """P 6 (Neiguan): 2 cun above the wrist crease, between the tendons of palmaris longus and flexor carpi radialis
Lu 7 (Lieque): 1.5 cun above the wrist crease, superior to the styloid process of the radius
Li 4 (Hegu): in the middle of the second metacarpal bone on the radial side
Li20 (Yingxiang): in the nasolabial groove, level with the midpoint of the lateral border of the ala nasi
Gv20 (Bahui): 5 cun posterior to the anterior head line
Ren 23 (Lianquan): at the upper border of hyoid bone
St 36 (Zusanli): four fingers' breadth below the lateral depression of the patella, one finger width lateral from the anterior border of the tibia
St 40 (Fenglong): 8 cun below the inferior border of the knee and two finger widths lateral to the anterior border of the tibia
Sp 6 (Sanyinjiao): 3 cun directly above the tip of the medial malleoulus on the posterior border of the tibia
Kd 6 (Zhaohai): in a depression below the tip of the medial malleolus""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT), Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Placebo acupuncture group: involved interventions such as insertion of needles into non-acupuncture points or use of non-penetrating needles.
No acupuncture group: received standard care, which typically included analgesics and physiotherapy, but did not receive any form of acupuncture or placebo acupuncture.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Brazil" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
