    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Some trials used non-penetrating needles.
Others used superficial needling at non-acupuncture points with fine needles, avoiding Qi and manual stimulation.
Some sham procedures involved electrical stimulation at non-acupuncture points.
Non-penetrating needles were used in some trials.
Laser turned off, held over symptomatic points without mechanical pressure was used in some trials.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Non-penetrative needling: No stimulation.
Superficial needling at non-acupuncture points: Avoiding Qi and manual stimulation.
Needling at acupuncture points: Indicator lights on, no electrical stimulation.
Needling at non-acupuncture points: Electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture).
Laser turned off, held over symptomatic points: No mechanical pressure.""" ;
