tara-kb:S-112625-905 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-905" ;
    dc:title "Electroacupuncture for Primary Insomnia: A Randomized Controlled Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Yintang (EX-HN3)
Baihui (GV20)
Bilateral ear Shenmen
Sishencong (EX-HN1)
Anmian (EX)
Selected based on systematic review and expert opinion.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group in this study received placebo acupuncture using Streitberger needles at the same acupoints as the intervention group, simulating the sensation of acupuncture without actual penetration." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Hong Kong" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified (the paper provides a trial registration number but does not explicitly mention the availability of a dataset or provide a direct link)" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "EX-HN 3, GV 20, Ear Shenmen, EX-HN 1, Anmian" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:3135569,
        TARA:3386254,
        TARA:3480360,
        TARA:9610280 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:3135569\": \"Yintang\", \"TARA:3386254\": \"GV 20\", \"TARA:9610280\": \"Sishencong\", \"TARA:3480360\": \"Anmian\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Ear Shenmen" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0013600 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-905 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-905 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total participants: 60
Participants within groups: Approximately 30 in each group (electroacupuncture and placebo acupuncture)
Participants who completed the study: 57""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure: Placebo acupuncture using Streitberger needles.
Needle type: Streitberger needles (sham).
Quantity and size: Not specified.
Location: Same acupoints as real electroacupuncture (Yintang, Baihui, bilateral ear Shenmen, Sishencong, Anmian).
Penetration: Non-penetrating.
Other details: The blunt needle was not fixed inside the copper handle, simulating puncturing without actual penetration.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used in the study was electroacupuncture, involving an electric stimulator (CE-FAR Acus II) delivering a constant-current, 0.45-ms, square-wave, brief-pulse stimulus of 4-Hz frequency. The needles were left in place for 30 minutes, and a \"de qian irradiating feeling\" was sought as an indicator of effective needling." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention a TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Primary insomnia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The study found that both electroacupuncture and placebo acupuncture showed significant improvements compared to baseline. However, there were no significant between-group differences in the primary outcome measure, the Insomnia Severity Index (ISI). Electroacupuncture showed significant improvements in sleep efficiency (SE) compared to placebo acupuncture. The proportions of participants achieving certain sleep quality criteria were significantly higher in the electroacupuncture group. The study concludes that there is a slight advantage of electroacupuncture over placebo acupuncture, but notes that further studies are needed due to limitations and uncertainties in the findings.
Yes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Insomnia Severity Index (ISI)
Secondary outcome measures:
Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS)
Sheehan Disability Index (SDI)
Credibility of Treatment Rating Scale (CTRS)
Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index (PSQI)
Sleep diary measures: TIB, SOL, WASO, TST, SE
Actigraphy measures: SOL, TST, WASO, SE""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes (needles left in place)
Treatment frequency: 3 times per week
Total treatment duration: 3 consecutive weeks""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "3 times per week for 3 weeks" .

