    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly translate BMS into TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Burning mouth syndrome (BMS)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """The total effective rate of blood pressure lowering in the acupuncture group was slightly higher than in the control group, but there was no significant difference between the two groups.
The acupuncture group showed a better total effective rate for symptom relief compared to the control group (P<0.05).
Both groups showed significant reductions in blood pressure before and after treatment, but the degrees of lowering were similar.
The acupuncture group had a significant reduction in the product of SBP and HR (P<0.01).
The lowering of nighttime blood pressure load was significantly greater in the acupuncture group compared to the control group (P<0.01).
The acupuncture intervention was effective compared to the control group for symptom relief and nighttime blood pressure load reduction, but not significantly more effective for overall blood pressure lowering.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Visual analogue scale
Secondary outcome measures: Beck Depression Inventory, LANSS pain scale, SF-36""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified" .

