tara-kb:S-112625-934 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-934" ;
    dc:title "Effects of Trigger Point Acupuncture Treatment on Temporomandibular Disorders: A Preliminary Randomized Clinical Trial" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Trigger points were located on the most important masticatory and cervical muscles.
Specific muscles examined for myofascial trigger points are listed in Table 1 (content not provided).
Needles were inserted into the skin over the trigger points to a depth of 5-15 mm.
The 'sparrow pecking' technique was used to elicit a local muscle twitch response.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "Sham acupuncture group: Received treatment with blunt-tipped needles that did not penetrate the skin, mimicking the sensation of acupuncture without actual penetration." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Japan" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005473 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "5e15 mm" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-934 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-934 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 16
Trigger point acupuncture group: 7
Sham acupuncture group: 8""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Stainless steel needles with cut-off tips to prevent penetration.
Quantity and size: Same as real acupuncture group (0.2 mm √Ç 50 mm).
Location: Same myofascial trigger points as the real acupuncture group.
Penetration: Non-penetrating.
Other details: Cut ends smoothed with sandpaper; same procedure applied as real acupuncture.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Manual manipulation using the 'sparrow pecking' technique to elicit a local twitch response." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM equivalent or description for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Temporomandibular disorders (TMDs), specifically chronic temporomandibular joint myofascial pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the control/sham group based on the primary outcome of pain intensity. The statistical significance is supported by p-values: p < 0.001 for the trigger point group and p < 0.050 for the sham group, with a significant difference between groups (p Z 0.0152 and p Z 0.003)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures:
Pain intensity (visual analogue scale)
Oral function (maximal mouth opening)
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: 15 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The frequency of treatment was once per week for a total of five sessions, with each session lasting 30 minutes. The treatment period spanned 10 weeks." .

