tara-kb:S-112625-937 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-937" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture in xerostomia -a systematic review" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Segmental points: ST 3, ST 4, ST 5, ST 6, ST 7, SI 17, LI 18, TE 17, ST 6, ST 7, TE 23, BL 2, CV 23, CV 24, GV 20, GV 26, Biantao, Quianzhen.
Non-segmental points: PC 6, HT 7, LI 4, LI 8, LI 10, SI 3, SI 7, GV 20, CV 9, CV 17, ST 36, KI 3, KI 5, SP 4, SP 6, SP 8, LI 11, TE 5, GB 41, LR 3.
Auricular points: Shemen, vegetativum, kidney, spleen, mouth, subcortex, pancreas, endocrine, hormone.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Study 19: Superficial needling (sham acupuncture)
Study 20: Superficial needling (sham acupuncture)
Study 21: Untreated control, waiting list""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition HP:0000217 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-937 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-937 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not provide explicit numbers for the sample size or the distribution of participants within groups)" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """For Blom et al. (19) and Blom et al. (20): Superficial needling was used as the sham procedure.
For List et al. (21): No sham acupuncture group was used; instead, an untreated control, waiting list was used.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Manual stimulation: One manual stimulation per treatment in studies by Blom et al. (19 and 20).
Electro-acupuncture (EA): Four manual and electric stimulations per treatment with a frequency of 2 Hz in the study by List et al. (21).
No mention of thermal (moxibustion) or laser stimulation.
No specific sensation sought during stimulation mentioned.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly mention any Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) terminology or conditions related to xerostomia)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Xerostomia" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Resting salivary flow rates, stimulated salivary flow rates
Secondary outcome measures: Subjective symptoms (burning sensation in the mouth, mouth dryness, eye dryness measured with visual analogue scale (VAS))""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Blom et al. (19): 20 minutes per session, two sessions per week for two 6-week periods
Blom et al. (20): 20 minutes per session, two sessions per week for two 6-week periods
List et al. (21): 30 minutes per session, two sessions per week for 10 weeks
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Study 1 (Blom et al., 19): Twice weekly, 20 minutes per treatment, for two 6-week periods.
Study 2 (Blom et al., 20): Twice weekly, 20 minutes per treatment, for two 6-week periods.
Study 3 (List et al., 21): Twice weekly, 30 minutes per treatment, for 10 weeks.""" .

