    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-96 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 187
Hegu acupuncture group: 64
Standardized acupuncture group: 60
Usual Care group: 63""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails "Not applicable (the paper does not describe a sham acupuncture group or procedure)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Standardized acupuncture: Manual manipulation by twirling needles at 10 minutes and before removal.
Hegu acupuncture: Manual manipulation by twirling and drawing back the needle, with multiple penetrations in different directions to achieve de qi sensation.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a specific TCM term for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Chronic low back pain (CLBP)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, both Hegu and standardized acupuncture were effective compared to the control group based on RMDQ and VAS scores, with Hegu being more effective than standardized acupuncture. Statistical significance was reported with p-values less than 0.001 for comparisons with the usual care group and p-values less than 0.05 for comparisons between Hegu and standardized acupuncture." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measures: Modified Roland-Morris Disability Questionnaire (RMDQ) for dysfunction, Visual Analogue Scale (VAS) for symptom severity
Secondary outcome measures: Diagnosis and Curative Effect Standard for Syndrome of TCM for CLBP, Physical and mental health component summary scores of the Medical Outcomes Study Short-Form 36 Health Survey (SF-36)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: Not specified
Duration needles were left in place: 20 minutes""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency """Frequency: Every other day for 3 weeks, then twice weekly for 4 weeks.
Total treatments: 18 over 7 weeks.""" .

