    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 275
Sample size per group: Initially planned for 70 per group""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture involved selecting nonspecific acupuncture points for low back pain.
These points were punctured following the same procedure as for true acupuncture.
Real needles were likely used, but the locations were not traditional acupuncture points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """True Acupuncture (TA): Manual insertion of needles following traditional Chinese medicine criteria.
Sham Acupuncture (SA): Manual insertion of needles at nonspecific points.
Placebo Acupuncture (PA): Momentary pressure with a semiblunted needle.
No additional stimulation techniques mentioned (e.g., manual manipulation, electrical stimulation, thermal stimulation, laser therapy).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not provide a TCM-specific diagnosis or terminology for the condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Acute nonspecific low back pain" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes, the acupuncture intervention was found to be effective compared to the control group based on the primary outcome. The study found that all three types of acupuncture were more effective than conventional treatment alone, with statistically significant differences. However, there were no significant differences among the three acupuncture modalities themselves." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Reduction in Roland Morris Disability Questionnaire scores of 35% or more after 2 weeks' treatment.
Secondary outcome measures: Pain intensity (visual analogue scale 0-100 mm), disability (relative change in RMQ), occupational disability due to LBP, persistence of the initial LBP, appearance of new episodes of LBP, improvement perceived by the patient, fear of LBP and conduct to avoid LBP (evaluated with the Fear Avoidance Beliefs Questionnaire).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified for TA and SA; momentary pressure for PA""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Five 20-minute sessions over a period of 2 weeks, approximately 2-3 sessions per week." .

