tara-kb:S-112625-977 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-977" ;
    dc:title "Randomized Trial of Acupuncture for Nicotine Withdrawal Symptoms" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Electroacupuncture Group (Group A): "Lung" point in each ear, located in a depression in the center of the cavum conchae, identified by inspection.
Sham Control Group (Group S): Needles placed superficially over the center of the mastoid bone (not an acupuncture point).""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Sham control procedure: Superficial needling over the mastoid bone with minimum noxious stimulation.
Sham control procedure: Transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation (TENS) pads fixed with adhesive tape over the mastoid bone.
Both sham procedures used an inactivated version of the EA apparatus to ensure no actual therapeutic effect.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United Kingdom" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "Lung" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "Lung" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0008575 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-977 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-977 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 76
Participants in electroacupuncture group: Not specified
Participants in sham control group: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham procedure involved two methods: needles placed superficially over the mastoid bone (non-acupuncture point) with minimum noxious stimulation, and TENS pads fixed with adhesive tape over the mastoid bone.
Needles used in sham procedure were similar to those used in real acupuncture but placed at non-acupuncture points.
Sham procedure was non-penetrating or minimally penetrating.
Leads from inactivated EA apparatus were attached to sham needles or TENS pads, with no actual electrical stimulation delivered.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "The stimulation used was 100-Hz electroacupuncture with needles inserted into the \"Lung\" point in each ear. The intensity was adjusted to just above the threshold of sensation. Needles were stimulated using electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture)." ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Nicotine Withdrawal Symptoms" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "No" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Daily withdrawal symptom score measured by visual analog scale scores for 6 questions related to nicotine withdrawal symptoms.
Secondary outcome measure: Smoking cessation assessed by self-reports and confirmed by expired air carbon monoxide concentration.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 20 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Not specified""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "The acupuncture treatments were administered on days 1, 3, and 7 of smoking cessation, with each session lasting 20 minutes." .

