tara-kb:S-112625-979 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-979" ;
    dc:title "A meta-analysis of ear-acupuncture, ear-acupressure and auriculotherapy for cigarette smoking cessation" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Lung (23 studies)
Shenmen (14 studies)
Mouth (9 studies)
Shoulder (6 studies)
Eye (3 studies)
Knee (2 studies)
Non-points as controls (5 studies)
Not specified: Detailed locations of these points on the body or criteria for choosing these points.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Systematic Review" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails """Pool 1: Inactive EAP/R controls, including "sham" acupuncture on non-specific points and "sham" acupuncture/acupressure using real points not specific for SC.
Pool 2: Other active SC therapies, such as SC-specific behavioural therapy and SC-specific body acupuncture.
Other controls: Wait-list, no intervention, oral placebo, medical therapy.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.drugalcdep. 2014.07.002" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0008575 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-979 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-979 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails "Total participants: 3,735. Participants within groups: Not specified in the text; likely detailed in tables." ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Sham acupuncture was performed on locations not listed as acupuncture points.
Sham acupuncture/acupressure used real points not specific for smoking cessation.
Non-points were used as controls in some studies, but exact locations were not specified.
Non-acupuncture points used as controls included Shoulder, Eye, and Knee.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails """Needles: Manual manipulation (participants stimulated points when cravings occurred), electrical stimulation (electroacupuncture), laser stimulation (1 minute per point).
Pressure: Manual manipulation (participants stimulated points when cravings occurred).
Electricity: Electrostimulation (20 minutes duration).
Laser: Laser stimulation (1 minute per point).
Sensation sought: Deqi sensation (Tehchi) in one study.
Needles not stimulated: Not specified if needles were stimulated after insertion.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not mention a specific TCM disease or condition)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cigarette smoking cessation" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings "Yes (effective compared to control/sham group(s) in Pool 1) / Maybe/Inconclusive (in Pool 2)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary outcome measure: Cigarette smoking cessation (SC) rates at end-of-treatment (EoT), three, six, and 12 months follow-up.
Secondary outcome measures: Not specified.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 15 to 30 minutes
Duration needles were left in place: Ear press-needles retained from 3 to 4 days up to 3 weeks; Ear beads retained from 3 to 14 days
Duration of electrostimulation: 20 minutes
Duration of laser stimulation: 1 minute per point""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Not specified (the paper provides information on treatment duration and session length but does not specify the frequency of treatment administration)" .

