tara-kb:S-112625-989 a TARA:6701896,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dc:identifier "tara-kb:S-112625-989" ;
    dc:title "Acupuncture for the Treatment of Cocaine Addiction Investigation of a Needle Puncture Control" ;
    tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol """Active Auricular Sites:
Sympathetic: located in the deltoid fossa at the junction of the infra-antihelix crus and the medial border of the helix
Lung: located in the center of the cavum concha
Shen men: located in the inferior corner of the bifurcating point of the antihelix
Active Body Site:
He gu (LI 4): located between the first and second metacarpal bones, approximately in the middle of the second metacarpal bone on the radial side
Control Sites:
Auricular: approximately 2 mm from the active auricular points
Body: close to the active point, in a site determined to be nonactive (no 'de qi' sensation elicited)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasClinicalTrialType "Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT) Pilot Study" ;
    tara-kb:hasControlGroupsDetails "The control group received sham acupuncture, where needles were inserted in control sites within 2-3 mm of the active auricular sites and in a nonactive body site with minimal depth and no twisting." ;
    tara-kb:hasCountryOfStudy "United States" ;
    tara-kb:hasDatasetLink "Not specified" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupoints "sympathetic, lung, shen men, hegu" ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMapped TARA:0859695,
        TARA:2442762 ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsMappedCurie "{\"TARA:2442762\": \"HT 7\", \"TARA:0859695\": \"LI 4\"}"^^rdf:JSON ;
    tara-kb:hasListedAcupointsUnmappable "lung",
        "sympathetic" ;
    tara-kb:hasMappedWesternCondition MONDO:0005186 ;
    tara-kb:hasNeedlingDetails """Auricular points: 2 mm
Body points (active): approximately 10 mm
Body points (control): 2 mm""" ;
    tara-kb:hasOCSIAppraisalID tara-kb:O-112625-989 ;
    tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID tara-kb:A-112625-989 ;
    tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails """Total sample size: 40
Active group: 20
Control group: 20""" ;
    tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails """Needle type: Real needles (stainless steel, 0.20 mm wide, 15 mm long)
Quantity: Three auricular sites plus one body site
Location: Control sites within 2-3 mm of active sites (non-traditional points)
Penetration: Penetrating
Depth: Auricular points 2 mm, body point minimal depth""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails "Not specified (the paper does not mention any type of stimulation beyond needle insertion)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedTCMCondition "Not specified (the paper does not explicitly state the disease/condition in TCM terminology)" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition "Cocaine dependence" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyFindings """"Overall, there was a positive response to treatment on a variety of drug-related and psychosocial measures. Cocaine use decreased significantly for patients in both needle puncture groups."
"The only statistically significant difference between the two types of needle puncture was on ratings of craving."
"There was no main effect for type of acupuncture received, and no significant interaction."
"Craving. There was a main effect for Time [F(6,168) = 5.05, p < .001], and a main effect for type of acupuncture [F(1,28) = 4.18, p < .05]."
"We found no statistically significant difference between the active and control needle puncture treatments on any measure, with the exception of craving; the active acupuncture group reported significantly less craving for cocaine during the course of the study than did the control needle puncture group."
"Power calculations were conducted to determine the sample size necessary to detect the difference between needle puncture groups for percentage of urines testing positive for cocaine during the course of the study."
The acupuncture intervention was not found to be significantly effective compared to the control/sham group for the primary outcome of cocaine use, but it was effective in reducing craving.""" ;
    tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure """Primary Outcome Measures:
Cocaine use determined by urine toxicology screens
Self-reported frequency of cocaine use
Self-reported amount of cocaine used
Cocaine craving measured on a scale
Secondary Outcome Measures:
Changes in depression (Beck depression scores)
Psychosocial functioning (ASI composite scores)
General symptoms of distress (SCL-90 subscale scores)
Acute effects of acupuncture (AEA scales)""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration """Duration of each acupuncture session: 45 minutes
Needles left in place during a session: 45 minutes
Treatment regimen: Daily sessions, 5 days a week, for 6 weeks""" ;
    tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency "Daily acupuncture treatments were administered 5 days a week (Monday through Friday) for a total of 6 weeks. Participants received an average of 18 treatments, with an average of three treatments per week." .

