        "Ventral ramus of first thoracic spinal nerve" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0003727 .

ILX:0794996 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Ilioinguinal nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The ilioinguinal nerve is a branch of the first lumbar nerve (L1). The ilioinguinal nerve then perforates the transversus abdominis near the anterior part of the iliac crest, and communicates with the iliohypogastric nerve between the transversus and the internal oblique muscle." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0034987 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794996 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0034987 ],
        UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0795286 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "clavipectoral triangle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A triangular region bounded by the clavicle superiorly, the pectoralis major medially, and the deltoid laterally." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0008785 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clavipectoral_triangle" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795286 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0008785 ],
        UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795289 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "radial fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The radial fossa, also called the anatomical snuffbox, is a triangular depression on the lateral wrist. It is bordered by the tendons of the extensor pollicis longus, extensor pollicis brevis, and abductor pollicis longus, with the scaphoid and trapezium forming its floor. It houses the radial artery and is clinically relevant for assessing scaphoid fractures or arterial pulse." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001461 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/radial-fossa-1537018612" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:23452,
        ILX:0795289 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001461 ],
        UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795291 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "mandibular notch" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The mandibular notch, also known as the sigmoid notch, is a groove in the ramus of the mandible. A curved depression between the coronoid and condylar processes of the mandible." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0003129 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandibular_notch" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:59481,
        ILX:0795291 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0003129 ],
        UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795293 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "lesser supraclavicular fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A small depression located superior to the clavicle and medial to the clavicular head of the sternocleidomastoid muscle." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0000974 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/lesser-supraclavicular-fossa-1536888804" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:84981,
        ILX:0795293 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0000974 ],
        UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795294 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "greater supraclavicular fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The greater supraclavicular fossa refers to the larger, lateral depression above the clavicle, located lateral to the sternocleidomastoid muscle." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0000974 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/greater-supraclavicular-fossa-1536888404" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:84958,
        ILX:0795294 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0000974 ],
        UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795296 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "sternal angle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The sternal angle (angle of Louis, Ludwig, or Ludovicus) is the inclined junction between the anterior surfaces of the manubrium and body of the sternum." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/skeletal-system/axial-skeleton/sternal-angle/18493" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:7547,
        ILX:0795296 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001443 ],
        UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795302 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "infrasternal angle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The infrasternal angle (subcostal angle) is formed in front of thoracic cage by the cartilages of the tenth, ninth, eighth, and seventh ribs, which ascend on either side, where the apex of which the xiphoid process projects." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0000916 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/infrasternal-angle-1537019816" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:7573,
        ILX:0795302 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0000916 ],
        UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795304 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "rectus femoris muscle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The rectus femoris is a muscle in the anterior compartment of the thigh. It forms part of the quadriceps femoris muscle complex, and is the only muscle in this group to cross both the hip joint and the knee joints." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0008784 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rectus_femoris_muscle" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795304 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0008784 ],
        UBERON:0001630 .

ILX:0795309 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "axillary fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A pyramidal depression located at the junction of the upper limb and thorax, commonly referred to as the armpit." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0008785 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/axillary-fossa-1536889648" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:61464,
        ILX:0795309 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0008785 ],
        UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795323 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "posterior axillary line" ;
    IAO:0000115 "Posterior axillary line is an imaginary reference line which can be drawn on the posterior torso. It extends vertically downwards from the posterior axillary fold. The posterior axillary line runs in parallel to the midaxillary and anterior axillary lines." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/posterior-axillary-line-1536888360" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:20260,
        ILX:0795323 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001443 ],
        UBERON:0006800 .

ILX:0795325 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "tibialis anterior tendon" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The tibialis anterior tendon is the tendon of the tibialis anterior muscle, located on the front of the lower leg. It passes along the ankle and inserts on the medial cuneiform and the first metatarsal. This tendon enables dorsiflexion and inversion of the foot. The tibialis anterior tendon (TAT) begins at the distal one-third of the tibia. It is the most medial tendon of the ankle and foot." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0000978 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tibialis_anterior_muscle" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:47050,
        ILX:0795325 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0000978 ],
        UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0795327 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "mentolabial sulcus" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The mentolabial sulcus is the vertical groove or fold that forms between the lower lip and the chin, marking the transition between the lower lip and the mental region of the face." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001456 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/mentolabial-sulcus-1536888420" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:75019,
        ILX:0795327 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001456 ],
        UBERON:0000093 .

ILX:0795328 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "hyoid tubercle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A small prominence on the posterior end of the greater horn of hyoid bone, serving as an attachment point for muscles and ligaments. Each tubercle of hyoid bone provides an attachment site for a lateral thyrohyoid ligament." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0000974 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyoid_bone" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795328 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0000974 ],
        UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795329 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "inguinal crease" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The inguinal crease refers to the skin fold or line that forms where the lower abdomen meets the thigh, often most noticeable when the hip is flexed. It marks the boundary between the abdominal and thigh regions." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0000916 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/medicine-and-dentistry/inguinal-region" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795329 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0000916 ],
        UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795336 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "extensor pollicis brevis tendon" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The tendon of the muscle extending the proximal phalanx of the thumb, positioned laterally in the forearm." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795336 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0795337 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "extensor pollicis longus tendon" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The tendon of the muscle responsible for extending the thumb at the interphalangeal joint." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795337 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0795338 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "lateral supraepicondylar ridge" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The lateral supracondylar ridge (lateral supraepicondylar ridge or lateral supracondylar crest) is the sharp, prominent margin located along the lateral aspect of the distal end of the body of the humerus. It is the less curved of the two supracondylar ridges of the humerus, the other being the medial supracondylar ridge." ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/skeletal-system/appendicular-skeleton/lateral-supracondylar-ridge/18104" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:75078,
        ILX:0795338 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795502 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "tendon of extensor digitorum" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The tendon of the muscle that extends the fingers and assists in wrist extension, located on the posterior forearm." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:40734,
        ILX:0795502 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0795503 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "tendon of extensor hallucis longus" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The tendon of the muscle extending the big toe and assisting in dorsiflexion of the foot." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:47065,
        ILX:0795503 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0797451 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "subcostal nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The anterior division (rami anteriores; ventral divisions) of the twelfth thoracic spinal nerve. It emerges below the twelfth" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797451 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0003726 .

ILX:0797461 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dorsal digital nerve of radial nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A sensory branch of the superficial radial nerve supplying the dorsal aspect of the lateral digits of the hand." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001492 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797461 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Dorsal digital branch of radial nerve" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001492 ],
        UBERON:0001027 .

ILX:0797478 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Lesser occipital nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A branch of the cervical plexus (primarily C2) that supplies sensation to the scalp posterior and superior to the ear." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0003725 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:6871,
        ILX:0797478 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Small occipital nerve" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0003725 ],
        UBERON:0001027 .

ILX:0797479 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Zygomatic branch of the facial nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A branch of the facial nerve that innervates muscles of facial expression in the zygomatic and orbital regions." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001647 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797479 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Malar branch of facial nerve" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001647 ],
        UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0797483 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Dorsal digital nerve of foot" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A digital sensory nerve supplying the dorsal surface of one or more toes. These nerves arise primarily from the superficial fibular, deep fibular, or sural nerves." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001466 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797483 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Dorsal digital nerve of pes" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001466 ],
        UBERON:0003435 .

ILX:0797486 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Muscular branch of the femoral nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A motor branch of the femoral nerve supplying muscles of the anterior compartment of the thigh, including the quadriceps femoris." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001267 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797486 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Motor branch of femoral nerve" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001267 ],
        UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0797487 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Long thoracic nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A nerve arising from C5-C7 roots that innervates the serratus anterior muscle and contributes to scapular stabilization." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001814 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:65275,
        ILX:0797487 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "External respiratory nerve of Bell" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001814 ],
        UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0797488 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Fourth common palmar digital nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The most medial common palmar digital nerve, arising from the superficial branch of the ulnar nerve and dividing into proper digital nerves for adjacent fingers." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001494 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:44844,
        ILX:0797488 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Common palmar digital nerve IV" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001494 ],
        UBERON:0001027 .

ILX:0797492 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Motor branches of the suprascapular nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "Terminal motor branches of the suprascapular nerve supplying the supraspinatus and infraspinatus muscles." ;
    isPartOf: ILX:0794966 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797492 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Muscular branches of suprascapular nerve" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom ILX:0794966 ],
        UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0797498 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Deep brachial vein" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A deep vein accompanying the profunda brachii artery and draining the posterior compartment of the arm." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:22938,
        ILX:0797498 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Profunda brachii vein" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0004260 .

ILX:0797499 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Ascending cervical vein" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A vein accompanying the ascending cervical artery that drains deep cervical structures into the vertebral or inferior thyroid venous systems." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797499 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Vena cervicalis ascendens" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0003502 .

ILX:0797509 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Inferior ulnar collateral artery" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A branch of the brachial artery arising above the elbow that contributes to the arterial anastomosis around the medial aspect of the elbow joint." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001398 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:22710,
        ILX:0797509 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Arteria collateralis ulnaris inferior" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001398 ],
        UBERON:0004260 .

ILX:0797512 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Superior ulnar collateral vein" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A vein accompanying the superior ulnar collateral artery that drains into the brachial venous system." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001413 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797512 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Vena collateralis ulnaris superior" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001413 ],
        UBERON:0004260 .

ILX:0797513 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Inferior ulnar collateral vein" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A vein accompanying the inferior ulnar collateral artery that drains the medial elbow region." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001413 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797513 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Vena collateralis ulnaris inferior" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001413 ],
        UBERON:0004260 .

ILX:0797522 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Superior cardiac nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A sympathetic cardiac nerve arising from the superior cervical ganglion that contributes to the cardiac plexus and autonomic innervation of the heart." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001989 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:6578,
        ILX:0797522 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Superior cardiac branch of sympathetic trunk",
        "Superior cervical cardiac nerve" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001989 ],
        UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0797523 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Medial supraclavicular nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A cutaneous branch of the cervical plexus that supplies sensation to the skin over the sternoclavicular region and upper chest near the midline." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0003725 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:0329233,
        ILX:0797523 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Anterior supraclavicular nerve",
        "Medial branch of supraclavicular nerve" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0003725 ],
        ILX:0797474 .

ILX:0797524 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Branch of ansa cervicalis" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A motor branch arising from the ansa cervicalis that innervates one or more infrahyoid muscles of the anterior neck." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:82555,
        ILX:0797524 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Muscular branch of ansa cervicalis" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0797527 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "First dorsal metacarpal artery" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The first branch of the dorsal metacarpal arterial system, supplying the thumb, index finger, and adjacent dorsal hand. It commonly arises from the radial artery near the anatomical snuffbox." ;
    isPartOf: UBERON:0001404 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:22761,
        ILX:0797527 ;
    OboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Arteria metacarpalis dorsalis prima",
        "First dorsal metacarpal branch" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty partOf: ;
            owl:someValuesFrom UBERON:0001404 ],
        UBERON:0001637 .

TARA:0095074 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ST 5" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 48. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407",
