    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "瘈脈(脉)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0000033 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The posterior auricular branch of the great auricular nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "headache, tinnitus, deafness, infantile convulsion." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the head, at the centre of the mastoid process, at the junction of the upper two thirds and lower one third of the curved line from tE17 to tE20." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture subcutaneously 0.3-0.5 inch or prick with a three-edged needle to cause bleeding. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
