        "[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "陶道(道)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0008231 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The medial branch of the posterior ramus of the first thoracic nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "stiffness of the back, headache, malaria, febrile diseases." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "In the upper back region, in the depression inferior to the spinous process of the first thoracic vertebra (T1), on the posterior median line." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture obliquely upward 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Taodao" ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation UBERON:0004626,
        ILX:0795312 ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "Du 13",
        "Governor Vessel 13",
        "VG 13" ;
    tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation "The posterior branch of the first intercostal artery." ;
    tara-ap:isLocatedOnMeridian TARA:0386099 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty tara-op:hasSpecificReferenceLocation ;
