    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The medial antebrachial cutaneous nerve, the medial brachial cutaneous nerve and the ulnar nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "pain in the cardiac and hypochondriac regions, shoulder and arm." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the medial aspect of the arm, just medial to the biceps brachii muscle, 3 B-cun superior to the cubital crease. Note: With the elbow flexed and the arm abducted, Ht2 is located at the junction of the upper two thirds and lower one third of the line connecting Ht1 with Ht3." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
