tara-ap:hasAcupointInformation a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Acupoint Information"@en ;
    dcterms:description "An annotation property grouping all textual descriptive attributes of an acupoint, including its anatomical location, needling method, indications, vasculature, and innervation. Subproperties further specialize the type of description."@en ;
    rdfs:domain TARA:1132428 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:topTARAAnnotaionProperty .

tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Acupuncture Protocol" ;
    IAO:0000112 """The value for this should be a structured information about the acupuncturue protocol used by the trial study. Here is an example structure:

Example 1:
Acupoints selection and grouping: Combination of scalp, body, and auricular acupuncture specific to the affected areas of the child and inclusive of both sides of the body.
| Needling details: Not specified.
| Stimulation details: Not specified.
| Sham protocol details: No sham arm.

Example 2:
Point selection and grouping: Trigger points in the gluteals isolated by palpation ensuring reproduction of symptoms, mostly in the region of the upper outer buttock quadrant, 3 to 5 points per subject.
| Needling details: Sterile acupuncture needles (Seirin Corp, Shizuoka, Japan), 0.30 mm diameter, 25 mm long; pierced skin and advanced into trigger point until reproduction of pain or local twitch response; partially withdrawn and repeatedly advanced into muscle until pain resolved and no further twitches seen; retention time Not specified.
| Stimulation details: Manual repeated advancement into the muscle; no electrical or thermal stimulation.
| Sham protocol details: Non-penetrating modified acupuncture needle with sharp tip removed and glued back in sheath; tip applied to the skin over the trigger point with pressure for 10 or more seconds and moved slightly to simulate real needling, repeated at each point for up to one minute.""" ;
    dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
    dcterms:description """A dual-purpose annotation property that serves as a super-property grouping the granular acupuncture intervention sub-properties (method, needling, stimulation, sham, and acupoints), while simultaneously acting as a direct container for a single, structured free-text summary of the full acupuncture protocol.

This field should conatin a structured summary combining acupoint selection and grouping, needling details, stimulation details, and sham protocol details into one field (see the 'example of usage' for full worked examples)."""@en ;
    tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol" ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "hasAcupunctureIntervention" ;
    rdfs:domain TARA:6701896 ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasAcupunctureStudyMetadata ;
    skos:altLabel "Acupuncture_Protocol" .

tara-kb:hasStudyDesignMetadata a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Study Design Metadata" ;
    dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
    dcterms:description "A grouping annotation property that organizes the sub-properties describing the study's design, comparator groups, sample retention, and treatment schedule."@en ;
    dcterms:type tara-kb:grouping ;
    tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyDesignMetadata" ;
    rdfs:domain TARA:6701896 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasAcupunctureStudyMetadata ;
    skos:altLabel "Study_Design_Metadata" .

tara-kb:hasStudyFindings a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Study Findings" ;
    IAO:0000112 """"Main Results: The primary outcome showed a mean reduction of 2·3 days (95% CI 1·9–2·7) in the verum acupuncture group, 1·5 days (1·1–2·0) in the sham acupuncture group, and 2·1 days (1·5–2·7) in the standard therapy group. These differences were statistically significant compared with baseline (p<0·0001), but not across the treatment groups (p=0·09).

Clinical Conclusions: Treatment outcomes for migraine do not differ between patients treated with sham acupuncture, verum acupuncture, or standard therapy."

The example above captures the study findings based on the results and conclusions from the study 'Efficacy of acupuncture for the prophylaxis of migraine: a multicentre randomised controlled clinical trial'; PubMed link: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16545747"""@en ;
    dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
    dcterms:description """A dual-purpose annotation property that serves as a super-property grouping the interpreted findings sub-properties (clinical conclusions, comparative findings, effectiveness, main results, and proposed mechanism), while simultaneously acting as a direct container for a general free-text stuctured summary of the study's findings when a more specific sub-property does not apply.

This field should faithfully summarize what the paper reports as main results (the core numeric and statistical information of the primary and secondary endpoints) and clinical conclusions in a structured way, potentially including short direct quotations where appropriate."""@en ;
    tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyFindings" ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "Study Outcomes" ;
    rdfs:comment "In systematic reviews and clinical trial metadata, \"Findings\" or \"Conclusions\" are explicitly separated from raw outcome measures because they capture the interpreted results, statistical significance, and final takeaways of the research." ;
    rdfs:domain TARA:6701896 ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasAcupunctureStudyMetadata ;
    skos:altLabel "Study_Findings" .

