    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The branch of the medial dorsal cutaneous nerve of the foot and the saphenous nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "hernia, pain in the external genitalia, nocturnal emission, retention of urine, distending pain in the hypochondrium." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the anteromedial aspect of the ankle, in the depression medial to the tibialis anterior tendon, anterior to the medial malleolus. Note: LR4 is located midway between SP5 and St41." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularl 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
