    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "委陽(阳)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0001465 ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "stiffness and pain of the lower back, distension and fullness of the lower abdomen, edema, dysuria, cramp of the leg and foot." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the posterolateral aspect of the knee, just medial to the biceps femoris tendon in the popliteal crease. Note: The biceps femoris tendon is more prominent when the knee is slightly flexed." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
