    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "飛(飞)揚(扬)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0003823 ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "headache, blurred vision, nasal obstruction, epistaxis, back pain, hemorrhoids, weakness of the leg." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the posterolateral aspect of the leg, between the inferior border of the lateral head of the gastrocnemius muscle and the calcaneal tendon, at the same level as 7 B-cun proximal to BL60. Note: BL58 is located 1 B-cun lateral and distal to BL57, proximal to BL60." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.7-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
