    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The medial cutaneous branches of the posterior rami of the tenth and eleventh thoracic nerves; deeper, their lateral branches." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "jaundice, bitter taste of the mouth, pain in the chest and hypochondriac region, pulmonary tuberculosis, afternoon fever." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "In the upper back region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the tenth thoracic vertebra (T10), 1.5 B- cun lateral to the posterior median line." ;
