    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The branch of the axillary nerve; deeper in the superior aspect, the radial nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "pain in the scapular region, motor impairment of the hand and arm." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the shoulder girdle, posteroinferior to the shoulder joint, 1 B-cun superior to the posterior axillary fold. Note: When the arm is adducted, SI 9 is located 1 B-cun superior to the posterior axillary fold, posterior to the deltoid muscle." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
