    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0005462 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The lateral cutaneous branch of the posterior ramus of the second lumbar nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "low back pain, irregular menstruation, dysmenorrhea, asthma." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "In the lumbar region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the third lumbar vertebra (L3), 1.5 B-cun lateral to the posterior median line." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
