TARA:1357729 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "LU 5" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 28. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407",
        "[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridians. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "尺澤(泽,沢)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0001461 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The lateral antebrachial cutaneous nerve and the radial nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "cough, hemoptysis, afternoon fever, asthma, sore throat, fullness in the chest, infantile convulsion, spasmodic pain of the elbow and arm, mastitis." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription """On the anterior aspect of the elbow, at the cubital crease, in the depression lateral to the biceps brachii tendon.
Note: With the elbow flexed, LU5 is located at the cubital crease, between LI11 and PC3, separated from PC3 by the biceps brachii tendon.""" ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1 inch." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Chize" ;
