    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "太衝(冲)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0002387 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The branch of the deep peroneal nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "headache, dizziness and vertigo, insomnia, congestion, swelling and pain of the eye, depression, infantile convulsion, deviation of the mouth, pain in the hypochondriac region, uterine bleeding, hernia, enuresis, retention of urine, epilepsy, pain in the anterior aspect of the medial malleolus." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the dorsum of the foot, between the first and second metatarsal bones, in the depression distal to the junction of the bases of the two bones, over the dorsalis pedis artery. Note: LR3 can be felt in the depression when moving proximally from Lr2 in the gap between the first and second metatarsal bones towards the base of two metatarsal bones." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Taichong" ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecialPointRole TARA:1840369,
        TARA:6705086 ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation UBERON:0001539,
        UBERON:0003650,
        UBERON:0003651 ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "LIV 3",
        "LV 3",
        "Liver 3" ;
    tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation "The dorsal venous network of the foot, the first dorsal metatarsal artery." ;
    tara-ap:isLocatedOnMeridian TARA:5419503 ;
